# Core lexicon: general vocabulary of everyday life and of modern subjects, sorted by keyword.
# A row with q is a draft that no speaker of the language has confirmed yet.
a = (i:3) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:his/her/its/their) (d:third person marker placed before a noun to show the possessor, as in {a pawlpihte}, its allies, and {a genna}, his statement; the prefix {a} of the other senses stands before a verb or describing word) (r:ts:12506/ts:10491/ts:10413) (q:draft)
a phakin = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:time/everyday) (w:at the age of/on reaching) (d:<a>, the subject marker, and a form of <phak>, reach, with the linking ending {-in}, written like <phakin>, be leprous, but another word: placed after <kum> and a number, when he or she reached that age, at the age of) (r:zd:11279/zd:23138) (q:draft)
a sawtna = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:eventually/in the long run/in the end) (d:<a> and <sawtna>, length of time: followed by <ciangin>, <ah> or <teh>, when much time has passed, eventually, in the long run) (r:zd:23113/zd:18958) (q:draft)
aa = (i:2) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:and/and so) (d:links two verbs or clauses in a row, and, and so; a spelling of the linking <a> written long after a verb or after <uh>, <hi> and <lo>, not the possessive {aa} after a possessor) (r:zd:25927/ts:3508/zd:25790) (q:draft)
aading = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:everyday) (j:ading) (r:zd:8667/zd:22140/zd:16765) (q:draft)
aadingin = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:everyday) (j:adingin) (r:zd:23863/zd:19108) (q:draft)
aakipan = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:everyday/time) (j:akipan) (r:zd:22550/zd:22658) (q:draft)
aalu = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (f:food) (w:potato) (d:the potato, a root crop cooked and eaten as a dish) (o:Burmese, alu) (r:zd:20131) (q:draft)
aana = (i:3) (t:v) (f:social) (w:be reluctant to impose/feel bad about troubling/hesitate) (d:a different word from {aana}, authority: feel that one would be troubling or imposing on someone and so hold back from asking; {aana lua} is feel very bad about imposing, {aana huai} is awkward to ask, and {aana lotak in} is without hesitation) (r:zd:23240/zd:22875) (q:draft)
aanaa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (j:aana) (r:zd:22992/zd:19239) (q:draft)
aang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (j:ang) (r:zd:20158) (q:draft)
aangsung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (j:angsung) (r:zd:23241/zd:23476) (q:draft)
aangtang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (j:angtang) (r:zd:19697/zd:25277) (q:draft)
aaom = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (j:aom) (r:zd:24333/zd:23952) (q:draft)
aap = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (j:ap) (r:zd:23301/zd:18234) (q:draft)
aapna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (j:apna) (r:zd:22778) (q:draft)
abaai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:the maimed/the injured) (d:<a> with <bai>, lame, written long and as one word; used in the pair {aliam abaai}, the wounded and the maimed, the injured) (j:a/bai) (r:zd:15811/zd:12124) (q:draft)
abaang = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:stained with/bearing) (d:<a> and <baang> written as one word: that which a thing clings to, as {si abaang}, stained with blood, and {min abaang}, bearing a name) (j:a/baang) (r:zd:16700/zd:23765) (q:draft)
abai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/media) (w:the maimed/the crippled/injured person) (d:<a> and <bai>, lame, written as one word; in news reports in the pair <aliam abai>, the injured and the maimed, with <aliam>: {aliam abai omlo} is no one was hurt) (j:a/bai) (r:zd:14736/zd:25027/ts:12263) (q:draft)
abaih = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:easy/the easy one) (d:<a> and <baih> written as one word: easy, what is easy; {abaih hetlo} is not easy at all) (j:a/baih) (r:zd:17971/zd:25173/zd:11375) (q:draft)
abaihsa = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:ready/in readiness/prepared) (d:<a> and <baihsa> written as one word, mostly as {abaihsa in om}: be ready, stand prepared) (j:a/baihsa) (r:zd:24047/zd:12176) (q:draft)
aban = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday/media) (w:next/furthermore/in addition) (d:with <ah>, at the head of a sentence: next, besides what has just been said; the same as <banah> written with <a> before it, and different from {aban} in a row, one after another) (r:zd:13070/zd:22990) (q:draft, low confidence)
abanban = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:one after another/in turn/in order) (d:<aban> and <ban> written as one word, usually followed by <in>: one after another, each in its turn) (s:banbanin) (j:aban/ban) (r:zd:15274/zd:20859/zd:12965) (q:draft)
abanbanin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:one after another/in turn/step by step) (d:<abanban> and <in> written as one word: one after the other, each in its turn, level by level) (j:abanban/in) (r:zd:24743/zd:24213) (q:draft)
abang = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:like/as/similar to) (d:<a> and <bang> written as one word, placed after the thing compared: that which is like it; <anuai abang> is as follows, like what is below) (j:a/bang) (r:zd:18150/zd:14791/zd:25109) (q:draft)
abangci = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:how) (d:<a> and <bangci> written as one word: how, in what way, in a question) (j:a/bangci) (r:zd:17526/zd:13314) (q:draft)
abangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:as/like/in the way of) (d:<a> and <bangin> written as one word; nearly always in <anuai abangin>, as below, as follows) (j:a/bangin) (r:zd:24182/zd:12336/zd:22341) (q:draft)
Abaraham = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (f:religion) (j:Abraham) (r:zd:20716) (q:draft)
abatleh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/media) (w:judging by/going by) (d:<abat>, be like, and <leh>, if, written as one word, placed after what one goes by: if it is as, judging by, as in {agendan uh abatleh}, going by what they say) (j:abat/leh) (r:zd:12171/zd:19801) (q:draft, low confidence)
abawk = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/body) (w:lump/swelling/tumour) (d:<a> and <bawk> written as one word: a swelling or lump on the body; also as a verb, it swelled) (j:a/bawk) (r:zd:17862/zd:17709) (q:draft)
abawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:make/do) (d:<a> and <bawl> written as one word: he or they make or do, or the one who makes) (j:a/bawl) (r:zd:15384/zd:25789/zd:11463) (q:draft)
abawlbawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:keep doing/be doing/carry on) (d:<a> and <bawlbawl> written as one word: he or they keep doing or making, the one who keeps doing) (j:a/bawlbawl) (r:zd:22435/ts:9370/zd:11675) (q:draft)
abawlden = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:always do/keep doing/do regularly) (d:<a> and <bawlden> written as one word: he or they keep doing it, or the one who does it regularly) (j:a/bawlden) (r:zd:17649/zd:22350) (q:draft)
abawlding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:will do/will make/will carry out) (d:<a>, <bawl> and <ding> written as one word: he will do or hold it, the one who is to do it, what is to be done) (j:a/bawl/ding) (r:zd:13005/zd:12016) (q:draft)
abawlkawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:while doing/while making) (d:<abawl>, he does, with <kawm>, while, written as one word and often followed by <in>: at the same time as doing something, in the course of doing it) (j:abawl/kawm) (r:zd:18303/zd:22223) (q:draft)
abawlkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:hold together/do jointly) (d:<a> and <bawlkhawm> written as one word: they hold or do it together, or those who hold it together) (j:a/bawlkhawm) (r:zd:16506/zd:16830) (q:draft)
abawlkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:make/produce/manufacture) (d:<a>, <bawl> and <khia> written as one word: the one that makes or produces something, as in {abawlkhia Company}, the company that manufactured it) (j:a/bawl/khia) (r:zd:16919/zd:15814) (q:draft)
abawlkhiapa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/everyday) (w:maker/creator/founder) (d:<abawlkhia>, that makes or produces, and <pa>, man, written as one word: the man who made, produced or founded something) (j:abawlkhia/pa) (r:zd:12376/zd:17450) (q:draft)
abawlkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:produce/manufacture/make) (d:<a>, <bawl> and <khiat> written as one word: that which he or they produced, said of goods that a company makes) (j:a/bawl/khiat) (r:zd:15097/zd:19355) (q:draft)
abawlkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have done/finish doing) (d:<a> and <bawlkhit> written as one word; {abawlkhit ciangin} is after he has done or made it) (j:a/bawlkhit) (r:zd:16757/zd:12618) (q:draft)
abawlkik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:do again/make again) (d:<a> and <bawlkik> written as one word: he does or they do it again, or what is done again) (j:a/bawlkik) (r:zd:14808/zd:11941) (q:draft)
abawllaitak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:while doing/while holding) (d:<a>, <bawl> and <laitak> written as one word: at the very time when he or she is doing or holding something) (j:a/bawl/laitak) (r:zd:19478/zd:15888) (q:draft)
abawllo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:not do/not make/who has not done) (d:<a> and <bawllo> written as one word: he did not make or do, or the one who has not made or done it, as a card or a registration) (j:a/bawllo) (r:zd:19143/zd:15397) (q:draft)
abawlna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/work) (w:doing/making/carrying out) (d:<a> and <bawlna> written as one word: his, her or their doing or making of something; {abawlna ah} is in what they did, and {abawlna pan} from or while doing it) (j:a/bawlna) (r:zd:24453/zd:24489) (q:draft)
abawlpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:maker/doer/the one who did it) (d:<a> and <bawlpa> written as one word: the one who made or did something) (j:a/bawlpa) (r:zd:17673/zd:13233) (q:draft)
abawlpah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:make at once/do immediately) (d:<a> and <bawlpah> written as one word: he, she or they make or do it at once; {Police Report abawlpah} is filed a police report at once) (j:a/bawlpah) (r:zd:14678/zd:14535) (q:draft)
abawlpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:the one who made/the one who did) (d:<a>, <bawl> and <pen> written as one word: the one who made or did it, or the doing of it, as the topic of the sentence; {Register abawlpen mi} are the people who registered) (j:a/bawl/pen) (r:zd:19470/zd:18911) (q:draft)
abawlsa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:made/already made/have made) (d:<a> and <bawlsa> written as one word: what he has made, or having already made or done it; before a noun it describes it, as {abawlsa nate}, the things he has made) (j:a/bawlsa) (r:zd:16376/zd:17269) (q:draft)
abawlsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:did for/carried out) (d:<a> and <bawlsak> written as one word: did or made something for someone, and the one who carried it out) (j:a/bawlsak) (r:zd:18248/zd:13309/zd:13186) (q:draft)
abawlsakding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:that will make/that will carry out) (d:<abawlsak> and <ding> written as one word: that will make or do something for someone) (j:abawlsak/ding) (r:zd:17668/zd:17822) (q:draft)
abawlsan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:be doing/be carrying out/be preparing) (d:<a> with <bawl>, make or do, and <san>, written as one word; almost always as {abawlsan laitak}, they are in the course of doing it, said of an investigation or of papers being prepared; the exact force of <san> is not clear, compare <sepsan>) (b:bawl) (r:zd:16647/zd:20466) (q:draft)
abawlsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:plan to do/try to do/be about to make) (d:<a>, <bawl>, do or make, and <sawm>, intend, written as one word: he or they intend or attempt to do it, the one who was about to do it) (j:a/bawl/sawm) (r:zd:16702/zd:19307/zd:14566) (q:draft)
abawlsia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:mistreat/abuse) (d:<a> and <bawlsia> written as one word: the one who mistreated or abused, who ill-treated) (j:a/bawlsia) (r:zd:15848/zd:14901) (q:draft)
abawlsiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:mistreat/abuse/harm) (d:<a> and <bawlsiat> written as one word: he mistreated, or the one whom he mistreated or abused) (j:a/bawlsiat) (r:zd:13024/zd:14613) (q:draft)
abawlsiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/media) (w:abuse/mistreatment) (d:<a> and <bawlsiatna> written as one word: the abuse someone did, or the abuse of the person named before it) (j:a/bawlsiatna) (r:zd:13266/zd:11592) (q:draft)
abawltawm = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/media) (w:self-made/home-made/fake) (d:<a> and <bawltawm> written as one word: that someone made himself, and so not the real or official thing, said of forged papers, false number plates and home-brewed drink) (j:a/bawltawm) (r:zd:11920/zd:13059) (q:draft)
abawlte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:those who do/those who make) (d:<a> and <bawlte> written as one word: the people who do or make what is named before it) (j:a/bawlte) (r:zd:17897/zd:11269) (q:draft)
abawltheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:be able to do/can carry out) (d:<a> and <bawltheih> written as one word, mostly before <nading> or <nadingin>: so that he, she or they can do or carry out what is named before it) (j:a/bawltheih) (r:zd:16885/zd:14836) (q:draft)
abawlzia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/work) (w:way of making/way of doing/method) (d:<a> and <bawlzia> written as one word: the way he, she or they make or do something) (j:a/bawlzia) (r:zd:19289/zd:16175) (q:draft)
abeh = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:his clan/her clan) (d:<a> and <beh> written as one word: his, her or their clan) (j:a/beh) (r:zd:18107/zd:15364) (q:draft)
abehlap = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:add/increase/addition) (d:<a> and <behlap> written as one word: he or they add, or what is added, an addition) (j:a/behlap) (r:zd:21262/zd:22782) (q:draft)
abei = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:end/expire/run out/be spent) (d:<bei> with the prefix <a> written joined, used as the predicate: come to an end, expire, said of a card or a term, or be spent, said of money; {abei sa} is past, gone by; not the adjective last of {abei ni}) (r:zd:16051/zd:25288/zd:15805) (q:draft)
abeiding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:time/everyday) (w:will end/will expire) (d:<a> and <beiding> written as one word: it will come to an end; {ahun abeiding} is its time will run out) (j:a/beiding) (r:zd:20912/zd:16729) (q:draft)
abeiding = (i:2) (t:v) (f:work) (w:will cost) (d:<a> and <beiding> written as one word, said of money: the amount that will be spent) (j:a/beiding) (r:zd:12980) (q:draft, low confidence)
abeikhitzawh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:time) (w:after it ended/after the expiry of) (d:<a>, <bei> and <khitzawh> written as one word: once something, as a deadline or programme, has come to an end) (j:a/bei/khitzawh) (r:zd:14505/zd:13270) (q:draft)
abeilawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:lose/spend) (d:<a> and <beilawh> written as one word: he loses or spends it for something; {nuntakna abeilawh} is lost his life) (j:a/beilawh) (r:zd:17703/zd:18896/zd:20979) (q:draft)
abeisa = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:time) (w:last/past/previous) (d:<a> and <beisa> written as one word: the past, the one that has gone by, placed before a month, a year or a date) (j:a/beisa) (r:ts:5440/ts:5293) (q:draft)
abeisa hun = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:the past/past times/former times) (d:<abeisa>, past, and <hun>, time: the time that has gone by; with <in> or <ah> it opens a sentence as in the past, previously, and {abeisa hun sung} is during the past period) (r:zd:10983/zd:25062) (q:draft)
abeisakum = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:last year) (d:<a>, <beisa>, past, and <kum>, year, written as one word: last year, the year that has gone by) (j:a/beisa/kum) (r:zd:11383/zd:16806/zd:11401) (q:draft)
abeisiang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be completely gone/be wiped out) (d:<a> and <beisiang> written as one word: they are all gone, with nothing left; {abeisiang mateng} is until none are left) (j:a/beisiang) (r:zd:14611) (q:draft, low confidence)
abeita = (i:1) (t:v) (f:time/everyday) (w:has ended/has expired/is over) (d:<a> and <beita> written as one word: it has now come to an end, said of a period or a deadline) (j:a/beita) (r:zd:20276/zd:19130) (q:draft)
abeizah = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:cost/amount spent/expense) (d:<a>, <bei>, be used up, and <zah>, amount, written as one word: how much is spent or used up, of money, time or fuel) (j:a/bei/zah) (r:zd:22571/zd:23077) (q:draft)
abeizawh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:time) (w:after it ended/after the expiry) (d:<a>, <bei> and <zawh> written as one word, <zawh> in the sense after: after it came to an end, said of a period or deadline) (j:a/bei/zawh) (r:zd:14505/zd:15397) (q:draft)
abelh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:take refuge in/shelter with) (d:<a> and <belh> written as one word: he takes refuge in, the one or the place in which someone takes refuge) (j:a/belh) (r:zd:25532/zd:25203) (q:draft)
abeng = (i:1) (t:v) (f:nature/work) (w:hunt/hunter of) (d:<a> and <beng>, hunt, written as one word after the animal or person pursued: the one who hunts it, or he hunts; the same spelling also stands for <a> with <beng>, clap, and for the ear in {abeng angong}, deaf) (j:a/beng) (r:zd:11594) (q:draft, low confidence)
abengding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/nature) (w:to hunt/to chase) (d:<a>, <beng> and <ding> written as one word: in order to hunt an animal or chase after someone, those who are to hunt) (j:a/beng/ding) (r:zd:16749) (q:draft)
abia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:religion) (w:worship) (d:<a> and <bia>, worship, written as one word: he worships, or the one who worships, as in {Pasian abia mite}, the people who worship God) (j:a/bia) (r:zd:8668/zd:15859) (q:draft)
Abiahang = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (f:religion) (j:Abraham) (r:zd:21939/zd:22827) (q:draft)
abiakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:his religion/their religion) (d:<a> and <biakna> written as one word: his, her or their religion; {abiakna kibatpih te} are those of the same religion) (j:a/biakna) (r:zd:11697/zd:12746) (q:draft)
abiang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:his cheek/her cheek) (d:<a> and <biang> written as one word: his or her cheek) (j:a/biang) (r:zd:17279/zd:25433) (q:draft)
abil = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:his ear/her ear) (d:<a>, his or her, and <bil>, ear, written as one word) (j:a/bil) (r:zd:21826/zd:12068) (q:draft)
abit = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:home/everyday) (w:closed/shut tight/enclosed/secure) (d:<a> and <bit> written as one word: closed in or shut tight so that nothing gets in or out; also firm, secure) (j:a/bit) (r:zd:17355/zd:21040) (q:draft)
abombi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:trousers/pants) (d:<a>, his or her, and <bombi>, trousers, written as one word: his or her trousers; {abombi sung} is inside the trousers) (j:a/bombi) (r:zd:15456/zd:17930) (q:draft)
abortion = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/politics) (w:abortion) (d:the ending of a pregnancy; mostly added in brackets after a Zolai wording such as <nauphiat>) (o:English) (r:zd:24144) (q:draft, low confidence)
abuai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be busy/be occupied/be troubled) (d:<a> and <buai> written as one word: he or they are busy or caught up in something, as {abuai laitak}, while busy; also be troubled or confused) (j:a/buai) (r:zd:12829/zd:17952) (q:draft)
abuaimahmah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:be very busy/be most occupied) (d:<a> and <buaimahmah> written as one word: that is very busy, when people or a place are at their busiest) (j:a/buaimahmah) (r:zd:11786/zd:10768) (q:draft)
abuaipih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:be busy with/attend to/deal with) (d:<a>, <buai> and <pih> written as one word: be busy with something, be taken up with dealing with it, as rescuers with an accident or soldiers with a conflict) (j:a/buai/pih) (r:zd:15792/zd:12355/zd:22214) (q:draft)
abuaipihkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:after working on/having dealt with) (d:<abuaipih> and <khit> written as one word, followed by {uh ciangin}: after they had worked on it for the time named) (j:abuaipih/khit) (r:zd:18012/zd:20535) (q:draft)
abuaisak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:trouble/disturb/cause unrest in) (d:<a> and <buaisak> written as one word: that troubles, the one who causes trouble or unrest in a place) (j:a/buaisak) (r:zd:15331/zd:15188) (q:draft)
abuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:pour on/throw on) (d:<a> and <buak> written as one word: he pours a liquid on someone, or the one who poured it) (j:a/buak) (r:zd:12598) (q:draft, low confidence)
abuan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:rape) (d:<a> with a verb meaning force a person to have sex, written as one word: he raped, the one who raped; that verb is spelled like <buan>, mud, but is a different word) (r:zd:15922) (q:draft)
abuanhuan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/media) (w:rape/gang-rape) (d:<a> and <buanhuan> written as one word: he or they raped, the ones who raped) (j:a/buanhuan) (r:zd:20482/zd:19540) (q:draft)
abuankhit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:after raping) (d:<abuan>, he raped, and <khit>, after, written as one word, in {abuankhit ciangin}: after he had raped her) (j:abuan/khit) (r:zd:12979) (q:draft)
abuanna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:rape/place of rape) (d:<abuan> with the ending <na>, written as one word: his raping of a person; {abuanna mun} is the place where he raped) (j:abuan/na) (r:zd:11333) (q:draft, low confidence)
abuanpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:rapist) (d:<a>, <buan> and <pa>, the man who, written as one word: the man who raped; <buan> here means rape, not mud) (j:a/buan/pa) (r:zd:15922/zd:16961) (q:draft)
abuansawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:try to rape) (d:<a> written together with <buansawm>: the one who tried to rape, or when he tried to rape; <buan> here is not mud but force a person sexually) (j:a/buan/sawm) (r:zd:18077/zd:12591) (q:draft)
abuansawmpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:attempted rapist/man who tried to rape) (d:<abuansawm> and <pa> written as one word: the man who tried to rape) (j:abuansawm/pa) (r:zd:17117) (q:draft)
abuante = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:rapists/those raped) (d:<abuan> with the plural <te> written as one word: those who rape, or with a noun before it the ones whom he raped) (j:abuan/te) (r:zd:20482) (q:draft)
abucing = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:complete/full/whole) (d:<a> and <bucing> written as one word: complete, in full; before a verb or verbal noun, completely) (j:a/bucing) (r:zd:23315/zd:24281) (q:draft)
abul = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/nature) (w:its base/its root/the beginning) (d:<a> and <bul>, base, written as one word: the foot or root end of a thing, and the beginning or origin of a matter; {abul abal} is a matter from its root, in full) (j:a/bul) (r:zd:18003/zd:22775) (q:draft)
abulh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:home/body) (w:wear/have on) (d:<a> and <bulh> written as one word: he or she wears on the hand, finger or foot, and the thing that is worn there, such as a watch, a ring or shoes) (j:a/bulh) (r:zd:16832/zd:12402) (q:draft)
abulpan = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:nature/everyday) (w:from the base/by the roots/from the root) (d:<a>, <bul>, base, and <pan>, from, written as one word: from its base or root, said of a tree that is torn out whole, of teeth, and of a matter taken from its beginning) (j:a/bul/pan) (r:zd:19925/zd:20188/zd:14587) (q:draft)
abulphuh = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/education) (w:based on/founded on) (d:<a> and <bulphuh> written as one word: that is based on, that takes something as its foundation) (j:a/bulphuh) (r:zd:19662/zd:24604) (q:draft)
abulpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:the foundation/the root/the main one) (d:<a> and <bulpi> written as one word: the foundation or source of something, and before a noun the main or basic ones) (j:a/bulpi) (r:zd:15274/zd:24336) (q:draft)
abuluh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:raid/attack/invade/rob) (d:<a> and <buluh> written as one word: he or they raid or attack, or the one that raids; said of robbers breaking into a shop and of an army invading a country) (j:a/buluh) (r:zd:25584/zd:25203/zd:16926) (q:draft)
abung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/everyday) (w:container/bottle/bin) (d:<a> and <bung> written as one word: its container, the tin, bottle, bin or cylinder that holds something) (j:a/bung) (r:zd:12638/zd:25251) (q:draft)
Academy = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/education) (w:Academy Award/academy) (d:in Myanmar usage the national film prize, the Myanmar Academy Award, and a title before the name of an actor who has won it; elsewhere part of the English name of a school or institute) (o:English) (r:zd:11348/zd:24422) (q:draft, low confidence)
Accelerator = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:accelerator/gas pedal) (d:the pedal of a motor vehicle that makes it go faster; {accelerator sik} is step on the accelerator) (o:English) (r:zd:21869/zd:19554/zd:15207) (q:draft)
accent = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/social) (w:accent) (d:the way a people or a region pronounces a language; the Zolai word is <awsuah>) (o:English) (r:zd:22802/zd:11837) (q:draft)
