aciahlam = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:travel/everyday) (w:on the way back/on the way home) (d:<a>, <ciah>, return, and <lam>, way, written as one word: while he, she or they were going back home, often followed by <in>) (j:a/ciah/lam) (r:zd:12261/zd:19465/zd:15228) (q:draft)
aciahna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/everyday) (w:his return/his way home) (d:<a> and <ciahna> written as one word: his or her going home; {aciahna lampi} is the way by which he goes home) (j:a/ciahna) (r:zd:11269/zd:11350) (q:draft)
aciahnading = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:travel) (w:for the return/in order to go back) (d:<aciah> and <nading> written as one word: for his or their going back home) (j:aciah/nading) (r:zd:20912/zd:13270) (q:draft)
aciahnuam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:want to go back/who wants to return) (d:<a>, <ciah>, go back, and <nuam>, want, written as one word: the one who wants to go home, or he wants to go back) (j:a/ciah/nuam) (r:zd:20276/zd:20257) (q:draft)
aciahsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:be about to return/be on the way home/intend to go back) (d:<aciah> and <sawm> written as one word: who means to go back or is on the way home) (j:aciah/sawm) (r:zd:17876/zd:15577) (q:draft)
aciahsuk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:going down/returning down) (d:<a> and <ciahsuk> written as one word: that goes or was going back down, said of a vehicle or traveller coming down from a higher place) (j:a/ciahsuk) (r:zd:20099/zd:19112) (q:draft)
aciahte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:those who return/those going home) (d:<aciah>, who returns, and the plural <te> written as one word: the people who go back or go home) (j:aciah/te) (r:zd:15469/zd:19569) (q:draft)
aciahtheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:be able to return/can go home) (d:<a>, <ciah>, return, and <theih>, be able, written as one word; before <nadingin> it means so that he can go home) (j:a/ciah/theih) (r:zd:11681/zd:17876) (q:draft)
acial = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:hire/employ) (d:<a> and <cial>, hire, written as one word: he or they hired someone, the one who hires) (j:a/cial) (r:zd:20505/zd:20222) (q:draft)
aciamnuih = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:joke/jest/as a joke) (d:<a> and <ciamnuih>, jest, written as one word: the joke, something said or done as a joke) (j:a/ciamnuih) (r:zd:14498/zd:21042) (q:draft)
aciamteh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/education) (w:record/note) (d:<a> and <ciamteh>, note or record, written as one word: that he records, what is recorded) (j:a/ciamteh) (r:zd:24068/zd:22097) (q:draft)
acian = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:remaining/the rest/left over) (d:<a> joined to a verb that means be left over: what is left after the part already named, often as {acian lai}, still remaining) (r:zd:11380/zd:10746) (q:draft)
aciang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:each to its extent/as far as one can) (d:<a> and <ciang>, extent, written as one word; said twice, {aciang aciang}, each as far as it reaches, everyone according to what they can) (j:a/ciang) (r:zd:19051) (q:draft, low confidence)
aciangtan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:time/everyday) (w:set/fix/appoint/limit) (d:<a> and <ciangtan> written as one word: that which is fixed or limited, or they fix it; {ahun aciangtan} is the appointed time and {aciangtan ani} the set day, the deadline) (j:a/ciangtan) (r:zd:13205/zd:11308/zd:11594) (q:draft)
acianlai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:remaining/left/still left) (d:who or what is still left when the others are gone or done; as a noun, the remainder, the remnant) (s:omlai) (r:zd:24064/zd:20387/zd:15317) (q:draft)
aciapteh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:designate/mark/regard as/recognise) (d:<a> with <ciapteh>, a form of <ciamteh>, written as one word: note, mark or officially designate something as what is named before it) (j:a/ciapteh) (r:zd:16431) (q:draft)
acici = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/social) (w:those who keep saying/who claim) (d:<a> and <cici> written as one word, after the words quoted: one who says so again and again, who keeps claiming; with <te>, the people who say so) (j:a/cici) (r:zd:16833/zd:14549/zd:10951) (q:draft)
