acidamna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:his health/her health/their health) (d:<a> and <cidamna> written as one word: his, her or its health) (j:a/cidamna) (r:zd:11508/zd:23830) (q:draft)
acidiam = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (d:<aci> and <diam> written as one word, after <bang>, what, and a clause with if: what would it say, that is, how would it be, what would come of it) (j:aci/diam) (r:zd:19021/zd:14783) (q:draft)
acih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:say/call/mean) (d:<a> and <cih> written as one word: what he says, what is called; {X acih bang hiam} is what is the thing called X, and {acih nopna} is what it means) (j:a/cih) (r:zd:21633/zd:22818/zd:24638) (q:draft)
acihcih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:keep calling/used to call) (d:<a> and <cihcih> written as one word: what people keep saying or calling, the so-called) (j:a/cihcih) (r:zd:12409) (q:draft, low confidence)
acihin = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (d:<acih> and <in> written as one word between a repeated word, for emphasis: {tam acihin tam} is many indeed, as many as one could say; with a verb, doing it to the full) (j:acih/in) (r:zd:15178/zd:15084) (q:draft, low confidence)
acihleh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:when he said/if it says) (d:<a>, <cih> and <leh> written as one word: when or if someone says so, placed after the words that are said) (j:a/cih/leh) (r:zd:23432/zd:13282) (q:draft)
acihmawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:be in distress/be in trouble/be desperate) (d:<a> and <cihmawh> written as one word: is in distress or at a loss what to do, or the one who is) (j:a/cihmawh) (r:zd:25928/zd:15579) (q:draft)
