Administration = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:administration/government) (d:the governing of a town, district or country and the office that does it, as in {Tedim Administration zumpi}; after the name of a president, his government) (o:English) (r:zd:20883/zd:24909) (q:draft, low confidence)
Administrator = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/work) (w:administrator) (d:an official who runs an office, a district or an organisation) (o:English) (r:zd:21843) (q:draft, low confidence)
admission = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/travel) (w:admission/enrolment) (d:acceptance into a school or university, with <bawl>, <ngah> or <pia>; also the admitting of people into a country) (o:English) (r:zd:15622/zd:23533) (q:draft)
ado = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:fight/attack/who fights) (d:<a> and <do> written as one word: he or they fight, the one who fights against; {gal ado} is wage war) (j:a/do) (r:zd:25582/zd:12179) (q:draft)
adon = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:pay attention/care for/attend to) (d:<a> and <don> written as one word: he heeds or attends to, the one who heeds; {adon lo} is who disregards) (j:a/don) (r:zd:14791/zd:13114) (q:draft)
adong = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:ask/inquire) (d:<a> and <dong> written as one word: he or she asks, or the one who asks) (j:a/dong) (r:zd:24502/zd:21655) (q:draft)
adot = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:ask/he asked) (d:<a> and <dot> written as one word: he or she asks, used before <leh>, <hangin> and <ciangin>) (j:a/dot) (r:zd:12669/zd:20289/zd:23136) (q:draft)
aduh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/food) (w:like/crave/want) (d:<a> and <duh> written as one word: he or she likes or craves it, what one craves, or with <te> those who like it; <duh> here is to want or be fond of, mostly of food) (j:a/duh) (r:zd:21961/zd:19447) (q:draft)
aduhlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food/everyday) (w:not like/not want) (d:<a> and <duhlo> written as one word: he or she does not like or want it; with <te>, those who do not like it) (j:a/duhlo) (r:zd:19447/zd:17022) (q:draft)
adum = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:blue/the blue one) (d:<a> and <dum>, blue, written as one word: what is blue, the blue colour; also said of violet) (j:a/dum) (r:zd:22289/zd:21703) (q:draft, low confidence)
advance = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/social) (w:advanced/ahead) (d:further on in knowledge or development; {advance zaw} is more advanced) (o:English) (r:zd:21134/zd:15274) (q:draft, low confidence)
advertisement = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/work) (w:advertisement/advertising) (d:a public notice that makes goods or a company known, in Zolai also called {kyawngia} from Burmese) (o:English) (r:zd:20207/zd:16748) (q:draft)
advice = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/work) (w:advice/counsel) (d:guidance given by someone who knows the matter, mostly of legal, medical or official advice; said with <pia>, give) (o:English) (r:zd:18159/zd:17903) (q:draft)
adviser = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/work) (w:adviser/advisor) (d:a person who gives advice, as a post in a government or an organisation) (o:English) (r:zd:17838) (q:draft, low confidence)
Advisors = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/work) (w:advisers/advisors) (d:the English plural used in Zolai for the people who advise a leader or the committee of an organisation) (o:English) (r:zd:21217/zd:24333) (q:draft, low confidence)
Advocate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/work) (w:advocate/lawyer) (d:a lawyer admitted to plead in court, also used as a title before a name; also someone who speaks up for a cause) (o:English) (r:zd:16210) (q:draft, low confidence)
Afghan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:politics) (w:Afghan) (d:of Afghanistan or its people; {Afghan mi} is an Afghan) (r:zd:11180/zd:10877/zd:12759) (q:draft)
Afghanistan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:politics) (w:Afghanistan) (d:country in Central Asia) (r:zd:26163/zd:12176) (q:draft)
AFPFL = (i:1) (t:name) (f:politics) (w:AFPFL/Anti-Fascist People's Freedom League) (d:the party that governed Burma after independence, known in Burmese as Pha-Sa-Pa-La; in 1958 it split into the Clean and the Stable AFPFL) (o:English) (r:zd:24714/zd:25263) (q:draft)
Africa = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel/politics) (w:Africa) (d:the continent of Africa, mostly as {Africa gam}; also in the names of its countries, as South Africa) (r:zd:23754/zd:20334) (q:draft)
African = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:social) (w:African) (d:of Africa or its people, the English word used before a noun or with <te>; {African te} are the Africans) (o:English) (r:zd:14502/zd:11027) (q:draft)
agah = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature/everyday) (w:its fruit/its result) (d:<a> and <gah> written as one word: the fruit of a plant, or the result of work or conduct; before a verb also it bears fruit) (j:a/gah) (r:zd:21822/zd:11251/zd:20657) (q:draft)
agai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/health) (w:be pregnant/conceive) (d:<a> and <gai> written as one word: she is pregnant, and her being pregnant; {agai lam} is the fact that she is pregnant) (j:a/gai) (r:zd:17372/zd:21793/zd:15286) (q:draft)
agaisak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/health) (w:one who made pregnant) (d:<a> and <gaisak>, make pregnant, written as one word before a noun: the man who made her pregnant) (j:a/gaisak) (r:zd:11782) (q:draft)
agal = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/travel) (w:across/at a distance/from afar) (d:<a> and <gal>, the far side, written as one word: the other side, a place some way off; {agal panin} is from across or from a distance, and {agal et} is look on from afar) (j:a/gal) (r:zd:12564/zd:21439) (q:draft)
agalkap = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:his soldiers/their troops) (d:<a> and <galkap> written as one word: his soldiers, their army) (j:a/galkap) (r:zd:10746/zd:18142) (q:draft)
agalkap = (i:2) (t:v) (f:media) (w:shoot at/fire at) (d:in reports of shootings, after <thautawh>, with a gun: shoot at someone, apparently <agal>, from a distance, with <kap>, shoot) (j:agal/kap) (r:zd:17491/zd:15976) (q:draft, low confidence)
agalkhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/travel) (w:the other side/the opposite side/a distance) (d:<a> and <galkhat> written as one word: the side across from a place, or a place some way off, as in {agalkhat panin}, from across the way) (j:a/galkhat) (r:zd:12345/zd:17664) (q:draft)
agalte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:enemies/his enemies/their enemies) (d:<a> and <galte> written as one word: his, her or their enemies) (j:a/galte) (r:zd:17672/zd:16488) (q:draft)
agam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:his country/their country/its country) (d:<a>, his, her, its, and <gam>, country, written as one word: the country of the one spoken of; {agam uh} is their country) (j:a/gam) (r:zd:22159/zd:19733/zd:20181) (q:draft)
agamah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:travel/politics) (w:to his country/to her country/home) (d:<a>, his or her, and <gamah> written as one word: to his or her own country, as in {agamah aciah}, return home, and {agamah kipuakkik}, be sent back, deported) (j:a/gamah) (r:zd:18007/zd:21968) (q:draft)
agamla = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:travel/everyday) (w:far/distant/far away) (d:<a> and <gamla> written as one word: far, the far one, a far place; {agamla pan} is from afar) (j:a/gamla) (r:zd:17499/zd:25630/zd:21426) (q:draft)
agamlakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:distance/distance away) (d:<a> with <gamlatna>, distance, written as one word and with k: after a measure and before <ah>, at that distance away from a place) (j:a/gamlatna) (r:zd:19054/zd:20219) (q:draft)
agamlalo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:travel/everyday) (w:not far/near) (d:<agamla> and <lo> written as one word: not far; after a place with <panin>, not far from that place) (j:agamla/lo) (r:zd:13224/zd:16107) (q:draft)
agamlapi = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/travel) (w:far away/afar/long-distance) (d:<a> and <gamlapi> written as one word: a far place, far away; {agamlapi panin} is from far away, and before a noun it is long-distance) (j:a/gamlapi) (r:zd:11405/zd:17707/zd:12338) (q:draft)
agamlatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:distance/at a distance of) (d:<a> and <gamlatna>, distance, written as one word, after a measure and mostly before <ah>: at that distance, that far away) (j:a/gamlatna) (r:zd:16515/zd:12214/zd:15405) (q:draft)
agammi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:its citizens/their citizens) (d:<a> and <gammi> written as one word: the citizens of that country, its own people) (j:a/gammi) (r:zd:16225/zd:18009) (q:draft)
agampan = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:politics/travel) (w:from his country/from its country/out of the country) (d:<a>, <gam> and <pan> written as one word: out of his, her or its own country, mostly of someone expelled or fleeing) (j:a/gam/pan) (r:zd:11598/zd:12005) (q:draft)
agamsung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/travel) (w:its country/their country/own territory) (d:<a>, his, its or their, and <gamsung>, inside the country, written as one word: the inside of the country of the one just named; {agamsung ah} is in its own country) (j:a/gamsung) (r:zd:11931/zd:12210) (q:draft)
agamta = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:act/behave) (d:<a> and <gamta> written as one word: he acts or behaves, or the one who acts so, as {hihbang in agamta te}, those who act in this way) (j:a/gamta) (r:zd:25016/zd:15056) (q:draft)
agamtang = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:moving/active) (d:<a> and <gamtang>, move, written as one word: one that moves; of a group, one that is active or operates in a place) (j:a/gamtang) (r:zd:20215/zd:14836/zd:21981) (q:draft)
agamtapa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:perpetrator/culprit) (d:<a> and <gamtapa> written as one word: the man who did it, the one who committed the act spoken of) (j:a/gamtapa) (r:zd:17568) (q:draft)
agamtat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:act/behave) (d:<a> and <gamtat> written as one word: his or their acting, what he did; {hihbang in agamtat pen} is that he acted in this way) (j:a/gamtat) (r:zd:12696/zd:15554/zd:16026) (q:draft)
agamtatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:his conduct/his behaviour/his action) (d:<a> and <gamtatna> written as one word: his, her or their conduct, the way someone acted) (j:a/gamtatna) (r:zd:12987/zd:21667/zd:15498) (q:draft)
agamtatzia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:his conduct/her behaviour/their way of acting) (d:<a> and <gamtatzia> written as one word: his, her or their conduct, the way someone acted) (j:a/gamtatzia) (r:zd:20622/zd:20984) (q:draft)
agawl = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:his neck/his throat) (d:<a> and <gawl> written as one word: his, her or its neck or throat) (j:a/gawl) (r:zd:25068/zd:18110) (q:draft)
agawlgui = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:his throat/her throat) (d:<a> and <gawlgui> written as one word: his or her throat) (j:a/gawlgui) (r:zd:12053/zd:12498) (q:draft)
agawlpan = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:body) (w:by the neck/by the throat) (d:<agawl>, his or her neck, and <pan>, from, written as one word: by the neck, at the throat, of seizing or strangling) (j:agawl/pan) (r:zd:15606) (q:draft)
agawm = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/work) (w:in total/altogether/combined) (d:<a> and <gawm>, add together, written as one word: added together, placed before the sum; {avekpi agawm} is all in all) (j:a/gawm) (r:zd:16862/zd:22435) (q:draft)
agawtbawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:mistreat/treat harshly/abuse) (d:<a> and <gawtbawl> written as one word: he mistreats, or the one who mistreats) (j:a/gawtbawl) (r:zd:12255) (q:draft)
ageel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:plan/devise) (d:<a> and <geel> written as one word: he plans, they planned, the one who plans) (j:a/geel) (r:zd:13076/zd:15007/zd:14805) (q:draft)
ageelna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/work) (w:his plan/the plan) (d:<a> and <geelna> written as one word: his, her or their plan, what was planned) (j:a/geelna) (r:zd:8667/zd:20012/zd:11427) (q:draft)
ageelsa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:planned/have planned) (d:<a> and <geelsa>, planned, written as one word: he or they had planned, or what has been planned) (j:a/geelsa) (r:zd:14883/zd:12623) (q:draft)
agei = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:beside/nearby/its side) (d:<a> and <gei> written as one word: the side of it or of him; {agei ah} is beside it, nearby, and {agei aom mite} are the people nearby) (j:a/gei) (r:zd:16026/zd:11217/zd:10874) (q:draft)
ageina = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:normal/usual) (d:the usual state of things, what is normal: {ageina hileh} is normally, {ageina sangin} than normal, {ageina mahbang in} as usual; probably a spelling of {a ngeina}, with <ngeina>, custom) (r:zd:12732/zd:15830/zd:16702) (q:draft, low confidence)
ageinai = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/travel) (w:nearby/near it/close by) (d:<a> and <geinai> written as one word: the place close to the person or thing spoken of; {ageinai aom} is that is nearby, and {ageinai panin} is from close by) (j:a/geinai) (r:zd:11738/zd:15266/zd:13173) (q:draft)
ageipan = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:from beside/from nearby) (d:<a>, <gei>, side, and <pan>, from, written as one word: from beside it, from close by, said of people who stand near and watch or act) (j:a/gei/pan) (r:zd:13024/zd:19141) (q:draft)
agel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (j:ageel) (r:zd:26097/zd:18050) (q:draft)
agelh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/media) (w:write/written by) (d:<a> and <gelh> written as one word: the one who wrote; placed before a name it means written by) (j:a/gelh) (r:zd:25462/zd:16820) (q:draft)
agelhkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/education) (w:write out/post/publish) (d:<a>, <gelh> and <khia> written as one word: he writes out or makes public in writing; also the one who wrote it) (j:a/gelh/khia) (r:zd:20181/zd:14581) (q:draft)
agelhkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/education) (w:wrote/posted/wrote out) (d:<a> and <gelhkhiat> written as one word: he or she wrote it out, or what someone wrote, said of posts on social media) (j:a/gelhkhiat) (r:zd:16865/zd:12571) (q:draft)
agelhkhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/it) (w:post/written statement) (d:<a>, <gelhkhiat> and the noun suffix <na> written as one word: what he or she wrote, a post or written statement; {Facebook tungah agelhkhiatna ah} is in what he wrote on Facebook) (j:a/gelhkhiat/na) (r:zd:20188/zd:17763) (q:draft)
agelhna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/education) (w:what he wrote/writing) (d:<a> and <gelhna>, writing, written as one word: what he or she wrote; {agelhna ah} introduces the words that someone wrote) (j:a/gelhna) (r:zd:12967/zd:12676) (q:draft)
agen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:say/tell) (d:<a> and <gen> written as one word: he or she says, what he or she says) (j:a/gen) (r:zd:19629/zd:23479/zd:24574) (q:draft)
agenbehna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media) (w:further statement/what he added) (d:<a>, his, <genbeh>, say in addition, and the noun suffix <na> written as one word; <agenbehna ah> introduces what a speaker went on to say) (j:a/genbeh/na) (r:zd:21409/zd:16093) (q:draft)
agenbehna ah = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:media) (w:added that/went on to say/further said) (d:<agenbehna>, what he added, and <ah>, in: a formula of news reports, placed after the speaker with <in> and before the reported statement, the speaker said further) (r:zd:21409/zd:19348/zd:16093) (q:draft)
agenda = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/work) (w:agenda/programme) (d:the list of matters to be dealt with at a meeting, or the plan of what someone intends to do) (o:English) (r:zd:19342/zd:23156/zd:12581) (q:draft)
agengen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:keep saying/go on talking about) (d:<a> and <gengen>, say again and again, written as one word: keep on saying; {athu in agengen} is merely to talk about a thing, as against doing it) (j:a/gengen) (r:zd:15116/zd:12564/zd:22550) (q:draft)
agenkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/everyday) (w:state/announce/declare) (d:<a> and <genkhia> written as one word: he stated, the one who stated or announced it) (j:a/genkhia) (r:zd:13236/zd:19635) (q:draft)
agenkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/everyday) (w:state/say/declare) (d:<a> and <genkhiat> written as one word: that he or she stated, what he or she said publicly) (j:a/genkhiat) (r:zd:12785/zd:11380) (q:draft)
agenkhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media) (w:statement/what was said) (d:<a> and <genkhiatna> written as one word: his or her statement; {agenkhiatna ah} after the name of a speaker and <in> introduces reported speech, in what that person stated) (j:a/genkhiatna) (r:zd:17834/zd:15756) (q:draft)
agenkhiatsa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/everyday) (w:have stated/have announced) (d:<agen>, he says, and <khiatsa>, out and already done, written as one word: what he or she has already stated or announced) (j:agen/khiatsa) (r:zd:20595/zd:15558) (q:draft)
agenkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:have said/finish telling) (d:<a> and <genkhit>, finish saying, written as one word; mostly {agenkhit ciangin}, after he or she had said it) (j:a/genkhit) (r:zd:17779/zd:15937) (q:draft)
agenna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/everyday) (w:what he said/his statement) (d:<a> and <genna> written as one word: what he or she said; in news reports {agenna ah} introduces the words of the person quoted) (j:a/genna) (r:zd:21461/zd:15759/zd:19530) (q:draft)
agennop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:want to say/mean) (d:<a> and <gennop> written as one word: what he or she wants to say, what is meant) (j:a/gennop) (r:zd:21739/zd:12487) (q:draft)
agennuam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:want to say/mean) (d:<a> and <gennuam> written as one word: the one who wants to say, what is meant) (j:a/gennuam) (r:zd:19523/zd:11416) (q:draft)
agensa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:said/what was said) (d:<a> and <gensa> written as one word: what he or she has said, the thing already said; {agensa mahbangin} is just as was said) (j:a/gensa) (r:zd:12756/zd:15000) (q:draft)
agensiapa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/media) (w:slanderer/one who insulted) (d:<a> and <gensiapa> written as one word: the man who spoke ill of someone) (j:a/gensiapa) (r:zd:11746/zd:11850) (q:draft)
agent = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/travel) (w:agent/broker) (d:a person who arranges work, travel or documents for others for payment; also an officer of a secret or police service, as in FBI Agent) (o:English) (r:zd:19051/zd:15814) (q:draft)
agente = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:speakers/those who say) (d:<a> and <gente> written as one word: the ones who say or tell something, set against {aza te}, the ones who hear) (j:a/gente) (r:zd:19676/zd:23112) (q:draft)
Agentte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/travel) (w:agents/recruitment agents) (d:English agent with the plural <te>: the agents or brokers who arrange work and travel abroad) (o:English) (r:zd:16760/zd:15109) (q:draft)
agiak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:home/travel) (w:stay overnight/lodge/board) (d:<a> and <giak> written as one word: he or they spend the night, or the ones who lodge or board in a place) (j:a/giak) (r:zd:15461/zd:16038) (q:draft)
agihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/body) (w:its weight/his weight) (d:<a> and <gihna> written as one word: his, her or its weight) (j:a/gihna) (r:zd:17899/zd:11582/zd:10759) (q:draft)
