akangtum = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/home) (w:burn down/be burnt up) (d:<a> and <kangtum> written as one word: burned down, the one that was destroyed by fire) (j:a/kangtum) (r:zd:16621/zd:11383/zd:15410) (q:draft)
akankan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:investigate/look into/study) (d:<a> and <kankan> written as one word: he or they keep searching into a matter) (j:a/kankan) (r:zd:15180/zd:23329) (q:draft)
akankhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:investigate/who investigates) (d:<a> and <kankhia>, search out, written as one word: he investigates, or the one who investigates a case or a crime) (j:a/kankhia) (r:zd:19801/zd:20526/zd:16720) (q:draft)
akankhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:investigate/find out/look into) (d:<a> and <kankhiat> written as one word: he or they investigate, what was found out; {akankhiat uhciangin} is when they looked into it) (j:a/kankhiat) (r:zd:14726/zd:14720) (q:draft)
akankhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:investigation/inquiry) (d:<a> and <kankhiatna> written as one word: his or their investigation; {akankhiatna ah} is according to their investigation) (j:a/kankhiatna) (r:zd:16143/zd:20099) (q:draft)
akankhiatsan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:be investigating/be looking into) (d:<akankhiat>, investigate, with an ending that shows the action is going on, mostly before <laitak>: {akankhiatsan laitak} is they are investigating it at present) (b:akankhiat) (r:zd:21581/zd:15178) (q:draft)
akansan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:investigate/be investigating) (d:<a> with <kansan>, look closely into a matter, written as one word: they investigate it; said of police and authorities, often followed by <laitak>, be in the course of) (j:a/kansan) (r:zd:20282/zd:15461) (q:draft)
akansawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:try to investigate/intend to look into) (d:<a>, <kan>, look into, and <sawm>, intend, written as one word: the ones who set out to investigate a matter) (j:a/kan/sawm) (r:zd:19801) (q:draft, low confidence)
akantan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:cross/pass through) (d:<a> with <kantan>, cross, written as one word: he or she crosses, or the one who crosses a road, a river or a stage) (j:a/kantan) (r:zd:14638/zd:15836/zd:17213) (q:draft)
akap = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:weep/the one who weeps) (d:<a> and <kap>, weep, written as one word: the one who weeps; {adah akap khempeuh} is all who grieve and weep, the bereaved, in words of condolence) (j:a/kap) (r:zd:20263/zd:23471) (q:draft)
akapgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:shoot/open fire on/gun down) (d:<a> and <kapgawp> written as one word: he or they shot at people, firing many shots; also the one who shot) (j:a/kapgawp) (r:zd:12803/zd:15554) (q:draft)
akapgawp = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/family) (w:cry hard/wail) (d:<a> with <kap>, weep, and <gawp> written as one word: he or she cried very hard) (j:a/kap/gawp) (r:zd:19565) (q:draft, low confidence)
akapkap = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:crying/weeping on and on) (d:<a> and <kapkap> written as one word: one who keeps crying, or the sound of crying on and on) (j:a/kapkap) (r:zd:15221/zd:13048) (q:draft)
akapkap = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:shooting repeatedly/spraying) (d:<a> with <kap>, shoot, said twice and written as one word: keep shooting, or keep spraying water or foam at something) (j:a/kap) (r:zd:14736/zd:10945) (q:draft)
akapkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/politics) (w:after shooting/having shot) (d:<a>, <kap>, shoot, and <khit>, after, written as one word, used before <ciangin>: after he shot) (j:a/kap/khit) (r:zd:19348/zd:15840) (q:draft)
akaplum = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:shoot dead/kill by shooting) (d:<a> and <kaplum> written as one word: he or she shot someone dead, the one who shot dead) (j:a/kaplum) (r:zd:11389/zd:19353) (q:draft)
akaplumpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/media) (w:gunman/shooter/killer) (d:<a>, <kaplum> and <pa> written as one word: the man who shot someone dead) (j:a/kaplum/pa) (r:zd:17703/zd:12603) (q:draft)
akaplup = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:shoot dead/kill by shooting) (d:<a>, <kap> and <lup> written as one word: the form of {a kaplum}, he shot dead, used before a noun or an ending; also the one who was shot dead) (j:a/kap/lup) (r:zd:20310/zd:14768) (q:draft)
akaplupna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:fatal shooting/shooting dead) (d:<a> and <kaplupna> written as one word: his or her shooting someone dead, the act or the reason of it) (j:a/kaplupna) (r:zd:12603/zd:20310) (q:draft)
akapna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:shooting/firing) (d:<a> and <kapna> written as one word: the shooting or firing that someone did, and what was shot at; {vanleng tawh akapna} is an attack from aircraft) (j:a/kapna) (r:ts:3805/zd:16236) (q:draft)
akappa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:shooter/gunman) (d:<a> and <kappa> written as one word: the man who shot, the gunman) (j:a/kappa) (r:zd:15840/zd:19929) (q:draft)
akappen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:politics/everyday) (w:the one who shot/the shooter) (d:<a> with <kap>, shoot, and the topic marker <pen> written as one word: the one who fired, mostly after <thau>, gun) (j:a/kap/pen) (r:zd:11934/zd:16236) (q:draft)
akapte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:mourners/those who weep) (d:<a> and <kapte.1> written as one word: those who weep; {adah akapte} is those who grieve and weep for the dead) (j:a/kapte) (r:zd:19866/zd:13183) (q:draft)
akapte = (i:2) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:shooters/gunmen) (d:<a> and <kapte.2> written as one word: those who shot at someone) (j:a/kapte) (r:zd:17969/zd:17439) (q:draft)
akaptuk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:shoot/shoot and hit/shoot down) (d:<a> and <kaptuk>, shoot and hit, written as one word: he or they shot someone, or the one who shot) (j:a/kaptuk) (r:zd:12579/zd:16811) (q:draft)
akat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:burn/catch fire/be on fire) (d:<a> and <kat>, burn, written as one word, mostly after <mei>, fire: {mei akat ciangin} is when the fire broke out, when it caught fire) (j:a/kat) (r:zd:20369/zd:22597/zd:18166) (q:draft)
akatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/home) (w:the burning/the fire) (d:<a> and <katna> written as one word: the burning of something, the fire; {akatna ahang} is the cause of the fire) (j:a/katna) (r:zd:12502/zd:15851/zd:17551) (q:draft)
akattum = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:burn up/burn down/be burnt up) (d:<a> and <kattum> written as one word: fire burns a thing up completely, or the thing burns up) (j:a/kattum) (r:zd:17800/ts:3284) (q:draft)
akawi = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/social) (w:crooked/devious) (d:<a> and <kawi> written as one word: what is crooked; {akawi amam in} is in a twisting way, now crooked now straight, not straightforwardly) (j:a/kawi) (r:zd:25923/zd:22719) (q:draft)
akawk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:point out/point to/indicate) (d:<a> and <kawk>, point at, written as one word: he points out, what it points to) (j:a/kawk) (r:zd:20877/zd:24749) (q:draft)
akawng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:waist) (d:<a> and <kawng> written as one word: his or her waist; {akawng ah} is at or around the waist) (j:a/kawng) (r:zd:19644/zd:17913/zd:19428) (q:draft)
akeh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:home/everyday) (w:leak/leaking) (d:<a> and <keh> written as one word: it leaks; {Gas akeh} is a gas leak, gas that is leaking) (j:a/keh) (r:zd:15949/zd:16137) (q:draft)
akehkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/nature) (w:leak out/escape) (d:<a> with <keh> and <khia> written as one word: it leaks out, that which leaks out, said of gas, fuel or a chemical) (j:a/keh/khia) (r:zd:19447/zd:19383) (q:draft)
akem = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/family) (w:keep/look after/guard/one who looks after) (d:<a> and <kem> written as one word: he or she keeps or looks after, or the one who looks after a child, a person or a thing; {akem ding} is the one who is to look after) (j:a/kem) (r:zd:21259/zd:17409/zd:21102) (q:draft)
akemding = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:family/everyday) (w:one to look after/in order to look after) (d:<akem> and <ding> written as one word: the person who is to look after or guard someone, or in order to look after; {akemding omlo} is there is nobody to look after him) (j:akem/ding) (r:zd:11550/zd:14883) (q:draft)
akemkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:happen to keep/have in one's keeping/possess) (d:<akem>, he keeps or the one who keeps, with <kha>, happen to, written as one word: anyone who happens to have kept or to be holding a thing) (j:akem/kha) (r:zd:19550/zd:21583) (q:draft)
akemte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/social) (w:caretakers/carers/keepers) (d:<a> and <kemte> written as one word: those who look after a child, an animal or a place) (j:a/kemte) (r:zd:16389/zd:15562) (q:draft)
akep = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/everyday) (w:look after/keep/raise) (d:<a> and <kep> written as one word: he looks after, the one he keeps or brings up) (j:a/kep) (r:zd:16976/zd:20807/zd:14597) (q:draft)
akepsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/everyday) (w:entrust/leave in the care of/look after for) (d:<a> and <kepsak> written as one word: he or she gives a child into the care of someone, or the one who looks after it for another) (j:a/kepsak) (r:zd:21476/zd:20540) (q:draft)
akeu = (i:1) (t:v) (f:nature/everyday) (w:be dry/dried/withered) (d:<a> and <keu> written as one word: it is dry, or that which is dry; {akeu khit ciangin} is after it has dried) (j:a/keu) (r:zd:20775/zd:11695) (q:draft)
akha = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion/body) (w:spirit/soul) (d:<a> and <kha> written as one word: his or her spirit or soul; the same spelling also stands for the month, as in {ani akha}, the day and the month) (j:a/kha) (r:ts:3369/zd:12166) (q:draft)
akhading = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/family) (w:to drop off/to see off/to take there) (d:<a>, <kha>, here see off or take a person to a place, and <ding> written as one word: in order to take and leave someone there, as a child at school) (j:a/kha/ding) (r:zd:17782/zd:19562) (q:draft, low confidence)
akhaguh = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:his jaw/her jaw/jawbone) (d:<a> and <khaguh> written as one word: his or her jaw or jawbone) (j:a/khaguh) (r:zd:12304/zd:15888) (q:draft)
akhah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:released/issued) (d:<a> and <khah>, release, written as one word: that someone released or let out, of prisoners set free and of a statement issued) (j:a/khah) (r:zd:25203/zd:14686) (q:draft)
akhahkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/it) (w:release/post/publish) (d:<a> and <khahkhia> written as one word: the one who released it, or that was released; in news mostly of a video or report put out on the internet, also of a person set free) (j:a/khahkhia) (r:zd:18056/zd:11585/zd:19530) (q:draft)
akhahkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/everyday) (w:release/publish/post) (d:<a> and <khahkhiat> written as one word: released, let out; in news mostly of a video, a statement or figures made public, also of a person set free) (j:a/khahkhiat) (r:zd:14768/zd:23851/zd:22422) (q:draft)
akhahkhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media) (w:release/publication) (d:<a> and <khahkhiatna> written as one word: the releasing or what is released, said in news reports of a statement or video that someone puts out; with <ah>, in the statement or video that they released) (j:a/khahkhiatna) (r:zd:15782/zd:11790) (q:draft)
akhahna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/everyday) (w:release/posting) (d:<a> and <khahna> written as one word: his or their letting something out, as the setting free of a prisoner or the putting out of a video or a notice; with <ah>, in what he posted) (j:a/khahna) (r:zd:12477/zd:17903) (q:draft)
akhak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:shut/close/block) (d:<a> and <khak> written as one word: he shut it, it is shut off or blocked) (j:a/khak) (r:zd:25260/zd:25346) (q:draft)
akhak = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:send/remit) (d:<a> and <khak> in the sense send written as one word: he sent it, of a message, a video or money) (j:a/khak) (r:zd:14883/zd:25009) (q:draft, low confidence)
akhakcip = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:shut/block/ban) (d:<a> and <khakcip> written as one word: he shuts or blocks it, or what is closed off or banned) (j:a/khakcip) (r:zd:12070/ts:6108/zd:17504) (q:draft)
akhaktan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:block/stop/hinder) (d:<a> and <khaktan> written as one word: he blocked it, or the one that blocks) (j:a/khaktan) (r:zd:23793/zd:15577) (q:draft)
akham = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food) (w:be full/be drunk/have enough) (d:<a> and <kham> written as one word: have eaten one's fill, or with <zu> be drunk; {an akham un} is to their fill) (j:a/kham) (r:zd:22550/zd:25923/zd:11801) (q:draft)
akhamcip = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:strictly forbid/ban/prohibit) (d:<a> and <khamcip> written as one word: he or they forbid it firmly, or the thing that is banned, as in {akhamcip Chemical}, a banned chemical) (j:a/khamcip) (r:zd:15237/zd:12746) (q:draft)
akhamkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food/social) (w:having got drunk/after drinking one's fill) (d:<a> and <khamkhit> written as one word: when he has had his fill, in these reports of strong drink; {zu akhamkhit uhciangin} is after they had got drunk) (j:a/khamkhit) (r:zd:14585/zd:13297) (q:draft)
akhang = (i:2) (t:n) (f:family/time) (w:generation) (d:<khang>, generation, with the prefix <a> written joined; doubled as {akhang akhangin}, from generation to generation) (r:zd:20808/zd:22228) (q:draft)
akhang = (i:3) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:increase/grow/rise) (d:the verb <khang>, increase or grow, with the prefix <a> written joined: it increases, it grows up; {natna akhang pen} is where the disease is increasing most) (r:zd:24453/zd:14791) (q:draft)
akhangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time/family) (w:from generation to generation) (d:<a> and <khangin> written as one word, in the phrase {akhang akhangin}: generation after generation) (j:a/khangin) (r:zd:22815/zd:19166) (q:draft)
akhangkhang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time/social) (w:generation after generation/through the generations) (d:<a> with <khang>, here generation, said twice, written as one word and mostly followed by <in>: from one generation to the next) (j:a/khang) (r:zd:19856/ts:9859) (q:draft)
akhangkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/social) (w:grow up/be brought up) (d:<a> and <khangkhia> written as one word: he or she grew up, the one who grew up, in a place or a family) (j:a/khangkhia) (r:zd:16257/zd:20874/zd:12192) (q:draft)
akhanglam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/nature) (w:lower side/south) (d:<a> and <khanglam> written as one word: the side that lies lower down, as below a road on a slope, and the south) (j:a/khanglam) (r:zd:17689/zd:20456) (q:draft)
akhangmoi = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/family) (w:young/the young one) (d:<a> and <khangmoi> written as one word: who is young; {akhangmoi pen} is the youngest) (j:a/khangmoi) (r:zd:21426/zd:12244) (q:draft)
akhangno = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:family/time) (w:young/the young one) (d:<a> and <khangno> written as one word: young, the one who is young; {akhangno lai} is while still young and {akhangno penpen} is the very youngest) (j:a/khangno) (r:zd:24155/ts:3160) (q:draft)
akhangto = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:social/politics) (w:developed/advanced/progressing) (d:<a> and <khangto> written as one word: that has grown or progressed; {akhangto gamte} are the developed countries) (j:a/khangto) (r:zd:22446/zd:21340/zd:23554) (q:draft)
akhangtosa = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:social/politics) (w:developed/already developed) (d:<akhangto> and <sa>, here already done, written as one word: that has already developed; {akhangtosa gamte} are the developed countries) (j:akhangto/sa) (r:zd:12752/zd:19550) (q:draft)
akhantawn = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time/everyday) (w:for life/lifelong/permanently/all his life) (d:<a>, <khan> and <tawn> written as one word: through the whole of his or her life, and so for good; often followed by <in>) (j:a/khan/tawn) (r:zd:14776/zd:19894/zd:13028) (q:draft)
akhantoh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:progress/develop/advance) (d:<a> and <khantoh> written as one word: it progresses or develops; {akhantoh nadingin} is for the progress of) (j:a/khantoh) (r:zd:17335/zd:11076/zd:23201) (q:draft)
akhantohna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:progress/development/advancement) (d:<a> and <khantohna> written as one word: its progress, the development of a country or people; {akhantohna ding} is for its development) (j:a/khantohna) (r:zd:19124/zd:12769) (q:draft)
akhasiat = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/social) (w:pitiful/sad) (d:<a> and <khasiat>, pity, written as one word and followed by <huai>: {akhasiat huai} is what is pitiful, the sad thing) (j:a/khasiat) (r:zd:12033/zd:15385) (q:draft)
akhasum = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:his salary/her pay/their wages) (d:<a>, his or her, and <khasum>, monthly pay, written as one word) (j:a/khasum) (r:zd:16257/zd:10951) (q:draft)
akhat = (i:1) (t:num) (f:everyday) (w:one/the one/the first) (d:<a> and <khat> written as one word: one of them, the one; {akhat veina} is the first time, {akhat leuleu} the other one, and {sawm akhat} one tenth) (j:a/khat) (r:zd:25650/zd:25928/zd:25924) (q:draft)
akhatna = (i:1) (t:num) (f:everyday) (w:the first/first place/first prize) (d:<a> and <khatna> written as one word: the first one, and in a contest the first place; {akhatna ngah} is win first place) (j:a/khatna) (r:zd:14928/zd:11734/zd:21042) (q:draft)
akhatpa = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:the other one/one of them) (d:<a> and <khatpa> written as one word: one man of a pair or group, or the other man) (j:a/khatpa) (r:zd:15125/zd:11752) (q:draft)
akhatpen = (i:1) (t:num) (f:everyday) (w:the one/the other one/one of them) (d:<akhat>, the one, with the topic marker <pen>, written as one word: one of them, or the other of two, as what the sentence is about) (j:akhat/pen) (r:zd:12146/zd:11296) (q:draft)
akhatveina = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:the first time/first) (d:<a> and <khatveina> written as one word: the first time, for the first time) (j:a/khatveina) (r:zd:24370/zd:15759) (q:draft)
akhatzaw = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:the other/the other one) (d:<a> and <khatzaw> written as one word: the other one of two that are spoken of) (j:a/khatzaw) (r:zd:19936/zd:15994) (q:draft)
akhau = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/everyday) (w:rope/cord/string/cable) (d:<a> and <khau> written as one word: its rope, cord, string, fuse or cable) (j:a/khau) (r:zd:12319/zd:25562) (q:draft)
akhauh = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:strong/hard/strict/severe) (d:<a> and <khauh>, hard, written as one word: of a smell or a drink strong, of words harsh, of a religion or rule strict) (j:a/khauh) (r:zd:18142/zd:12634/zd:15358) (q:draft)
akhauhna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature/everyday) (w:strength/intensity/force) (d:<a> and <khauhna> written as one word: its strength, how strong a wind, an earthquake, a fire or a bomb is) (j:a/khauhna) (r:zd:16741/zd:16352) (q:draft)
akhauhpai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/social) (w:fierce/intense/tough/severe) (d:<a> and <khauhpai> written as one word: the one that is strong and forceful) (j:a/khauhpai) (r:zd:14901/zd:11166) (q:draft)
akhauhpenpen = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/media) (w:strongest/most severe/harshest) (d:<a>, <khauh>, strong, and <penpen>, the very most, written as one word: the strongest or most severe of all) (j:a/khauh/penpen) (r:zd:15089/zd:15054) (q:draft)
akhauhzaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:stronger/harder/more severe) (d:<a> and <khauhzaw> written as one word: the stronger or more severe one; after <sangin>, stronger than) (j:a/khauhzaw) (r:zd:24250/zd:17252) (q:draft)
akhawi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:home/nature) (w:keep/rear/raise) (d:<a> and <khawi> written as one word: he keeps or rears an animal, or the one that is kept) (j:a/khawi) (r:zd:11148/zd:15996/zd:15848) (q:draft)
akhawisa = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:home/nature) (w:that he keeps/reared/kept) (d:<a>, <khawi> and <sa> written as one word: that someone has kept and reared, said of a pet or of livestock) (j:a/khawi/sa) (r:zd:15848/zd:17446) (q:draft)
akhawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:stop/cease/retire) (d:<a> and <khawl> written as one word: it stops, comes to a halt, or he leaves off a work or service) (j:a/khawl) (r:zd:12733/zd:17616/zd:17070) (q:draft)
akhawlcip = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:stop completely/come to a standstill) (d:<a> and <khawlcip> written as one word: it stops and stays stopped, the one that has come to a halt) (j:a/khawlcip) (r:zd:15002/zd:16200) (q:draft)
akhawlding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/travel) (w:to stop/to step down/to retire) (d:<a> and <khawlding> written as one word: that he or it should stop; of a vehicle, to pull up; of an office or a job, to step down or retire) (j:a/khawlding) (r:zd:17138/zd:19602) (q:draft)
akhawlna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/work) (w:stopping place/where it stops/stopping) (d:<a> and <khawlna> written as one word: the place where a vehicle or ship stops or berths, or the stopping of a work or action) (j:a/khawlna) (r:zd:19536/zd:20369/zd:11932) (q:draft)
akhawlnading = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:travel/everyday) (w:stopping place/in order to stop) (d:<a>, <khawl>, stop, and <nading>, for, written as one word: before a noun, the place where a vehicle is to stop; with <in> or <un>, so that it stops, in order to make it stop) (j:a/khawl/nading) (r:zd:10768/zd:19837/zd:20104) (q:draft)
akhawlsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel/work) (w:stop/halt/dismiss) (d:<a> and <khawlsak> written as one word: he or they make stop, of a vehicle pulled over, of work halted, or of a person removed from a post) (j:a/khawlsak) (r:zd:17372/zd:18030/zd:19671) (q:draft)
akhe = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:his foot/his leg/her leg) (d:<a> and <khe> written as one word: his, her or its foot or leg) (j:a/khe) (r:zd:22658/zd:22589) (q:draft)
akhedap = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:his shoe/her shoes/the shoes) (d:<a> and <khedap>, shoe, written as one word: his or her shoes) (j:a/khedap) (r:zd:25433/zd:19231) (q:draft)
akhel = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:unusual/peculiar/odd) (d:<a> and <khel> written as one word before a noun or alone: out of the ordinary, different from what is usual, said of things and of behaviour) (j:a/khel) (r:zd:19530/zd:15996/zd:21102) (q:draft, low confidence)
akhen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:divide/separate/distinguish) (d:<a> and <khen> written as one word: he divides or tells apart, when divided; also the part that is divided off, a section) (j:a/khen) (r:zd:13186/zd:21463) (q:draft)
akhentat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:decide/resolve) (d:<a> and <khentat> written as one word: he, she or they decided; that which was decided) (j:a/khentat) (r:zd:12641/zd:19275/zd:20587) (q:draft)
akhetawh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:body/everyday) (w:with his foot/on foot) (d:<a>, <khe> and <tawh> written as one word: with his feet; said of running away on foot and of kicking or stamping on someone) (j:a/khe/tawh) (r:zd:21341/zd:15531/zd:19536) (q:draft)
akhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:drop/put out/pay out) (d:<a> and <khia> written as one word: he or they drop, put out or pay out something; the one who does so) (j:a/khia) (r:zd:22658/zd:23958) (q:draft, low confidence)
akhialhna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/religion) (w:his mistake/its fault/their wrong) (d:<a> and <khialhna> written as one word: his, her, its or their mistake, fault or wrongdoing) (j:a/khialhna) (r:zd:15946/zd:23492) (q:draft)
akhiasuk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:threw down/who dropped) (d:<a> and <khiasuk> written as one word: he threw or dropped something down from a height, or the one who did so) (j:a/khiasuk) (r:zd:13046/zd:17267) (q:draft)
akhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:drop/put in) (d:<a> and <khiat> written as one word: that he dropped or put down; said of a bomb dropped from a plane and, with <thong>, of sending a person to prison) (j:a/khiat) (r:zd:22658/zd:22550) (q:draft)
akhiatna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:dropping/bombing) (d:<khiat> in its meaning let fall, with the prefix <a> and the noun suffix <na>: the dropping of a bomb, after the word <bomb>; not the meaning of a word) (r:ts:5232/zd:26124) (q:draft, low confidence)
akhiatsuk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:dropped/threw down) (d:<a> and <khiatsuk> written as one word: he dropped or threw something down, as a bomb from the air) (j:a/khiatsuk) (r:zd:13046/zd:26124) (q:draft)
akhitui = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body/everyday) (w:his tears/her tears/their tears) (d:<a> and <khitui> written as one word: his, her or their tears) (j:a/khitui) (r:zd:25937/zd:19526/zd:17049) (q:draft)
akho = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/social) (w:firm/stable/secure/lasting) (d:<a> and <kho> written as one word: firm and lasting; mostly in the pair {akip akho}, stable and secure) (j:a/kho) (r:zd:20406/zd:23554) (q:draft)
akhoi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/family) (w:carer/nurse) (d:<a> and <khoi> written as one word: the one who cares for a sick person; often paired as {akem akhoi}, those who look after and nurse) (j:a/khoi) (r:zd:17409/zd:19733) (q:draft)
akhoih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:body/everyday) (w:touch/who touches) (d:<a> and <khoih> written as one word: he touches, or the one who touches) (j:a/khoih) (r:zd:15689/zd:16865) (q:draft)
akhu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature/health) (w:its smoke/fumes/vapour) (d:<a> and <khu>, smoke, written as one word: the smoke, fumes or vapour of a thing) (j:a/khu) (r:zd:22658/zd:13112) (q:draft)
akhu = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/home) (w:wear on the head) (d:<a> and <khu>, wear on the head, written as one word: he wears or the one wearing a hat or helmet) (j:a/khu) (r:zd:12994) (q:draft)
akhua = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/travel) (w:his village/home town) (d:<a>, his or their, and <khua>, village or town, written as one word: his own village, their home town; {akhua atui} is his native place) (j:a/khua) (r:zd:19357/zd:18107) (q:draft)
akhuak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body/health) (w:brain/mind) (d:<a>, his or her, with <khuak> in its sense of brain, written as one word: the brain; also the mind or intelligence, as in {akhuak hoih}, clever) (j:a/khuak) (r:zd:19289/zd:18183/zd:15236) (q:draft)
akhuakhua = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:social) (w:village by village/in each village) (d:<a> and <khua>, village, doubled, written as one word: each village, every village in turn) (j:a/khua) (r:zd:24038/zd:24731) (q:draft)
akhual = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:care for/have regard for/be concerned about) (d:<a> and <khual>, have regard for, written as one word: one who cares about a person or thing; {angsung bek akhual} is one who looks only to his own interest) (j:a/khual) (r:zd:24360/zd:15286/zd:16897) (q:draft)
akhualna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:concern for/regard for/sake) (d:<a> and <khualna>, concern, written as one word: his or her care for someone; {akhualna in} is out of concern for, for the sake of) (j:a/khualna) (r:zd:18952/zd:19396) (q:draft)
akhualzin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:travel/journey) (d:<a> and <khualzin> written as one word: he travels, his or their travelling; {akhualzin nading} is for his journey) (j:a/khualzin) (r:zd:16942/zd:13233) (q:draft)
akhualzinna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:his journey/their trip/travel) (d:<a> and <khualzinna> written as one word: his, her or their journey, the trip someone makes) (j:a/khualzinna) (r:zd:21406/zd:12364) (q:draft)
akhuam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/work) (w:its pillar/post/pole) (d:<a> and <khuam> written as one word: its post or pillar, the posts of a building) (j:a/khuam) (r:zd:16784/zd:14722) (q:draft)
akhuan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/work) (w:permission/leave/opportunity) (d:leave or a chance to do something, asked of or given by someone; {akhuan ngen} is ask permission and {akhuan pia} give permission or an opportunity) (s:khuan/phalna) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:24594/zd:18955) (q:draft)
akhuanung = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:later/afterwards/in the end) (d:at a later time, in the end; mostly as {akhuanung ah}) (r:zd:19695/zd:16490/zd:14559) (q:draft)
akhuapih = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:his fellow villager/person from the same village) (d:<a> and <khuapih> written as one word: someone from his or her own village or town) (j:a/khuapih) (r:zd:14931/zd:11508) (q:draft)
akhuasung = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:travel/social) (w:in his village/in her town) (d:<a> and <khuasung> written as one word: his, her or their village or town, in his village) (j:a/khuasung) (r:zd:16257/zd:14919) (q:draft)
akhuk = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:his knee/her knee) (d:<a>, his or her, and <khuk> written as one word: his or her knee) (j:a/khuk) (r:zd:11994/zd:26097) (q:draft)
akhum = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:food/everyday) (w:sweet/pleasant) (d:<a> and <khum>, sweet, written as one word: sweet, that which is sweet, of taste and also of words, songs and life; paired with <akha>, bitter) (j:a/khum) (r:zd:15396/zd:12166/zd:23974) (q:draft)
akhut = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:his hand/her hand) (d:<a> and <khut> written as one word: his, her or its hand or hands) (j:a/khut) (r:zd:15384/zd:12736) (q:draft)
akhut akhe = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:his hands and feet/his limbs/her limbs) (d:<akhut>, his hand, and <akhe>, his foot, set side by side without <leh>: his or her hands and feet, the limbs as a whole; {khut leh khe} with the possessive <a> on each word) (r:zd:14928/zd:21667) (q:draft)
akhutguak = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:body/everyday) (w:with bare hands/his bare hand) (d:<akhut>, his or her hand, and <guak>, bare, written as one word: the bare hand, without gloves, tools or safety gear; mostly with <tawh> or <in>) (j:akhut/guak) (r:zd:20000/zd:16323) (q:draft)
akhutma = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body/politics) (w:fingerprint/his fingerprint) (d:<a>, his or her, and <khutma>, the mark of the hand, written as one word: his or her fingerprint, often with the English word after it) (j:a/khutma) (r:zd:13241) (q:draft)
akhutma = (i:2) (t:n) (f:religion/work) (w:his handiwork/work of his hands) (d:<a>, his or her, and <khutma>, handiwork, written as one word: what someone has done or made) (j:a/khutma) (r:zd:25572) (q:draft, low confidence)
akhutme = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:his finger/her finger) (d:<a>, his or her, and <khutme> written as one word: his or her finger or fingers) (j:a/khutme) (r:zd:17558/zd:14624) (q:draft)
akhutpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:his thumb/her thumb) (d:<a> and <khutpi> written as one word: his or her thumb; one article seems to use it of the whole hand) (j:a/khutpi) (r:zd:22977) (q:draft, low confidence)
akhutsung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:his hand/her hand) (d:<a> and <khutsung> written as one word: his or her hand as what holds a thing; {akhutsung ah} is in his hand) (j:a/khutsung) (r:zd:15374/zd:12542) (q:draft)
akhuttawh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:body) (w:with his hand/by hand) (d:<a>, his or her, <khut>, hand, and <tawh>, with, written as one word: with his or her hand) (j:a/khut/tawh) (r:zd:13258/zd:16811) (q:draft)
akhutte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:his hands/her hands/their hands) (d:<a> and <khutte> written as one word: his, her or their hands) (b:akhut) (j:a/khutte) (r:zd:11172/zd:15264) (q:draft)
akhuttum = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:his fist/her fist) (d:<a> and <khuttum> written as one word: his or her fist) (j:a/khuttum) (r:zd:16020/zd:21723) (q:draft)
akhutzong = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:body) (w:his hand also/her hand too) (d:<akhut> and <zong> written as one word: his or her hand as well) (j:akhut/zong) (r:zd:20056/zd:21611) (q:draft)
aki = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<a> and the verb prefix <ki> written as one word and apart from the verb that follows: {aki phuankhia} is it was founded, {aki ci} the one that is called) (j:a/ki) (r:zd:14531/zd:17945/zd:21239) (q:draft)
akia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:fell/crashed/that fell) (d:<a> and <kia> written as one word: it fell, or the one that fell; said of an aircraft it is crashed, and {thong akia} is one who has been put in prison) (j:a/kia) (r:zd:12215/zd:11376) (q:draft)
akiading = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:to fall/to serve) (d:<a>, <kia> and <ding> written as one word: that will or should fall; with <thong>, to serve a prison term, and of a person thought to have fallen) (j:a/kia/ding) (r:zd:22056/zd:16961) (q:draft)
akiam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:decrease/be reduced) (d:<a> and <kiam> written as one word: it has decreased, what is less, the one that is reduced) (j:a/kiam) (r:zd:15274/zd:25068/zd:23988) (q:draft)
akiang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/travel) (w:nearby/beside it/near it) (d:<a> and <kiang> written as one word: the place beside him or it, its neighbourhood; {akim akiang} is the area all around) (j:a/kiang) (r:zd:24038/zd:14867) (q:draft)
akiasuk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:fall down/fallen) (d:<a> and <kiasuk> written as one word: he or it fell down, or the one that fell down) (j:a/kiasuk) (r:zd:15489/zd:17115) (q:draft)
akiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:fall/crash) (d:<a> and <kiat>, the form of <kia>, fall, written as one word: it fell, its falling; of an aircraft, crash; {akiat laitak} is the moment it fell) (j:a/kiat) (r:zd:11532/zd:16651) (q:draft)
akiatding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:will serve in prison/will fall) (d:<akiat>, he falls, and <ding>, will, written as one word: after <thong> and a length of time, the prison term he is to serve; elsewhere that it will fall) (j:akiat/ding) (r:zd:16717/zd:18139) (q:draft)
akiatkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:after falling/have fallen) (d:<a>, <kiat>, fall, and <khit>, finished, written as one word: after it fell or crashed, mostly before <ciangin> or <phetin>) (j:a/kiat/khit) (r:zd:17517/zd:12831) (q:draft)
akiatlam = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:that it fell/the falling) (d:<a>, <kiat>, fall, and <lam> written as one word: the fact that someone or something fell or dropped, as the thing known, noticed or reported) (j:a/kiat/lam) (r:zd:15715/zd:12831/zd:14799) (q:draft)
akiatleh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:if it falls/whether it falls) (d:<akiat> and <leh>, if, written as one word: if or whether it falls; {thong akiatleh akiatlohding} is whether he will go to prison or not) (j:akiat/leh) (r:zd:19725) (q:draft, low confidence)
akiatlohding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:will not fall/not to fall) (d:<akiat> and <lohding> written as one word: that it will not fall; after <akiatleh>, or not, as in {thong akiatleh akiatlohding}, whether he will go to prison or not) (j:akiat/lohding) (r:zd:19671) (q:draft, low confidence)
akiatma = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:before it fell/before the crash) (d:<akiat> and <ma> written as one word, mostly followed by <in>: before it or she fell, before an aircraft crashed) (j:akiat/ma) (r:zd:19480/zd:11376) (q:draft)
akiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/everyday) (w:fall/crash/place of falling) (d:<a> and <kiatna> written as one word: its falling, said of an aircraft that crashes or a bomb that lands; {akiatna mun} is the place where it fell) (j:a/kiatna) (r:zd:18091/zd:13084/zd:19182) (q:draft)
akiatsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:sentence/bring down) (d:<a> and <kiatsak> written as one word: he or they made it fall; {thong akiatsak} is the prison term that was passed) (j:a/kiatsak) (r:zd:13127) (q:draft, low confidence)
akiatsuk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:fall down/crash down) (d:<a>, <kiat> and <suk> written as one word: he, she or it falls down; {akiatsuk ciangin} is when it fell down) (j:a/kiat/suk) (r:zd:17713/zd:17079/zd:15372) (q:draft)
akiatsukna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/travel) (w:fall/place of the fall) (d:<a>, <kiat>, <suk> and <na> written as one word: his or its falling down, or, before a noun, where it fell down) (j:a/kiat/suk/na) (r:zd:17517/zd:11783) (q:draft)
akibang = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:same/alike/similar) (d:<a> and <kibang> written as one word: that is the same, that is like; <tawh akibang> is like, similar to) (j:a/kibang) (r:zd:17162/zd:22802/zd:15754) (q:draft)
akibangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:equally/alike/likewise) (d:<a> and <kibangin> written as one word: in the same way; after <tawh>, together with and in the same way as) (j:a/kibangin) (r:zd:15996/zd:25110/zd:11296) (q:draft)
akibanglo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:different/unlike/not the same) (d:<a>, <kibang> and <lo> written as one word: that which is not alike, different) (j:a/kibang/lo) (r:zd:14865/zd:24064/zd:25562) (q:draft)
akibangpian = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:resembling/similar-looking/something like) (d:<akibang>, that is like, and <pian>, likeness, written as one word: that looks like or is of the same kind as the thing named before it with <tawh>) (j:akibang/pian) (r:zd:16970/zd:18063) (q:draft)
akibat = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:alike/similar/the same) (d:<a> and <kibat>, be alike, written as one word; with <tawh> it means be like something, and with <loh> or <kei> not be the same) (j:a/kibat) (r:zd:14581/zd:24381/zd:24068) (q:draft)
akibawlbawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health/work) (w:keep being done/be under way) (d:<a> and <kibawlbawl> written as one word: something is being done again and again or is going on, as treatment, an inspection or repair work; with {laitak in}, while it was being done) (j:a/kibawlbawl) (r:zd:12359/zd:21244) (q:draft)
akibawlding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:be held/be done/be treated) (d:<a>, <kibawl> and <ding> written as one word: that will be held or done; of an injured person taken to hospital, to be treated) (j:a/kibawl/ding) (r:zd:12827/zd:17234/zd:13034) (q:draft)
akibawlkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/it) (w:be recorded/happen to be made) (d:<a>, <kibawl>, be made, and <kha>, happen to, written as one word: that happened to be made; in news reports of a video recording that a camera happened to make of an event) (j:a/kibawl/kha) (r:zd:19465/zd:13078/zd:16137) (q:draft)
akibawlkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:be manufactured/be produced/be made) (d:<akibawl> and <khia> written as one word: that is made or produced, said of goods from a company or a country) (j:akibawl/khia) (r:zd:13161/zd:20345) (q:draft)
akibawlkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:have been done/be finished/be completed) (d:<a>, <kibawl>, be done, and <khit>, finished, written as one word: when it has been done; {akibawlkhit ciangin} is after it was done and {akibawlkhit asawtlo} not long after it was done) (j:a/kibawl/khit) (r:zd:20535/zd:17239/zd:16045) (q:draft)
akibawlna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:where it is done/its being done) (d:<a> and <kibawlna> written as one word: the place, time or occasion at which something is made, done or held) (j:a/kibawlna) (r:zd:21551/zd:13355) (q:draft)
akibawlni = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time/everyday) (w:day it was held/day it was made) (d:<akibawl>, that is made or held, and <ni>, day, written as one word: the day on which a thing was done or held, as a report, an operation or an election) (j:akibawl/ni) (r:zd:11484/zd:20320) (q:draft)
akibawlpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/media) (w:what was made/what was held) (d:<akibawl>, that which is made or done, and the topic marker <pen> written as one word: the thing made, the event held or the act done, as the topic of the sentence) (j:akibawl/pen) (r:zd:16563/zd:13133) (q:draft)
akibawlsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/work) (w:ready-made/already made/prepared) (d:<a> and <kibawlsa>, already made, written as one word: that has been made, prepared or registered beforehand) (j:a/kibawlsa) (r:zd:23925/zd:22193/zd:19818) (q:draft)
akibawlsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be done for/be made for/be performed on) (d:<a> and <kibawlsak> written as one word: that which is made, done or carried out for or on someone, as an operation, a test or a document) (j:a/kibawlsak) (r:zd:19981/zd:13215) (q:draft)
akibawlsan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be under way/be being done) (d:<akibawl>, is made or done, with an added ending whose sense is not certain; before <laitak> it says that something is being carried out at this very time) (b:akibawl) (r:zd:20721/zd:20732) (q:draft, low confidence)
akibawlsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:be planned/be attempted/be about to be held) (d:<aki> and <bawlsawm> written as one word: that was planned or attempted, that people intended to hold or carry out) (j:aki/bawlsawm) (r:zd:15602/zd:20254) (q:draft)
akibawlsia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:be mistreated/be abused) (d:<a> and <kibawlsia> written as one word: who is mistreated or abused, the one harmed; with {nang leh nang}, harming yourself) (j:a/kibawlsia) (r:zd:22812/zd:22778) (q:draft)
akibawlsiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:be persecuted/be mistreated) (d:<a> and <kibawlsiat> written as one word: who is persecuted or abused, the fact of being mistreated) (j:a/kibawlsiat) (r:zd:14947) (q:draft)
akibawltawm = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/work) (w:man-made/artificial/fake) (d:<a> and <kibawltawm> written as one word: made by people, not natural; after <atuh> it says that goods are counterfeit) (j:a/kibawltawm) (r:zd:11438/zd:22805/zd:19307) (q:draft)
akibawlte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:those made/things done) (d:<akibawl> with the plural <te>, written as one word: the things that were made or done, the ones that were made) (j:akibawl/te) (r:zd:20367/zd:22457) (q:draft)
akibawltheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:can be made/can be done) (d:<akibawl> and <theih> written as one word: that it can be made or carried out; {akibawltheih nadingin} is so that it can be done) (j:akibawl/theih) (r:zd:14519/zd:15397) (q:draft)
akibawlzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:have been made/be carried out/be completed) (d:<a> and <kibawlzawh> written as one word: that has been made or done, after it was done; {akibawlzawh nading} is so that it can be done) (j:a/kibawlzawh) (r:zd:17017/zd:11076/zd:19493) (q:draft)
akibehlap = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:be added/increase) (d:<a> and <kibehlap> written as one word: it is added, or before a noun what has been added; {akibehlap toto} is keeps increasing) (j:a/kibehlap) (r:zd:16942/zd:11707/zd:24141) (q:draft)
akibuai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:be in turmoil/be in conflict/be in commotion) (d:<a> and <kibuai> written as one word: it is in trouble or uproar, or the one that is in turmoil; said of a place in conflict and of people in a commotion) (j:a/kibuai) (r:zd:25622/zd:15043) (q:draft)
akibuan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:be raped) (d:<a> and <kibuan> written as one word: was raped, the one who was raped) (j:a/kibuan) (r:zd:17510/zd:11193) (q:draft)
akibung = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:overturn/capsize/roll over) (d:<a>, <ki> and <bung> written as one word: a vehicle or boat that turned over, the one that overturned) (j:a/ki/bung) (r:zd:16334/zd:14888/zd:12906) (q:draft)
akibut = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:overturn/turn over/derail) (d:<a> with <kibut>, of a vehicle or a train: it turned over or left the track, the one that overturned) (j:a/kibut) (r:zd:16334/zd:13171) (q:draft, low confidence)
akicial = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:be hired/be employed) (d:<a> and <kicial> written as one word: he, she or they were hired for pay; the one who is hired) (j:a/kicial) (r:zd:11934/zd:20197/zd:12434) (q:draft)
akiciamteh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/everyday) (w:be recorded/be regarded as/be listed) (d:<a> and <kiciamteh> written as one word: that is recorded or regarded; after <in> it means recorded as, regarded as) (j:a/kiciamteh) (r:zd:12567/zd:16784/zd:15397) (q:draft)
akician = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:exact/definite/certain/detailed) (d:<a> and <kician>, firm and sure, written as one word: what is definite and reliable; {akician in} is exactly, in detail, said of knowing or telling a matter) (j:a/kician) (r:zd:22618/zd:23977/zd:20203) (q:draft)
akiciangtan = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:limited/fixed/set/restricted) (d:<a> and <kiciangtan> written as one word: that which is limited or fixed, as {akiciangtan hun}, the set time) (j:a/kiciangtan) (r:zd:23670/zd:12557) (q:draft)
akicianin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/media) (w:exactly/in detail/for certain) (d:<akician> and <in> written as one word: exactly, in detail, said of knowing, telling or examining a matter) (j:akician/in) (r:zd:11048/zd:15788) (q:draft)
akiciantak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:clearly/definitely/exactly) (d:<a> and <kiciantak> written as one word: clear and definite, in a definite way) (j:a/kiciantak) (r:ts:5132/zd:19373) (q:draft)
akicianzaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:media/everyday) (w:more exact/more detailed/clearer) (d:<a>, <kician> and <zaw> written as one word: the more exact or fuller one; {akicianzaw in} is in more detail) (j:a/kician/zaw) (r:zd:11532/zd:20492/zd:19222) (q:draft)
akicih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be called/be said) (d:<a> and <kicih> written as one word: what is called, that it is said, used before nouns and endings) (j:a/kicih) (r:zd:21369/zd:13348/zd:25173) (q:draft)
akicihna = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/media) (w:so-called/the place called) (d:<a> and <kicihna> written as one word, placed after a name: that which is called by this name, as {Lake Abaya akicihna}, the place called Lake Abaya) (j:a/kicihna) (r:zd:20076/zd:16225) (q:draft)
akiciliang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:that is even called/so-called) (d:<a> and <kiciliang> written as one word, placed after a name or description: that is even called so, that goes by that name) (j:a/kiciliang) (r:zd:15890/zd:18872) (q:draft)
akicim = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/nature) (w:collapse/that collapsed) (d:<a> and <kicim> written as one word: it collapsed, or the one that collapsed, said of buildings, roads and bridges) (j:a/kicim) (r:zd:17584/zd:20749) (q:draft)
akicimsuk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:collapse/fall in) (d:<a> and <kicimsuk> written as one word: it collapsed, or the one that collapsed, said of buildings, ceilings and ground) (j:a/kicimsuk) (r:zd:17256/zd:14969/zd:21244) (q:draft)
akicin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be complete/be fulfilled/be enough) (d:<a> and <kicin> written as one word: it is complete, fulfilled or sufficient; {akicin lohna} is where something is lacking) (j:a/kicin) (r:zd:15572/zd:20045/ts:10698) (q:draft)
akicing = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:complete/sufficient/full) (d:<a> and <kicing> written as one word: what is complete or enough; {akicing in} or {akicing takin} is in full, sufficiently) (j:a/kicing) (r:zd:23988/zd:14831/zd:24316) (q:draft)
akicingin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:fully/completely/in full) (d:<a> and <kicingin> written as one word: in full, with nothing lacking; {athu akicingin} is the whole of the matter, in full detail) (j:a/kicingin) (r:zd:18046/zd:17166) (q:draft)
akicingtak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:fully/sufficiently/in full) (d:<a> and <kicingtak> written as one word, mostly followed by <in>: in full, enough, as of time that is given) (j:a/kicingtak) (r:zd:16009/zd:20365) (q:draft)
akicingzaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/media) (w:more complete/fuller) (d:<a> and <kicingzaw> written as one word: the fuller one; {akicingzaw in} is more fully, in full) (j:a/kicingzaw) (r:zd:11405/zd:16325/zd:17877) (q:draft)
akicip = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:collapse/cave in) (d:<a> and <kicip> written as one word: it collapses, said of a building, a wall or the ground) (j:a/kicip) (r:zd:20749/ts:2349/zd:17777) (q:draft)
akicipa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/media) (w:the man called/man named) (d:<a> and <kicipa> written as one word: the man who is called by the name that stands before it) (j:a/kicipa) (r:zd:20000/zd:16924) (q:draft)
akicipen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:the one called/the so-called) (d:<akici>, that is called, and the topic marker <pen> written as one word, placed after a name: the one called by that name, as the topic of the sentence) (j:akici/pen) (r:zd:20023/zd:13332) (q:draft)
akicipna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:collapse/place of collapse) (d:<a> and <kicipna> written as one word: the collapsing of a building, a tower or the ground, or the place where it gave way) (j:a/kicipna) (r:zd:19303/zd:20456) (q:draft)
akicipsuk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/home) (w:collapse/fall in/cave in) (d:<akicip>, it collapses, with <suk>, down, written as one word: it collapses downward, said of a building, a tower or a ceiling) (j:akicip/suk) (r:zd:19303/zd:19002) (q:draft)
akicite = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/media) (w:those called/the so-called) (d:<a> and <kicite> written as one word and placed after a name: those who are called by that name, the so-called) (j:a/kicite) (r:zd:12425/zd:11558) (q:draft)
akidal = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be protected/be shielded) (d:<a> and <kidal> written as one word: it is shielded or protected, or shields itself, from something) (j:a/kidal) (r:zd:12589/zd:16450) (q:draft)
akidalna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/everyday) (w:barrier/divider/guardrail/fence) (d:<a> and <kidalna> written as one word: what screens or blocks off, in the news mostly the divider or guardrail of a road) (j:a/kidalna) (r:zd:17856/zd:14581) (q:draft)
akidawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/home) (w:laid across/stretched out/spanning) (d:<a> and <kidawh> written as one word: that is stretched or laid out, said of a bridge, flyover or pier built across something and of a cloth held out) (j:a/kidawh) (r:zd:20749/zd:15362) (q:draft)
akidawk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be seen/be exposed/stick out) (d:<a> and <kidawk> written as one word: that shows, that is exposed or sticks out) (j:a/kidawk) (r:zd:21013/zd:14997) (q:draft)
akidawt = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:be stabbed/was stabbed) (d:<a>, <ki> and <dawt> written as one word: he or she was stabbed) (j:a/ki/dawt) (r:zd:12823/zd:22267) (q:draft)
akidawtlum = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be stabbed to death) (d:<a>, <ki>, <dawt>, stab, and <lum>, to death, written as one word: was stabbed to death, the one stabbed to death; with {amah leh amah}, stabbed himself or herself to death) (j:a/ki/dawt/lum) (r:zd:17701/zd:16968) (q:draft)
akidawtna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/media) (w:stab wound/stabbing/being stabbed) (d:<akidawt>, was stabbed, with the ending {-na} written as one word: the place where a person was stabbed, the wound, or the stabbing itself) (j:akidawt/na) (r:zd:17609/zd:20282) (q:draft)
akideih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:be wanted/be needed/be popular) (d:<a> and <kideih> written as one word: it is wanted or required; of a person, wanted by the police, or much liked) (j:a/kideih) (r:zd:14740/zd:12623) (q:draft)
akidelhleh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (d:<a>, <kidelh> and <leh> written as one word: when they chased one another) (j:a/kidelh/leh) (r:zd:16922) (q:draft, low confidence)
akidem = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:compete/contest/run for) (d:<a> and <kidem> written as one word: competes, the one who competes, said of rivals in business, a contest or an election) (j:a/kidem) (r:zd:11844/zd:23597/zd:24354) (q:draft)
akidim = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:full of/filled with) (d:<a> and <kidim>, be filled, written as one word: that is full; after a noun with <tawh> it means full of or filled with that thing) (j:a/kidim) (r:zd:21426/zd:25433/zd:10992) (q:draft)
akido = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:fight/be at war) (d:<a> and <kido> written as one word: they fight each other, or the ones fighting; {gal akido} is they wage war) (j:a/kido) (r:zd:22597/zd:11862/ts:11323) (q:draft)
akidong = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:be asked/be questioned) (d:<a>, the verb prefix <ki> and <dong>, ask, written as one word: was asked, the one who was asked; of money, was asked for, collected) (j:a/ki/dong) (r:zd:21400/zd:19805) (q:draft)
akidop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be careful/take care/be on guard) (d:<a> and <kidop> written as one word: that someone is careful; {akidop nadingin} is so that they take care) (j:a/kidop) (r:ts:8105/zd:20008) (q:draft)
akidot = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:be asked/be questioned) (d:<a> and <kidot> written as one word, mostly as {akidot ciangin}: when he was asked) (j:a/kidot) (r:zd:12619/zd:11700) (q:draft)
akigam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:be far from/be distant) (d:<a> and <kigam> written as one word, the first part of <kigamla>: that is far from something, after <tawh>) (j:a/kigam) (r:zd:22550) (q:draft)
akigam = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (j:akigawm) (r:zd:15820) (q:draft, low confidence)
akigamla = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:be far from/be distant/be at a distance of) (d:<a> and <kigamla> written as one word: that is far from, lying at the distance named; {akigamla lo} is not far away) (j:a/kigamla) (r:zd:20322/zd:21426/zd:19262) (q:draft)
akigamlatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:at a distance of/the distance away) (d:<a> and <kigamlatna>, distance apart, written as one word: after a measure, that lies so far away, as in {tai 3 akigamlatna}, three miles away) (j:a/kigamlatna) (r:zd:19262/zd:23281) (q:draft)
akigawm = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:in total/altogether/combined) (d:<a> and <kigawm> written as one word: what is joined or added together; {akigawm in} is in total, altogether, and before a noun it means that has joined) (j:a/kigawm) (r:zd:20387/zd:11582/zd:15905) (q:draft)
akigawmkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:joined together/united/combined) (d:<a> and <kigawmkhawm> written as one word: that are joined into one, united) (j:a/kigawmkhawm) (r:zd:17630/zd:25097) (q:draft)
akigeel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/politics) (w:be planned/be intended) (d:<a> and <kigeel>, be planned, written as one word: that is planned, it is planned; {dingin akigeel} is it is planned to) (j:a/kigeel) (r:zd:17668/zd:14888) (q:draft)
akigelh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/media) (w:be written/be recorded) (d:<a> and <kigelh> written as one word: it is written, or that which is written) (j:a/kigelh) (r:zd:22557/zd:12707/zd:15554) (q:draft)
akigelhna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/media) (w:where it is written/what is written) (d:<a> and <kigelhna> written as one word: the place or text in which something is written, mostly as {akigelhna ah}, in what is written) (j:a/kigelhna) (r:zd:13320/zd:13278) (q:draft)
akigen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:be said/be spoken of/be told) (d:<a> and <kigen> written as one word: it is said, what is said or spoken of) (j:a/kigen) (r:zd:19602/zd:11714) (q:draft)
akigenna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media) (w:what is said/report/account) (d:<a> and <kigenna>, the telling, written as one word: what is said or reported about something; {athu akigenna ah} is according to what is reported) (j:a/kigenna) (r:zd:21793/zd:16910) (q:draft)
akigenna ah = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:media) (w:according to reports/as reported/it is said that) (d:<akigenna>, what is said, and <ah>, in: in what is told, according to the report; it opens a news sentence, mostly as {athu akigenna ah}, and the sentence often ends in <kici> or <cihi>) (r:zd:21793/zd:22828) (q:draft)
akigin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:prepare/get ready) (d:<a> and <kigin>, get ready, written as one word: he or they get ready) (j:a/kigin) (r:zd:19164/zd:13270) (q:draft)
akiging = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be ready/be prepared) (d:<a> and <kiging> written as one word: is ready, the one who is prepared) (j:a/kiging) (r:zd:24068/zd:19947) (q:draft)
akigingsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/social) (w:ready/prepared/on standby) (d:<a> and <kigingsa> written as one word, mostly followed by <in> and a form of <om>: in readiness, on the alert) (j:a/kigingsa) (r:zd:12420/zd:15811) (q:draft)
akigu = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:be stolen) (d:<a> and <kigu> written as one word: it was stolen, or beside a noun the one that was stolen) (j:a/kigu) (r:zd:19929/zd:17614) (q:draft)
akigual = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:line up/queue) (d:<a> and <kigual> written as one word: those who are lined up or standing in a queue) (j:a/kigual) (r:zd:19197/zd:20653/zd:12309) (q:draft)
akihal = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be burned/be set on fire/burn) (d:<a> and <kihal>, be burned, written as one word: it was burning, or that which was set on fire; of a fire also one that was lit on purpose) (j:a/kihal) (r:zd:16772/zd:15288/zd:18145) (q:draft)
akihalsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be set on fire/be burned on purpose) (d:<a> and <kihalsak> written as one word: it was set on fire by someone, said of a fire that was started deliberately) (j:a/kihalsak) (r:zd:15461/zd:20717) (q:draft)
akihawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:be distributed/be allotted/be shared out) (d:<a> and <kihawm> written as one word: that is divided or given out) (j:a/kihawm) (r:zd:20263/zd:24325/zd:24489) (q:draft)
akihawmkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media) (w:released/published/distributed) (d:<a> and <kihawmkhia> written as one word: that was released or published, of a film or of news) (j:a/kihawmkhia) (r:zd:14890) (q:draft)
akihel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be included/take part/be involved) (d:<a> and <kihel> written as one word: who takes part, that is included or involved, said of people in an event and of things in a whole) (j:a/kihel) (r:zd:11064/zd:21168/zd:11504) (q:draft)
akihelding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:will take part/be involved/be included) (d:<a>, <kihel>, take part, and <ding>, will, written as one word: who or what will take part or be included; {akihelding in aki ummawh} is suspected of being involved) (j:a/kihel/ding) (r:zd:20446/zd:14795/zd:14740) (q:draft)
akihelkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be involved/be included/be among) (d:<a>, <kihel> and <kha> written as one word: that happens to be involved or included in something) (j:a/kihel/kha) (r:zd:19082/zd:16598/zd:19127) (q:draft)
akihello = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not be included/be without) (d:<a> and <kihello> written as one word: the one that is not included, that which has nothing mixed in) (j:a/kihello) (r:ts:4909/zd:11941) (q:draft)
akihelna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:participation/involvement) (d:<a> and <kihelna> written as one word: his or their taking part, or that in which someone is involved) (j:a/kihelna) (r:ts:12037/zd:17760) (q:draft)
akihelte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:participants/members/those included) (d:<akihel> with the plural <te> written as one word: those who take part or are included) (j:akihel/te) (r:ts:11162/zd:17635) (q:draft)
akihemkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/social) (w:be evacuated/be moved out/be removed) (d:<a> and <kihemkhia> written as one word: who moved or were moved away from a place of danger, also of animals taken away) (j:a/kihemkhia) (r:zd:14712/zd:14871) (q:draft)
akihhuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/social) (w:disgusting/loathsome/detestable) (d:<a> and <kihhuai> written as one word: disgusting, that which is loathsome) (j:a/kihhuai) (r:zd:16949/zd:24014) (q:draft)
akihilh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education) (w:be taught/what is taught) (d:<a> and <kihilh> written as one word: it is taught, or that which is taught) (j:a/kihilh) (r:zd:15361/zd:12121) (q:draft)
akiho = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:talk together/converse) (d:<a> and <kiho> written as one word: who talk with one another, when they talk together) (j:a/kiho) (r:zd:12196/zd:15396) (q:draft)
akihon = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be opened/open/reopen) (d:<a> and <kihon> written as one word: it is opened, that which is opened, said of doors, schools, shops and businesses; {akihon kik} is reopen) (j:a/kihon) (r:zd:24651/zd:19495/zd:23641) (q:draft)
akihona = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:conversation/talks) (d:<a> and <kihona> written as one word: his or their conversation, the talks they hold) (j:a/kihona) (r:zd:11373/ts:1428) (q:draft)
akihong = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be opened/open) (d:<a> and <kihong>, be opened, written as one word: it is opened, or before a noun the one that is open, said of schools, shops and railway lines) (j:a/kihong) (r:zd:24140/zd:25068/zd:14555) (q:draft)
akihongding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:will be opened/which will open) (d:<akihong>, it is opened, with <ding>, will, written as one word: that which is going to be opened, as a shop or a building) (j:akihong/ding) (r:zd:19648) (q:draft)
akihtak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:fear/be afraid/dread) (d:<a> and <kihtak>, fear, written as one word: the one who is afraid, or what he fears; paired with <alau>) (j:a/kihtak) (r:zd:25203/zd:17395) (q:draft)
akihuh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:be helped/help one another) (d:<a> and <kihuh> written as one word: who is helped, or who help one another) (j:a/kihuh) (r:ts:10400/zd:15305) (q:draft)
akiim = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/travel) (w:surroundings/around it) (d:<a> and <kiim> written as one word: the area around it; {akiim apam} is all around, the whole neighbourhood) (j:a/kiim) (r:zd:12772/zd:15581) (q:draft)
akik = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time/everyday) (w:the next time/next time/later) (d:<a> and <kik>, again, written as one word: the next one, the time after this; {akik ciangin} and {akik ah} are next time, afterwards) (j:a/kik) (r:zd:16243/zd:11135) (q:draft)
akikaikhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:gathered/collected/assembled) (d:<a> and <kikaikhawm> written as one word: that has been collected, or that have gathered in one place) (j:a/kikaikhawm) (r:zd:14941/zd:14957) (q:draft)
akikal = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:middle/space between/meantime) (d:<a> and <kikal> written as one word: what lies between two places, parties or times; {akikal ah} is in between or in the meantime, {akikal panin} is from the middle, as a go-between) (j:a/kikal) (r:zd:15558/zd:20263) (q:draft)
akikan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/politics) (w:be investigated/be looked into) (d:<a> and <kikan> written as one word: when it was investigated or inquired into; {akikan ciangin} is on investigation) (j:a/kikan) (r:zd:10992/zd:15609) (q:draft)
akikanna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/media) (w:investigation/inquiry) (d:<a> and <kikanna> written as one word: the looking into a matter; {athu akikanna ah} is on investigation of the matter) (j:a/kikanna) (r:zd:20743/zd:19033) (q:draft)
akikap = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:be shot/shoot at each other) (d:<a> and <kikap> written as one word: was shot, there was shooting, they fired at each other) (j:a/kikap) (r:zd:19468/zd:25630) (q:draft)
akikapkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/health) (w:be shot/be hit by gunfire) (d:<a>, <kikap> and <kha> written as one word: who was hit by a shot, the one who was shot) (j:a/kikap/kha) (r:zd:15833/zd:11932) (q:draft)
akikaplum = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:was shot dead/the one shot dead) (d:<a> and <kikaplum> written as one word: was shot dead, or before a noun the one who was shot dead) (j:a/kikaplum) (r:zd:15684/zd:12854) (q:draft)
akikapna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/media) (w:shooting/exchange of fire/gunfight) (d:<a> and <kikapna> written as one word: the shooting, either the fighting of two sides with guns or the shooting of one person; {akikapna liamma} is a gunshot wound) (j:a/kikapna) (r:zd:17868/zd:19025) (q:draft)
akikapzia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/media) (w:how he was shot/manner of the shooting) (d:<akikap>, was shot, with <zia>, way or manner: the way in which someone was shot, the circumstances of a shooting) (j:akikap/zia) (r:zd:11878) (q:draft, low confidence)
akikem = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:be kept/be looked after/be held) (d:<a> and <kikem> written as one word: is kept or cared for, the one who is kept, as a patient in hospital or a prisoner in detention; also he keeps himself or guards his mouth) (j:a/kikem) (r:zd:17547/zd:12557/zd:23045) (q:draft)
akikep = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:be kept/be held/be looked after) (d:<a> and <kikep> written as one word: being kept, held or cared for, as a patient in hospital or a person in custody; {akikep laitak} is is now being kept) (j:a/kikep) (r:zd:19860/zd:14543) (q:draft)
akikepna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:place where one is kept/place of custody) (d:<a> and <kikepna> written as one word, here the noun of <kikem>, be kept: where someone is kept, held or cared for, placed before the name of the place, as a prison, a zoo, a hospital or a school) (j:a/kikepna) (r:zd:17794/zd:16389/zd:13059) (q:draft)
akikhahkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/politics) (w:released/that was released) (d:<a> and <kikhahkhia> written as one word: that was released, said of prisoners set free and of photos or video made public) (j:a/kikhahkhia) (r:zd:17551/ts:9739) (q:draft)
akikhai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:hang/be hung/be hanged) (d:<a> and <kikhai> written as one word: that hangs or is hung up, hanging) (j:a/kikhai) (r:zd:15756/zd:17755) (q:draft)
akikhai = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:differ/be far apart) (d:<a> and <kikhai> written as one word, here in the sense be apart: differ from one another) (j:a/kikhai) (r:zd:22639) (q:draft, low confidence)
akikhailum = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:hang oneself/be hanged) (d:<a> and <kikhailum> written as one word: he or she hanged himself or herself, or the one who is put to death by hanging) (j:a/kikhailum) (r:zd:23830) (q:draft)
akikhak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be closed/be shut) (d:<a> and <kikhak> written as one word: it is closed, the one that is shut, said of doors, schools, offices and businesses) (j:a/kikhak) (r:zd:22981/zd:19299/zd:25322) (q:draft)
akikham = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:be forbidden/be prohibited) (d:<a> and <kikham> written as one word: it is forbidden, that which is forbidden) (j:a/kikham) (r:zd:13346/zd:12389/ts:3227) (q:draft)
akikhamcip = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:be strictly forbidden/be banned) (d:<aki> and <khamcip> written as one word: it is strictly forbidden, that which is banned) (j:aki/khamcip) (r:zd:17301/zd:11654) (q:draft)
akikhan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/politics) (w:be increased/be raised/be stepped up) (d:<a> and <kikhan>, be enlarged, written as one word: it is increased, said of pay and of security measures; {amah tawh akikhan} is one who grew up with him) (j:a/kikhan) (r:zd:18079/zd:25916) (q:draft, low confidence)
akikhawi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:nature/work) (w:be kept/be reared/that is reared) (d:<a> and <kikhawi> written as one word: that is kept or reared, said of animals on a farm or in a zoo) (j:a/kikhawi) (r:zd:14664/zd:20150) (q:draft)
akikhawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:get along with/associate with) (d:<a> and <kikhawl> written as one word: who keeps company with others; {mite tawh akikhawl thei} is one who can get along with people) (j:a/kikhawl) (r:zd:23717/zd:17295) (q:draft)
akikhawl = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:be stopped/stand still) (d:<a>, <ki> and <khawl>, here stop or rest, written as one word: that has stopped or stands still; {tui akikhawl} is water left standing and {nasep akikhawl sak} is one whose work has been stopped) (r:zd:22658/zd:24067) (q:draft)
akikhawlsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:be stopped/be suspended/be laid off) (d:<a> and <kikhawlsak> written as one word: that was stopped or suspended, the one who was made to stop work) (j:a/kikhawlsak) (r:zd:24492/zd:11010) (q:draft)
akikhawm = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion/social) (w:those gathered/worshippers/congregation) (d:<a> and <kikhawm> written as one word: those who gather, the people who attend a meeting or worship) (j:a/kikhawm) (r:zd:16068/zd:21042) (q:draft)
akikhek = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be exchanged/be swapped) (d:<a> and <kikhek> written as one word: it is exchanged, what is exchanged for another thing) (j:a/kikhek) (r:zd:12005/zd:22704) (q:draft)
akikhel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:change/be changed) (d:<a> and <kikhel> written as one word: it changes, or before a noun the one that changes; {akikhel ngeilo} is never changing) (j:a/kikhel) (r:zd:22557/zd:15422) (q:draft)
akikhen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/social) (w:separate/divorce/split/be divided) (d:<a> and <kikhen> written as one word: they separate or are divided, the one who is separated; said of husband and wife who part and of a group that splits) (j:a/kikhen) (r:zd:14678/zd:25473/zd:21025) (q:draft)
akikhial = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be mistaken/be wrong) (d:<a> and <kikhial> written as one word: it is a mistake, or what is mistaken, an error) (j:a/kikhial) (r:zd:15489/zd:16947/zd:23957) (q:draft)
akikhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:be dropped/be imposed) (d:<a> and <kikhiat> written as one word: that was dropped, said of a bomb, and that is imposed, said of a prison sentence) (j:a/kikhiat) (r:zd:22658/zd:24322) (q:draft)
akikhol = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be stored/be accumulated) (d:<a> and <kikhol> written as one word: that which has been stored up or has piled up) (j:a/kikhol) (r:zd:18044) (q:draft)
akikhung = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/home) (w:be strung/be stretched across/be put up) (d:<a> and <kikhung> written as one word: that is stretched or put up across a space, of a wire, cable, bar or signboard) (j:a/kikhung) (r:zd:17175/zd:15579) (q:draft)
akikim = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:equal/equally) (d:<a> and <kikim> written as one word: equal, the same in amount; with <in>, equally) (j:a/kikim) (r:zd:24091/zd:25260) (q:draft)
akikoih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be placed/be kept/that is put) (d:<a> and <kikoih> written as one word: it is put or kept somewhere, or before a noun the thing that is put there) (j:a/kikoih) (r:zd:14507/zd:11889/zd:12267) (q:draft)
akikoihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/home) (w:place where something is kept) (d:<a> and <kikoihna> written as one word: the place or container in which the thing named before it is kept, followed by the name of the place or container) (j:a/kikoihna) (r:zd:21659/zd:11352) (q:draft)
akikum = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:discuss/confer) (d:<a> and <kikum> written as one word: they discuss, what is discussed, the ones who discuss) (j:a/kikum) (r:zd:19335/zd:11568) (q:draft)
akikup = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:discuss) (d:<a> and <kikup> written as one word: they discuss, or what is discussed) (j:a/kikup) (r:zd:22504/zd:25016/zd:19416) (q:draft)
akila = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:be taken/be collected/be drawn) (d:<a> and <kila> written as one word: that which is taken; said of data taken from a source, a tax or fee that is charged, and goods or water brought from a place) (j:a/kila) (r:zd:11846/ts:8144) (q:draft)
akilah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/everyday) (w:be shown/be examined/consult) (d:<a> and <kilah> written as one word: when it is shown, as a performance; of a sick person, show oneself to a doctor or at a clinic, be examined) (j:a/kilah) (r:zd:16389/zd:15435) (q:draft)
akilai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:fight/brawl) (d:<a> and <kilai> written as one word: they fight, those who fight one another) (j:a/kilai) (r:zd:16343/zd:18014) (q:draft)
akilaih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be changed/be replaced/change) (d:<a> and <kilaih> written as one word: is changed or replaced, the one that has changed; <pan> marks what it was before and <ah> what it becomes) (j:a/kilaih) (r:zd:26252/zd:22070/zd:14751) (q:draft)
akilak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:be shown/be revealed) (d:<a> and <kilak> written as one word: that is shown, displayed or revealed, as a film or a culture shown to the public) (j:a/kilak) (r:zd:25589/zd:13268) (q:draft)
akilak = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:be taken/be captured) (d:<a> and <kilak> written as one word: that is taken, as leave from work, a tooth that is pulled, or a camp captured in war) (j:a/kilak) (r:zd:13096/ts:3446) (q:draft)
akilam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:home/work) (w:be built) (d:<a> and <kilam> written as one word: was built, the one that is built) (j:a/kilam) (r:zd:10945/zd:13009/zd:19516) (q:draft)
akilamdang = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:different/that differs) (d:<a> and <kilamdang>, be different, written as one word: that is different, what differs, with <tawh> for what it differs from) (j:a/kilamdang) (r:zd:15396/zd:22802) (q:draft)
akilamsan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:be under construction/be being built) (d:<a>, <kilam>, be built, and the ending {-san}, in progress, written as one word: that is being built; {akilamsan laitak} is while it was under construction) (b:kilam) (r:zd:19692/zd:12448) (q:draft)
akilamthak = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:home/work) (w:newly built) (d:<akilam>, that is built, and <thak>, new, written as one word: newly built, said of a bridge, a prison or a stadium) (j:akilam/thak) (r:zd:16619/zd:18140) (q:draft)
akilamzawh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:home/work) (d:<akilam> and <zawh>, finish, written as one word: since it was built, after its building was finished, followed by a length of time) (j:akilam/zawh) (r:zd:14679/zd:17097) (q:draft)
akilang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:appear/be shown/be evident) (d:<a> and <kilang>, appear, written as one word: it appears, that which is shown; {akilang sak} is the one that makes it show) (j:a/kilang) (r:zd:12214) (q:draft)
akilangh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:appear/show/be evident) (d:<a> and <kilangh>, appear, written as one word: that shows, what is evident; {akilangh pen} is the most evident thing) (j:a/kilangh) (r:zd:21463/zd:24155) (q:draft)
akilawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health) (w:spread/be contagious/be infected) (d:<a> and <kilawh> written as one word: of a disease, pass from one person to another, or the ones to whom it has passed; {akilawh thei natna} is a contagious disease) (j:a/kilawh) (r:zd:24429/zd:12167/zd:24143) (q:draft)
akilawh thei = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:health) (w:contagious/infectious/communicable) (d:<akilawh>, that spreads from one to another, and <thei>, can: contagious, infectious; it stands before the noun, {akilawh thei natna} is a contagious disease) (r:zd:24429/zd:22652) (q:draft)
akilawhthei = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:health) (w:contagious/infectious/transmissible) (d:<a> and <kilawhthei> written as one word: that can spread, said of a disease that passes from an animal, an insect, food or a person; {panin akilawhthei} is that spreads from) (j:a/kilawhthei) (r:zd:18093/zd:20547) (q:draft)
akilawmlo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:social) (w:improper/unfitting/inappropriate/indecent) (d:<akilawm>, fitting, with <lo>, not, written as one word; {akilawmlo in gamtatna} is improper or indecent behaviour) (a:akilawm) (j:akilawm/lo) (r:zd:15674/zd:24220) (q:draft)
akilawn = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be thrown/be set off) (d:<a> and <kilawn> written as one word: that is thrown or flung, said also of firecrackers that are set off) (j:a/kilawn) (r:zd:13230/zd:14616) (q:draft)
akileh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:go back and forth/go about/run to and fro) (d:<a> and <kileh> written as one word: that goes to and fro, often with <kawikawi>, of people patrolling, of trains running between two places and of animals running about) (j:a/kileh) (r:zd:12345/zd:17994) (q:draft)
akilehbulh = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/religion) (w:contrary/opposite/contradictory) (d:<a> and <kilehbulh> written as one word, used with <tawh>: that is contrary or opposite to something) (j:a/kilehbulh) (r:zd:25224/zd:23979) (q:draft)
akilehkik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:return/turn back/come back) (d:<a> and <kilehkik> written as one word: it turned back, when someone comes back; said often of an aircraft returning) (j:a/kilehkik) (r:zd:15270/zd:15878) (q:draft)
akilei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:be bought/be purchased) (d:<a> and <kilei> written as one word: it was bought, or that which is bought; with <tawh> for the price) (j:a/kilei) (r:zd:15874/zd:15842) (q:draft)
akilem = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:get along/be on good terms/agree) (d:<a> and <kilem> written as one word: they are at peace or get along with one another; in the dictionary data also what fits or is in harmony) (j:a/kilem) (r:zd:25097/zd:19619) (q:draft)
akilimzat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:that is widely used/popular) (d:<a> and <kilimzat> written as one word: that is much used, widely used or popular) (j:a/kilimzat) (r:zd:18140/zd:13233) (q:draft)
akilot = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:be thrown/be fired) (d:<a> and <kilot> written as one word: it is thrown or shot, what is thrown) (j:a/kilot) (r:zd:11819/zd:17062) (q:draft)
akilut = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:enter/be entered) (d:<a> and <kilut> written as one word: people go in, a place is entered; before <ciangin>, when one enters) (j:a/kilut) (r:zd:14897/zd:13089) (q:draft)
akim = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/travel) (w:surroundings/area around/neighbourhood) (d:<a> and <kim> written as one word: the area around it; {akim akiang} and {akim apam} are the whole surrounding area) (j:a/kim) (r:zd:26097/zd:25680/zd:24038) (q:draft)
akim = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:complete/full/satisfied) (d:<a> and <kim> written as one word: complete, with none missing; {akim in} is in full or all of them, and {lung akim} is be satisfied) (j:a/kim) (r:zd:12280/zd:20906/zd:24040) (q:draft)
akimang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be in effect/last/be of use) (d:<a> and <kimang> written as one word: that is in use or in force, that lasts for a time, that is of use) (j:a/kimang) (r:zd:23554/zd:21050) (q:draft)
akimankhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:was arrested/was caught) (d:<a>, the passive prefix <ki> and <mankhia> written as one word: he was arrested, or the one who was arrested) (j:a/ki/mankhia) (r:zd:13063/zd:11883) (q:draft)
akimankhin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:have been arrested/already arrested) (d:<a> and <kimankhin> written as one word: who have already been arrested, those arrested so far) (j:a/kimankhin) (r:zd:14505/zd:13205) (q:draft)
akimanpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:arrested man/detainee/man in custody) (d:<a>, <kiman>, be arrested, and <pa>, man, written as one word: the man who was arrested) (j:a/kiman/pa) (r:zd:11396/zd:10767) (q:draft)
akimanpah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:was arrested at once/was caught immediately) (d:<a> and <kimanpah> written as one word: he or she was arrested right away) (j:a/kimanpah) (r:zd:17558/zd:12782) (q:draft)
akimanpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:politics/media) (w:the one arrested) (d:<a>, <kiman>, be arrested, and the topic marker <pen>, written as one word: the person who was arrested, as the topic of the sentence) (j:a/kiman/pen) (r:zd:16916/zd:21400) (q:draft)
akimansuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:be arrested/be detained) (d:<a>, <kiman>, be arrested, and <suak>, right through, written as one word: was arrested and taken away, or those who were arrested) (j:a/kiman/suak) (r:zd:14570/zd:21613) (q:draft)
akimante = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:those arrested/the arrested/detainees) (d:<a> and <kimante> written as one word: the people who were caught or arrested) (j:a/kimante) (r:zd:15745/zd:14533) (q:draft)
akimanteng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/everyday) (w:all that was seized/all those arrested) (d:<a>, <kiman> and <teng>, here all, written as one word: everything that was seized, or all the people who were arrested) (j:a/kiman/teng) (r:zd:15475/zd:19863) (q:draft)
akimanthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/politics) (w:could be caught/was arrested) (d:<a> and <kimanthei>, can be caught, written as one word: the one who could be caught or arrested, mostly as {akimanthei ahihi}, it was thus that he could be caught) (j:a/kimanthei) (r:zd:11099/zd:10881) (q:draft)
akimat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:be arrested/be caught/be seized) (d:<a> and <kimat> written as one word: the one who was arrested, what was seized, or when he was arrested) (j:a/kimat) (r:zd:15374/zd:17293) (q:draft)
akimatding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:will be arrested/being arrested) (d:<akimat>, be arrested, and <ding>, will, written as one word: that he or she will be arrested; often before a word of fear, as {akimatding lau}, afraid of being arrested) (j:akimat/ding) (r:zd:13002/zd:12542) (q:draft)
akimatkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:after being arrested/after being seized) (d:<akimat>, was arrested or seized, and <khit>, after, written as one word, mostly before <ciangin>) (j:akimat/khit) (r:zd:18231/zd:20661) (q:draft)
akimatleh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:if arrested/if caught) (d:<akimat> and <leh>, if, written as one word: if he is arrested) (j:akimat/leh) (r:zd:16130) (q:draft, low confidence)
akimatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:arrest/seizure/place of arrest) (d:<a> and <kimatna> written as one word: the arrest of someone or the seizure of something, or the place of it or reason for it) (j:a/kimatna) (r:zd:14609/zd:11345) (q:draft)
akimawhsakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:accusation/charge) (d:<a> and <kimawhsakna> written as one word: the accusation made against someone, the charge that is brought) (j:a/kimawhsakna) (r:zd:25474/zd:24536) (q:draft)
akimawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:play/playing) (d:<a> and <kimawl> written as one word: he or they play, or the one who plays, a player) (j:a/kimawl) (r:zd:15317/zd:19997/zd:17694) (q:draft)
akimawlmawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:play about/keep playing/be playing) (d:<a> and <kimawlmawl> written as one word: he or they are playing, or the one who plays on and on with something) (j:a/kimawlmawl) (r:zd:15756/zd:13163) (q:draft)
akimawlna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/family) (w:toy/plaything/play) (d:<a> and <kimawlna> written as one word: what a child plays with, or his playing and the place of it) (j:a/kimawlna) (r:zd:22828/zd:15756) (q:draft)
akimin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:in full/completely/in detail) (d:<a> and <kimin> written as one word: the whole of it, with nothing left out; of news, in full detail) (j:a/kimin) (r:zd:17872/zd:17841) (q:draft)
akimu = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be seen/be found) (d:<a> and <kimu> written as one word, here as the passive of <mu>, see: that is seen or found; {akimu theilo} is unseen, invisible) (j:a/kimu) (r:zd:12341/zd:22557) (q:draft)
akimuang = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:social/everyday) (w:trusted/relied on/confident) (d:<a> and <kimuang> written as one word: the one who is trusted or relied on; also being confident, sure of oneself) (j:a/kimuang) (r:zd:22803) (q:draft)
akimuding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:will meet/to meet) (d:<a> and <kimuding> written as one word: who will meet, in order to meet) (j:a/kimuding) (r:zd:16806/zd:11698) (q:draft)
akimuh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:be found/be seen) (d:<a> and <kimuh> written as one word: it was found or seen, mostly before <ciangin>, when) (j:a/kimuh) (r:zd:24432/zd:17023) (q:draft)
akimuh = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:meet/see each other) (d:<a> and <kimuh> written as one word: they meet or met each other) (j:a/kimuh) (r:zd:12183) (q:draft)
akimuhkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:be found/be discovered) (d:<a>, <kimuh> and <khiat> written as one word: it was found or discovered; the form used before a noun or a word such as <ciangin>, as {akimuhkhiat hun}, the time it was found) (j:a/kimuh/khiat) (r:zd:16177/zd:20254/zd:15886) (q:draft)
akimuhleh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:if found/if seen) (d:<a>, <kimuh>, be found, and <leh>, if, written as one word: if it is found, if someone is found or caught doing it) (j:a/kimuh/leh) (r:zd:17649/zd:15545) (q:draft)
akimuhna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:place where it was found/being found/being seen) (d:<a> and <kimuhna> written as one word: the place where, or the fact that, something was found or seen; also their meeting each other) (j:a/kimuhna) (r:zd:17707/zd:20219/zd:15389) (q:draft)
akimukhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:be found/be discovered) (d:<a> and <kimukhia> written as one word: was found, was discovered, or the one that was found) (j:a/kimukhia) (r:zd:20227/zd:16563) (q:draft)
akimuthei = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:visible/that can be seen) (d:<a> and <kimuthei> written as one word: what can be seen, the visible; the opposite is <akimutheilo>, the unseen) (j:a/kimuthei) (r:zd:20202/zd:12341/zd:20829) (q:draft)
akimutheilo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/religion) (w:invisible/unseen) (d:<a>, <kimuthei> and <lo> written as one word: that cannot be seen) (j:a/kimuthei/lo) (r:zd:20568/zd:19816/zd:20997) (q:draft)
akin = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:urgent/pressing/eager) (d:<a> and <kin> written as one word: what is urgent, or one who is eager and cares about something; before a verb, urgently or with care) (j:a/kin) (r:zd:14895/zd:15489) (q:draft, low confidence)
akinai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/travel) (w:near/close/nearest) (d:<a> and <kinai> written as one word: that is near or close to something, used with <tawh>; with <pen> the nearest; also of a close relation) (j:a/kinai) (r:zd:24635/zd:15445/zd:17707) (q:draft)
akinaipen = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:travel/everyday) (w:nearest/closest) (d:<a> and <kinaipen> written as one word: the nearest, with <tawh> for the place it is nearest to) (j:a/kinaipen) (r:zd:15123/zd:11889) (q:draft)
akinei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be had/be held/have) (d:<a> and <kinei> written as one word: that is had or held, what people have, as a view, a feeling or a meeting) (j:a/kinei) (r:zd:20929/zd:24120/zd:24155) (q:draft)
akineih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:pretend/pose as) (d:<a> and <kineih>, pretend, written as one word: one who makes himself out to be what he is not; follows the thing pretended) (j:a/kineih) (r:zd:18908/zd:13145) (q:draft)
akineih = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be held/be carried out) (d:<a>, the prefix <ki> and <neih>, have or hold, written as one word: that is held or carried out, of a meeting, a check or an attitude) (j:a/ki/neih) (r:zd:18876) (q:draft, low confidence)
akineihkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:after it has been held/has been held) (d:<aki> and <neihkhit>, have held, written as one word: with <ciangin>, after a hearing, meeting or event has been held) (j:aki/neihkhit) (r:zd:16637/zd:19805) (q:draft)
akineihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/politics) (w:holding/hearing/session) (d:<a>, <ki> and <neihna> written as one word: the holding of something, or the occasion and place at which an inquiry, a hearing or a protest is held, as {thusitna akineihna}, the hearing that was held) (j:a/ki/neihna) (r:zd:14957/zd:20676) (q:draft)
akingah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be obtained/be got/be received) (d:<a> and <kingah> written as one word: it is obtained, or that which is got or received) (j:a/kingah) (r:zd:24325/zd:23933/zd:24014) (q:draft)
akingai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/social) (w:be lovers/love each other) (d:<a> and <kingai> written as one word: those who love each other as man and woman, or the one someone is in love with) (j:a/kingai) (r:zd:17854/zd:19396) (q:draft)
akinusia = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:left behind/abandoned/left) (d:<a> and <kinusia>, be left, written as one word: that has been left behind or abandoned, of a child, a thing or a message) (j:a/kinusia) (r:zd:17841/zd:15729/zd:16398) (q:draft)
akip = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/politics) (w:stable/firm/established) (d:<a> and <kip> written as one word: what is firm or established, be firmly established; {akip akho} is stable and lasting) (j:a/kip) (r:zd:12166/zd:20406/zd:21050) (q:draft)
akipaai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/family) (w:thrown away/abandoned/discarded) (d:<a> and <kipaai>, be thrown away, written as one word before a noun or <khat>: one that was thrown away; said here of a newborn baby that was abandoned) (j:a/kipaai) (r:zd:11240/zd:12725) (q:draft)
akipai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be thrown away/be abandoned) (d:<a> and <kipai> written as one word, here in the sense be thrown away: that was thrown away or left behind, said of rubbish and of an abandoned baby) (j:a/kipai) (r:zd:15830/zd:13224) (q:draft)
akipai = (i:2) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:go/travel) (d:<a> and <kipai> written as one word: when one goes, the going) (j:a/kipai) (r:zd:17822) (q:draft, low confidence)
akipanding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:time/everyday) (w:will begin/be about to start) (d:<a>, <kipan> and <ding> written as one word: it will begin, that which is to begin; often with a date and {hita hi}) (j:a/kipan/ding) (r:zd:21334/zd:15303/zd:11329) (q:draft)
akipankhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:begin/start/originate) (d:<a> and <kipankhia> written as one word: that began or started out from a time, a place or a source) (j:a/kipankhia) (r:zd:17289/zd:13220/zd:17607) (q:draft)
akipankhin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:has already begun/has already started) (d:<a> and <kipankhin> written as one word: it has already begun or been started) (j:a/kipankhin) (r:zd:16735/zd:16490) (q:draft)
akipanta = (i:1) (t:v) (f:time/everyday) (w:have begun/has started) (d:<a> and <kipanta> written as one word: it has now begun) (j:a/kipanta) (r:zd:19381/zd:12774) (q:draft)
akipat = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:begin/start/break out) (d:<kipat>, begin, with the prefix <a> written joined, as the verb of a clause before <ciangin>, <laitak> or <hun>: it began, as a fire or a meeting; not the adjective first) (r:zd:18947/zd:21624/zd:15572) (q:draft)
akipatcil = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:beginning/start) (d:<a> and <kipatcil> written as one word: the beginning; {akipatcil in} is at first, at the beginning) (j:a/kipatcil) (r:zd:19803/zd:15264/zd:18145) (q:draft)
akipatkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:time/work) (w:begin/start/be started) (d:<a> with <kipat>, begin, and <khiat>, out, written as one word: that or when something was started; {akipatkhiat kum} is the year it began) (j:a/kipat/khiat) (r:zd:12194/zd:16901/zd:12063) (q:draft)
akipatma = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:before it begins/before the start) (d:<a> and <kipatma> written as one word: before something begins, often with <in> or with a length of time after it) (j:a/kipatma) (r:zd:19563/zd:19775) (q:draft)
akipatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:beginning/origin/starting point) (d:<a> and <kipatna> written as one word: its beginning, the place or cause from which something started) (j:a/kipatna) (r:zd:12673/zd:17202/zd:16952) (q:draft)
akipatpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:time/media) (w:began/the start of it) (d:<a>, <kipat>, begin, and the topic marker <pen> written as one word: as for when or where something began) (j:a/kipat/pen) (r:zd:17058/zd:14871) (q:draft)
akipatzawh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:since it began/since starting) (d:<a>, <kipat> and <zawh> written as one word, with <zawh> in the sense after: since something began, followed by the length of time that has passed) (j:a/kipat/zawh) (r:zd:15575/zd:15276/zd:22704) (q:draft)
akipawlkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:allied/joined together/associated) (d:<a> and <kipawlkhawm>, join together, written as one word: who have joined together, those allied with someone) (j:a/kipawlkhawm) (r:zd:19220/zd:15477) (q:draft)
akipawlpih = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:politics/social) (w:allied/associated/partner) (d:<a> and <kipawlpih> written as one word before a noun: that is allied with, its ally or partner) (j:a/kipawlpih) (r:ts:3110/zd:14681) (q:draft)
akipawlpihte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:allies/associates) (d:<a> and <kipawlpihte> written as one word: those who are joined with them, their allies) (j:a/kipawlpihte) (r:ts:8027/ts:7272) (q:draft)
akipei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/it) (w:spin/rotate/turn round) (d:<a> and <kipei> written as one word: it spins, the one that turns round, said of machines, blades and wheels) (j:a/kipei) (r:zd:14829/zd:12456) (q:draft)
akipelh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:miss/avoid/be at variance with) (d:<a> and <kipelh> written as one word: what is avoided or missed; after <tawh>, what does not agree with a rule or a record, and {akipelh thei lo} is unavoidable) (j:a/kipelh) (r:zd:12138/zd:24068/zd:14593) (q:draft)
akiphallo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:not allowed/forbidden/prohibited) (d:<a>, <kiphal> be allowed and the negative <lo> written as one word: that is not permitted; after a verb with <ding>, not allowed to do it) (j:a/kiphal/lo) (r:zd:17649/zd:12097/zd:16101) (q:draft)
akipho = (i:1) (t:v) (f:home) (w:be hung out/be spread out to dry) (d:<a> and <kipho> written as one word: that is hung or spread out, said of washing put out to dry) (j:a/kipho) (r:zd:21035) (q:draft)
akiphuan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:founded/established/formed) (d:<a>, the passive prefix <ki> and <phuan>, set up, written as one word: that was founded, of an association, a committee or a court) (j:a/ki/phuan) (r:zd:21042/zd:24737/zd:15763) (q:draft)
akiphuankhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:founded/established/formed) (d:<a> and <kiphuankhia> written as one word: that was founded, of a school, a district or an organisation) (j:a/kiphuankhia) (r:zd:15961/zd:14575) (q:draft)
akiphukha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:collide/crash into each other) (d:<a> and <kiphukha>, collide, written as one word: they collided, the ones that collided, said of vehicles) (j:a/kiphukha) (r:zd:17353/zd:18129/zd:15613) (q:draft)
akiphum = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be buried/buried) (d:<a> and <kiphum> written as one word: that is buried, said of a body, a mine or a pipe under the ground) (j:a/kiphum) (r:zd:12772/zd:13140) (q:draft)
akiphut = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:be set up/be founded/be planted) (d:<a> and <kiphut> written as one word: that was set up or founded, as an organisation, or that is fixed or stuck in something) (j:a/kiphut) (r:zd:14792) (q:draft)
akiphut = (i:2) (t:v) (f:social/travel) (w:crowd/throng) (d:<a> and <kiphut> written as one word, said of people: who are crowding together in a place, as {akiphut ziahziah}) (j:a/kiphut) (r:zd:14694) (q:draft, low confidence)
akipia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:given/be given) (d:<a> and <kipia> written as one word: that is given, the one to whom something is given) (j:a/kipia) (r:zd:15116/zd:14767) (q:draft)
akipiak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be given/that is given) (d:<a> and <kipiak> written as one word: it is given, that which is given; {akipiak nadingin} is in order that it be given) (j:a/kipiak) (r:zd:11732/zd:24810/zd:20482) (q:draft)
akipiakhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:devote oneself/volunteer/be given out) (d:<a> and <kipiakhia> written as one word: one who gives himself to a cause, a volunteer; also what is given out) (j:a/kipiakhia) (r:zd:17410/zd:15763) (q:draft)
akipiakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:giving/being given) (d:<a> and <kipiakna> written as one word: the giving of a thing, the fact that or the reason why it was given) (j:a/kipiakna) (r:zd:19674/zd:11984) (q:draft)
akipialo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/work) (w:not given/unpaid/not granted) (d:<a> and <kipialo> written as one word: that is not given, said of a permit not granted and of a tax or debt not paid) (j:a/kipialo) (r:zd:21665/zd:12190) (q:draft)
akipiasa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:given/already given) (d:<a> and <kipiasa> written as one word: that has been given) (j:a/kipiasa) (r:zd:19824/zd:11078) (q:draft)
akipilsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:think oneself wise/be conceited) (d:<a> and <kipilsak> written as one word: the one who thinks himself wise, those who make themselves out to be wise) (j:a/kipilsak) (r:zd:19641/zd:23554) (q:draft)
akipsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:confirm/establish/make firm) (d:<a> and <kipsak> written as one word: he confirmed or settled it, or the one or the thing that makes firm) (j:a/kipsak) (r:zd:11648/zd:17046) (q:draft)
akipua = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/work) (w:be carried/be transported) (d:<a> and <kipua> written as one word: that is carried or loaded, what a vehicle or ship is carrying) (j:a/kipua) (r:zd:11138/zd:17141/zd:15667) (q:draft)
akipuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/work) (w:be sent/be taken/be delivered) (d:<a> and <kipuak> written as one word: it is sent or taken somewhere, the one that is sent) (j:a/kipuak) (r:zd:17605/zd:19529) (q:draft)
akipuakding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/politics) (w:to be sent/to be delivered/bound for) (d:<a> and <kipuakding> written as one word: that is to be sent or taken to a place) (j:a/kipuakding) (r:zd:16869/zd:14609) (q:draft)
akipuakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/travel) (w:where one was taken/being sent) (d:<a> and <kipuakna> written as one word: the place to which someone was taken, as {zato akipuakna}, the hospital he was taken to; also the sending or shipping of something) (j:a/kipuakna) (r:zd:22545/zd:11044) (q:draft)
akipuaksawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/work) (w:be about to be sent/be meant to be carried) (d:<a>, <kipuak> be carried or sent and <sawm> intend, written as one word: that was going to be sent, carried or smuggled to a place) (j:a/kipuak/sawm) (r:zd:14609/zd:12519/zd:11133) (q:draft)
akipuk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:fell/collapsed/that fell) (d:<a> and <kipuk> written as one word: fell down or collapsed, and the thing that fell) (j:a/kipuk) (r:zd:12287/zd:19303) (q:draft)
akipumpiak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:surrender/give oneself up) (d:<a> and <kipumpiak> written as one word: who surrendered, the one who gives himself up to the other side in war) (j:a/kipumpiak) (r:ts:8967/ts:3759) (q:draft)
akisai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:concerning/related) (d:<a> and <kisai> written as one word: that which concerns, what is related; {tawh akisai} is concerning, connected with) (j:a/kisai) (r:zd:22081/zd:19262) (q:draft)
akisaikha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:concerned/involved) (d:<akisai> with <kha> written as one word: those who are concerned in or touched by a matter; {akisaikha kumpi thunei te} is the authorities concerned) (j:akisai/kha) (r:zd:20291/zd:12279) (q:draft)
akisailo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:unrelated/irrelevant/not concerning) (d:<akisai>, concerning, and <lo>, not, written as one word: that has nothing to do with; the thing it is unrelated to stands before it with <tawh>) (j:akisai/lo) (r:zd:24566/zd:20019) (q:draft)
akisam = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:needed/necessary/required) (d:<a> and <kisam> written as one word: that is needed, what is necessary; <akisam bangin> is as needed) (j:a/kisam) (r:zd:23594/zd:24673/zd:25004) (q:draft)
akisam bangbang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/work) (w:as needed/whatever is needed) (d:<akisam>, what is needed, with <bangbang.2>, just as: according to need, in whatever way is required; mostly with <in> before a verb, {akisam bangbang in}, and also before a noun, whatever is needed) (r:zd:18159/zd:15180) (q:draft)
akisam bangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/work) (w:as needed/as required/as necessary) (d:<akisam>, what is needed, and <bangin>, according to: as the need is, as the case requires; it stands before the verb, often in official statements, as in {akisam bangin thu kibawlding hi}, action will be taken as necessary) (r:zd:25004/zd:16504/zd:17974) (q:draft)
akisambang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/politics) (w:as needed/as necessary/as required) (d:<akisam> and <bang> written as one word, followed by <in>: according to what is needed) (j:akisam/bang) (r:zd:14566/zd:19300/zd:16895) (q:draft)
akisamte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:those in need/the things needed) (d:<a>, <kisam> and the plural <te> written as one word: the people who need something, as in {panpihna akisamte}, those who need help, or the things that are needed) (j:a/kisam/te) (r:zd:23629/zd:24012) (q:draft)
akisamteng = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/work) (w:all that is needed/everything necessary) (d:<a> <kisam> and <teng>, here all, written as one word: all the things that are needed) (j:a/kisam/teng) (r:zd:12063/zd:19143/zd:17120) (q:draft)
akisap = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be needed/what is needed) (d:<a> and <kisap> written as one word: what is needed; {akisap leh} is if needed, {akisap bang in} as is needed, and before a noun it means the needed one) (j:a/kisap) (r:zd:16202/zd:23808/zd:25917) (q:draft)
akisapleh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:if needed/if necessary) (d:<a>, <kisap> and <leh> written as one word: if it is needed, when necessary) (j:a/kisap/leh) (r:zd:11407/zd:15216) (q:draft)
akisapna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:need/what is needed) (d:<a> and <kisapna> written as one word: the need for something, what is needed; {akisapna zui in} is according to need) (j:a/kisapna) (r:zd:11778/zd:21262/zd:20999) (q:draft)
akisat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:be beaten/be struck/be hacked) (d:<a> and <kisat> written as one word: he or it is beaten, struck or cut with a blade, the one who is struck) (j:a/kisat) (r:zd:12538/zd:18014) (q:draft)
akisat = (i:2) (t:v) (f:social) (w:be founded/be established) (d:<a> and <kisat> written as one word, of a village: {khua akisat} is the village was founded) (j:a/kisat) (r:zd:24029) (q:draft, low confidence)
akisawhkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:be involved in/be connected with/come into contact with) (d:<a> and <kisawhkha> written as one word, after <tawh>: the one who is involved in a matter, or who has come into contact with a thing) (j:a/kisawhkha) (r:zd:16323/zd:15286/zd:18112) (q:draft)
akisawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:be told/be ordered/be sent) (d:<a> and <kisawl> written as one word: he or they were told or ordered to do something, or the one who is sent; {akisawl nana mun} is wherever one is sent) (j:a/kisawl) (r:zd:15054/zd:25243/zd:20635) (q:draft)
akisel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:hidden/be hidden) (d:<a> and <kisel> written as one word, <kisel> here in the sense of be hidden and not of argue: that is hidden or concealed) (j:a/kisel) (r:zd:22557/zd:15422) (q:draft)
akiselsim = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:hidden/concealed) (d:<a> and <kiselsim>, be concealed, written as one word: that is hidden or kept out of sight) (j:a/kiselsim) (r:zd:15475/zd:12422) (q:draft)
akisem = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:be done/be made/be carried out) (d:<a> and <kisem> written as one word: it is done, that which is done or made) (j:a/kisem) (r:zd:13151/ts:6842) (q:draft)
akisia = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:ruined/damaged/broken down) (d:<a> and <kisia> written as one word: that which is ruined or spoiled, or it is ruined) (j:a/kisia) (r:zd:19427/zd:11403/zd:24068) (q:draft)
akisiacip = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/travel) (w:wrecked/completely ruined) (d:<a> and <kisiacip> written as one word: the one that is wrecked, it is completely ruined) (j:a/kisiacip) (r:zd:12349/ts:2556) (q:draft)
akisial = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:be laid/lie/be placed) (d:<aki> and <sial>, lay down, written as one word: who is laid or is lying on a bed, a table or a stretcher or in a cradle or tomb) (j:aki/sial) (r:zd:17779/zd:14965) (q:draft)
akisial = (i:2) (t:v) (f:social) (w:boast/brag) (d:<a> and <kisial>, boast, written as one word: who boasts; {akisial mahmah} is those who brag a great deal) (j:a/kisial) (r:zd:11587) (q:draft, low confidence)
akisiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:break down/be damaged/be ruined) (d:<a> and <kisiat> written as one word: it breaks down, is damaged or spoiled, the one that is damaged; of a couple, fall out) (j:a/kisiat) (r:zd:15031/zd:24290/zd:21330) (q:draft)
akisiatheilo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:religion/everyday) (w:imperishable/indestructible/incorruptible) (d:<akisia> and <theilo> written as one word: that cannot be ruined or destroyed, often paired with <akimutheilo>, invisible) (j:akisia/theilo) (r:zd:19976/zd:20997) (q:draft)
akisik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:religion/social) (w:repent/regret) (d:<a> and <kisik> written as one word: he repents, or before a noun the one who repents; {akisik kik} is turn back in repentance) (j:a/kisik) (r:zd:18924/zd:17883) (q:draft)
akisil = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/body) (w:bathe/take a bath) (d:<a> and <kisil> written as one word: he or she bathes; {akisil laitak} is while bathing) (j:a/kisil) (r:zd:11823/zd:19521) (q:draft)
akisin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/everyday) (w:practise/train/be learned) (d:<a> and <kisin> written as one word: he practises or trains, or what is learned; {akisin laitak} is while practising) (j:a/kisin) (r:zd:20069/zd:17512/zd:26097) (q:draft)
akisit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/health) (w:be examined/be tested/be tried) (d:<a> and <kisit>, be examined, written as one word: is examined, checked or tested; {thu akisit} is the case is heard in court) (j:a/kisit) (r:zd:17709/zd:24535) (q:draft)
akisitna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:trial/examination) (d:<a>, <kisit> and the noun suffix <na> written as one word: the examining of a case, the trial; {thu akisitna} is the hearing of the case) (j:a/kisit/na) (r:zd:16365) (q:draft, low confidence)
akisitna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:covering/cover) (d:<a> and <kisitna> written as one word: that with which something is covered, as the cover of a drain) (j:a/kisitna) (r:zd:16410) (q:draft, low confidence)
akisuah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be made into/be divided into/become) (d:<a> and <kisuah> written as one word: it is made into something or split into parts, or that which is so made) (j:a/kisuah) (r:zd:15570/zd:15810) (q:draft)
akisuamlum = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:assassinated/murdered) (d:<a>, <ki> and <suamlum> written as one word: who was attacked and killed, said before the name of the victim) (j:a/ki/suamlum) (r:zd:11366/zd:11535) (q:draft)
akisuang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/home) (w:be put up/be displayed/be posted) (d:<a> and <kisuang>, be set on, written as one word: is put up, hung or written on a wall or other place for people to see, of a picture, a notice or a name) (j:a/kisuang) (r:zd:14954/zd:16966/zd:11409) (q:draft)
akisun = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health) (w:be injected/be vaccinated) (d:<a> joined to a passive verb meaning be pierced with a needle, not <kisun> in its sense like: the one who has been given an injection, in the articles a vaccine; {akisun nuamlo} is one who does not want the injection) (r:zd:25243/zd:24500) (q:draft)
akisun = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:resembling/in the likeness of) (d:<a> and <kisun>, like, written as one word: looking like someone, as a statue made in the likeness of a person) (j:a/kisun) (r:zd:13157) (q:draft, low confidence)
akitaih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:collide/crash/be hit) (d:<a> and <kitaih>, collide, written as one word: of vehicles, collide or be run into) (j:a/kitaih) (r:zd:12825/zd:13318) (q:draft)
akitaih = (i:2) (t:v) (f:social) (w:be robbed/be held up) (d:<a> and <kitaih> written as one word after <damiah>, robber: be held up and robbed) (j:a/kitaih) (r:zd:15913) (q:draft)
akitaihkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/media) (w:collide/be hit/crash) (d:<a> and <kitaihkha> written as one word: they collided, it was hit, or the one that was hit) (j:a/kitaihkha) (r:zd:20353/zd:13318) (q:draft)
akitam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:burst/explode/break) (d:<a> and <kitam> written as one word: it broke or burst, or the one that broke; said of a bomb or shell that explodes, a tyre that bursts and a screen that cracks) (j:a/kitam) (r:ts:2189/zd:12349) (q:draft)
akitan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:body/health) (w:be cut off/be severed/be broken) (d:<a> and <kitan> written as one word: that is cut off or broken through, said of a limb, a finger, a cord or another long thing) (j:a/kitan) (r:zd:13224/zd:19414) (q:draft)
akitankhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:body/health) (w:be cut off/be severed) (d:<a> with <ki>, <tan>, cut, and <khia> written as one word: that was cut off, the severed part, said of a limb or a cord; not the same as <kitankhia>, be redeemed) (j:a/ki/tan/khia) (r:zd:20056/zd:12014) (q:draft)
akitansak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:body) (w:be cut off/have cut off) (d:<a> and <kitansak> written as one word: was cut off, the one whose limb was cut off) (j:a/kitansak) (r:zd:15505) (q:draft, low confidence)
akitapna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:bursting/explosion/break) (d:<a> and <kitapna> written as one word: the bursting, snapping or exploding of a thing such as a pipe, a tyre, a tank or a bomb, and with <mun> the place where it burst) (j:a/kitapna) (r:zd:17834/zd:14628) (q:draft)
akitat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:snap/be cut off/break) (d:<a> and <kitat>, be cut off, written as one word: of a rope or thread, that it snaps) (j:a/kitat) (r:zd:11197/zd:23670) (q:draft)
akitawhna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/nature) (w:place of digging/mine/excavation) (d:<a> and <kitawhna> written as one word: the place where the ground is dug, as a tunnel for a railway or a pit where gems are dug) (j:a/kitawhna) (r:zd:15729/zd:19543) (q:draft)
akitawi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be held/be carried) (d:<a> and <kitawi> written as one word: that is held or carried, the one being held) (j:a/kitawi) (r:zd:11587/zd:12732) (q:draft)
akitawng = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:quarrelled/fought) (d:<a> and <kitawng> written as one word: they quarrelled or fought, and those who did so) (j:a/kitawng) (r:zd:15157/zd:15698) (q:draft)
akitawnggawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:who brawled/who fought) (d:<a> and <kitawnggawp> written as one word: the ones who fought violently, or they brawled) (j:a/kitawnggawp) (r:zd:22267) (q:draft)
akiteel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:be chosen/be elected/be selected) (d:<a> and <kiteel> written as one word: he or it is chosen or elected, and before a noun the one that is chosen) (j:a/kiteel) (r:zd:19441/zd:24414/zd:19172) (q:draft)
akiteelkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:be chosen/be selected) (d:<a> and <kiteelkhia> written as one word: it was chosen, or before a noun the one that was chosen or selected) (j:a/kiteelkhia) (r:zd:19671/zd:11846) (q:draft)
akiteen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family) (w:marry/be married) (d:<a> and <kiteen>, the short form of <kiteeng>, written as one word: they marry or married; {akiteen laitak} is at the time they married) (j:a/kiteen) (r:zd:12567/zd:21025) (q:draft)
akiteending = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family) (w:be going to marry/be about to marry) (d:<akiteeng> and <ding> written as one word: that they will marry, their coming marriage) (j:akiteeng/ding) (r:zd:13260/zd:16922) (q:draft)
akiteeng = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family) (w:marry/be married) (d:<a> and <kiteeng> written as one word: they married, the ones who are married) (j:a/kiteeng) (r:zd:13260/zd:12409) (q:draft)
akiteenna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/social) (w:their marriage/his marriage) (d:<a> and <kiteenna> written as one word: his, her or their marriage) (j:a/kiteenna) (r:zd:14577) (q:draft)
akiteenzawh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:family/time) (w:after marrying/since they married) (d:<a>, <kiteen>, marry, and <zawh>, having finished, written as one word: after they married, counted from the time of the marriage) (j:a/kiteen/zawh) (r:zd:12567/zd:15114) (q:draft)
akiteh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be measured/be compared) (d:<a> and <kiteh>, be measured, written as one word: that which is measured, or when it is measured; {akiteh theilo} is beyond measure or comparison) (j:a/kiteh) (r:zd:11350/zd:23830/zd:20200) (q:draft)
akitel = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:clear/plain/certain) (d:<a> and <kitel> written as one word: that is clear, that is understood or settled) (j:a/kitel) (r:zd:23977/zd:25479/zd:21900) (q:draft)
akithahna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/media) (w:killing/murder) (d:<a> and <kithahna> written as one word: the killing of someone, his being killed) (j:a/kithahna) (r:zd:19906) (q:draft)
akithat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:be killed/be murdered) (d:<a> and <kithat> written as one word: who was killed; with {amah leh amah} it means who killed himself) (j:a/kithat) (r:zd:25281/zd:10894) (q:draft)
akithatlum = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/politics) (w:killed/be killed/the one killed) (d:<a> and <kithatlum> written as one word: who was killed, placed before the person; {amah leh amah akithatlum} is one who killed himself) (j:a/kithatlum) (r:zd:15463/zd:17357) (q:draft)
akithawi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:was preparing/was getting ready/was about to) (d:<a> and <kithawi> written as one word: he was getting ready; after a verb with {ding in} it means was preparing to or was about to) (j:a/kithawi) (r:zd:21328/zd:14557) (q:draft)
akithawithawi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be preparing/be getting ready) (d:<a> and <kithawithawi> written as one word: he or they are getting ready to do something, and those who are preparing) (j:a/kithawithawi) (r:zd:14597/zd:11823) (q:draft)
akitheh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be scattered/be sprinkled/be spread) (d:<a> and <kitheh> written as one word: that is sprinkled or scattered; {akitheh thang} is scattered abroad, of a people) (j:a/kitheh) (r:zd:21025/zd:25275) (q:draft)
akithehzak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/it) (w:spread/circulate/go viral) (d:<a> and <kithehzak> written as one word: that has spread widely, said of a video, picture or report passed around on social media; also of wreckage scattered about) (j:a/kithehzak) (r:zd:15674/zd:16600) (q:draft)
akithei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be known/be well known) (d:<a> and <kithei> written as one word: it is known, the one that is known, or they know each other; {akithei mahmah} is very well known) (j:a/kithei) (r:zd:23830/zd:13142/zd:12021) (q:draft)
akitheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:be known/become known) (d:<a> and <kitheih>, be known, written as one word; {akitheih ciangin} is when it became known, when it was noticed) (j:a/kitheih) (r:zd:15276/zd:11398/zd:12420) (q:draft)
akitheihleh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:if it is known/if found out) (d:<a>, <kitheih>, be known, and <leh>, if, written as one word: if it becomes known, if someone is found out doing it) (j:a/kitheih/leh) (r:zd:21540/zd:18893) (q:draft)
akitheihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media) (w:what is known/information) (d:<a> and <kitheihna> written as one word: that which is known, the information to hand; {tuciangciang akitheihna ah} is as far as is known so far) (j:a/kitheihna) (r:zd:15551/zd:14678) (q:draft)
akitheikhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:be found out/come to light/become known) (d:<a> and <kitheikhia> written as one word: it was found out, it came to light) (j:a/kitheikhia) (r:zd:16899/zd:17986) (q:draft)
akitheilo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/media) (w:unknown/unrecognisable) (d:<a> and <kitheilo> written as one word: that is not known or cannot be recognised; {amin akitheilo} is whose name is not known, and {akitheilo dingin} is so as not to be recognised) (j:a/kitheilo) (r:zd:19872/zd:17450) (q:draft)
akithuah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/family) (w:accompany/be with/associate with) (d:<a> and <kithuah> written as one word, of people: the one who is together with or keeps company with someone, who is marked by <tawh>) (j:a/kithuah) (r:zd:15307/zd:17295) (q:draft)
akithuah = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:be fitted/be installed/be attached) (d:<a> and <kithuah> written as one word, of things: that is fitted, installed or attached in a place or to something) (j:a/kithuah) (r:zd:18181/zd:13184) (q:draft)
akithukim = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:agreed/agreed upon) (d:<a> and <kithukim>, agree together, written as one word: that which has been agreed, or they agreed; with <pih>, agree on a matter) (j:a/kithukim) (r:zd:24500/zd:24691) (q:draft)
akitom = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (d:<a> and <kitom> written as one word: the one who struggles or puts up a fight, who acts wildly) (j:a/kitom) (r:zd:22775) (q:draft, low confidence)
akitomgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:struggle violently/make a scene/brawl) (d:<a> and <kitomgawp> written as one word: he, she or they struggled wildly or made a violent scene) (j:a/kitomgawp) (r:zd:19562/zd:12754) (q:draft)
akitot = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/family) (w:quarrel/fight/argue) (d:<a> and <kitot> written as one word: they quarrel, those who quarrel, and their quarrel) (j:a/kitot) (r:zd:20732/zd:17455) (q:draft)
akituah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:agree with/fit/match) (d:<a> with <kituah>, here the form of <kituak> used before <leh> and <ding>: that agrees with or fits something, marked by <tawh>) (j:a/kituah) (r:zd:14910/zd:21461) (q:draft)
akituah = (i:2) (t:v) (f:travel/home) (w:move/relocate) (d:<a> with <kituah> in the sense of moving house or office to another place, marked by <ah>: moved to, that is moved to) (j:a/kituah) (r:zd:12409/zd:23733) (q:draft)
akituahna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:junction/meeting point) (d:<a> and <kituahna> written as one word: the place where two or more things meet, as railway lines or countries) (j:a/kituahna) (r:zd:11780/zd:19061) (q:draft)
akituak = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:fitting/suitable/appropriate) (d:<a> and <kituak> written as one word: what fits or agrees; <tawh> marks what it is suited to, as {cidamna tawh akituak}, good for health) (j:a/kituak) (r:zd:22856/zd:13252/zd:19355) (q:draft)
akituaklo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:social/politics) (w:not in accordance with/contrary to/unfitting/unsuitable) (d:<a>, <kituak>, agree or fit, and the negative <lo> written as one word: that does not agree with or fit something, which is named with <tawh>; {thukhun tawh akituaklo} is against the law, illegal) (j:a/kituak/lo) (r:zd:17570/zd:22873/zd:16974) (q:draft)
