akituat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:be calculated/be valued/be reckoned) (d:<a> with the passive <ki> and <tuat>, calculate, written as one word, mostly as {akituat ciangin}: when it is worked out, when its value is reckoned) (j:a/ki/tuat) (r:zd:12140/zd:15296) (q:draft)
akituh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:compete/contend/scramble) (d:<a> and <kituh> written as one word: they compete for something or struggle with one another to get it; of seed, the one that is sown) (j:a/kituh) (r:zd:11064/zd:19441) (q:draft)
akitun = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/home) (w:wrapped/that is wrapped) (d:<a> and <kitun>, be wrapped, written as one word: that is wrapped, or the one wrapped in something) (j:a/kitun) (r:zd:23385/zd:11637) (q:draft)
akiu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/home) (w:corner/its corner/edge) (d:<a> and <kiu>, corner, written as one word: the corner or edge of a thing or place; {akiu khat} is a corner somewhere) (j:a/kiu) (r:zd:10929/zd:15437) (q:draft)
akivaihawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/politics) (w:be organised/be arranged/be managed) (d:<a>, the passive <ki> and <vaihawm> written as one word: that is organised, arranged or run by someone) (j:a/ki/vaihawm) (r:zd:20276/zd:11392) (q:draft)
akivak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:make a living/live on) (d:<a> and <kivak> written as one word: who makes a living, the work marked by <tawh> or <in>) (j:a/kivak) (r:zd:12567/zd:16979/zd:12715) (q:draft)
akivui = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:be buried) (d:<a> and <kivui> written as one word: he is buried, the one who is being buried) (j:a/kivui) (r:zd:15344/zd:20589) (q:draft)
