akizomsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:still attached/still connected) (d:{akizom sa} written as one word, <akizom>, connected, followed by a word for already: in the state of being joined, with the connection not cut or removed) (b:akizom) (r:zd:14822/zd:12776) (q:draft)
akizon = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be searched for/be sought) (d:<a> and <kizon> written as one word: he, she or it is searched for, or the place is searched; {akizon ciangin} is when a search was made) (j:a/kizon) (r:zd:17439/zd:13039) (q:draft)
akizong = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be sought/be looked for/be searched) (d:<a> and <kizong> written as one word: it is looked for or searched, the one that is sought) (j:a/kizong) (r:zd:20045/zd:19571) (q:draft)
akizonna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/work) (w:search/the search for) (d:<aki> and <zonna> written as one word: the searching for a missing person or thing, the search that is made) (j:aki/zonna) (r:zd:11588/zd:14969) (q:draft)
akizop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:be connected/be joined/continue) (d:<a> and <kizop> written as one word: its being joined or connected with something, usually after <tawh>; also be continued) (j:a/kizop) (r:zd:12487/zd:14939) (q:draft)
akizopna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:relationship/connection/link) (d:<a> and <kizopna> written as one word: their relationship or dealings with someone, or the place where things join) (j:a/kizopna) (r:zd:25488/zd:25016/zd:20582) (q:draft)
akizoppih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:be connected with/be linked to) (d:<a> and <kizoppih> written as one word: who is connected with, the one in contact with someone; also an associate) (j:a/kizoppih) (r:zd:12183/zd:15828) (q:draft)
akizuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:be sold/be on sale) (d:<a> and <kizuak>, be sold, written as one word: it is sold, or before a noun the one that is sold) (j:a/kizuak) (r:zd:15167/zd:21954) (q:draft)
akizuakkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:be sold/be put on sale/be exported) (d:<akizuak> and <khia>, out, written as one word: it is sold out to buyers, or before a noun the thing that is put on sale or sold abroad) (j:akizuak/khia) (r:zd:19130/zd:17643) (q:draft)
akizuakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:place of sale/where it is sold) (d:<a> and <kizuakna> written as one word after the name of the goods: the place where they are sold, or their sale) (j:a/kizuakna) (r:zd:20472/ts:1202) (q:draft)
akizuih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be followed/be observed/be kept) (d:<a> and <kizuih> written as one word: that is followed or kept, of a rule or an agreement) (j:a/kizuih) (r:ts:11992) (q:draft, low confidence)
