akop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:combine/go together/pair) (d:<a> and <kop> written as one word: be joined or paired with something, have two things together; doubled, {akop akop in}, in pairs) (j:a/kop) (r:zd:19676/zd:24381/zd:18200) (q:draft)
akpul = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature/health) (w:fowl plague/poultry disease) (d:<ak>, chicken, and <pul>, plague: a deadly disease that spreads among chickens, and the chickens that die of it) (j:ak/pul) (r:zd:11829/zd:23754) (q:draft)
