akta = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (f:nature) (w:chicken/young chicken) (d:a fowl, known from proverbs such as {akta duhgawl kilawhkhuh}; the exact age or kind of fowl is not certain) (r:zd:10738) (q:draft, low confidence)
aktui = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:egg) (d:the egg of a hen) (s:tuii) (q:draft)
akua = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:whoever/everyone) (d:<a> and <kua> written as one word, used before <mahpeuh>, <mapeuh> or {ma ciat}: whoever it is, each and every one) (j:a/kua) (r:zd:17335/zd:21232) (q:draft)
