akuang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/nature) (w:burn/blaze/catch fire) (d:<a> and <kuang>, burn, written as one word: it burns or caught fire, that which burns; {mei akuang} is a fire broke out) (j:a/kuang) (r:zd:13161/zd:20122/zd:11606) (q:draft)
akuanggawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:burn fiercely/go up in flames/burst into flames) (d:<a>, <kuang>, burn, and <gawp> written as one word: it burned fiercely or was wholly consumed by fire, usually as {mei akuanggawp}) (j:a/kuang/gawp) (r:zd:17924/zd:20335) (q:draft)
akuankhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:set out/go out/leave) (d:<a> and <kuankhia> written as one word: he or she set out from home, for work or for some task) (j:a/kuankhia) (r:zd:15816/zd:12296) (q:draft)
akul = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be necessary/must/have to) (d:<a> and <kul> written as one word, placed after a verb: it is necessary to do it) (j:a/kul) (r:zd:21945/zd:23191/zd:17087) (q:draft)
akulna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:need/where needed) (d:<a> and <kulna> written as one word: the need for it, what is necessary; {akulna mun} is the place where it is needed) (j:a/kulna) (r:zd:24230/zd:24207) (q:draft)
akum = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time/family) (w:age/his age) (d:<a> and <kum> written as one word: his, her or its years, mostly the age of a person; {akum akum in} is year by year) (j:a/kum) (r:zd:14730/zd:12409) (q:draft)
akumpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:king/ruler/government) (d:<a> and <kumpi> written as one word: his or their king, ruler or government; before a noun, royal, as in {akumpi tokhom}, his throne) (j:a/kumpi) (r:zd:24469/zd:24120) (q:draft)
akumsuk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:descend/land/get off) (d:<a> and <kumsuk>, come down, written as one word: it comes down, said of an aeroplane landing and of people getting down from a vehicle) (j:a/kumsuk) (r:zd:11081/zd:17664) (q:draft)
akumtam = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:time/family) (w:old/of great age) (d:<akum> and <tam> written as one word: having many years, old; {akumtam penpen} is the oldest) (j:akum/tam) (r:zd:20150/zd:22097) (q:draft)
akuul = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be necessary/need) (d:<a> and <kuul> written as one word: that is necessary, what has to be done; {akuul hilo} is it is not a must) (j:a/kuul) (r:zd:22334/zd:13077) (q:draft)
alaam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:dance/be dancing) (d:<a> and <laam>, dance, written as one word: he dances, the one who dances) (j:a/laam) (r:zd:18069/zd:24207) (q:draft)
alaam = (i:2) (t:v) (f:nature) (w:float) (d:<a> and <laam>, float, written as one word: that floats on water) (j:a/laam) (r:zd:21025) (q:draft, low confidence)
Alabama = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel/media) (w:Alabama) (d:a state in the south-east of the United States of America) (r:zd:21978/zd:25336) (q:draft)
alading = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:take/collect/take on) (d:<a>, <la>, here take, and <ding>, will, written as one word: who will take it, in order to take or fetch; {mawhpuak alading} is to take on a responsibility) (j:a/la/ding) (r:zd:11378/zd:14931) (q:draft)
alahna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:showing/display/sign) (d:<a> and <lahna> written as one word: the showing of it, what shows something, or where something is shown; {alahna ahihi} is it is what shows that) (j:a/lahna) (r:zd:16205/zd:22614) (q:draft)
alahuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/health) (w:dangerous/alarming/fearful) (d:<a> and <lahuai>, a spelling of <lauhuai>, written as one word: that is dangerous or to be feared) (j:a/lahuai) (r:zd:23746/zd:25610) (q:draft)
alai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:his writing/his letter/his document) (d:<a> and <lai> written as one word: his or her writing, letter or paper) (j:a/lai) (r:zd:16254/zd:20434) (q:draft)
alai = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday/family) (w:the middle/the middle one) (d:<a> with <lai>, middle, written as one word: the middle of something, or the middle one of several, as the middle child) (r:zd:17448) (q:draft)
alaibu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:his book/her book) (d:<a> and <laibu> written as one word: his or her book) (j:a/laibu) (r:zd:24502) (q:draft)
alaigelh = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/media) (w:what he wrote/his writing/her note) (d:<a> and <laigelh> written as one word: what he or she wrote or writes, a note, letter or post) (j:a/laigelh) (r:zd:11391/zd:14686) (q:draft)
alaigui = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body/health) (w:its umbilical cord/umbilical cord) (d:<a> and <laigui>, umbilical cord, written as one word: the umbilical cord of the baby) (j:a/laigui) (r:zd:11924/zd:15048) (q:draft)
alaih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:replace/change/succeed) (d:<a> and <laih> written as one word: he replaced it, the one who takes the place of another, what is put in its place) (j:a/laih) (r:zd:24411/zd:15259/zd:10935) (q:draft)
alaihsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/home) (w:change/replace) (d:<a> and <laihsak> written as one word: he or she changes one thing for another, or the one who changes it) (j:a/laihsak) (r:zd:16137/zd:14928) (q:draft)
alaizang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/travel) (w:the middle/the centre) (d:<a> and <laizang> written as one word: the middle of it; {alaizang ah} is in the middle) (j:a/laizang) (r:zd:20513/zd:19414/zd:15579) (q:draft)
alak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:take/taken) (d:<a> and <lak> written as one word: he takes, the one who takes, or what is taken; {aana alak} is he took power) (j:a/lak) (r:zd:11034/zd:23156) (q:draft)
alakding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:to take/will take/to fetch) (d:<a> and <lakding> written as one word: that he, she or they are to take; {Action alakding} is to take action) (j:a/lakding) (r:zd:17188/zd:16490) (q:draft)
alakkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:show/express/display) (d:<a> and <lakkhia> written as one word: he shows, the one who shows or brings out into view) (j:a/lakkhia) (r:zd:24376/zd:17770) (q:draft)
alakkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:take out/remove) (d:<a> and <lakkhiat> written as one word: he or they take something out, or the taking out of it) (j:a/lakkhiat) (r:zd:13002/zd:17271) (q:draft)
alaksak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:took away/seized) (d:<a> and <laksak> written as one word: he took it away from someone, or what was taken away) (j:a/laksak) (r:zd:16998/zd:18067/zd:12628) (q:draft)
alal = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/social) (w:migrate/move away/migrant) (d:<a> and <lal>, migrate, written as one word: he moves to live elsewhere, and the one who has moved, a migrant) (j:a/lal) (r:zd:23767/zd:19453) (q:draft)
alamdang = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:strange/amazing/wonderful/unusual) (d:<a> and <lamdang> written as one word: what is strange or causes wonder) (j:a/lamdang) (r:zd:24014/zd:11831/zd:23977) (q:draft)
alamdangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:religion/everyday) (w:wonderfully/remarkably) (d:<a> and <lamdangin> written as one word: in a wonderful or surprising way; frequent in condolences, {Topa'n alamdangin hong hehnem ta hen}, may the Lord wonderfully comfort) (j:a/lamdangin) (r:zd:14826/zd:21550) (q:draft)
alamet = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:expect/hope for) (d:<a> and <lamet> written as one word: he or they expect, or what is expected; {alamet zahsangin} is more than expected) (j:a/lamet) (r:zd:13201/zd:19991) (q:draft)
alampi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/everyday) (w:the road/the way) (d:<a> and <lampi> written as one word: its road, or the way by which something can be done) (j:a/lampi) (r:zd:22550/zd:25909/zd:19476) (q:draft)
alang = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:side/one side) (d:one of the two sides of a place, a group or a matter, not half an amount; {alang khat ah} is on the other side or on the other hand, {alang alang ah} and {alangleh alang ah} are on both sides) (r:zd:25630/zd:12427/zd:22650) (q:draft)
alangkhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body/everyday) (w:one of a pair/one side) (d:<a> and <langkhat>, one side, written as one word: one of the two, of hands, legs and other things in pairs; {akhe alangkhat} is one of her legs) (j:a/langkhat) (r:zd:14694/zd:20193) (q:draft)
alangkhat = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:on the other hand/on the other side) (d:<a> and <langkhat> written as one word, with <ah> or <lamah>: on the other hand, seen from the other side, bringing in a second point of view) (j:a/langkhat) (r:zd:24950/zd:23215) (q:draft)
alanglam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/everyday) (w:other side/opposite side) (d:<a>, <lang> side and <lam> direction written as one word: the other side of a road, river or building, or the other party of two) (j:a/lang/lam) (r:zd:14865/zd:11234) (q:draft)
alangleh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/travel) (w:both sides/either side) (d:<a>, <lang>, side, and <leh>, and, written as one word; always in {alangleh alang}, the one side and the other, both sides of a road) (j:a/lang/leh) (r:zd:11685/zd:12427) (q:draft)
alangnih = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/body) (w:both/both sides) (d:<a> and <langnih> written as one word: both of a pair, as hands, feet or two parties; {alangnih in} is on both sides and {alangnih tuakin} is each of the two) (j:a/langnih) (r:zd:15505/zd:25567) (q:draft)
alangnihtuak = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/politics) (w:both sides/each of the two sides) (d:<alangnih>, both sides, and <tuak>, each, written as one word: the two parties, each of them) (j:alangnih/tuak) (r:zd:24950) (q:draft)
alangpan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:oppose/be against/opponent) (d:<a> and <langpan> written as one word: the one who opposes, those against; in a count of votes, against) (j:a/langpan) (r:zd:25625/zd:23597/zd:10687) (q:draft)
alangpang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:opponent/opposition) (d:<a> and <langpang> written as one word: the one who opposes it, the opposition; also as a verb, oppose it) (j:a/langpang) (r:zd:26252/zd:24749/zd:15174) (q:draft)
alangtuak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:both sides/each side/half each/in halves) (d:<alang> and <tuak> written as one word: each of the two halves or sides; with <in>, in two halves or half each, and with <panin>, from both sides) (j:alang/tuak) (r:zd:15305/zd:15002/zd:11308) (q:draft)
alangval = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:more than half/over half) (d:<alang>, half, and <val>, exceed, written as one word: more than half of a number or amount) (j:alang/val) (r:zd:21020/zd:15276) (q:draft)
alaplo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:miss/fail to make) (d:<a>, <lap> and <lo> written as one word: one who did not make it in time, who missed a deadline or a train) (j:a/lap/lo) (r:zd:19442/zd:19143) (q:draft)
Alarm = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/it) (w:alarm) (d:device that gives a warning sound, and the sound it gives; mostly in English compounds such as {Fire Alarm} and {Smoke Alarm}) (o:English) (r:zd:17301/zd:11897/zd:14954) (q:draft)
Alaska = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel/politics) (w:Alaska) (d:a state of the United States) (r:zd:24681/zd:25610) (q:draft)
alau = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:fear/be afraid) (d:<a> and <lau> written as one word: he fears, the one who is afraid; {alau man in} is because he was afraid, and {alau huai} is frightening) (j:a/lau) (r:zd:21739/zd:15080) (q:draft)
alauhuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:dangerous/frightening/dreadful) (d:<a> and <lauhuai> written as one word: that which is to be feared, dangerous or frightening; before a noun or as the statement itself) (j:a/lauhuai) (r:zd:25206/zd:22550/zd:15631) (q:draft)
alauthawng = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:be frightened/be alarmed) (d:<a> and <lauthawng> written as one word: they are frightened; with <sak>, frighten or alarm people) (j:a/lauthawng) (r:zd:16232/zd:19552) (q:draft)
alauthawngsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:frighten/terrorise/alarm) (d:<a> and <lauthawngsak> written as one word: he frightened, or the one who frightens the people named before it) (j:a/lauthawngsak) (r:zd:20013/zd:15398) (q:draft)
alawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:gain/reap/earn) (d:<a> and <lawh> written as one word, <lawh> here in the sense of getting something as the result of what one did: what someone gains or reaps) (j:a/lawh) (r:zd:19474) (q:draft, low confidence)
alawhcin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:succeed) (d:<a> and <lawhcin> written as one word: it succeeds, or its success; often before <nading>, so that it may succeed) (j:a/lawhcin) (r:zd:25322/zd:24673/zd:20912) (q:draft)
alawhcing = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:work/social) (w:successful) (d:<a> and <lawhcing> succeed written as one word: successful, the one who succeeds) (j:a/lawhcing) (r:zd:12110/zd:12166) (q:draft)
alawm = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:his friend/her friend) (d:<a> and <lawm> written as one word: his, her or their friend; {alawm te} is his friends) (j:a/lawm) (r:zd:15568/zd:16820) (q:draft)
alawm agual = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:his friends/her friends/friends and companions) (d:<alawm>, his friend, and <agual>, his peers, said as a pair: all the friends and companions of a person, the circle of friends; the form with {a-} of {lawm le gual}, often followed by <te> or <teng>) (r:zd:16376/zd:16257) (q:draft)
alawmdang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:his other friends/her other companions) (d:<alawm> and <dang> written as one word: his, her or their other friends, the rest of the companions, also the others of the same kind) (j:alawm/dang) (r:zd:12444/zd:11945) (q:draft)
alawmngaih = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:girlfriend/boyfriend/lover/sweetheart) (d:<a>, his or her, with <lawm>, friend, and <ngaih>, beloved, written as one word: his or her lover; glossed Girlfriend in the articles) (j:a/lawm/ngaih) (r:zd:15777) (q:draft)
alawmngaihnu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:his girlfriend/his sweetheart) (d:<a> and <lawmngaihnu> written as one word: his girlfriend, the woman he is courting) (j:a/lawmngaihnu) (r:zd:17491/zd:11545) (q:draft)
alawmnu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:his girlfriend/his fiancee/her female friend) (d:<a> and <lawmnu> written as one word: his girlfriend or fiancee, or the female friend of the person spoken of) (j:a/lawmnu) (r:zd:21070/zd:21518) (q:draft)
alawmpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:his friend/her boyfriend) (d:<a> and <lawmpa> written as one word: his or her male friend; in news reports often the boyfriend of a woman) (j:a/lawmpa) (r:zd:11384/zd:14931) (q:draft)
alawmte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:his friends/her friends/their friends) (d:<a>, his or her, and <lawmte>, friends, written as one word) (j:a/lawmte) (r:zd:23148/zd:9446/zd:12490) (q:draft)
alawn = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:throw) (d:<a> and <lawn>, throw, written as one word: he or they throw; before a noun, the one who threw) (j:a/lawn) (r:zd:17062/zd:14963) (q:draft)
alawp = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/religion) (w:eager/zealous/enthusiastic) (d:<a> and <lawp> written as one word: is eager, or the one who is eager; in church talk, the one who is zealous in faith) (j:a/lawp) (r:ts:1180/zd:19239) (q:draft)
