alehlam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:other side/opposite side/reverse/the contrary) (d:the side or direction opposite to the one meant: the back of a coin, the wrong side of a road, the opposite way of thinking) (r:ts:6531/zd:11319) (q:draft)
alei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:buy/bought) (d:<a> and <lei>, buy, written as one word: he or they buy, bought, the one who buys) (j:a/lei) (r:zd:15517/zd:25182/zd:12660) (q:draft)
aleiding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:to buy/buyer) (d:<a>, <lei>, buy, and <ding> written as one word: in order to buy; {aleiding te} is those who will buy, the buyers) (j:a/lei/ding) (r:zd:16749/zd:11974) (q:draft)
aleikha = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/everyday) (w:buyer/whoever has bought) (d:<a>, <lei>, buy, and <kha>, happen to, written as one word: one who has bought the thing, whoever happens to have bought it) (j:a/lei/kha) (r:zd:17538/zd:19550/zd:11915) (q:draft)
aleisawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:plan to buy/one who plans to buy) (d:<a> and <leisawm> written as one word: the one who intends to buy) (j:a/leisawm) (r:zd:19775) (q:draft)
aleitang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature/politics) (w:its land/its soil/its territory) (d:<a> and <leitang> written as one word: the land, soil or territory of the country spoken of) (j:a/leitang) (r:zd:15905/zd:11548) (q:draft)
alel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:lose/be defeated/loser) (d:<a> and <lel> written as one word: he or it loses, or the one who loses; {azo alel} is winning and losing, the winner and the loser) (j:a/lel) (r:zd:21251/zd:17963/zd:24544) (q:draft)
alem = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:be suitable/be convenient/be agreeable) (d:<a> and <lem> written as one word, with <lem> in the sense fit, be in agreement: it suits, it is convenient or acceptable; {alem thei} is those who can manage it) (j:a/lem) (r:zd:20814/zd:17295/zd:16148) (q:draft)
alempen = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:most suitable/most convenient) (d:<alem>, be suitable or convenient, with the superlative <pen>, written as one word: the most suitable, the most convenient) (j:alem/pen) (r:zd:15043/zd:15996) (q:draft)
alen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:hold/grasp) (d:<a> and <len>, hold, written as one word: the one who holds or takes hold; of a doctor, the one who holds a field, a specialist) (j:a/len) (r:zd:19428/zd:19798) (q:draft)
alen = (i:2) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:fly) (d:<a> with <len>, a form of <leng>, fly, written as one word: said of an aircraft that is in flight) (r:zd:12893/zd:12128) (q:draft)
alending = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:flight/departure by air) (d:<a>, <len> and <ding> written as one word, <len> here being the form of <leng> in its sense fly: the flying that is to take place, a planned flight) (j:a/len/ding) (r:zd:12494/zd:12000/zd:15669) (q:draft)
alending = (i:2) (t:v) (f:work) (w:who will take over) (d:<a>, <len>, hold, and <ding> written as one word: the one who is to take or hold a post; seen in one sentence only) (j:a/len/ding) (r:zd:15025) (q:draft, low confidence)
aleng = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:fly/flying) (d:<a> and <leeng>, fly, written as one word: it flies, the one that flies; before a noun, flying, as in {aleng vanleng}, the plane that was flying) (j:a/leeng) (r:zd:19100/zd:19025/zd:12873) (q:draft)
alengding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:due to fly/will fly/to fly) (d:<a>, the verb fly, <leeng>, here written with one e, and <ding> for what is to come, written as one word: that is to fly, or those who are going to fly) (j:a/leeng/ding) (r:zd:13030/zd:22376) (q:draft)
alengkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:took off/flew out) (d:<a> and <lengkhia> written as one word, here in the sense of <leengkhia>, fly out: it took off, or the one that took off, said of an aircraft; also said of a person who jumped from a height) (j:a/lengkhia) (r:zd:12831/zd:15403) (q:draft)
alengkhiading = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:be about to take off/be about to fly out) (d:<a>, <lengkhia> and <ding> written as one word, with <lengkhia> in the sense fly out: about to take off or to fly away, said of an aircraft and of those who travel in it) (j:a/lengkhia/ding) (r:zd:19807/zd:14748/zd:12494) (q:draft)
alengkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:take off/fly off/depart by air) (d:<aleng> and <khiat.1> written as one word: of an aircraft or its passengers, fly off, leave by air; {alengkhiat madeuh in} is just before it took off) (j:aleng/khiat) (r:zd:19860/zd:12309) (q:draft)
alengkhiatzawh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:travel) (w:after takeoff/after taking off) (d:<a> with <leeng>, <khiat> and <zawh>, here after, written as one word: after it took off, said of an aircraft; mostly followed by {asawtlo in}, not long) (j:a/leeng/khiat/zawh) (r:zd:19271/zd:19860) (q:draft)
alenkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:take off/fly out/fly away) (d:<a> joined to {lenkhiat}, the form of <leengkhia>, fly out, used before words such as <khit> and <kul>: its taking off, of an aircraft or of a person leaving by air) (r:zd:12936/zd:19095) (q:draft)
alenkhiatsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:try to jump off/be about to fly out) (d:{a lengkhiat sawm} written as one word, the form of <alengkhia> used before <sawm>, intend or be about to: he tried to jump down from a height, or he was about to leave by plane) (r:zd:14589/zd:15296) (q:draft)
alenkhiatzawh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:travel) (w:after takeoff) (d:{a lenkhiat zawh} written as one word: after it took off, said of an aircraft; mostly followed by {asawtlo in}, not long after) (r:zd:11376/zd:21366) (q:draft)
alenlaitak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:travel) (w:while flying/in flight) (d:<a>, <leen>, fly, here spelled with one e, and <laitak>, while, written as one word: while it was flying, of an aircraft in the air) (j:a/leen/laitak) (r:zd:17421/zd:19054/zd:17846) (q:draft)
Aleppo = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:politics) (w:Aleppo) (d:city and province in the north of Syria) (r:zd:10702/zd:11233) (q:draft)
alet = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:hold/keep hold of) (d:<a> and <let> written as one word: holding in the hand, or holding a post or power) (j:a/let) (r:zd:23773/zd:24714/zd:12741) (q:draft)
alet = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:muddled/confused/topsy-turvy) (d:in the pair {alum alet}, lying and turned over: mixed up, in disorder, said of talk, writing or thinking) (r:zd:16157/zd:16801) (q:draft)
alet = (i:3) (t:v) (f:education/media) (w:translate) (d:<a> with <let> in the sense of translate: translated, the one that was translated into another language) (r:zd:17478) (q:draft, low confidence)
Algeria = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:politics/travel) (w:Algeria) (d:a country in North Africa) (r:zd:19182/zd:13127) (q:draft)
aliam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/media) (w:the injured/the wounded/injured person) (d:<a> and <liam> written as one word: the one who is injured, the injured; in news reports <asi aliam> is the dead and the injured, casualties) (j:a/liam) (r:zd:10931/zd:13094/zd:11466) (q:draft)
aliam abai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/media) (w:the injured/anyone hurt/casualties) (d:<aliam>, the wounded, paired with <abai>, the maimed: anyone hurt in an accident or attack; in news reports mostly with <omlo> or {kuamah omlo}, nobody was injured) (r:zd:25027/zd:20013) (q:draft)
aliamgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health) (w:be badly injured/be severely wounded) (d:<a> and <liamgawp> written as one word: is badly injured, or the one who is badly injured) (j:a/liamgawp) (r:zd:15069/zd:11773) (q:draft)
aliamgawplua = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health) (w:be very badly injured/be critically injured) (d:<aliamgawp> and <lua> written as one word: the one who is very badly injured; in the articles mostly with a negative, nobody is very badly injured) (j:aliamgawp/lua) (r:zd:17952/zd:11982) (q:draft)
aliamlawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/media) (w:be injured/get hurt) (d:<a> and <liamlawh> written as one word: he, she or they got hurt as a result of something, or the ones who got hurt) (j:a/liamlawh) (r:zd:17558/zd:11327) (q:draft)
aliamma = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/body) (w:his injury/his wound) (d:<a> and <liamma> written as one word: his or her wound, the injuries of the person spoken of) (j:a/liamma) (r:zd:15698/zd:12900/zd:19810) (q:draft)
aliamna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/body) (w:injury/wound) (d:<a> and <liamna> written as one word: his, her or its injury, the wound received) (j:a/liamna) (r:zd:22977/zd:11994) (q:draft)
aliampa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/media) (w:the injured man/injured man) (d:<aliam> and <pa> written as one word: the man who was injured) (j:aliam/pa) (r:zd:15669/zd:12748) (q:draft)
aliampen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:health/media) (w:the injured/those injured) (d:<a>, <liam> and <pen> written as one word: the injured, as for those who were hurt, used when their number is given) (j:a/liam/pen) (r:zd:11856/zd:17836/zd:19303) (q:draft)
aliamte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:the wounded/the injured) (d:<a> and <liamte> written as one word: those who are injured) (j:a/liamte) (r:zd:21676/zd:17472/zd:22688) (q:draft)
aliamzong = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:health/media) (w:the injured also) (d:<a> <liam>, those who are injured, and <zong>, also, written as one word: the injured as well, named after the dead in reports of accidents) (j:a/liam/zong) (r:zd:17794/zd:17461/zd:11562) (q:draft)
aliang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:shoulder) (d:<a>, his or her, and <liang>, shoulder, written as one word: his or her shoulder) (j:a/liang) (r:zd:15260/zd:21411/zd:19868) (q:draft)
alianpenpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/work) (w:chief/head/director) (d:<a> and <lianpenpa> written as one word: the man of highest rank in an office or force) (j:a/lianpenpa) (r:zd:19674/zd:14618) (q:draft)
alianzaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:larger/greater/bigger one) (d:<a> and <lianzaw>, larger, written as one word: the larger or greater one; what it is compared with takes <sangin>, than) (j:a/lianzaw) (r:zd:23767/zd:22557) (q:draft)
aliat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be great/be big) (d:<a> and <liat> written as one word: that it is great, its being great, before words such as <leh>, <manin> and <theihna>) (j:a/liat) (r:zd:17955/zd:15553) (q:draft)
alignment = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/work) (w:alignment/road alignment/route) (d:the line surveyed for a road to follow, in accounts of how the roads of the Chin Hills were built) (o:English) (r:zd:22586/zd:23252) (q:draft)
alimlim = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:in any case/in general/at any rate) (d:<a> with <limlim>, at all, written as one word; {alimlim in} opens a sentence that states what holds in every case: in any case, as a rule) (r:zd:16249/zd:20440) (q:draft, low confidence)
alimzat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:use much/favour/be popular) (d:<a> with <limzat>, use much and gladly, written as one word: that people use a great deal, much used, popular) (j:a/limzat) (r:zd:11164/zd:16809) (q:draft)
alimzonsan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:hunt hard for/search intensively for) (d:<a>, <lim> in the sense thoroughly, and <zonsan> written as one word: of the police or authorities, be searching hard for a person in order to arrest him) (j:a/lim/zonsan) (r:zd:19247/zd:20472) (q:draft)
alin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:nature) (w:shake/quake) (d:<a> and <lin> written as one word, said of an earthquake: {zin alin ciangin} is when the earth quaked) (j:a/lin) (r:zd:20655/zd:17202) (q:draft)
alina = (i:1) (t:num) (f:everyday) (w:fourth/the fourth) (d:<a> and <lina> written as one word: the fourth; {alina ah} is fourthly) (j:a/lina) (r:zd:19449/zd:23821) (q:draft)
aling = (i:1) (t:v) (f:nature) (w:it shook/it quaked) (d:<a> with <ling> used as a verb, shake, as in <zinling>, written as one word and said of an earthquake: it shook, it struck) (j:a/ling) (r:zd:11610/zd:11738/zd:16490) (q:draft)
aling = (i:2) (t:n) (f:nature) (w:its thorns) (d:<a> and <ling>, thorn, written as one word: its thorn or thorns) (j:a/ling) (r:zd:15767) (q:draft, low confidence)
alipkhap = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/media) (w:dreadful/horrifying) (d:<a> and <lipkhap>, be horrified, written as one word, always followed by <huai>: {alipkhap huai} is dreadful, horrifying) (s:lipkhaphuai) (j:a/lipkhap) (r:zd:15651/zd:17472) (q:draft)
Allah = (i:1) (t:name) (f:religion) (w:Allah) (d:the name of God in Islam, often as {Allah pasian}) (o:Arabic) (r:zd:23022/zd:25115) (q:draft)
alolzaw = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:earlier/ahead of time) (d:before the set time, said of a train that leaves earlier than its timetable; it follows the amount of time or <sangin>, than, and ends in <zaw>, more) (r:zd:16229/zd:19712) (q:draft, low confidence)
alom = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:in great numbers/in bulk/in heaps) (d:<a> and <lom>, heap, written as one word; nearly always in the pair {alom atang in}, in heaps and masses: in great numbers, in large amounts, all at once) (j:a/lom) (r:zd:25397/zd:23641/zd:16404) (q:draft)
alomlom = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:in groups/in masses/in large numbers) (d:<lom> a lump or batch, doubled, with <a>; mostly with <in>: in batches, in crowds, many together) (b:lom) (r:zd:25532/zd:19242/zd:12752) (q:draft)
alotkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:throw out/launch/release) (d:<a> and <lotkhiat> written as one word: he or they threw out, said of things thrown from a building, of a missile fired, and of a video put out on social media) (j:a/lotkhiat) (r:zd:15253/zd:11801/zd:15051) (q:draft)
alphabet = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:alphabet) (d:the set of letters with which a language is written; {Roman alphabet} is the Latin script in which Zolai is written) (o:English) (r:zd:23770/zd:24377/zd:24058) (q:draft)
alto = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/religion) (w:alto) (d:the alto part in singing in parts, beside tenor and bass) (o:English) (r:zd:25572) (q:draft)
alu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:his head/her head/head) (d:<a> and <lu> written as one word: the head of the person or animal spoken of) (j:a/lu) (r:zd:20164/zd:21723) (q:draft)
aluah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:inherit/occupy/take possession of) (d:<a> and <luah> written as one word: he inherits or takes over, the one who takes possession) (j:a/luah) (r:zd:16856/zd:21042) (q:draft)
aluan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:nature) (w:flow) (d:<a> and <luan> written as one word: that flows, where it flows) (j:a/luan) (r:zd:12765) (q:draft)
aluang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/nature) (w:flow/run) (d:<a> and <luang>, flow, written as one word, of tears, blood or a river: it flows, or the one that flows) (j:a/luang) (r:zd:17448) (q:draft)
aluang = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:body/corpse/remains) (d:<a>, his or her, written as one word with a noun for the body: the body of a person who has died; compare <luanghawm>) (r:zd:19733/zd:11398) (q:draft)
aluanghawm = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/media) (w:his body/her body/corpse) (d:<a> and <luanghawm> written as one word: the dead body of the person spoken of) (j:a/luanghawm) (r:zd:12039/zd:10842) (q:draft)
aluangkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/nature) (w:flow out/leak out/what flows out) (d:<a> and <luangkhia>, flow out, written as one word: it flows out, or the liquid that has flowed out) (j:a/luangkhia) (r:zd:16876/zd:19383) (q:draft)
alubek = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:body) (w:only his head/just the head) (d:<alu> and <bek> written as one word: only his or her head, the head alone) (j:alu/bek) (r:zd:14935/zd:17856) (q:draft)
aluguh = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:his skull/her skull/the skull) (d:<a>, his, her or its, and <luguh>, skull, written as one word) (j:a/luguh) (r:zd:20508) (q:draft)
aluite = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:old ones/older ones) (d:<alui>, the old one, and the plural <te> written as one word: the old or older ones, as older models of a thing) (j:alui/te) (r:zd:11506/zd:16735) (q:draft)
alukham = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:his pillow/her pillow) (d:<a> and <lukham> written as one word: his or her pillow, what the head rests on) (j:a/lukham) (r:zd:12591/zd:26097) (q:draft)
alukun = (i:1) (t:v) (f:body/social) (w:bow his head/with bowed head) (d:<a> and <lukun> written as one word: he bows his head, or the one whose head is bowed) (j:a/lukun) (r:zd:16832/zd:21659) (q:draft)
alum = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/home) (w:lie/lie down/sleep) (d:<a> and <lum> written as one word: he lies or sleeps, or the one lying; in the pair {alum alet}, turned over, upside down; the same spelling is also {a lum}, warm) (j:a/lum) (r:zd:12901/zd:17271) (q:draft)
aluminium = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:aluminium) (d:the light metal aluminium; the English word is used unchanged) (o:English) (r:ts:11162) (q:draft, low confidence)
alumkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:who sleeps with/sleep with) (d:<a> and <lumkhawm>, lie down together, written as one word: the one who lies with someone, said of sexual relations; the partner is marked by <tawh>) (j:a/lumkhawm) (r:zd:11732/zd:14613) (q:draft)
alumna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature/everyday) (w:temperature/warmth/heat) (d:<a> and <lumna> written as one word: its warmth, how warm something is) (j:a/lumna) (r:zd:22557/zd:15422) (q:draft)
alung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:his heart/his mind/her heart) (d:<a> and <lung> written as one word: his, her or their heart or mind, in expressions of feeling such as {alung dam}, he is glad, {alung kim}, he is satisfied, and {alung kia}, he loses heart) (j:a/lung) (r:zd:19525/zd:11953/zd:23639) (q:draft)
alungdam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be glad/be happy) (d:<a> and <lungdam> written as one word: he or she is glad, the one who is glad; {alungdam huai} is a thing to be glad about) (j:a/lungdam) (r:zd:25616/zd:25925/zd:24117) (q:draft)
alungdamhuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:gladdening/pleasing/joyful) (d:<a> and <lungdamhuai> written as one word: that which gives joy, a thing to be glad about) (j:a/lungdamhuai) (r:zd:11587/zd:23135) (q:draft)
alungdamna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:his joy/his thanks/gratitude) (d:<a> and <lungdamna> written as one word: his or her joy, and often his or her thanks; {alungdamna uh} is their thanks) (j:a/lungdamna) (r:zd:24123/zd:24566) (q:draft)
alunggulh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:desire/long for/wish for) (d:<a> and <lunggulh> written as one word: he or she longs for, and what someone longs for, a wish) (j:a/lunggulh) (r:zd:8668/zd:24327/zd:11204) (q:draft)
alunghimawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:worry/be anxious/fear) (d:<a> and <lunghimawh> written as one word: he, she or they worry, or the one who is worried) (j:a/lunghimawh) (r:zd:22334/zd:13258) (q:draft)
alungkham = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be worried/be distressed) (d:<a> and <lungkham> written as one word: he or she is worried, the one who is distressed) (j:a/lungkham) (r:zd:17465/zd:15199) (q:draft)
alungkia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be discouraged/lose heart) (d:<a> and <lungkia> written as one word: he loses heart, the one who is discouraged) (j:a/lungkia) (r:zd:19733/zd:19262) (q:draft)
alungkim = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:be satisfied/be pleased/be content) (d:<a> and <lungkim> written as one word: he or she is satisfied, or the one who is satisfied) (j:a/lungkim) (r:zd:21815/zd:15422/zd:22159) (q:draft)
alungkimlo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:social/politics) (w:dissatisfied/displeased/discontented) (d:<a> and <lungkimlo> written as one word: being unhappy about a matter, or those who are unhappy about it) (j:a/lungkimlo) (r:zd:19213/zd:15602) (q:draft)
alungleng = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/family) (w:miss/long for/be lonesome) (d:<a> and <lungleng> written as one word: the one who misses and longs for someone; in condolences {adah akap alungleng khuangai} is those who mourn, weep and long for the one who died) (j:a/lungleng) (r:zd:12371/zd:25645) (q:draft)
alungleng khuangai = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:social) (w:grieving and missing/bereaved) (d:<alungleng>, who long for, and <khuangai>, feel lonely and miss: a pair of words used in messages of condolence for those who mourn and miss the dead, placed before <tanau meltheih>, relatives and acquaintances) (r:zd:25645) (q:draft)
alunglut = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/social) (w:interested/keen) (d:<a> and <lunglut> written as one word: one who is interested, those who take an interest; {alunglut lo} is uninterested) (j:a/lunglut) (r:zd:14941/zd:12336) (q:draft)
alungnop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be glad/be pleased/be happy) (d:<a> and <lungnop> written as one word: he is glad, his being pleased; {alungnop huai} is delightful) (j:a/lungnop) (r:zd:16398/zd:16360) (q:draft)
alungnuam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be glad/be happy/be at ease) (d:<a> and <lungnuam> written as one word: he or she is glad, happy at heart or at ease) (j:a/lungnuam) (r:zd:26097/zd:19571/zd:21667) (q:draft)
alungsim = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/body) (w:his mind/his heart/their mind) (d:<a> and <lungsim> written as one word: his, her or its mind or heart; with <uh> after it, their mind) (j:a/lungsim) (r:zd:24574/zd:22557/zd:13328) (q:draft)
alungtang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body/health) (w:heart) (d:<a> and <lungtang> written as one word: his or her heart) (j:a/lungtang) (r:zd:12208/zd:25150) (q:draft)
alup = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:lie/sleep/be in bed) (d:<a> and <lup> written as one word: he or she lies or sleeps; {alup laitak} is while he was asleep, and {zato ah alup} is lie in hospital) (j:a/lup) (r:zd:19871/zd:24422) (q:draft)
alupen = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:his head/her head) (d:<alu> and the topic marker <pen> written as one word: as for his or her head) (j:alu/pen) (r:zd:16362/zd:13117) (q:draft)
alupna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:his bed/her bed) (d:<a> and <lupna> written as one word: his or her bed, the place where he or she sleeps) (j:a/lupna) (r:zd:26097/zd:17271/zd:19266) (q:draft)
alut = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:enter/go in/come in) (d:<a> and <lut> written as one word: he, she or it entered, or the one that enters; also join, as in {palik alut}, joined the police) (j:a/lut) (r:zd:15274/zd:17147/zd:12302) (q:draft)
alutang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:his head/her head) (d:<a> and <lutang>, head, written as one word: his or her head) (j:a/lutang) (r:zd:11345/zd:12359) (q:draft)
alutding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:enter/go in) (d:<a>, <lut> and <ding> written as one word: that will enter, or the act of going in that is to happen) (j:a/lut/ding) (r:zd:11835/zd:14904) (q:draft)
alutkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:get into/happen to enter) (d:<a> and <lutkha> written as one word: it got in or he happened to enter, without this being intended; {nasep alutkha} is one who happened to join the work) (j:a/lutkha) (r:zd:17834/zd:21022) (q:draft)
alutkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:after entering/have entered) (d:<a> and <lutkhit> written as one word: after he or she went in, mostly before <ciangin> or <phetin>) (j:a/lutkhit) (r:zd:17930/zd:12866) (q:draft)
alutkik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:go back in/re-enter/enter again) (d:<a> and <lutkik> written as one word: he, she or they go in again, or the ones who enter again) (j:a/lutkik) (r:zd:12565/zd:20012) (q:draft)
alutlaitak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/travel) (w:while entering) (d:<a>, <lut> and <laitak> written as one word: at the very time when he or they were going in) (j:a/lut/laitak) (r:zd:15021/zd:17919) (q:draft)
alutleh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:when enter/on going in) (d:<a>, <lut>, enter, and <leh>, when or if, written as one word: when or as he went in, and also if someone goes in) (j:a/lut/leh) (r:zd:12261/zd:17232) (q:draft)
alutma = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/travel) (w:before entering/before going in) (d:<a>, <lut> and <ma> written as one word, followed by <in>: before he, she or it enters a place) (j:a/lut/ma) (r:zd:13067/zd:17143/zd:19824) (q:draft)
alutman = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/travel) (w:entrance fee/admission) (d:<a> and <lutman> written as one word: its entrance fee, the fee for those who enter) (j:a/lutman) (r:zd:16381) (q:draft)
alutna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/home) (w:entrance/way in/entry) (d:<a> and <lutna> written as one word: its entrance, or his entering or joining) (j:a/lutna) (r:zd:21042/zd:16966) (q:draft)
alutnuam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:want to enter/want to join) (d:<a> and <lutnuam> written as one word: he wants to enter or join, or the one who wants to) (j:a/lutnuam) (r:zd:16452/zd:25243) (q:draft)
alutphei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:went in/entered/who crossed into) (d:<a> and <lutphei> written as one word: went over and into a place, and the one who did so) (j:a/lutphei) (r:zd:17501/zd:14979) (q:draft)
alutpih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/family) (w:bring in/take in) (d:<a> and <lutpih> written as one word: whom he or she brings in, the one brought in) (j:a/lutpih) (r:zd:11587) (q:draft, low confidence)
alutsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:social) (w:already joined/already entered) (d:<a>, <lut> enter and <sa>, already, written as one word: one who has already entered or joined) (j:a/lut/sa) (r:zd:22880/zd:25154) (q:draft)
alutsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:put in/let in/pay in) (d:<a> and <lutsak> written as one word: he or she puts or lets something in, of money paid into an account, a ball into the goal, a person into a land) (j:a/lutsak) (r:zd:20676/zd:16897) (q:draft)
alutsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/politics) (w:try to enter/attempt to enter) (d:<a> with <lut>, enter, and <sawm>, intend, written as one word: the one who tried to get into a place) (j:a/lut/sawm) (r:zd:11762/zd:11805) (q:draft)
alutsuk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:go in/enter/go down into) (d:<a> and <lutsuk> written as one word: he, she or it went into a place, or the one going in) (j:a/lutsuk) (r:zd:12565/zd:12858) (q:draft)
alutte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/everyday) (w:those who enter/those who entered) (d:<a> and <lutte> written as one word: the people who go or went into a place) (j:a/lutte) (r:zd:16423/zd:11762) (q:draft)
alutthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:can enter/be able to get in) (d:<a> and <lutthei> written as one word: he, she or it is able to enter, or what is able to get in) (j:a/lutthei) (r:zd:20416/zd:11637) (q:draft)
aluttheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:be able to enter/get in) (d:<a> and <luttheih> written as one word: he or they can enter; {aluttheih nadingin} is so that they may enter) (j:a/luttheih) (r:zd:11285/zd:11303/zd:25601) (q:draft)
aluttheihloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:be unable to enter/cannot get in) (d:<aluttheih> and <loh> written as one word: that he or they cannot enter; {aluttheihloh nadingin} is so that no one can enter) (j:aluttheih/loh) (r:zd:12212/zd:16637/zd:16733) (q:draft)
alutung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:his head/her head/top of the head) (d:<a> and <lutung> written as one word: the top of the head of the one spoken of; {alutung ah} is on his or her head) (j:a/lutung) (r:zd:12487) (q:draft)
aluu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:potato) (o:Burmese, alu) (r:zd:21243/zd:24276) (q:draft)
aluvun = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:scalp) (d:<alu>, his or her head, and <vun>, skin, written as one word: the skin of the head, the scalp) (j:alu/vun) (r:zd:11780/zd:11172) (q:draft)
aluzang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:top of his head/crown of the head) (d:<a> and <luzang> written as one word: the top of his or her head) (j:a/luzang) (r:zd:25150/zd:19428) (q:draft)
am = (i:2) (t:n) (f:time) (w:a.m./in the morning) (d:the English abbreviation written after a clock time for the hours before noon, often together with <zingsang>; not the glowing coal) (o:English, a.m.) (r:zd:24610/zd:10892) (q:draft)
ama genna = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:media) (w:according to him/in his words/by her account) (d:<ama>, his or her, and <genna>, statement: followed by <ah> it opens a sentence that reports what a person has said, and that sentence often closes with <cihi> or {ci'n genkhia hi}) (r:zd:15103/zd:19671) (q:draft)
amaa = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (j:ama) (r:zd:23479/zd:22584) (q:draft, low confidence)
amaban = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/work) (w:what comes next/the rest/future) (d:<a> and <maban> written as one word: what lies ahead of someone or of a work begun; {amaban sem} is go on with the work, and of a person it is his future) (j:a/maban) (r:zd:18119/zd:25601/zd:12508) (q:draft)
amah = (i:2) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:he/she) (d:third person singular pronoun used of a person, man or woman) (r:zai:he) (q:draft)
amahbek = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:only he/only she/he alone/by himself) (d:<amah>, he or she, and <bek>, only, written as one word: that person and no one else, or that person alone without help) (j:amah/bek) (r:zd:15188/zd:21174/zd:11504) (q:draft)
amahguak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:alone/by himself/by herself) (d:<amah> and <guak> written as one word: he or she alone, by himself or herself, with no one else) (j:amah/guak) (r:zd:15199/zd:16786/zd:15264) (q:draft)
amahleh = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:himself/herself/he and) (d:<amah>, he or she, and <leh>, and, written as one word: <amahleh amah>, he and he, is himself or herself, by himself, said of what a person does to or by himself; before another noun it is he and) (j:amah/leh) (r:zd:20743/zd:16598/zd:11995) (q:draft)
amahleh amah = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:himself/herself/by himself/by herself) (d:<amahleh>, he and, with <amah>, he or she: the reflexive of the third person, said of what a person does to himself or does alone; the verb after it often carries the reflexive prefix <ki>) (r:zd:20743/zd:16598) (q:draft)
amahngiat = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:he himself/she herself/in person) (d:<amah>, he or she, and <ngiat>, indeed, written as one word: that very person and no other) (j:amah/ngiat) (r:zd:12785/zd:12215) (q:draft)
amahpen = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:he/she) (d:<amah> with the topic marker <pen>, written as one word: he or she, as the one spoken about) (j:amah/pen) (r:zd:19414/zd:15966/zd:18119) (q:draft)
amahtawh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:with him/with her) (d:<amah>, he or she, and <tawh>, with, written as one word: together with him or her, or in relation to him or her) (j:amah/tawh) (r:zd:11545/zd:10767) (q:draft)
amahzong = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:he too/she too/he also) (d:<amah>, he or she, and <zong>, also, written as one word) (j:amah/zong) (r:zd:17558/zd:11932) (q:draft)
amaibuk = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:front seat/front of a vehicle/cab) (d:<a> with {maibuk}, from <mai>, front: the front part of a vehicle where the driver and the front passenger sit) (r:zd:14689/zd:11048) (q:draft)
amailam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/travel) (w:front/front part) (d:<a> and <mailam.2> written as one word: its front, the front side of a vehicle or a thing) (j:a/mailam) (r:zd:16873/zd:18005/zd:15429) (q:draft)
amailian = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/travel) (w:right in front/directly before) (d:<amai> and <lian> written as one word, with <lian> in the sense exactly: the place right in front of a person or thing, most often {amailian ah}, right in front of) (j:amai/lian) (r:zd:15008/zd:20446/zd:14528) (q:draft)
amaipan = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/travel) (w:from the front/in front) (d:<amai> and <pan> written as one word: from in front of him, her or it; set against <anungpan>, from behind) (a:anungpan) (j:amai/pan) (r:zd:15467/zd:17727) (q:draft)
amaitai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/social) (w:cheerful/smiling/bright-faced) (d:<a> and <maitai> written as one word: cheerful, or the cheerful one, a person with a bright face) (j:a/maitai) (r:zd:25068/zd:16308/zd:11619) (q:draft)
amaitang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:his face/her face) (d:<a>, his or her, and <maitang>, face, written as one word) (j:a/maitang) (r:zd:17661/zd:24062) (q:draft)
amaiteng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:his whole face/her whole face) (d:<amai>, his or her face, with <teng>, here all of: the whole of the face) (r:zd:17147/zd:12754) (q:draft)
amakai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:leader) (d:<a> and <makai> written as one word: the leader, their leader, the one who leads) (j:a/makai) (r:zd:11275/zd:23038) (q:draft)
amakaih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:lead/guide) (d:<a> and <makaih>, lead, written as one word: he leads, the one who leads, and what he has led) (j:a/makaih) (r:zd:13268/zd:21042) (q:draft)
amakaihding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/politics) (w:will lead/be to lead) (d:<a>, <makaih> and <ding> written as one word: the one who is to lead, or in order to lead) (j:a/makaih/ding) (r:zd:14795/zd:17593) (q:draft)
amakaipi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:ringleader/chief leader/mastermind) (d:<a> and <makaipi> written as one word: the chief leader of it, in news mostly the leader of a gang, an attack or a plot) (j:a/makaipi) (r:zd:11568/zd:12159) (q:draft)
amakaite = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:leaders/their leaders) (d:<a> and <makaite> written as one word: the leaders, its or their leaders) (j:a/makaite) (r:zd:22981/zd:22228) (q:draft)
amakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:his son-in-law/her son-in-law) (d:<a> and <makpa> written as one word: his or her son-in-law) (j:a/makpa) (r:zd:16294/zd:12132) (q:draft)
amalkim = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:education/media) (w:in full/spelled out) (d:<a>, <mal>, letter or unit, and <kim>, complete, written as one word: with all its letters, said of the full form of an abbreviation) (j:a/mal/kim) (r:zd:12959/zd:14756) (q:draft)
aman = (i:3) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:he/she) (d:<amah>, he or she, run together with the subject marker <in>: he or she as the one who does the action, at the start of a clause; not {a man}, true) (s:amahin) (r:zd:25194/zd:17060/zd:24673) (q:draft)
amanawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:head for/go toward) (d:<a> and <manawh> written as one word: it heads for or moves toward, mostly after <lam>, direction) (j:a/manawh) (r:zd:16262/zd:15011) (q:draft)
amancip = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media) (w:disappear/go missing) (d:<a> with <mangcip>, vanish completely, written as one word and without the g: it disappeared, he went missing; in one article the same spelling seems to be <a> with <mancip>, seize) (j:a/mangcip) (r:zd:11664/zd:13032) (q:draft, low confidence)
amancipzawh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:media/time) (w:after going missing/since disappearing) (d:<amancip>, he or it went missing, and <zawh>, here after, written as one word: after the disappearance, followed by the length of time that has passed) (j:amancip/zawh) (r:zd:22298/zd:11664) (q:draft)
amanding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:to arrest/to catch) (d:<a>, <man> and <ding> written as one word, usually followed by <in>: in order to arrest or catch someone) (j:a/man/ding) (r:zd:14859/zd:11484) (q:draft)
amang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:obey) (d:<a> and <mang>, obey, written as one word: he obeys, the one who obeys) (j:a/mang) (r:zd:17488/zd:24453) (q:draft)
amang = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be lost/disappear) (d:<a> with <mang>, be lost or vanish, written as one word; {amang sak} is to lose a thing) (j:a/mang) (r:zd:20577) (q:draft, low confidence)
amangcip = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:media/everyday) (w:missing/disappeared/lost) (d:<a> with <mangcip>, go missing, from <mang>, disappear, and <cip>, completely, written as one word: one that has gone missing and is not found) (r:zd:12349/zd:16858) (q:draft)
amangciplai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:media/everyday) (w:still missing) (d:<amangcip>, missing, with <lai>, still, written as one word: those who are still missing) (j:amangcip/lai) (r:zd:12936/zd:20401) (q:draft)
amangte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/religion) (w:those who obey/the obedient) (d:<amang>, obey, with the plural <te>: the ones who obey, after <thu> or <sawlna>, a word or command) (j:amang/te) (r:zd:24167/zd:16488) (q:draft)
amangte = (i:2) (t:n) (f:media) (w:the missing/missing people) (d:{a mang}, the one who is lost, with the plural <te>, written as one word: those who are missing, in {asi amangte}, the dead and the missing) (j:a/mang/te) (r:zd:20023) (q:draft, low confidence)
amangthang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be lost/disappear/perish) (d:<a> and <mangthang> written as one word: that is lost, that has disappeared or perished; {amangthang lohna ding} is so that it is not lost) (j:a/mangthang) (r:zd:19662/zd:13181/zd:25433) (q:draft)
amangthangcip = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:disappear/go missing/vanish completely) (d:<a>, <mangthang>, disappear, and <cip>, completely, written as one word: it or he disappeared for good, went missing) (j:a/mangthang/cip) (r:zd:11588/zd:14583) (q:draft)
amankhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:arrest/seize/catch) (d:<a> and <mankhia> written as one word: arrested or seized, said of the police taking persons or finding things) (j:a/mankhia) (r:zd:13282/zd:11331/zd:19439) (q:draft)
amankhin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:who has finished/have completed) (d:<a> and <mankhin> written as one word: the one who has finished or completed something) (j:a/mankhin) (r:zd:17304/zd:12280) (q:draft)
amankhit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:finish/be over) (d:<a> and <mankhit> written as one word: it has finished; {amankhit ciangin} is after it was over, after finishing) (j:a/mankhit) (r:zd:14699/zd:16257/zd:11259) (q:draft)
amanlang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:quickly/fast/soon) (d:<a> and <manlang> written as one word; mostly with <in>, {amanlang in}, quickly, at once, and {amanlang thei pen in} is as quickly as possible) (j:a/manlang) (r:zd:20577/zd:20721/zd:21035) (q:draft)
amanlo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:false/untrue/incorrect/wrong) (d:<a> and <manlo> written as one word: what is not true or not correct; {amanlo in} is falsely or incorrectly) (j:a/manlo) (r:zd:12269/zd:23935/zd:19677) (q:draft)
amanmah = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:media/everyday) (w:true indeed/really true/confirmed) (d:<aman>, true, and the emphatic <mah> written as one word; {amanmah hi}, it is indeed true, is how news reports say that an official confirmed an event) (j:aman/mah) (r:zd:14778/zd:11350) (q:draft)
amansiang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/time) (w:be completed/be finished) (d:<a> and <mansiang> written as one word: it is completely finished; with <ciangin>, when it is completed) (j:a/mansiang) (r:zd:11438/zd:17864/zd:17551) (q:draft)
amante = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/nature) (w:those who catch/catchers) (d:<a> and <mante> written as one word: the ones who catch or have caught an animal or a person) (j:a/mante) (r:zd:12434) (q:draft)
amanzah = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:its value/its price) (d:<a>, its, with <manzah>, value, written as one word: what a thing is worth; {amanzah akituat ciangin} is when its value is reckoned) (j:a/manzah) (r:zd:16869/zd:19725) (q:draft)
amanzahding = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:its value/estimated worth) (d:<a>, <manzah> and <ding> written as one word: what a thing would be worth, its value when reckoned in money) (j:a/manzah/ding) (r:zd:19863/zd:19725/zd:20661) (q:draft)
amanzong = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:he also/she also/he too) (d:<amah> with <in>, he or she as the one who acts, and <zong>, also, written as one word: he too, she for her part) (j:amah/in/zong) (r:zd:14694/zd:10973) (q:draft)
amapang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:take part/contribute) (d:<a> and <mapang> written as one word: the one who takes part, who is active in a cause) (j:a/mapang) (r:zd:24481/zd:16612) (q:draft)
amasak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:put first/do first) (d:<a> and <masak> written as one word: the one put first, what is done first, giving first place to) (j:a/masak) (r:zd:24604/zd:19416) (q:draft)
amasapen = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:first/very first/the first one) (d:<a> and <masapen> written as one word: the first of all, in time or in order) (j:a/masapen) (r:zd:25203/zd:24532/zd:11438) (q:draft)
amasapenpen = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/time) (w:very first/first ever) (d:<amasa>, first, and <penpen> written as one word: the very first of all) (j:amasa/penpen) (r:zd:19648/zd:17097) (q:draft)
amasung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/body) (w:her own body/her own womb) (d:<ama>, her, and <sung>, inside, written as one word: her own body; {amasung panin apiang} is born of herself, said of a mother's own child) (j:ama/sung) (r:zd:15994/zd:16175) (q:draft)
amat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:arrest/seize/catch/capture) (d:<a> and <mat> written as one word: he or they seized or arrested, or the one seized; {amat uh} is they arrested) (j:a/mat) (r:zd:14599/ts:1368/zd:12860) (q:draft)
amatgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:arrest in numbers/seize roughly/round up) (d:<amat> and <gawp> written as one word: they arrested or seized, done harshly or to many at once) (j:amat/gawp) (r:zd:12587/zd:20912) (q:draft)
amathu = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:by oneself/on one's own/of one's own accord/spontaneously) (d:usually followed by <in>: by itself or by oneself, without the help or prompting of anyone else) (r:zd:12542/zd:15451/zd:17285) (q:draft)
amatkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:catch/arrest/seize) (d:<a> and <matkhak> written as one word: whom or what they caught, those arrested or the things seized) (j:a/matkhak) (r:zd:20661/zd:15920) (q:draft)
amatkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:seize/arrest/confiscate) (d:<a>, <mat> and <khiat> written as one word: that they seized or arrested, said of goods taken or persons caught by the police) (j:a/mat/khiat) (r:zd:15374/zd:15163) (q:draft)
amatkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:after arresting/have arrested/have caught) (d:<amat> and <khit> written as one word: he or they have seized or arrested; {amatkhit uhciangin} is after they arrested him) (j:amat/khit) (r:zd:20661/zd:16502) (q:draft)
amatsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:seized/confiscated/caught) (d:<a> and <matsak> written as one word: that which was seized, said of goods taken by the authorities, or the catching of something) (j:a/matsak) (r:zd:14585/zd:13151) (q:draft)
