asakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:finding/view/opinion) (d:<a> and <sakna> written as one word, after a describing word: the fact that someone finds a thing to be so, as in {lamdang asakna}, their finding it strange, and {hoih asakna}, what they think good) (j:a/sakna) (r:zd:16332/zd:23898) (q:draft)
asalo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not consider/not find/not think) (d:<a>, <sa> in the sense of consider or feel, and <lo> written as one word after a describing word: who does not find it so; {hoih asalo} is who does not think it good) (j:a/sa/lo) (r:zd:23943/zd:21174) (q:draft)
asam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:hair) (d:<a>, his or her, with <sam>, the hair of the head, written as one word: his or her hair) (r:zd:12466/zd:19203) (q:draft)
asam = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:call/summon/invite) (d:<a> and <sam> written as one word: he calls, or the one who calls, by telephone or as an invitation) (j:a/sam) (r:zd:19262/zd:19147) (q:draft)
asamahmah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:find very hard/suffer greatly) (d:<a> and <samahmah> written as one word, after <hamsa>: one who finds life very hard, or that it is very hard) (j:a/samahmah) (r:zd:10821/zd:16257) (q:draft)
asamahmah = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:nature/everyday) (w:very hot) (d:<a>, <sa>, hot, and <mahmah>, very, written as one word: that is very hot) (j:a/sa/mahmah) (r:zd:17733) (q:draft, low confidence)
asampan = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:body) (w:by the hair) (d:<a>, his or her, <sam>, here the hair of the head, and <pan>, from, written as one word: by his or her hair, said of seizing, holding or dragging someone) (j:a/sam/pan) (r:zd:19428/zd:11592) (q:draft)
asan = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:red/the red one) (d:<a> and <san>, red, written as one word: what is red, the red part) (j:a/san) (r:zd:14890/zd:15435) (q:draft)
asan = (i:2) (t:v) (f:social) (w:accept/receive) (d:<a> with <san>, a form of <sang>, accept, written as one word: the one who accepts, or the accepting of something; set against <anial>, the one who refuses) (r:zd:22873/zd:17927) (q:draft, low confidence)
asang = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:accept/receive/take) (d:the prefix <a> written together with <sang> in its meaning accept or receive: the one who accepts something offered, as in {apia leh asang}, the giver and the receiver, and {asang thei}, able to accept; not the adjective high) (r:zd:14701/zd:20019/zd:25789) (q:draft)
asanggam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:his sibling/her sibling/his brother/her sister) (d:<a> and <sanggam> written as one word: his or her brother or sister) (j:a/sanggam) (r:zd:16899/zd:15554) (q:draft)
asanggamnu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:his sister/her sister) (d:<a>, his or her, and <sanggamnu> written as one word) (j:a/sanggamnu) (r:zd:15953/zd:12548) (q:draft)
asanggampa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:his brother/her brother) (d:<a>, his or her, and <sanggampa> written as one word) (j:a/sanggampa) (r:zd:16170/zd:22967) (q:draft)
asanggamte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:his siblings/her siblings/his brothers and sisters) (d:<a>, his or her, and <sanggamte>, brothers and sisters, written as one word) (j:a/sanggamte) (r:zd:17768) (q:draft)
asangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:travel/everyday) (w:at a height of/high) (d:<asang>, high, and <in> written as one word, placed after a measure: so high, at that height) (j:asang/in) (r:zd:11846/zd:12888) (q:draft)
asangkah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education) (w:attend school/go to school) (d:<a> and <sangkah> written as one word: he or she goes to school; {asangkah lai} is while he or she was at school) (j:a/sangkah) (r:zd:15391/zd:17945) (q:draft)
asangkahna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:his school/her school/place of study) (d:<a> and <sangkahna> written as one word: the school or college that he or she attends, or attended) (j:a/sangkahna) (r:zd:11148/zd:13157) (q:draft)
asangpen = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:highest/tallest) (d:<a> and <sangpen> written as one word: the highest, the tallest) (j:a/sangpen) (r:zd:15946/zd:16901) (q:draft)
asangpenpen = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:highest/tallest/the very highest) (d:<asang>, high, and <penpen>, the very most, written as one word: the highest or tallest of all; also said of the heaviest punishment) (j:asang/penpen) (r:zd:11438/zd:17711/zd:10945) (q:draft)
asangte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion/social) (w:those who accept/those who receive) (d:<a> and <sangte> written as one word, with <sang> in the sense receive: those who accept a teaching, a belief or a person) (j:a/sangte) (r:zd:15926/zd:20833) (q:draft)
asanna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/nature) (w:its height/height) (d:<a> and <sanna> written as one word: its height, how high or tall a thing is) (j:a/sanna) (r:zd:12014/zd:11229/zd:18200) (q:draft)
asap = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:call/invite/summon) (d:<a> and <sap> written as one word: he called or invited, the one who is called) (j:a/sap) (r:zd:26097/zd:14801) (q:draft)
asapsap = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/it) (w:keep calling/call again and again) (d:<a> and <sapsap> written as one word: he, she or they keep calling someone, often by phone; mostly before <hangin>, although) (j:a/sapsap) (r:zd:18020/zd:14883) (q:draft)
asat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:strike/hit/shine) (d:<a> and <sat> written as one word: he hits or strikes something; also said of a clock that strikes the hour and of the sun that shines) (j:a/sat) (r:zd:25918/zd:14730/zd:16584) (q:draft)
asat = (i:2) (t:v) (f:social) (w:found/establish) (d:<a> and <sat> written as one word: he founds a village or town, or the one who founded it) (j:a/sat) (r:ts:617) (q:draft, low confidence)
asate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:those who consider/those who find) (d:<a>, <sa>, think or feel, and <te> written as one word after a describing word: those who find something so, as in {hoih asate}, those who think it good) (j:a/sa/te) (r:zd:23130/zd:17971) (q:draft)
asatgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:beat severely/beat up) (d:<a> and <satgawp> written as one word: he beat someone severely, or the one who beat or was beaten) (j:a/satgawp) (r:zd:16667) (q:draft)
asatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:striking/blow) (d:<a> and <satna> written as one word: his striking, the place where one was struck or the thing to strike with) (j:a/satna) (r:zd:17672/zd:19637) (q:draft, low confidence)
asatna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:nature) (w:hot place/heat) (d:<a> with <satna> in the sense of heat, from the word for hot: where it is hot, set beside {akeuna}, where it is dry) (r:zd:24054) (q:draft, low confidence)
asau = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:long) (d:{asau} placed after a measure and before the thing measured, or after the thing: that is so much long, long; the relative form of <sau>, where sense 1 names the length itself) (s:sau) (r:zd:15781/zd:12725/zd:19141) (q:draft)
asaupen = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:longest) (d:<asau>, long or length, with the superlative <pen>, written as one word: the longest, in measure or in time) (j:asau/pen) (r:zd:11461/zd:12434) (q:draft)
asawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:send/order) (d:<a> and <sawl> written as one word: he sent or ordered, the one who sends, what he orders) (j:a/sawl) (r:zd:25918/zd:14941) (q:draft)
asawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:intend/plan/try) (d:<a> and <sawm> written as one word, placed after a verb or noun: he or they intend, plan or try to do it; {atup asawm} is what one aims at and plans) (j:a/sawm) (r:zd:25919/zd:20300/zd:21321) (q:draft)
asawm = (i:2) (t:num) (f:everyday) (w:ten/tens) (d:<a> and <sawm>, ten, written as one word: the ten, by tens; with {-na} it forms the ordinals of the tens) (j:a/sawm) (r:zd:21904) (q:draft, low confidence)
asawnkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:push out/push off) (d:<a> and <sawnkhiat> written as one word: he or she pushes someone out or off) (j:a/sawnkhiat) (r:zd:15888) (q:draft)
