atheinuam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:want to know/wish to know) (d:<a> and <theinuam> written as one word: the one who wants to know; {atheinuam te} is those who want to know) (j:a/theinuam) (r:zd:16383/zd:16216) (q:draft)
athem = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:piece/fragment/bit) (d:<a> and <them> written as one word: its pieces, the small broken bits of something) (j:a/them) (r:zd:17713/zd:17591) (q:draft)
athemneng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:fragments/debris/wreckage/scraps) (d:<a>, <them> and <neng> written as one word: the small broken pieces of something, as the wreckage of an aeroplane or the splinters of a blast) (j:a/them/neng) (r:zd:12888/zd:11588/zd:17164) (q:draft)
athoh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/politics) (w:withdraw/issue/take out) (d:<a> with <thoh>, a Burmese loan, take out or issue: withdraw money from a bank, or issue an order, a warrant or a curfew) (j:a/thoh) (r:zd:12437/zd:24947/zd:25068) (q:draft, low confidence)
athongkiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:be imprisoned/serve a prison term) (d:<a> and <thongkiat> written as one word: his or her being in prison; {athongkiat zahding} is the length of the prison term) (j:a/thongkiat) (r:zd:19906) (q:draft)
athu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:the matter/the facts) (d:<a> and <thu> written as one word: the matter in question, its facts or content) (j:a/thu) (r:zd:21251/zd:21357/zd:20579) (q:draft)
athu akician = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/everyday) (w:the exact facts/the details/the particulars) (d:<athu>, the matter, and <akician>, exact: the exact facts or full details of a matter; mostly followed by <in>, {athu akician in}, in detail, exactly, before a verb of telling, announcing or finding out) (r:zd:20717/zd:12874/zd:19635) (q:draft)
athu ala = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/everyday) (w:the details/the facts of the matter/the particulars) (d:<athu>, the matter, and {a la}, its song, written as one word and not the exclamation: the pair {thu leh la}, word and song, means the whole of a matter, so {athu ala} is all the details of what happened; in news reports the object of <kancian>, investigate) (r:zd:15019/zd:19745) (q:draft)
athuah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:wear/put on) (d:<a> and <thuah>, put on over or in addition, written as one word: he wears or the one wearing, said of a mask and other things put on the body) (j:a/thuah) (r:zd:24333/zd:24219/zd:17661) (q:draft)
athuah = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:do together/add) (d:<a> and <thuah>, in addition, written as one word: do one thing along with another, add one thing to another) (j:a/thuah) (r:zd:24750) (q:draft, low confidence)
athuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:suffer/undergo/endure) (d:<a> and <thuak> written as one word: who suffers or bears something; after a verb form it names the person to whom the thing was done, as <mat athuak>, the one arrested, and {zuak athuak}, the one who was sold) (j:a/thuak) (r:zd:22556/zd:18009) (q:draft)
athuakding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:will suffer/will undergo) (d:<a>, <thuak>, undergo, and <ding>, will, written as one word: that he or she will undergo, the punishment or trial that awaits someone) (j:a/thuak/ding) (r:zd:12085/zd:12817/zd:16131) (q:draft)
athuakkha = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/media) (w:victim/the one affected) (d:<a> and <thuakkha> written as one word: the one who has suffered something, a victim; with <te>, the victims) (j:a/thuakkha) (r:zd:11360/zd:15469/zd:11837) (q:draft)
athuaklah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/everyday) (w:suffer badly/be hard hit/find hard to bear) (d:<a> and <thuaklah> written as one word: who suffers much from something, or what is hard to bear) (j:a/thuaklah) (r:zd:15067/zd:14519) (q:draft)
