athuakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:victim/the one who suffered) (d:<a> and <thuakpa> written as one word, placed after the word for what was done: the man to whom it was done, as in {mat athuakpa}, the man who was arrested) (j:a/thuakpa) (r:zd:21030/zd:19868/zd:20492) (q:draft)
athuakpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:social/media) (w:the victim/the one who suffered) (d:<a>, <thuak>, undergo, and the topic marker <pen> written as one word, placed after the word for what was done: the one to whom it was done, as the topic of the sentence) (j:a/thuak/pen) (r:zd:12598/zd:19213) (q:draft)
athuaksak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:made suffer/inflicted/imposed) (d:<a> and <thuaksak> written as one word: made someone undergo something, such as a punishment named before it) (j:a/thuaksak) (r:zd:19318/zd:11598) (q:draft)
athuakte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/media) (w:victims/those who suffer/sufferers) (d:<a> and <thuakte> written as one word, placed after what was suffered: those who underwent it, as in {kapliam athuakte}, those wounded by shooting, and {hih natna athuakte}, those who have this disease) (j:a/thuakte) (r:zd:24014/zd:15000) (q:draft)
athuakzawh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:after suffering/after undergoing) (d:<a> and <thuak>, suffer, with <zawh>, after, written as one word: after he or she has suffered it, often followed by a length of time) (j:a/thuak/zawh) (r:zd:18020) (q:draft)
athugen = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/religion) (w:what he says/his speech/his words) (d:<a>, his or her, and <thugen>, written as one word: what a person says or said, a speech or sermon; {athugen ding} is what he is going to speak about) (j:a/thugen) (r:zd:22550/zd:17305) (q:draft)
athugenna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:his speech/his address/what he said) (d:<a>, his or her, and <thugenna>, speech, written as one word) (j:a/thugenna) (r:zd:19302/zd:15933) (q:draft)
athugente = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/religion) (w:his words/what he said) (d:<a>, <thugen> and the plural <te> written as one word: the things that he said) (j:a/thugen/te) (r:zd:20673/zd:25342) (q:draft)
athuhilh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/religion) (w:teach/preach/instruct) (d:<a> and <thuhilh> written as one word: he teaches or preaches, what he teaches; also said of correcting children) (j:a/thuhilh) (r:zd:17883/zd:22778) (q:draft)
