atuamtuamte = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:various/different kinds of) (d:<atuamtuam>, various, with the plural <te>, placed after a noun: the various ones, of many kinds) (b:atuamtuam) (j:atuamtuam/te) (r:zd:17161/zd:15998) (q:draft)
atuan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:ride/travel in/be on board) (d:<a> and <tuan>, the form of <tuang>, ride, written as one word: he rides, the ones riding in a vehicle; {atuan ciangin} is when he rides) (j:a/tuan) (r:zd:12628/zd:14829/zd:19902) (q:draft)
atuang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:ride/be on board/travel in) (d:<a> and <tuang> written as one word: he, she or they ride in a vehicle; before a noun, who are on board, as in {atuang mi}, the people on board) (j:a/tuang) (r:zd:10670/zd:17790/zd:12982) (q:draft)
atuangding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:to ride/to board/be about to travel on) (d:<a>, <tuang> and <ding> written as one word: who is going to ride or travel on a vehicle, ship or aeroplane; {atuangding in} is in order to board) (j:a/tuang/ding) (r:zd:21294/zd:18091/zd:12105) (q:draft)
atuangkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:be on board/happen to be riding) (d:<a>, <tuang> ride and <kha> written as one word: those who happened to be riding in a vehicle, the passengers on board) (j:a/tuang/kha) (r:zd:20915/zd:19157) (q:draft)
atuangkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:ride together/travel together) (d:<a>, <tuang> and <khawm> written as one word: they ride together in or on one vehicle, or those who ride together) (j:a/tuang/khawm) (r:zd:11752/zd:14954/zd:11827) (q:draft)
atuangpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:rider/passenger) (d:<a> and <tuangpa> written as one word: the one riding on a motorcycle or in a car) (j:a/tuangpa) (r:zd:17455/zd:11495) (q:draft)
atuangpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:travel) (w:those on board/the passengers) (d:<a> <tuang> <pen> written as one word: those riding in a vehicle, as the topic of the sentence) (j:a/tuang/pen) (r:zd:15639/zd:11992/zd:15631) (q:draft)
atuangte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:passengers/riders) (d:<a> and <tuangte> written as one word: those who ride in a car, bus or plane, the passengers) (j:a/tuangte) (r:zd:11265/zd:17100/zd:22545) (q:draft)
atuangteng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:all on board/all the passengers) (d:<atuang>, who ride, and <teng>, here all, written as one word: everyone who was riding in the plane or vehicle) (j:atuang/teng) (r:zd:11982/zd:17064) (q:draft)
atuangthei = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:travel) (w:able to carry/seating) (d:<a>, <tuang> and <thei> written as one word after a number of people: that so many can ride in, said of a vehicle or aircraft) (j:a/tuang/thei) (r:zd:17941/zd:14829) (q:draft)
atuankawm = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:travel) (w:while riding) (d:<atuan>, he rides, and <kawm>, while, written as one word: while riding on something, as a motorcycle or an escalator) (j:atuan/kawm) (r:zd:18069/zd:15307) (q:draft)
atuanlaitak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:while riding/while on board) (d:<a>, <tuan>, the form of <tuang>, ride, and <laitak>, while, written as one word: while he or she is riding in a vehicle, on an escalator or in a lift) (j:a/tuan/laitak) (r:zd:20099/zd:21385/zd:14566) (q:draft)
atuanna = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:travel) (w:carrying/with on board) (d:<a> and <tuanna> written as one word: on which someone rides, said of a vehicle after the number of people in it; {mi 71 atuanna vanleng} is a plane with 71 people on board) (j:a/tuanna) (r:zd:18099/zd:17800) (q:draft)
atuanpih = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:fellow passenger/one riding along) (d:<a>, <tuan>, ride, and <pih>, together with, written as one word: the one who rides in the same vehicle, a fellow passenger) (j:a/tuan/pih) (r:zd:16942/zd:13276/zd:19939) (q:draft)
atuap = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body/health) (w:his lungs/the lungs) (d:<a> and <tuap> written as one word: his, her or their lungs) (j:a/tuap) (r:zd:11560/zd:13112) (q:draft)
atuat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/education) (w:reckon/calculate/suppose) (d:<a> and <tuat> written as one word: he or they reckon, work out or take something to be so) (j:a/tuat) (r:zd:11099/zd:21739) (q:draft)
atuding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:due to land/about to land) (d:<a> with <tu>, sit or of an aircraft land, and <ding>, will, written as one word: that is to land; also those who are going to sit down) (j:a/tu/ding) (r:zd:17554/zd:19176) (q:draft)
atuh = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:work/social) (w:fake/counterfeit/forged/imitation) (d:not genuine, made to pass for the real thing; placed after the noun, as {Passport atuh}, a forged passport, and {zu atuh}, bootleg liquor) (o:Burmese, atu) (r:zd:17262/zd:11990/zd:15814) (q:draft)
atui = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food/nature) (w:its water/its juice/its liquid) (d:<a> and <tui> written as one word: the water, juice or liquid of something) (j:a/tui) (r:zd:21826) (q:draft)
atui = (i:2) (t:n) (f:social/home) (w:home village/native place) (d:in the pair {akhua atui}, his village and its water: the home village or native place of a person) (j:a/tui) (r:zd:18107/zd:10863) (q:draft, low confidence)
atuk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:fall/fall down) (d:<a> and <tuk>, fall, written as one word: he or it falls, the one that fell) (j:a/tuk) (r:zd:11407/zd:11775/zd:15779) (q:draft)
atukkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:after falling/having fallen) (d:<atuk>, he falls, with <khit>, done, written as one word and followed by <ciangin>: after he fell; also after an aircraft landed, and after a snake bit) (j:atuk/khit) (r:zd:12053/zd:12349) (q:draft)
atukna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:place where it fell/where it lands) (d:<a> and <tukna>, falling, written as one word: the place where someone or something fell or comes down; of a snake, the place where it bit) (j:a/tukna) (r:zd:11698/zd:19871/zd:24014) (q:draft)
atuksa = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:fallen/lying fallen) (d:<atuk> and <sa>, here the ending for a completed state, written as one word: having fallen down, lying where he fell) (j:atuk/sa) (r:zd:11698) (q:draft, low confidence)
atuksawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:be about to land/come in to land) (d:<a>, <tuk>, come down, and <sawm>, be about to, written as one word: said of an aircraft that is about to land; mostly before <laitak>, just as it was landing) (j:a/tuk/sawm) (r:zd:12124/zd:13007/zd:11982) (q:draft)
atuksuk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:fall down/fall to the ground) (d:<a> and <tuksuk> written as one word: it fell down, or the place where it fell; {atuksuk ciangin} is when it fell down) (j:a/tuksuk) (r:zd:21563/zd:15372) (q:draft)
atum = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:play/sound/set) (d:<a> and <tum> written as one word: he plays or sounds an instrument, or the one who plays; in {ni atum hun} it is another verb of the same spelling, the time when the sun sets) (j:a/tum) (r:zd:23036/zd:20719) (q:draft, low confidence)
atun = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:arrive/reach) (d:<a> and <tun> written as one word: he, she or they arrive; mostly before <ciangin>, when they arrived, or after the place that is reached) (j:a/tun) (r:zd:13041/zd:22802/zd:11497) (q:draft)
atunciang = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/time) (w:when he arrived/on arrival) (d:<a>, <tun> and <ciang> written as one word: when he, she or it arrived, or until it arrives) (j:a/tun/ciang) (r:zd:12596/zd:13080) (q:draft)
atung = (i:2) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:arrive/reach/come) (d:<tung.1>, arrive, with the prefix <a> written together: he or they arrive, after the name of the place reached, or of a time that is to come; not {atung} the top or what is above) (r:zd:24063/zd:16313/zd:21929) (q:draft)
atunga = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/media) (w:above/above-mentioned) (d:<a> and <tunga> written as one word: the one above, said of what was written or shown earlier in a text, as {hih atunga thute}, these things above) (j:a/tunga) (r:zd:9449/zd:19427/zd:22350) (q:draft)
atungaa = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/media) (w:the above/aforementioned) (d:<atung> and <aa> written as one word: what is above, said of what was stated earlier in a text) (j:atung/aa) (r:zd:24141/zd:19506) (q:draft)
atungah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:on it/on top of it/above) (d:<a> and <tungah> written as one word: on it, on top of it or above it; in a text also above, in what was said before) (j:a/tungah) (r:zd:18211/zd:12974/zd:13334) (q:draft)
atungdawl = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/travel) (w:upper floor/upper storey/upper deck) (d:<atung> the top and <dawl> floor, written as one word: the upper floor of a building or the upper deck of a bus) (j:atung/dawl) (r:zd:15167/zd:16952/zd:15368) (q:draft)
atungdawn = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/home) (w:top/very top/rooftop) (d:<atung> and <dawn> written as one word: the very top of a building, a pole, a vehicle or a hill) (j:atung/dawn) (r:zd:13022/zd:15920) (q:draft)
atungding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:be about to arrive/will come) (d:<a>, <tung> and <ding> written as one word: that will arrive or come, of a person, a vehicle, a time or an event) (j:a/tung/ding) (r:zd:17758/zd:13303/zd:12468) (q:draft)
atungkhin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:have arrived/have reached) (d:<a> and <tungkhin> written as one word: he or they have already arrived, or before a noun the one who has already arrived) (j:a/tungkhin) (r:zd:12338/zd:11918/zd:11283) (q:draft)
atungkhuh = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/travel) (w:roof/cover/lid) (d:<a> and <tungkhuh>, covering, written as one word: what covers the top of something, the roof of a house or car, the lid of a coffin) (j:a/tungkhuh) (r:zd:17299/zd:15657) (q:draft)
atungkhum = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/travel) (w:roof/its roof/top) (d:<a>, its, and <tungkhum>, roof, written as one word: the roof or top of a building or a car) (j:a/tungkhum) (r:zd:23784/zd:15437) (q:draft)
atunglam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:top/upper part/above) (d:<a> and <tunglam> written as one word: the upper part or top of a thing, the floor or side above; {atunglam ah} is on top, above) (j:a/tunglam) (r:zd:11945/zd:15167/zd:20369) (q:draft)
atunglian = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:right above/directly above/the spot just over) (d:<atung>, the top or what is above, with <lian> in its use as exactly, not large, written as one word: the place straight above something; {atunglian panin} is from directly above. In one article it is instead {a tung lian}, just arrived) (r:zd:14692/zd:17256/zd:20153) (q:draft)
atungpan = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:from above/from the top) (d:<atung>, the top, and <pan>, from, written as one word: from above, from on top of it; often followed by <in>) (j:atung/pan) (r:zd:18074/zd:11691/zd:14528) (q:draft)
atungpen = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:topmost/the very top) (d:<atung>, top, and <pen>, most, written as one word: the highest part or the outermost layer; {atungpen ah} is on the very top) (j:atung/pen) (r:zd:12691/zd:15777) (q:draft)
atungsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:travel/social) (w:arrived/having arrived/settled) (d:<a> and <tungsa> written as one word: who have already arrived, said mostly of people who have reached another country) (j:a/tungsa) (r:zd:17572/zd:12504/zd:15433) (q:draft)
atungsiah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:and above/or more/upward) (d:<a> and <tungsiah> written as one word: from the stated number, amount or age upward, after <pan>) (j:a/tungsiah) (r:zd:14867/zd:21042/zd:15379) (q:draft)
atungtham = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:surface/outside/outward appearance) (d:<a> and <tungtham> written as one word: the surface, what is only on the outside; {atungtham bek} is only superficially) (j:a/tungtham) (r:zd:17976/zd:25601) (q:draft)
atunkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:have arrived/after arriving) (d:<a> and <tunkhit> written as one word: he, she or they have arrived; mostly before <ciangin>, after arriving) (j:a/tunkhit) (r:zd:17750/zd:12888/zd:17407) (q:draft)
atunkik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:arrive back/return) (d:<a> and <tunkik> written as one word: he, she or they arrive back, mostly before <ciangin>, when) (j:a/tunkik) (r:zd:12272/zd:21025) (q:draft)
atunlawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:end up in/be taken to as a result) (d:<a>, <tun> and <lawh> written as one word: arrive somewhere as a result of what happened; {zato atunlawh} is those who ended up in hospital) (j:a/tun/lawh) (r:zd:17538/zd:22805/zd:12011) (q:draft)
atunlian = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:just arrive/arrive at that moment) (d:<atun>, he arrives, with <lian>, here exactly or just, written as one word: at the very moment of arriving, mostly before <ciangin>, when) (j:atun/lian) (r:zd:19872/zd:15236) (q:draft)
atunma = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time/travel) (w:before arriving/before it comes) (d:<a> and <tunma> written as one word, followed by <in>: before someone reaches a place, or before an event comes) (j:a/tunma) (r:zd:14846/zd:17899/zd:10759) (q:draft)
atunna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:place of arrival/where one arrives) (d:<a> and <tunna> written as one word: the place he, she or it reaches, or the reaching of it; {atunna ding} is where it is to arrive) (j:a/tunna) (r:zd:23821/zd:14716) (q:draft)
atunphet = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:travel/time) (w:as soon as arriving/on arrival) (d:<a>, <tun>, arrive, and <phet>, just, written as one word and followed by <in>, after the place reached: the moment he, she or it arrived there) (j:a/tun/phet) (r:zd:12374/zd:11627) (q:draft)
atuntheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:be able to reach/can arrive) (d:<a>, <tun> and <theih> written as one word, before <nading>: so that one can reach or arrive) (j:a/tun/theih) (r:zd:21588/zd:20263) (q:draft)
atuntun = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:wherever they arrive/everywhere they come) (d:<a> and <tuntun> written as one word, mostly followed by <na>: every place that he or they come to) (j:a/tuntun) (r:zd:23554/zd:11697) (q:draft)
atuntunna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/everyday) (w:wherever one arrives/every place reached) (d:<a> and <tuntunna> written as one word: each place that they come to) (j:a/tuntunna) (r:zd:11697/zd:20125) (q:draft)
atunu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:his granddaughter/her granddaughter/niece) (d:<a> and <tunu> written as one word: his or her granddaughter; in the news also said of a niece) (j:a/tunu) (r:zd:12512/zd:12532) (q:draft)
atunzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:after arriving/have arrived) (d:<a> and <tunzawh> written as one word: after he or it arrived; {atunzawh asawtlo in} is not long after arriving) (j:a/tunzawh) (r:zd:23142/zd:12673) (q:draft)
atup = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:aim/intention/goal) (d:<a> and <tup> written as one word: what he aims at, his aim; often paired as {atup angimna}, his aims and goals) (j:a/tup) (r:zd:25919/zd:16216) (q:draft)
atupa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:his grandson/her grandson) (d:<a>, his or her, and <tupa>, grandson, written as one word) (j:a/tupa) (r:zd:11256/zd:12919) (q:draft)
atupna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:his aim/his purpose/her goal) (d:<a> and <tupna> written as one word: his, her or its aim, often paired as {angimna atupna}) (j:a/tupna) (r:zd:23022/zd:22719) (q:draft)
atut = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/body) (w:sit/be sitting) (d:<a> and <tut> written as one word: he or she sits, the one sitting; {atut laitak} is while he was sitting) (j:a/tut) (r:zd:17661/zd:15021/zd:23240) (q:draft)
atute = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:his grandchildren/her grandchildren) (d:<a> and <tute> written as one word: his, her or their grandchildren) (j:a/tute) (r:zd:16294/zd:17565) (q:draft)
atutlaitak = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/body) (w:while sitting) (d:<atut>, he sits, with <laitak>, at the very time, written as one word: while he or she was sitting) (j:atut/laitak) (r:zd:15456/zd:19707) (q:draft)
atutna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/travel) (w:his seat/seat) (d:<a> and <tutna>, seat, written as one word: his or her seat, the place where someone sits) (j:a/tutna) (r:zd:15216/zd:23249/zd:16137) (q:draft)
