aza = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/body) (w:hear/have heard) (d:<a> and <za>, hear, written as one word: he hears, they hear, and the one who hears) (j:a/za) (r:zd:22658/zd:12352) (q:draft)
aza = (i:2) (t:n) (f:work/politics) (w:his rank/his office/his position) (d:<a> and <za>, rank or office, written as one word: the post a person holds; {aza kia} is lose one's post) (j:a/za) (r:zd:21040) (q:draft, low confidence)
azadah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:dislike/resent) (d:<a> and <zadah> written as one word: the one who dislikes or takes offence, those who resent it) (j:a/zadah) (r:zd:24682/zd:23066) (q:draft)
azah tampi = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:many times over/manifold/many times as much) (d:<azah>, times as much, and <tampi>, many: many times over; with <tawh> or <in> after it in a blessing that God may repay a gift many times over, and after <sangin> in a comparison, many times more than) (r:zd:21379/zd:19137) (q:draft)
azahmawh = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:private parts/genitals) (d:<a>, his or her, and <zahmawh> written as one word: his or her private parts; {azahmawh zuaksak} is to sell someone for sex) (j:a/zahmawh) (r:zd:18038) (q:draft)
azahnih = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:double/twice as much/twofold) (d:<a> and <zahnih> written as one word: twice the amount or degree of something; {azahnih in} is twice as, and {sangin azahnih} is double compared with) (j:a/zahnih) (r:zd:11922/zd:14791/zd:20717) (q:draft)
azahtak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:respect/honor) (d:<a> and <zahtak> written as one word: who respects, the one that respects; {azahtak huai} is worthy of respect, respectable) (j:a/zahtak) (r:zd:24376/zd:26967/zd:21345) (q:draft)
azai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:wide/broad/spacious/width) (d:<a> and <zai> written as one word: that which is wide, or the width or extent of something, also after a measure) (j:a/zai) (r:zd:20627/zd:19952/zd:19134) (q:draft)
azaih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/it) (w:take a photo/record/film/scan) (d:<a> and <zaih>, take a photograph, record a video or make a scan, written as one word: he or she took it, or the one who took it) (j:a/zaih) (r:zd:20291/zd:14572/zd:19318) (q:draft)
azaihkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/it) (w:record/film/capture on camera) (d:<a> and <zaihkha> written as one word: the one who recorded it or happened to film it; {Video azaihkha} is the person who filmed the video) (j:a/zaihkha) (r:zd:16634/zd:15362) (q:draft)
azaihkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/it) (w:happen to record/film/photograph) (d:<a>, <zaih>, record or photograph, and <khak>, happen to, written as one word: the one who took the picture or video, he or she happened to record it) (j:a/zaih/khak) (r:zd:12525/zd:20490) (q:draft)
azaihsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media) (w:photograph/film/record) (d:<a> and <zaihsak> written as one word: he took the photo or video, or the one who took it) (j:a/zaihsak) (r:zd:12763/zd:16667) (q:draft)
azaihsim = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/it) (w:film secretly/record secretly) (d:<a>, <zaih>, record a picture or video, and <sim>, here in the sense secretly, written as one word: that someone filmed or photographed in secret) (j:a/zaih/sim) (r:zd:17003/zd:14566) (q:draft)
azaina = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:its width/its area/its breadth) (d:<a> and <zaina> written as one word: its width, paired with <asauna>, its length; also the area or extent of a place) (j:a/zaina) (r:zd:15274/zd:11438) (q:draft)
azak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:hear) (d:<a> and <zak> written as one word: he or she hears, mostly before <ciangin>, when he heard; also what is heard, as in {azak nop}, pleasant to hear) (j:a/zak) (r:zd:17049/zd:19565/zd:24714) (q:draft)
azakciangin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:when he heard) (d:<a>, <zak> and <ciangin> written as one word: when he or she heard it) (j:a/zak/ciangin) (r:zd:11148/zd:24139) (q:draft)
azakha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:happen to hear/hear of) (d:<a> and <zakha> written as one word: the one who happens to hear, those who come to hear of something; {azakha khempeuh} is all who heard of it) (j:a/zakha) (r:zd:11398/zd:25342/zd:14498) (q:draft)
azaksak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:report/inform/notify) (d:<a> and <zaksak>, cause to hear, written as one word: he or they informed, often of reporting something to the police or the authorities) (j:a/zaksak) (r:zd:19289/zd:16733) (q:draft)
azan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:night/by night) (d:<a> and <zan> written as one word: the night; {asun azan} is day and night, and {azan nitaklam} is the evening before) (j:a/zan) (r:zd:24948/zd:22580/ts:7679) (q:draft)
azang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:use/user) (d:<a> and <zang> written as one word: the one who uses, those who use) (j:a/zang) (r:zd:22833/zd:15354/zd:12009) (q:draft)
azang = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:light) (d:<a> with <zang>, here light in weight, the opposite of <gik>, heavy: the light one) (j:a/zang) (r:zd:21826) (q:draft, low confidence)
azangden = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/it) (w:use regularly/be a regular user) (d:<a>, <zang> and <den> written as one word: the one who always uses a thing; said of regular users of a service and of people who habitually take drugs) (j:a/zang/den) (r:zd:14720/zd:15517) (q:draft)
azangding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:will use/will spend/to use) (d:<a> and <zangding> written as one word: he or they will use or spend, the one who is to use; with <in>, in order to spend a time or a holiday) (j:a/zangding) (r:zd:16162/zd:16828/zd:22911) (q:draft)
azangh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:use/the one who uses) (d:<a> and <zangh> written as one word: uses, or the one or those who use a thing) (j:a/zangh) (r:zd:20999/zd:11110) (q:draft)
azanghiam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:whether he uses/does he use) (d:<a>, <zang> and <hiam> written as one word: whether he or they used it, mostly in reports of a drug test) (j:a/zang/hiam) (r:zd:12493/zd:15443) (q:draft)
azangkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:have used/happen to use) (d:<a> and <zangkha>, happen to use, written as one word: who has used, those who have used a product, a drug or a word) (j:a/zangkha) (r:zd:20466/zd:11396) (q:draft)
azangkhat = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:one who uses/one using) (d:<azang>, the one who uses, and <khat>, one, written as one word: a person or thing that uses something) (j:azang/khat) (r:zd:11880) (q:draft)
azangno = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:trigger) (d:the trigger of a gun, the small part that is pressed to fire it, also written {thau-zangno}; also used of a thing that sets something off) (r:zd:11657/zd:19991) (q:draft)
azangpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/it) (w:the users/those who use) (d:<a>, <zang>, use, and the topic marker <pen>, written as one word: as for those who use it, as for what uses it) (j:a/zang/pen) (r:zd:12357/zd:13151) (q:draft)
azangte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/it) (w:users/those who use) (d:<a> and <zangte> written as one word: the people who use something) (j:a/zangte) (r:zd:22707/zd:14620/zd:22833) (q:draft)
azanni = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:the day before/the previous day) (d:<a> and <zanni>, yesterday, written as one word: the day before the day spoken of, often followed by <in> or by the name of the day) (j:a/zanni) (r:zd:16621/zd:26124) (q:draft)
azanzan = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:that very night/in the night) (d:<zan>, night, said twice after <a> and mostly followed by <in>: in the night itself, that same night without waiting for morning) (j:a/zan) (r:zd:23281/zd:17527) (q:draft)
azat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:used/that is used/he uses) (d:<a> and <zat> written as one word: which someone uses, that is used; {azat huai} is worth using, useful) (j:a/zat) (r:zd:10955/zd:22802) (q:draft)
azatdan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:way of using it/how to use it) (d:<a> and <zatdan> written as one word: the way something is used or should be used) (j:a/zatdan) (r:zd:25915/zd:25924) (q:draft)
azatding = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:to be used/for his use/that he is to use) (d:<a> and <zatding> written as one word: which is to be used, or his or her using of something; {azatding uh dial} is the cloth they are to use) (j:a/zatding) (r:zd:19743/zd:15201) (q:draft)
azatkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:after using/have used/after spending) (d:<azat> and <khit> written as one word before <ciangin> or <uhciangin>: after someone has used a thing or spent a day) (j:azat/khit) (r:zd:13199/zd:17085) (q:draft)
azatlam = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:health/everyday) (w:that he used/the fact of using) (d:<azat>, he uses, and <lam>, way, written as one word: the fact that someone has used something, in the news of a drug test, {azatlam kimukhia}, it was found that he had used it) (j:azat/lam) (r:zd:17909) (q:draft)
azatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:use/usage/its use) (d:<a> and <zatna> written as one word: the use of something, the way or the place it is used, or his using of it) (j:a/zatna) (r:zd:25928/zd:23060/zd:24058) (q:draft)
azatsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/home) (w:used/already used) (d:<a> and <zatsa> written as one word: that he or she has used, placed before the thing named) (j:a/zatsa) (r:zd:19743/zd:13199) (q:draft)
azatsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:intend to use/plan to use) (d:<a> and <zatsawm> written as one word: he or they intend to use, or what is intended to be used) (j:a/zatsawm) (r:zd:12302/zd:11527) (q:draft)
azatte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:things used/those used) (d:<azat>, that is used, with the plural <te>: the things or people that someone uses) (j:azat/te) (r:zd:23191/zd:13084) (q:draft)
azattheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:can be used/be able to use) (d:<a> and <zattheih> written as one word: that someone can use or employ, mostly before <nading>) (j:a/zattheih) (r:zd:20276/zd:17083) (q:draft)
azatzat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:keep using/use regularly/have long used) (d:<a> and <zatzat> written as one word: which someone keeps using, what is or was in regular use) (j:a/zatzat) (r:zd:11308/zd:11167) (q:draft)
azawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/education) (w:finish/complete/pass/win) (d:<a> and <zawh> written as one word: he finishes or passes it, or wins; {tan 10 azawh ciang in} is after finishing the tenth grade) (j:a/zawh) (r:zd:22556/zd:24595/zd:18297) (q:draft)
azenzen = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:if by chance/in case/should it happen) (d:<a> and <zenzen> written as one word; {azenzen in} opens a clause about something that may happen: if by any chance, in case) (j:a/zenzen) (r:zd:12096/zd:11034) (q:draft)
azenzenin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:if by chance/in case/supposing) (d:<azenzen> and <in> written as one word, at the start of a sentence: if it should happen that) (j:azenzen/in) (r:zd:23957) (q:draft)
azepgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:thrash/cane/beat severely) (d:<a> and <zepgawp> written as one word: he or she beats someone hard with a cane, belt or hose, or the one who did so) (j:a/zepgawp) (r:zd:16667/zd:16628) (q:draft)
Azerbaijan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:politics/travel) (w:Azerbaijan) (d:country in the Caucasus, between Russia and Iran) (r:zd:21400/zd:15163) (q:draft)
azi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:his wife/wife) (d:<a>, his, and <zi>, wife, written as one word) (j:a/zi) (r:zd:18020/zd:17363/zd:17323) (q:draft)
azia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:manner/way/nature) (d:<a>, its, and <zia>, way, written as one word: the way something is or is done, its nature; often paired as {adan leh azia} and {azia atong}) (j:a/zia) (r:zd:20875/zd:22464) (q:draft)
aziakai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:time/everyday) (w:be late/be delayed/take long) (d:<a> with <ziakai>, another spelling of <zekai>, be late, written as one word: it is late or delayed; after a length of time, it takes that long) (j:a/zekai) (r:zd:19699/zd:22557/zd:11527) (q:draft)
azilui = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:his former wife/his ex-wife) (d:<a>, <zi> and <lui> written as one word: his former wife, the woman he was married to before) (j:a/zi/lui) (r:zd:15172) (q:draft)
azin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:travel/visit) (d:<a> and <zin> written as one word: who travels, who is visiting; {khual azin} is one who is on a journey) (j:a/zin) (r:zd:11401/zd:23928) (q:draft)
azinding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/politics) (w:to visit/will travel/planned visit) (d:<a> and <zinding> written as one word: who is to travel to a place, or his or her coming visit) (j:a/zinding) (r:zd:11005/zd:11835) (q:draft)
azing = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:the next day/the following morning) (d:<a> and <zing>, morning, written as one word, nearly always in {azing ciang}: on the next day, the morning after; compare <zingciang>) (j:a/zing) (r:zd:16038/zd:25625/zd:24574) (q:draft)
azingciang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:the next day/the following day) (d:<a> and <zingciang> written as one word: the day after the event just told) (j:a/zingciang) (r:zd:14642/zd:11529) (q:draft)
azinkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:set out/depart/go abroad) (d:<a> and <zinkhia> written as one word: he, she or it set out on a journey; also the one who travels out) (j:a/zinkhia) (r:zd:17844/zd:11271/zd:16979) (q:draft)
azinkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:travel away/go abroad/be away on a journey) (d:<a>, <zin>, travel, and <khiat>, out, written as one word: he or she goes away on a journey; {gampua azinkhiat} is travels abroad) (j:a/zin/khiat) (r:zd:19894/zd:16068) (q:draft)
azinna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:trip/journey/visit) (d:<a> and <zinna> written as one word: his or her journey, the trip someone made to a place) (j:a/zinna) (r:zd:19355/zd:25847) (q:draft)
azinpak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:be on a visit/be on a trip) (d:<azin> and <pak>, for a short while, written as one word: who is travelling there for a short time, as a tourist or visitor) (j:azin/pak) (r:zd:12364/zd:12136) (q:draft)
azinsung = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:travel/time) (w:during the visit/while travelling) (d:<azin> and <sung> written as one word: during his or their visit or journey, while travelling) (j:azin/sung) (r:zd:12546/zd:12384) (q:draft)
azipen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:family) (w:his wife) (d:<a>, <zi> and <pen> written as one word: his wife, as the one the sentence is about) (j:a/zi/pen) (r:zd:12319/zd:14658) (q:draft)
azizong = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:family) (w:his wife also/the wife too) (d:<azi>, his wife, and <zong>, also, written as one word) (j:azi/zong) (r:zd:20522/zd:11941) (q:draft)
azo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/education) (w:finish/complete/pass/win) (d:<a> and <zo> written as one word: he finishes or has completed, the one who has completed or passed, as a school grade or an interview; {azo alel} is winning and losing) (j:a/zo) (r:zd:16777/zd:14543/zd:21251) (q:draft)
azol = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:entice/lure/recruit) (d:<a> and <zol> written as one word: he or she entices, or the one who entices or lures a person) (j:a/zol) (r:zd:15824/zd:11435) (q:draft)
azol = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:smooth/sleek) (d:smooth, said of a surface, a stone or a voice; written with <a> as one word, and apart in meaning from <zol>, entice) (r:zd:21626) (q:draft, low confidence)
azom = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/media) (w:next/continuation/the following) (d:<a> and <zom> written as one word: what comes next, the continuation; also printed where an article is continued) (j:a/zom) (r:zd:24276/zd:21085) (q:draft)
azon = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:search/look for) (d:<a> and <zon> written as one word: he or they searched, and the one that is looked for) (j:a/zon) (r:zd:25616/zd:20434/zd:13106) (q:draft)
azong = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:seek/look for/search for) (d:<a> and <zong>, seek, written as one word: he or she looks for it, the one who looks for it; not <zong>, also) (j:a/zong) (r:zd:14696/zd:20406/zd:24139) (q:draft)
azongding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:to search for/in order to look for) (d:<azong>, look for it, and <ding> written as one word: the one who is to look for it; {azongding in} is in order to search for it) (j:azong/ding) (r:zd:12888/zd:17792) (q:draft)
azongin = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:searching for/looking for/in search of) (d:<azong>, he looks for it, with <in>, written as one word: while searching for or in order to look for the person or thing named before it) (j:azong/in) (r:zd:12490/zd:17323) (q:draft)
azongzong = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be looking for/keep seeking) (d:<a> and <zongzong> written as one word: is looking for, or the one who keeps seeking) (j:a/zongzong) (r:zd:16216/zd:20263) (q:draft)
azonkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:search out/search/look for and find) (d:<azon> and <khiat> written as one word: they searched it out, searched through; {azonkhiat ciangin} is when they searched) (j:azon/khiat) (r:zd:13032/zd:21406/zd:16236) (q:draft)
azonsan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/politics) (w:search for/hunt for/pursue) (d:<a> with <zon>, seek, and the ending {-san}, after or toward, written as one word: be searching for someone, as the police for a suspect; {azonsan laitak} is are now searching for) (b:zon) (r:zd:17661/zd:18091) (q:draft)
azonzon = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:keep searching/search and search) (d:<a> and <zonzon>, keep searching, written as one word: he or they keep looking for, the one being sought) (j:a/zonzon) (r:zd:15491/zd:23935) (q:draft)
azuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:sell/selling) (d:<a> and <zuak> written as one word: he sells, or the one who sells, as in {aksakan azuak te}, those who sell fried chicken) (j:a/zuak) (r:zd:14531/zd:11409/zd:25601) (q:draft)
azuakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:sale/proceeds of sale) (d:<a> and <zuakna>, selling, written as one word: their selling of a thing, and the money got from it) (j:a/zuakna) (r:zd:16257/zd:23910) (q:draft)
azuakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:seller/the man who sells) (d:<a> and <zuakpa> written as one word: the man who sells the thing named before it) (j:a/zuakpa) (r:zd:11364) (q:draft)
azuaksak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:sell/sell off) (d:<a>, <zuak>, sell, and <sak> written as one word: who sold something, who had it sold) (j:a/zuak/sak) (r:zd:16162) (q:draft, low confidence)
azuakte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:sellers/those who sell) (d:<a> and <zuakte> written as one word: the people who sell something) (j:a/zuakte) (r:zd:12299/zd:16684/zd:12685) (q:draft)
azuan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:bound for/heading for) (d:<a> and <zuan> written as one word: that is heading for the place named before it, bound for) (j:a/zuan) (r:zd:18270/zd:16598/zd:17474) (q:draft)
azuanding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:be bound for/head for) (d:<a>, <zuan>, head for, and <ding>, will, written as one word after a place name: that is going to that place, bound for it) (j:a/zuan/ding) (r:zd:16398/zd:19719) (q:draft)
azuat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:head for/be on the way to) (d:<a> and <zuat> written as one word: he, she or it heads for a place; {azuat laitak} is while on the way there) (j:a/zuat) (r:zd:16815/zd:13293) (q:draft)
azuau = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:lie/falsehood/false) (d:<a> and <zuau>, lie, written as one word: what is false, a lie, the opposite of <atakpi>; {azuau phuak} is make up a lie) (j:a/zuau) (r:zd:14728/zd:16892) (q:draft)
azui = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:follow/go along with/keep) (d:<a> and <zui> written as one word: he follows, or the one who follows; said of following a person, riding along in a vehicle and keeping a faith or a rule) (j:a/zui) (r:zd:21174/zd:17444/zd:15103) (q:draft)
azuih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:follow/obey/keep) (d:<a> and <zuih> written as one word: that he follows, that they are to obey; {azuih kul} is must obey) (j:a/zuih) (r:zd:24737/zd:24219) (q:draft)
azuihding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:to follow/to obey/to be followed) (d:<a> and <zuihding> written as one word: that he, she or they are to follow or keep, as a rule; also to go along with) (j:a/zuihding) (r:zd:17301/zd:17102) (q:draft)
azuikha = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:travel/everyday) (w:the one following/one who came along) (d:<a> and <zuikha> written as one word: the one that happened to follow behind or to be travelling along) (j:a/zuikha) (r:zd:14521/zd:17455) (q:draft)
azuilo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:not follow/not obey/not comply with) (d:<a>, <zui>, follow, and the negative <lo> written as one word: who does not follow or keep a rule; {thukhun azuilo} is one who breaks the law) (a:zui) (j:a/zui/lo) (r:zd:11778/zd:19367/zd:15822) (q:draft)
azuk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:nature) (w:rain/fall) (d:<a> and <zuk> written as one word, said of rain: {guah azuk ciangin} is when it rains) (j:a/zuk) (r:zd:15489/zd:20625/zd:19351) (q:draft)
azum = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/politics) (w:his office/her office/their office) (d:<a> and <zum>, office, written as one word: the office of the person spoken of, the place where he or she works) (j:a/zum) (r:zd:25572/zd:21981) (q:draft)
azumkhan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:his office/her office/office room) (d:<azum>, his or her office, with a second part that means room, as in Burmese: the office room of the person spoken of; {azumkhan sungah} is inside his office) (b:azum) (r:zd:19824) (q:draft)
azun = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body/health) (w:his urine/her urine) (d:<a> and <zun> urine written as one word: his, her or their urine) (j:a/zun) (r:zd:15443/zd:12347) (q:draft)
azuun = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:tend/maintain/the one who tends) (d:<a> and <zuun> written as one word: he or she tends and keeps in order, or the tending of something) (j:a/zuun) (r:zd:21102) (q:draft)
baaina = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/everyday) (w:injury/damage/harm) (d:lasting hurt or damage; usually paired with <liamna>, wound, or <supna>, loss, as in {liamna baaina}, wounds and injuries) (r:zd:23767/zd:22650) (q:draft, low confidence)
baak = (i:2) (t:n) (f:nature) (w:bat) (d:the flying animal of the night, a spelling of <bak.1>, as in {baak natna}, a disease of bats; not the counting word for a piece of meat) (s:bak) (r:zd:23727/zd:16385) (q:draft)
baan = (i:3) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:addition/besides) (d:what comes next to or on top of something, with the place marker <ah>; {tua baan ah} is besides that, in addition, and opens a sentence that adds a further point; also written <ban>) (s:ban) (r:zd:20545/zd:17339/zd:17675) (q:draft)
baang = (i:3) (t:v) (f:travel/social) (w:stop by/call in/stay) (d:of a traveller, stop at a house or a place on the way and stay there for a while; after <hong> or {ong} and a place with <ah>, as in {inn ah hong baang un}, an invitation to call in) (r:zd:20727/zd:19371/zd:21690) (q:draft)
baang = (i:4) (t:adj) (f:social) (w:worthy of/deserving) (d:after <zahtak>, respect: deserving it, so {zahtak baang} is worthy of respect; the same pattern as {ngaih baang}, lovely) (r:zd:24751/zd:19676) (q:draft, low confidence)
baangkua = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/home) (w:household/family) (d:the people of one house, often paired with <innsung> or <innkuan>) (s:innkuan) (r:zd:24452/zd:11076) (q:draft)
baanuh = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:everyday) (w:besides/in addition to) (d:<ban>, what comes on top, here written with a long vowel, with the plural marker <uh>, followed by <ah>: {a neihloh baanuh ah} is besides their not having, on top of that) (j:ban/uh) (r:zd:19239/zd:17060) (q:draft, low confidence)
baba = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:loudly/noisily/on and on) (d:placed after a verb of speaking, laughing, crying or barking: doing it aloud and without restraint, as {nui baba}, laugh out loud) (r:zd:22896/zd:16860) (q:draft, low confidence)
Babysitter = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/work) (w:babysitter/childminder) (d:a person paid to look after the small children of others; written with a capital letter and often added to explain {naukepsak}) (o:English) (r:zd:20721/zd:20540) (q:draft)
Bachelor = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:bachelor's degree/bachelor) (d:the first university degree) (o:English) (r:zd:23140/zd:16245) (q:draft, low confidence)
background = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:background/past record) (d:the past and the circumstances of a person or a thing, as checked by an employer or an authority) (o:English) (r:zd:22520/zd:13020) (q:draft)
Backpack = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/everyday) (w:backpack/rucksack) (d:a bag carried on the back, written with a capital in the articles and often followed by a Zolai word for bag) (s:thungip) (o:English) (r:zd:11495/zd:11717) (q:draft)
backup = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/it) (w:backup/reinforcement/reserve) (d:help or a spare kept ready behind the first: more police called in to help, a second power supply, a copy of computer data) (o:English) (r:zd:17069/zd:11326/zd:19554) (q:draft)
bacteria = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:bacteria) (d:very small living things, some of which cause disease; often said with <lungno> as {bacteria lungno}) (o:English) (r:zd:19330/zd:18058/zd:17335) (q:draft)
Bag = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/everyday) (w:bag) (d:a bag for carrying things; in capitals {BAG} is the abbreviation of a church name and is not this word) (o:English) (r:zd:11452/zd:12579) (q:draft)
Bagan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel/politics) (w:Bagan/Pagan) (d:old royal city of the Burmese kings on the Irrawaddy in central Myanmar, known for its many pagodas) (r:zd:8667/zd:17202) (q:draft)
Baggage = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:baggage/luggage) (d:the English word, in the articles set beside <vanpuak>, the things a traveller carries) (o:English) (r:zd:13094/zd:20416) (q:draft)
Baghdad = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:politics/travel) (w:Baghdad) (d:the capital city of Iraq) (r:zd:19279/zd:11327) (q:draft)
Bago = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city/land) (f:travel) (w:Bago) (d:a city and region of lower Myanmar north-east of Yangon, formerly Pegu) (r:zd:14726/zd:16621) (q:draft)
Bahasa = (i:1) (t:name) (f:education/social) (w:Bahasa/Malay language) (d:Malay word for language, used in {Bahasa Malaysia}, the Malay language as the national language of Malaysia) (s:Malay) (o:Malay) (r:zd:20367/zd:11837) (q:draft)
Bahmaw = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:politics/travel) (w:Bhamo) (d:town in Kachin State, Myanmar) (r:ts:8689/ts:9743) (q:draft)
baho = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:politics) (w:central) (d:central, of the government of the whole country or a central body, as in {baho kumpi}, the central government) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:16087) (q:draft, low confidence)
Bahoo = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:central body/centre/headquarters) (d:the central level of an organisation or government, as in {planning Bahoo}, the central planning body) (o:Burmese, baho) (r:zd:19166/zd:20176) (q:draft, low confidence)
Bahrain = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:politics) (w:Bahrain) (d:island country in the Persian Gulf) (r:zd:10924) (q:draft)
Bahru = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Johor Bahru) (d:second word of the name Johor Bahru, the city at the southern end of Malaysia opposite Singapore) (r:zd:12950/zd:17832) (q:draft)
baht = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:baht) (d:the money unit of Thailand, written after or before the amount) (o:Thai) (r:zd:17649/zd:13334) (q:draft)
Baibek = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (f:nature) (w:bulbul) (d:a bulbul, a common songbird) (r:zd:25288) (q:draft, low confidence)
baih = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:early/soon/quickly) (d:placed after a verb: early, soon or quickly; {tho baih} is rise early) (s:tungin/pak) (q:draft)
baih = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:easy) (d:not hard to do; {baih zaw} means easier) (s:ol) (a:haksa/hak) (q:draft)
baihding = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:will soon/will quickly/will easily) (d:<baih>, soon or easily, and the future marker <ding>, written as one word after a verb: will soon or easily do or become) (j:baih/ding) (r:zd:21075/zd:22416) (q:draft)
Baihlamtak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:easily/with ease) (d:<baihlam>, easy, with <tak>, which makes an adverb of manner: in an easy way; found here in the book title {Baihlamtak a Nalianpi Sepna}, doing great work easily) (s:baihlam-a) (r:zd:21110) (q:draft, low confidence)
baihlo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:not easy/difficult/hard) (d:<baih>, easy, and <lo>, not, written as one word) (j:baih/lo) (r:zd:20572/zd:21848) (q:draft)
baihmahmah = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:very easy) (d:<baih>, easy, and <mahmah>, very, written as one word) (j:baih/mahmah) (r:zd:16317/zd:12752) (q:draft)
baihno = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:easy) (d:<baih>, easy, with a second syllable as in <olno>; found as {baihno takin}, easily, and paired as {olno tak leh baihno takin}, easily and without effort) (s:olno) (a:haksa) (b:baih) (r:zd:16779/zd:20560) (q:draft)
baihsa = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:find easy/think easy) (d:<baih>, easy, with <sa>, feel or consider, placed after a verb: find the action easy to do; without the <a> and <in> of {a baihsa-in}, in readiness) (r:zd:8668/zd:25115/zd:16385) (q:draft)
baihsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:make easy/make likely/bring on easily) (d:<baih>, easy, with <sak>, cause: make a thing easy or quick to happen; with <lo>, not treat a thing as easy, not do it lightly) (j:baih/sak) (r:zd:20761/zd:21168) (q:draft)
baihtak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:easily/readily/without difficulty) (d:<baih> and <tak> written as one word, mostly as {baihtak in}: easily, without trouble or delay) (j:baih/tak) (r:zd:24047/zd:21259/zd:23655) (q:draft)
bail = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:bail) (d:money or a pledge on which an arrested person is set free until the trial; {bail tawh khahkhia} is release on bail) (o:English) (r:zd:15499/zd:13209/zd:12546) (q:draft)
baina = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:loss/damage/harm) (d:paired with <supna>, loss, as {supna baina} or {ih sup ih baina}: the loss and damage that comes from war, quarrels or a decision, with no thought of bodily laming) (r:zd:20454/zd:16404/zd:21080) (q:draft)
Balai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:police station) (d:Malay word for a hall or station, used by Zomi in Malaysia for a police station, in full {Balai Polis}, usually with the name of the place) (o:Malay) (r:zd:23629) (q:draft, low confidence)
Balakong = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Balakong) (d:a township in Selangor, Malaysia, near Kajang, where Zomi live and work) (r:zd:14692) (q:draft)
balance = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/politics) (w:balance) (d:a state in which things are of equal weight or in the right proportion; also used as a verb, be or keep in balance) (o:English) (r:zd:23780) (q:draft, low confidence)
Balcony = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:balcony) (d:a platform with a railing on the outside of an upper floor of a building) (o:English) (r:zd:12240/zd:16673) (q:draft)
Bali = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Bali) (d:island of Indonesia) (r:zd:15382/zd:20369) (q:draft)
Balloon = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:balloon) (d:a balloon, the toy or the large one that carries people through the air) (o:English) (r:zd:15592/zd:17664) (q:draft, low confidence)
Baltimore = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Baltimore) (d:city in the state of Maryland in the United States) (r:zd:11899) (q:draft)
Bamar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:politics/social) (w:Bamar/Burman) (d:the majority people of Myanmar, in Zolai also called {Kawl}) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:20348) (q:draft)
Bamaw = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel/politics) (w:Bhamo) (d:town in Kachin State, Myanmar, on the Irrawaddy river) (r:ts:12506/ts:8689) (q:draft)
banban = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:one after another/in turn/in order/successively) (d:usually as {a banban in}: one after the other, each in its turn) (r:zd:23129/ts:6835/zd:23394) (q:draft)
Band = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/social) (w:band/music group) (d:a group of musicians who play together) (o:English) (r:zd:16337/zd:21550) (q:draft)
Bandage = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:bandage) (d:a strip of cloth wrapped round a wound; {Bandage tawh kituam} is be wrapped in a bandage) (o:English) (r:zd:11938/zd:12364) (q:draft)
Bandung = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Bandung) (d:city in West Java, Indonesia) (r:zd:16702/zd:17450) (q:draft)
bang = (i:1) (t:det) (f:everyday) (w:what) (d:Question word, what; it also begins the phrases {bang hangin}, why, and {bang ci}, how.) (r:44.21.22)
bang = (i:3) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:about/approximately/or so) (d:placed after a number or an amount, often after <val>, to show that it is not exact: {100 val bang} is something over 100) (r:ts:3284/ts:1428/ts:479) (q:draft)
bang ahia = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:what is it/what is) (d:<bang>, what, and <ahia>, the sentence-final question word: closes a question that asks what the thing named before it is or means; after a quoted word with <cih> or <acih> it asks what that word means) (r:zd:24068/zd:16777/zd:16897) (q:draft)
bang hang = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:why) (d:asks the reason, often as {bang hang hiam}) (r:zai:why) (q:draft)
bang hanga = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:why/for what reason) (d:<bang>, what, and <hanga>, because of: opens a question about the reason, which usually ends in <hiam>; also the reason why, before a clause closed by <cih>) (s:banghangin/bang hang) (r:zd:16210/zd:9448) (q:draft)
bang phading = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/media) (w:about/approximately/an estimated) (d:<bang>, here about or as much as and not the question word what, and <phading>, will come to: placed after a number or a measure when the amount is an estimate, it comes to about so many; <cihi> or {kici hi}, it is said, often follows) (r:zd:12519/zd:12307) (q:draft)
bangaa = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:like/as/according to) (d:<bang>, like, and the linking <aa>, written as one word after a noun or clause: in the way of, of the kind of; {tua bangaa} is such, in that way) (j:bang/aa) (r:zd:21796/zd:19683/zd:21869) (q:draft)
bangah = (i:3) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:in for example/in such as) (d:after the name of a place or thing and not after a number: in that one taken as an example, as {America bangah}, in America for instance; <bang>, like, with the place marker <ah>) (r:zd:19775/zd:21848/zd:23603) (q:draft)
Bangalore = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Bangalore/Bengaluru) (d:city in the state of Karnataka in southern India, where many Zomi study theology) (r:zd:10812/zd:15803) (q:draft)
bangbang hileh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:anyway/in any case/whatever the case) (d:<bangbang>, whatever, and <hileh>, if it is: whatever it may be; stands at the head of a sentence and sets aside what was said before, in any case, anyway) (r:zd:23037/zd:22784) (q:draft)
bangbanga = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:just as/according to/however) (d:<bangbang>, just as, with the linking ending <a> before a verb: in whatever way; {ut bangbanga} is just as one pleases) (b:bangbang) (r:zd:9429/zd:9434) (q:draft)
bangbek = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:only about/just about/no more than) (d:after a number or an amount, <bang> in its meaning about, with <bek>, only: only about that many and no more, as in {mi 2 bangbek}, only about two people) (r:zd:21388/zd:17694/zd:11548) (q:draft)
bangci = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:how) (d:Question word, how, in what way; also with the ending <in>, {bangci-in}.) (s:koici)
bangci = (i:3) (t:det) (f:everyday) (w:what kind of/what sort of) (d:before a noun, asking about its nature and not about a way of doing: {bangci mi}, what kind of person; before a verb the word means how) (r:zd:22487) (q:draft, low confidence)
bangci bangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:how/in what way/by what means) (d:<bangci>, how, and <bangin>, in the manner of: a fuller form of the question word how, asking for the way or the means; it opens a direct question or stands before the verb of an indirect one that ends in <cih>) (s:bangci) (r:zd:25711/zd:13171/zd:15243) (q:draft)
bangcia = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:why) for what reason or purpose
bangciang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:how far/to what extent/how much) (d:<bang> and <ciang> written as one word, a question word: up to what point, how far, to what extent) (j:bang/ciang) (r:zd:16442/zd:21456) (q:draft)
bangcibang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:how/in what way/what kind of) (d:<bangci> and <bang> written as one word: how, in what way, of what kind; often {bangcibang in}) (j:bangci/bang) (r:zd:12567/zd:18183/zd:11148) (q:draft)
bangcibangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:how/in what way) (d:<bangci>, how, and <bangin>, like, written as one word: in what way, by what means) (j:bangci/bangin) (r:zd:21135/zd:10793) (q:draft)
bangciciang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:how far/to what extent/to what outcome) (d:<bangci>, how, and <ciang>, as far as, written as one word: a question about how far a matter has gone or how it will turn out) (j:bangci/ciang) (r:zd:15425/zd:16580/zd:11551) (q:draft)
bangcidan = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:how/in what way/what kind of) (d:<bangci>, how, and <dan>, manner, written as one word: in what manner; before a noun, what kind of) (j:bangci/dan) (r:zd:19111/zd:15541/zd:16216) (q:draft)
bangcihding = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:what to do/how to do) (d:<bangcih>, how, and <ding> written as one word: what is to be done, how one should act) (j:bangcih/ding) (r:zd:18110/zd:11729/zd:12217) (q:draft)
bangcihiam = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:how is it) (d:<bangci>, how, and the question particle <hiam> written as one word: how is it, how is someone or something doing) (j:bangci/hiam) (r:zd:17818/zd:12992) (q:draft)
bangdan = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:everyday) (w:like/as/in the manner of) (d:<bang>, like, and <dan>, manner, written as one word after a noun or a clause and mostly followed by <in>: in the way of, like; {tua bangdan} is that kind of thing) (j:bang/dan) (r:zd:11642/zd:18893/zd:22116) (q:draft)
bangdan = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:how/in what way) (d:question word, <bang>, what, and <dan>, manner, written as one word and mostly followed by <in>: in what way) (s:bangci) (j:bang/dan) (r:zd:22643/zd:15727) (q:draft)
bangdanin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:like/as/in the manner of) (d:<bang>, like, and <danin>, in the way, written as one word after a noun: in the same way as, as if it were) (j:bang/danin) (r:zd:12240/zd:19355/zd:19902) (q:draft)
bangdanin = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:how/in what way) (d:<bang>, what, and <danin>, in the way, written as one word in a question: in what way, how) (j:bang/danin) (r:zd:19579) (q:draft, low confidence)
bangdante = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:such ones/the likes of/things like) (d:<bangdan>, like, with the plural <te>: those of that kind, people or things like the one named before) (b:bangdan) (r:zd:23089) (q:draft)
