beubau = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (d:descriptive word placed after a verb for something thick, puffed or bulging all over, as cheeks full of food, thick clothing or a flushed face) (r:zd:24310/zd:19812) (q:draft, low confidence)
Bhopal = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Bhopal) (d:city in central India, capital of the state of Madhya Pradesh, known for the gas disaster of 1984) (r:zd:12398/zd:19277) (q:draft)
Bhutan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel/politics) (w:Bhutan) (d:country in the Himalaya between India and China, often written {Bhutan gam}) (r:zd:24227) (q:draft)
biabua = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:all over/everywhere/in profusion) (d:placed after a verb or describing word: spread or smeared all over a place, as flowers in bloom, notices put up or a mouth red with betel) (r:zd:19812/zd:11553) (q:draft, low confidence)
biakinn = (i:2) (t:n) (f:social) (w:church/church building) (d:a house of worship, the building where a congregation meets) (r:zai:church) (q:draft)
biakinnpi = (i:2) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:cathedral/main church) (d:the large or main church building of a town or a denomination today, as after a church name or after the English word cathedral; not the temple of Jerusalem) (r:zd:14765/zd:12130/zd:21027) (q:draft)
