biaknasia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:religious teacher/cleric/minister) (d:<biakna>, religion, with <sia>, teacher: a teacher or leader of a religion, said of Christian ministers and of Muslim clerics alike) (j:biakna/sia) (r:zd:20363/zd:17277) (q:draft)
biakpiak = (i:2) (t:v) (f:religion) (w:worship/hold a service) (d:worship God together with song and prayer, as a church does on Sunday, with no offering of an animal; also names the service itself, as in {biakpiak kikhopna}, worship service, {biakpiak hun}, time of worship, and {biakpiak zia}, form of worship) (r:zd:24186/zd:20786/zd:24194) (q:draft)
biakpiakna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:worship service/worship/service) (d:a gathering in which people worship God together, as in a church; this is the present-day use, with <kinei> or <nei> for holding a service and {biakpiakna munte} for places of worship, not a thing given to God) (r:zd:25265/zd:20016/zd:24217) (q:draft)
bial = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:constituency/district/area) (d:an area marked off as one unit, above all the area that elects one member of a parliament or assembly) (r:zd:21137/zd:11720) (q:draft)
bialbual = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:complicated/confused/mixed up/patchy) (d:not plain or of one kind: tangled, mixed or unclear; {kitel bialbual lo} is not clearly understood) (r:ts:8105/zd:11195) (q:draft, low confidence)
biangbuang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:hurriedly/in a rush/hastily/frantically) (d:placed after a verb: doing it in a great hurry, in haste and without care) (r:zd:22658/zd:11110/zd:20297) (q:draft)
