Bihar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel) (w:Bihar) (d:a state in the east of India) (r:zd:13195/zd:12403) (q:draft)
bilbel = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:in fact/just/as it turned out) (d:placed after a verb or a negated verb, before <hi> or <in>: stresses that this is simply how it is or how it turned out; {omlo bilbel hi} is there turned out to be none) (r:zd:14591/zd:17994/zd:23616) (q:draft, low confidence)
bilbial = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:all mixed together/jumbled) (d:placed after a verb or after <teng>, all these: mixed up together, in a tangle, all of it at once; {hih teng bilbial kawmkal ah} is in the midst of all this) (r:zd:22606/zd:16951) (q:draft, low confidence)
