buaihuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/social) (w:troublesome/bothersome/complicated) (d:<buai>, be troubled, with <huai>, causing that feeling: causing trouble or bother; {buaihuai sa} is find it a bother) (b:buai) (r:zd:21605/zd:24396/zd:23087) (q:draft)
buailai = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:politics/time) (w:during the unrest/at the time of the trouble) (d:<buai>, be in turmoil, and <lai>, here the time when, written as one word after a year or place: at the time of the unrest there; before <mahmah> it means being very busy) (j:buai/lai) (r:zd:22981/zd:22641) (q:draft)
buailawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:be troubled by/suffer trouble) (d:get into trouble or be kept busy as a result of something; <buai>, be troubled, with <lawh>, be affected by) (b:buai) (r:zd:19912/zd:21459) (q:draft)
buailo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:not be involved with/not bother with) (d:<buai>, here be busy or concerned with, and <lo>, not, written as one word, placed after <tawh>: not be occupied or involved with something) (j:buai/lo) (r:zd:22592) (q:draft)
buailua = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be too busy/be too taken up) (d:<buai>, be busy or troubled, and <lua>, too much, written as one word: be too busy, be too much taken up with something, which is marked with <tawh>) (j:buai/lua) (r:zd:23985/zd:22779) (q:draft)
buaimahmah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:be very busy/be much occupied) (d:<buai> and <mahmah>, very, written as one word: be very busy with something, or be in great trouble or turmoil) (j:buai/mahmah) (r:zd:17551/zd:15216/zd:11821) (q:draft)
buaina thupiang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/social) (w:incident/disturbance) (d:<buaina>, trouble, and <thupiang>, happening: a fixed term of news reports for an incident, a fight, robbery or other disturbance; usually after <hih> or <tuabang>, and sometimes followed by the English word Incident) (r:zd:21601/zd:17947) (q:draft)
buainate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:troubles/problems/conflicts) (d:plural of <buaina>: troubles and difficulties in life, and unrest or conflicts in a country) (b:buaina) (r:zd:23975/zd:17055) (q:draft)
buainavai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/media) (w:incident/trouble/dispute) (d:<buaina> and <vai> written as one word: a matter of trouble, an incident or dispute that is reported or looked into) (j:buaina/vai) (r:zd:18145/zd:16026) (q:draft)
buaipih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:attend to/deal with/be busy with) (d:<buai>, be occupied, with <pih>, together with or for: take trouble over a matter or over a person in need, as a sick person or a prisoner) (b:buai) (r:zd:14615/zd:16216) (q:draft)
buaipihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:concern/trouble taken/matter dealt with) (d:<buaipih>, be busy with, with the noun suffix <na>: what one is occupied with or takes trouble over, a problem that has to be dealt with) (b:buaipih) (r:zd:24168/zd:23201) (q:draft)
buakhuan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:flock to/swarm/throng) (d:come or go in great numbers and with force toward a person, a place or a cause, of a crowd that rushes to support or to attack) (r:zd:12487/zd:25580) (q:draft, low confidence)
bualpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature) (w:pool/large pool/lake) (d:<bual>, pool, with <pi>, great: a large pool or lake; also used of a field of activity that people enter) (b:bual) (r:zd:17620) (q:draft, low confidence)
buan = (i:2) (t:v) (f:social) (w:rape) (d:a verb, not the word for mud: force a person to have sex, often with <zawhthawh thutawh>, by force; {buan thuak} is be raped) (r:zd:26838/zd:12979) (q:draft)
buan = (i:3) (t:v) (f:everyday/body) (w:wrestle/grapple) (d:take hold of someone and struggle with him body to body, as Jacob with God; {ki buan} is wrestle with each other, also of two wills that are in conflict) (r:zd:10963/zd:23022) (q:draft, low confidence)
buan athuak = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:social/media) (w:raped/sexually assaulted) (d:<buan>, here a verb, seize and force, rape, not the noun for mud, and <athuak>, the one who suffers it: placed before the word for the person, as {buan athuak numeino}, the girl who was raped; a term of crime reports) (r:zd:12979/zd:11484) (q:draft)
buanciim = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature) (w:mud/slush/mire) (d:thin wet mud, as left by a flood or on a road in the rainy season; also said of flowing lava) (r:zd:16724/zd:20456) (q:draft)
buanden = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:rape repeatedly/keep raping) (d:<buan>, here in the sense seize and violate a person sexually, and <den>, continually, written as one word) (j:buan/den) (r:zd:15082) (q:draft, low confidence)
buangawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/media) (w:rape/assault/maul) (d:a verb spelled like <buan>, mud, but meaning seize and force, with <gawp>, violently: assault brutally; with <zawhthawh thutawh>, by force, rape; of an animal, maul) (r:zd:19536/zd:25043) (q:draft, low confidence)
buangleh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:unless/except if) (d:<buang> and <leh>, if, written as one word after a negative, as in {ahih kei buangleh}: unless it is, except in the case of) (j:buang/leh) (r:ts:301/zd:16523) (q:draft)
buangnai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/work) (w:rubber/elastic) (d:rubber, the stretchy material of tyres, erasers and elastic bands; {buangnai thautang} is a rubber bullet) (r:ts:9171/zd:22451) (q:draft)
buanhuan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/media) (w:rape/gang-rape) (d:force a person to have sex; in news reports mostly of several men together or one after another; built on a verb for rape that is spelled like <buan>, mud, but is a different word) (r:zd:19540/zd:22813) (q:draft, low confidence)
buanlak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature) (w:mud/quagmire/muddy ground) (d:<buan>, mud, with <lak>, the midst: a stretch of soft wet mud, a place where one sinks in) (r:zd:15405/zd:22557) (q:draft)
