christian biakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:Christianity/the Christian religion) (d:<Christian> and <biakna>, religion: the Christian religion, Christianity) (r:zd:20667/ts:7051) (q:draft)
christian upna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:Christianity/Christian faith) (d:the English word Christian with <upna>, faith: the Christian faith, Christianity as a religion; {i Christian upna} is our Christian faith) (r:zd:23086/zd:15274/zd:16640) (q:draft)
Christmas = (i:1) (t:name) (f:religion/time) (w:Christmas) (d:the Christian festival of the birth of Jesus, kept on 25 December) (o:English) (r:zd:21659/zd:24112) (q:draft)
Churachandpur = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel/politics) (w:Churachandpur) (d:town and district in the south of Manipur, India, home of many Zomi; the town is also called Lamka) (r:ts:1734) (q:draft)
ci = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:say/tell) (d:say; stands after the words quoted, as in {a ci hi}, he said, and {ci-in}, saying) (r:1.21.24)
ci = (i:4) (t:n) (f:food) (w:salt) (r:zai:salt) (q:draft)
cia = (i:2) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:indeed/you know) (d:sentence-final word of colloquial speech that gives a statement emphasis or feeling, often followed by <maw>; not the {cia} of size, which follows a noun) (r:zd:22775/zd:25714) (q:draft, low confidence)
ciacia = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:everyday) (w:as big as/the size of/about the size of) (d:<cia>, as big as, said twice and placed after a thing or a measure: of just that size, each about that big; {mihing ciacia} is life-size) (b:cia) (r:zd:19242/zd:15689) (q:draft)
ciah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:return/go home/go back) (d:go back to one's home or to the place one came from) (s:ciahkik/paikik/kilehkik) (r:40.9.7)
ciahding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:to return/going home) (d:<ciah> and <ding> written as one word: to go home, about to return) (j:ciah/ding) (r:zd:12628/zd:11529/zd:15344) (q:draft)
ciahkhiatding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/politics) (w:to leave/to depart/will leave) (d:<ciahkhiat>, leave, and <ding> written as one word: to leave or go away from a country or place, mostly of what is ordered, allowed or forbidden) (j:ciahkhiat/ding) (r:zd:12005/zd:11627/zd:19442) (q:draft)
ciahkik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:return/go back/come back) (d:{Ciah}, return, with <kik>, back or again: go or come back to where one was.) (s:ciah/paikik/kilehkik) (b:ciah) (r:1.3.19)
ciahkikding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:will return/to go back) (d:<ciahkik>, return, and <ding>, the marker of what is to come, written as one word: will go back, or to go back) (j:ciahkik/ding) (r:zd:11011/zd:16257) (q:draft)
ciahlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:not go home/not return) (d:<ciah> and <lo> written as one word: not go back home) (j:ciah/lo) (r:zd:16173/zd:20260) (q:draft)
ciahna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/travel) (w:return/going home/homecoming) (d:<ciah>, go home, with the noun suffix {-na}: the going home or the way home; paired with <hawhna> or <kuanna> for going out and coming back) (b:ciah) (r:zd:14992/zd:24310/zd:13255) (q:draft)
ciahta = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:go home now/have gone home) (d:<ciah>, go home, and <ta>, now or already, written as one word) (j:ciah/ta) (r:zd:25908/zd:19451) (q:draft)
ciahte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/travel) (w:those who return/returnees) (d:<ciah>, go home, and the plural <te>, written as one word: the people who come or go back home, as in {gamdang pan hong ciahte}, those who came home from abroad) (j:ciah/te) (r:zd:23935/zd:24393) (q:draft)
ciahthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:be able to return/can go home) (d:<ciah>, return or go home, and <thei>, able, written as one word) (j:ciah/thei) (r:zd:15473/zd:23737) (q:draft)
ciai = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:sentence-final expression of colloquial speech, from <ci>, say: it adds feeling to a statement or a remark, much like indeed or I must say) (r:zd:12432/zd:20545) (q:draft, low confidence)
ciaiciai = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:nature/everyday) (d:placed after a verb of sounding such as <ham> or <khuang>: with a shrill sound that goes on and on, of insects humming or singing) (r:zd:22928/zd:26097) (q:draft, low confidence)
ciakngeingai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/media) (w:clamour/make an uproar/chatter noisily) (d:<ciak> with the expressive word <ngeingai>, written as one word: many people talking loudly at once, in merriment or in heated comment and argument) (j:ciak/ngeingai) (r:zd:15425/zd:19277) (q:draft)
cial = (i:3) (t:v) (f:social) (w:invite/ask/call on) (d:ask someone to come, to take part or to do something, with no thought of pay, as a singer to sing or a guest to visit; in appeals {kong cial uh hi}, we call on you) (r:zd:16387/zd:23641/zd:23422) (q:draft)
cialna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:social) (w:invitation/appeal/call/request) (d:a public invitation or appeal asking people to come, pray or take part, not hiring for pay; {cialna nei} is make an appeal) (r:zd:15905/zd:23930/ts:689) (q:draft)
cialpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:crusade/revival meeting/evangelistic meeting) (d:a large series of Christian meetings held to preach salvation and renew the churches; {cialpi bawl} is hold a crusade) (r:zd:9249/zd:23215/zd:9245) (q:draft)
cialpite = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:crusades/revival meetings) (d:plural of <cialpi>: the evangelistic meetings of a preacher) (b:cialpi) (r:zd:9232/zd:9262) (q:draft)
ciam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:promise/swear/vow) (d:Give one’s word or swear an oath; often with <thu>, as in {thu ciam}, make a promise on oath) (s:kiciam/kamciam) (q:draft)
ciamnuih = (i:2) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:joke/tease) (d:used as a verb, with the prefix <ki> as {ki ciamnuih}: joke with one another in fun) (r:zd:22802/zd:24462) (q:draft)
ciamtehkhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media) (w:one recorded as/one regarded as) (d:<ciamteh>, record, and <khat>, one, written as one word; after <aki> it means one that is recorded or regarded as what is named before it) (j:ciamteh/khat) (r:zd:16959/zd:20000) (q:draft)
ciamtehphot = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/politics) (w:record for now/note provisionally) (d:<ciamteh>, record, and <phot>, for the time being, written as one word: put on record as such for now, until more is known) (j:ciamteh/phot) (r:zd:17421/zd:19871) (q:draft)
cian = (i:3) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:remain/be left) (d:be left over or still there after the rest is gone, often with <lai>, still, or <nawnlo>, no longer; not the adverb that follows a verb of knowing or saying) (r:ts:7320/ts:5105) (q:draft, low confidence)
ciang bekin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:only when/only after/not until/only then) (d:<ciang>, when or up to, and <bekin>, only: closes a clause or a phrase of time and says that what follows happens only when that has come about, often with <pan> in the main clause, only then begin to; after a noun it is only with or only as far as that) (r:zd:20742/ts:3280/zd:25216) (q:draft)
ciangaa = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday/time) (w:when/after) (d:<ciang> with the marker <a> written <aa>, used like <ciangin>: when, at the time that, after) (j:ciang/aa) (r:zd:19166/zd:22922) (q:draft)
ciangbang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:about/approximately/up to about) (d:<ciang>, up to, and <bang>, about, written as one word after a number or amount: roughly that much, up to about) (j:ciang/bang) (r:zd:21006/zd:20747/zd:20959) (q:draft)
ciangbek = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:only then/only when) (d:<ciang> in its meaning when, with <bek>, only: not until that has happened, mostly as {tua ciangbek}, only then, where the other sense sets a limit that is not passed) (r:zd:15720/zd:11955) (q:draft)
ciangciangah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time/everyday) (w:up to/as far as/until) (d:<ciangciang> and <ah> written as one word: as far as a point reaches; {tu ciangciangah} is up to now, {abei sa ciangciangah} in time past, and after a verb as far as one can) (j:ciangciang/ah) (r:zd:21941/zd:9430/zd:25947) (q:draft)
ciangciangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time/everyday) (w:up to/as far as/until) (d:<ciangciang> and <in> written as one word: right up to a day or point; {tu ni ciangciangin} is up to today, and {a ciangciangin} is by its levels or bounds) (j:ciangciang/in) (r:zd:20518/zd:22046/zd:19241) (q:draft)
ciangdong = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:time/everyday) (w:until/up to/as far as) (d:<ciang> and <dong> written as one word after a time, a place or a clause: right up to that point) (j:ciang/dong) (r:zd:15743/zd:20003/zd:24672) (q:draft)
ciangh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday/time) (j:ciang) (r:zd:20647/zd:20035) (q:draft)
ciangin = (i:3) (t:conj) (f:everyday/time) (w:and/when) (d:joins a clause to what follows: when or after this happened, and then) as in Let there be light, and there was light"
ciangin = (i:4) (t:ppm) (f:time) (w:at/in/by) (d:placed after a word of time such as <hun>, <ni> or <kum> to say when something happens: at that time, on that day, in or by that year) (r:ts:6443/ts:2731/ts:479) (q:draft)
cianginzong = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday/time) (w:even when/also when) (d:<ciangin>, when, and <zong>, also, written as one word: even when, also at the time when; after a day or time, on that day too) (j:ciangin/zong) (r:zd:17143/zd:15764/zd:11303) (q:draft)
ciangkhat = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:to some extent/to a certain degree) (d:<ciang>, as far as, and <khat>, one, written as one word: up to a certain point, to some extent; the same letters can also be {ciang khat}, one stick) (j:ciang/khat) (r:zd:17990/zd:24630) (q:draft, low confidence)
ciangtanding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:to limit/will limit/to be limited) (d:<ciangtan>, set a limit, and <ding> written as one word: to limit, or the limiting of, a power or a number) (j:ciangtan/ding) (r:zd:17102) (q:draft)
ciangtanh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:limit/restrict/fix) (d:set a limit or a fixed measure for something; with <ki>, be limited or fixed; the noun is written <ciangtan>) (r:zd:24121/zd:22827) (q:draft)
ciangtanna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:limit/limitation/restriction) (d:<ciangtan>, set a limit, with the noun suffix <na>: a limit that is set, a restriction; {ciangtanna omlo in} is without limit) (b:ciangtan) (r:zd:23365/zd:22704/zd:22446) (q:draft)
ciangtawh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:with a stick/with a rod) (d:<ciang>, here stick or rod, and <tawh>, with, written as one word: with a stick, as in {ciangtawh sat}, beat with a stick) (r:zd:11403/zd:15767) (q:draft)
ciangtawh = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:to the extent of/as far as) (d:<ciang>, as far as, and <tawh>, with, written as one word after a phrase: with as much as that, to that extent) (j:ciang/tawh) (r:zd:20481/zd:23742) (q:draft, low confidence)
ciangtawn = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/home) (w:stick/rod/pole) (d:a long piece of wood held in the hand, used to strike, push or lever) (r:zd:15431/zd:15920) (q:draft)
ciangzong = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday/time) (w:even when/also when) (d:<ciang>, when, with <zong>, also, written as one word after a clause: when that happens too, even when) (j:ciang/zong) (r:zd:23977/zd:16114) (q:draft)
cianlai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:remain/be left) (d:still be there after the rest is gone or done; {a cianlai} is the rest, those who remain) (s:omlai) (r:zd:22586/zd:19185/zd:22435) (q:draft)
cianna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:media/everyday) (w:clarification/exact statement/detail) (d:<cian>, clearly and thoroughly, with the noun suffix <na>, after a verb of saying, asking or looking: the doing of it clearly and in full, {gen cianna} an exact statement, {hilh cianna} a clear explanation, {et cianna} a close examination; not the building of a wall) (r:ts:4369/zd:24399/zd:15493) (q:draft)
ciantak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:clearly/exactly/definitely/for certain) (d:<cian>, clear and definite as in <kician>, with <tak>; mostly followed by <in> and also written {ki ciantak in}: clearly, exactly, with certainty) (r:zd:24852/zd:21908/zd:20030) (q:draft)
ciapteh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/education) (j:ciamteh) (r:zd:21083/zd:20864/zd:26092) (q:draft)
ciaptehding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/education) (w:to note/should record/will be fixed) (d:<ciapteh>, note down or mark, and <ding>, will, written as one word: something to take note of, to be recorded or set) (j:ciapteh/ding) (r:zd:10881) (q:draft)
ciaptehna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:education/media) (w:record/note/register) (d:what is written down to be kept or remembered, a record or note, and the standing that is so recorded, as in {ciaptehna ngah}, be put on record as; not a mark or seal on a thing) (r:zd:15099/zd:22650) (q:draft)
ciaptehnate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/education) (w:marks/records/notes) (d:plural of <ciaptehna>: marks or signs put on something, and things written down as a record) (b:ciaptehna) (r:zd:23670/zd:12370) (q:draft)
ciaptehsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:record for/register/have recorded/note for) (d:<ciapteh>, note or record, with <sak>, for another or cause: put something on record for someone, register a person as something, or have it recorded) (j:ciamtehsak) (r:zd:22877/zd:22986) (q:draft)
ciatciat = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:each/every one/each in turn) (d:placed after a verb, or a noun such as <mihing>, like single <ciat>: every one does the thing, each for himself, where the Bible sense is each one’s own kind or land) (s:ciat) (r:ts:261/zd:23348) (q:draft)
ciatding = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:each should/each will) (d:<ciat> and <ding> written as one word after a verb: each one should or will do it) (j:ciat/ding) (r:zd:15726/zd:19805) (q:draft)
ciatni = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:let us each/let us all) (d:<ciat>, each, and the verb ending {-ni}, let us, written as one word after a verb: let each of us do it) (j:ciat/ni) (r:zd:14554/zd:20440/zd:19249) (q:draft)
ciatpan = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:from each/each from) (d:<ciat>, each, and <pan.1>, from, written as one word after a noun: from each of them, each from its own) (j:ciat/pan) (r:zd:24234/zd:25097) (q:draft)
ciatta = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/religion) (w:each one/every one) (d:<ciat>, each, and the particle <ta> written as one word, placed after a verb in a wish or request, before <hen> or <un>: may each one, let each one) (j:ciat/ta) (r:zd:22289/zd:25027) (q:draft)
Ciau = (i:1) (t:name) (c:river/place) (f:travel/nature) (w:Ciau/Tiau) (d:the river on the border between Chin State in Myanmar and Mizoram in India, and the border crossing near Rih that is reached by the road from Tedim) (r:zd:17530/zd:20760) (q:draft, low confidence)
ciauciau = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:little by little/bit by bit) (d:placed after a verb: the action is done in small repeated bits and keeps on, as birds chirping, an animal nibbling or money saved a little at a time) (r:zd:9211/zd:21246/zd:14563) (q:draft)
cibang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:such as/like that/of that kind) (d:<ci>, say, with <bang>, like, written as one word: of the kind just named, and the like; {bang cibang} is how, in what way, and {tua cibang in} is in that way) (j:ci/bang) (r:zd:23394/zd:24036/zd:15671) (q:draft)
cibawk = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/body) (w:lump/swelling/tumor) (d:a lump or swelling that forms on or in the body) (r:zd:14650/zd:19337) (q:draft)
cibilbel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media) (w:it is said/reportedly) (d:<ci>, say, and <bilbel> written as one word, closing a news report: it is said that, as it turned out, mostly of harm that did not happen) (j:ci/bilbel) (r:zd:19394/zd:11148/zd:15403) (q:draft, low confidence)
cibuang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:say after all/as the saying goes) (d:<ci>, say, and the particle <buang> written as one word after quoted words, mostly as {cibuang hiven}: as they do say, as the saying goes) (j:ci/buang) (r:zd:19166) (q:draft, low confidence)
cicitciat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media) (w:say/report) (d:<ci>, say, with an expressive ending, closing a sentence that reports what someone says or what is being told; the exact shade of the ending is not certain) (r:zd:16259) (q:draft, low confidence)
cidam = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:health/everyday) (w:healthy/well) (d:in good health; {cidam lo} is sick) (a:cina) (q:draft)
cidamlo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:health) (w:unwell/sick/unhealthy) (d:<cidam>, healthy, and <lo>, not, written as one word: not in good health; {lungsim cidamlo} is mentally ill) (s:cina) (j:cidam/lo) (r:zd:14597/zd:13110/zd:25215) (q:draft)
cidamlohna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:illness/ill health/sickness) (d:<cidam>, healthy, and <lohna>, the state of not being, written as one word: the state of not being well) (a:cidamna) (j:cidam/lohna) (r:zd:18882/zd:21198) (q:draft)
cidamna lamsang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/politics) (w:health sector/field of health/health matters) (d:<cidamna>, health, with <lamsang>, side: the health side of public life, the health sector; with <ah>, in the field of health, and before a noun, health as in health work or health benefit) (r:zd:19118/zd:19818) (q:draft)
cidamnading = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:health) (w:for health/in order to be healthy) (d:<cidam>, healthy, and <nading>, for, written as one word: for the sake of health, so as to be well) (j:cidam/nading) (r:zd:14665/zd:11833) (q:draft)
cidamtak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:health) (w:healthily/in good health/safely) (d:<cidam>, healthy, and <tak> written as one word, usually followed by <in>: in good health, safe and sound) (j:cidam/tak) (r:zd:17112/zd:17135) (q:draft)
cidan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:way/manner) (d:<ci> and <dan>, way, written as one word: the way something is or is done; {bang cidan} is how, of what kind, and {hih cidan in} is in this way) (j:ci/dan) (r:zd:11862/zd:15424) (q:draft, low confidence)
ciden = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:keep saying/always say) (d:<ci>, say, and <den>, always, written as one word: say again and again or as a habit) (j:ci/den) (r:zd:11278/zd:23676) (q:draft)
ciding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:will say/would say/should say) (d:<ci>, say, with <ding>, will, written as one word: will say, is to say; in a question, shall one say) (j:ci/ding) (r:zd:23676/zd:17383) (q:draft)
Cigarette = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/health) (w:cigarette) (d:a cigarette; also explained as <zatep>) (o:English) (r:zd:17301/zd:12817) (q:draft)
cih = (i:2) (t:conj) (f:everyday/media) (w:that) (d:placed after a statement it marks it as what is said, heard or known, as in {cih kiza hi}, it is heard that, and {cih thu}, the news that) (r:ts:6954/ts:6447/ts:8304) (q:draft)
cih kimukhia = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:media) (w:it was found that/it turned out that/it was discovered that) (d:<cih>, the marker that closes what is said, and <kimukhia>, be found out: placed after a whole clause and before the final <hi>, it presents the clause as what an inquiry, a test or a count has brought to light) (r:zd:24691/zd:19552/zd:20466) (q:draft)
cih kiza = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:media) (w:it is reported that/it is said that) (d:<cih>, the marker that closes what is said, and <kiza>, be heard: placed after a whole clause and before the final <hi>, it presents the clause as news that is heard and not confirmed by the writer) (r:ts:12002/ts:10007/ts:10679) (q:draft)
cih thadah = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:let alone/not to mention/far from) (d:<cih>, saying, and <thadah>, lazy, literally too lazy to say: placed after a word or clause, it sets that aside as out of the question and the clause that follows, often with <nangawn>, even, names the lesser thing that is the case) (r:zd:15874/zd:19800) (q:draft)
cihbang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:such as/like/things like) (d:<cih> and <bang> written as one word: after a word or a list, such a thing as, things like; after a verb of saying with its subject, as was said) (j:cih/bang) (r:ts:3366/zd:23011) (q:draft)
cihbang omlo = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:there is no such thing as/nothing like) (d:<cihbang>, things like, and <omlo>, there is not: placed after a word or a clause and before <hi>, denies that anything of the kind exists) (r:zd:22203/zd:23443) (q:draft)
cihbangbang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:whatever is said/just as said) (d:<cih>, say, and <bangbang>, whatever, written as one word: whatever someone says, exactly as someone says, after the one who speaks; {a cihbangbang} is whatever he says) (j:cih/bangbang) (r:zd:21028/zd:19774/zd:25926) (q:draft)
cihbangdan = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:such as/in the manner of/things like) (d:<cih>, <bang> and <dan> written as one word, placed after quoted words or a list: in that kind of way, things of that sort) (j:cih/bang/dan) (r:zd:17526/zd:17062) (q:draft)
cihbangin = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:and so on/such as/for instance) (d:placed after a list of names, numbers or examples, which are only samples of what the sentence goes on to say: in such ways as these) (r:zd:19159/zd:18893/zd:24276) (q:draft)
cihbangpeuh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:and all such things/anything like) (d:<cihbang> and <peuh> written as one word after a list: any such things as these, whatever is of that kind) (j:cihbang/peuh) (r:zd:11466/zd:11790) (q:draft)
cihbangte = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:such things as/and the like) (d:<cih> and <bangte> written as one word, placed after a list: things such as these, and the like) (j:cih/bangte) (r:zd:24276/zd:22833) (q:draft)
cihbangteng = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:all such as/and the like/and so on) (d:<cihbang>, such as, and <teng>, here all of them, written as one word after a list: all the things just named and those like them) (j:cihbang/teng) (r:zd:16819/zd:16869) (q:draft)
cihbangzong = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:such things as also/even the like) (d:<cihbang>, such as, and <zong>, also, written as one word: after a word or a list, things like these too, or not even such a thing) (j:cihbang/zong) (r:zd:15288/zd:13155) (q:draft)
cihbek = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:only/just/merely) (d:<cih>, saying, and <bek>, only, written as one word after a quoted word or statement: only that and nothing more is said, known or written) (j:cih/bek) (r:zd:12967/zd:20092) (q:draft)
cihbel = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<cih>, saying or that, and the particle <bel>, here as for, written as one word: placed after a word or clause to make it the topic, as for whether or as for what is called, mostly before a negative statement) (j:cih/bel) (r:zd:23977/zd:17060/zd:23776) (q:draft)
cihciang = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:as for what is called/only that much) (d:<cih> and <ciang> written as one word. After a word or statement, {cihciang in} takes it up as the topic: when one says this, what is meant by it. With <bek> or alone before a verb of knowing or hearing it limits what is known: only this much, no more than that) (j:cih/ciang) (r:zd:22771/zd:10729/zd:15629) (q:draft)
cihciangbek = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/media) (w:only as/merely as) (d:<cih>, saying, with <ciangbek>, only as far as, written as one word: placed after a name or word to show that no more than this is said or known) (j:cih/ciangbek) (r:zd:11256/zd:11721) (q:draft)
cihciangin = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:when one says) (d:<cih> and <ciangin> written as one word: when one says, used to take up a word or statement and then explain what it means) (j:cih/ciangin) (r:zd:23594/zd:21741) (q:draft)
cihcihte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:what is called/the things said) (d:<cihcih> and <te> written as one word: the things people keep saying or calling so; {i cihcihte} is the things we speak of, what we call) (j:cihcih/te) (r:zd:10698/zd:21590) (q:draft)
cihdan = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:such as/and the like/that sort of) (d:<cih>, saying, and <dan>, manner, written as one word after a list, an example or a quoted thought: things such as these, the kind of thing just said; {cihdan in} is in such a way) (j:cih/dan) (r:zd:11548/zd:23797/zd:22157) (q:draft)
cihdanin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:in the manner of/as if to say) (d:<cihdan> and <in> written as one word, after a quoted thought or an example: in such a way, as if saying so) (j:cihdan/in) (r:zd:24121/zd:20944) (q:draft)
cihdante = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:such things as/and the like) (d:<cihdan>, such as, with the plural <te> written as one word after a list or a quoted saying: things of that kind) (j:cihdan/te) (r:zd:24276) (q:draft)
cihding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:to be said/to be called) (d:<cih> and <ding> written as one word: that is to be said or called, what one may say; {cihding ahihi} is it must be said, one may say) (j:cih/ding) (r:zd:23943/zd:21376/zd:16442) (q:draft)
cihdong = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:even to/down to/to the point of) (d:<cih>, saying, and <dong>, until, written as one word after a clause or a list: up to and including what was just named, to the extent of saying so; followed by <in> or <ah>) (j:cih/dong) (r:zd:25342/zd:12763) (q:draft)
cihhang = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:just because/although it is said) (d:<cih> and <hang> written as one word, after a statement: because it is said to be so, merely on the ground that; with <in> also although it is said that) (j:cih/hang) (r:zd:23343/zd:12502) (q:draft, low confidence)
cihhangin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:although it is said/even though) (d:<cih>, saying, and <hangin>, although, written as one word after a statement: although it is said to be so, even so) (j:cih/hangin) (r:zd:11162/zd:11083) (q:draft)
cihhuai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:make one wonder/be worth saying) (d:<cih> and <huai> written as one word: it deserves to be said; after a question ending in <hiam> it means one cannot help wondering whether) (j:cih/huai) (r:zd:8667/zd:24320) (q:draft)
cihi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:said/it is said) (d:<ci>, say, and the sentence-final <hi> written as one word; in news reports it closes a statement that is passed on from others: it is said) (j:ci/hi) (r:zd:15368/zd:17542) (q:draft)
cihiau = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:say abruptly/blurt out) (d:<ci>, say, with <hiau>, a word that shows a quick and direct action, written as one word after the words quoted: say straight out or all at once) (j:ci/hiau) (r:zd:12564) (q:draft, low confidence)
cihkammal = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:the word/the term) (d:<cih> and <kammal>, word, written as one word after a word that is quoted: the word so called, the term) (j:cih/kammal) (r:zd:20917/zd:21900) (q:draft)
cihkhat = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:something called/one called) (d:<cih> and <khat> written as one word, placed after a name or a quoted saying: a thing or person that is called so) (j:cih/khat) (r:zd:23394/ts:3366/zd:8668) (q:draft)
cihkhawng = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:and the like/such things as) (d:<cih> and <khawng> written as one word, placed after one or more examples: things like that, and so on) (j:cih/khawng) (r:zd:16365/zd:12128) (q:draft)
cihkhawngzong = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:such things as/and the like also) (d:<cih>, <khawng> and <zong> written as one word after a statement: things such as this also, there are even cases like this) (j:cih/khawng/zong) (r:zd:15433/zd:16949/zd:17085) (q:draft)
cihla = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:media) (w:the song called) (d:<cih> and <la>, song, written as one word, placed after the title or the first words of a song: the song called so, the song that says so) (j:cih/la) (r:zd:21326/zd:10874) (q:draft)
cihlah = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<cih>, that or such as, and the emphatic <lah>, written as one word before a negative: not even that, nothing like; {gim cihlah nei lo} is having no such thing as tiredness) (j:cih/lah) (r:zd:21974/zd:17647) (q:draft, low confidence)
cihlai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:still say/keep saying) (d:<cih>, say, and <lai> in the sense still, written as one word: still saying, go on saying for the time being) (j:cih/lai) (r:zd:12337) (q:draft, low confidence)
cihlam = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:the sense that/to the effect that) (d:<cih> and <lam> written as one word after a quoted thought: the direction or sense of saying so, to the effect that) (j:cih/lam) (r:zd:21908/zd:23860) (q:draft)
cihleh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:if one says/because) (d:<cih> and <leh> written as one word: if one says or asks; {banghang hiam cihleh} is if one asks why, that is, because) (j:cih/leh) (r:zd:13066/zd:12998/zd:21989) (q:draft)
cihloh = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:everyday) (w:except/apart from/other than/besides) (d:<cih> and <loh> written as one word, not saying: placed after a noun, apart from that one; often followed by {a dang om kei}, there is no other) (j:cih/loh) (r:zd:23037/zd:9428) (q:draft)
cihmah = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:just as said/the very saying) (d:<cih>, saying, and the emphatic <mah> written as one word: the very thing that is said; {a cihmah bangin} is just as he said) (j:cih/mah) (r:zd:22159/zd:15794) (q:draft)
cihna ahihi = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:it means/that is to say/which means) (d:<cihna>, the saying or meaning, and <ahihi>, it is: placed at the end of a sentence after a statement, it presents that statement as the meaning or consequence of what was said before, it means that) (r:zd:21826/zd:25926/zd:11416) (q:draft)
cihna hilo = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:does not mean/it is not to say) (d:<cihna>, saying or meaning, and <hilo>, is not: placed after a whole statement and usually followed by <hi>, it denies that the statement is what is meant; {ka cihna hilo hi} is I do not mean) (r:zd:24231/zd:16820/zd:20875) (q:draft)
cihnading = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:what to do) (d:<cih>, here do, and <nading>, for, written as one word: what one should do; nearly always with <theilo>, not know what to do, be at a loss) (j:cih/nading) (r:zd:23700/zd:21164/zd:15435) (q:draft)
cihnop huai = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/media) (w:one feels like saying/it makes one want to say) (d:<cihnop>, want to say, with the suffix <huai>, causing that feeling: placed after a quoted remark or question, often with <mahmah> or <mawk>, the writer's way of adding a comment, one cannot help saying) (r:zd:20592/zd:20930) (q:draft)
cihnopna ah = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:that is to say/in other words/what is meant is) (d:<cihnopna>, meaning, and <ah>, at: opens a sentence that explains what was just said, often closed by {cihna ahi hi}; with a possessive before it, {ka cihnopna ah} is what I mean is and {a cihnopna ah} is what he means is) (r:zd:24365/zd:24028/zd:12096) (q:draft)
cihpen = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:what is called/as for) (d:<cih> and the topic marker <pen> written as one word, placed after a word or phrase to make it the subject spoken about: what is called, the thing named) (j:cih/pen) (r:zd:23112/zd:19898) (q:draft)
cihpeuh = (i:1) (t:det) (f:everyday) (w:any such/whatever is called) (d:<cih> and <peuh> written as one word, placed after a word or clause: anything of that name, any such thing as that) (j:cih/peuh) (r:zd:23039/zd:25390) (q:draft)
cihsang = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:rather than/more than) (d:<cih>, saying, with the word for than, as in {cih sang in}, written as one word and often followed by <in>: rather than saying or being so, with <zaw> on the thing preferred) (j:cih/sang) (r:zd:25919/zd:22597) (q:draft)
cihtak = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:in earnest/really/thoroughly) (d:between a verb and its repetition, usually with <in>, it says that the action is done for real and to the full, as in {sim cihtak in ka sim} I read it in earnest; not about loyalty) (r:zd:17488/zd:11403) (q:draft)
cihtaknate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/religion) (w:faithfulness/loyalties/acts of faithfulness) (d:plural of <cihtakna>: the ways in which a person is faithful and true) (b:cihtakna) (r:zd:9215/zd:16142) (q:draft)
cihtawh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/media) (w:with what is called/with the saying) (d:<cih> and <tawh> written as one word after quoted words or a clause: with what is said or named; {cihtawh kisai} is concerning the statement that) (j:cih/tawh) (r:zd:17344/zd:21529) (q:draft)
cihtawh thu = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:politics/media) (w:on a charge of/charged with) (d:<cihtawh>, with what is called, and <thu.2>, a case: placed after the name of an offence or of a section of law and before <kibawl> or <bawl>, a case is opened under that name, the person is charged with it) (r:zd:14689/zd:11538) (q:draft)
cihte akipan = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/media) (w:starting with/including/from ... onward) (d:<cihte>, such things as, and <akipan>, beginning with: placed after one or more examples that have been named, beginning with these and going on to the rest of the same kind) (r:zd:17177/zd:16152) (q:draft, low confidence)
cihte pawl = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:and the like/such things as) (d:<cihte>, those called, and <pawl>, group: placed after one example or a list of examples, things or people of that kind, the likes of these) (r:zd:23301/zd:15881) (q:draft, low confidence)
cihteh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/education) (w:when one says/by this is meant) (d:<cih>, say, and <teh> written as one word after the word or statement that is explained, often with <ka> or <ih> before it: when one says this, what is meant by it is) (j:cih/teh) (r:zd:23987/zd:24457) (q:draft)
cihteng = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<cih> and <teng>, here meaning all, written as one word, placed after a list: all these, all the things just named) (j:cih/teng) (r:zd:15232/zd:12314) (q:draft)
cihtepawl = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:such as/and the like/those of the kind) (d:<cihte> and <pawl> written as one word, placed after a name, a list or a quoted saying: those called so and others like them, people or things of that kind) (j:cihte/pawl) (r:zd:23488/zd:13030) (q:draft)
cihtepen = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:such things as) (d:<cihte> and the topic marker <pen> written as one word, placed after a list or a name: as for such things as these, as for what is called) (j:cihte/pen) (r:zd:17941/zd:12395) (q:draft)
cihtetawh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:with such things as) (d:<cihte>, such things as, and <tawh>, with, written as one word after a list: with these and the like) (j:cihte/tawh) (r:zd:17293/zd:20136) (q:draft)
cihtezong = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:and the like also/such things too) (d:<cihte>, such things as, and <zong>, also, written as one word after a list: these things too, things such as these as well) (j:cihte/zong) (r:zd:12192/zd:11167) (q:draft)
cihthadah = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:let alone/not to mention/far from) (d:<cih> and <thadah> written as one word, a fixed expression after a phrase: let alone that, never mind that, what follows being a smaller thing that also fails) (j:cih/thadah) (r:zd:25224/zd:14720) (q:draft)
cihtham = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:worth mentioning/significant) (d:<cih> with <tham>, worth: worth saying; mostly with a negative, as {cihtham hetlo}, not worth mentioning, nothing by comparison) (j:cih/tham) (r:zd:24699/zd:12998) (q:draft)
cihtheihna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:ground for saying/possibility of saying) (d:<cih>, say, with <theih>, can, and the noun suffix <na>: that something can be said, or the reason why one can say it, {tua bang ka cihtheihna in} the reason I can say so is; not the state of being well off) (r:zd:17060/zd:22827) (q:draft)
cihthu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/everyday) (w:the news that/the report that) (d:<cih>, which closes what is said, and <thu>, word or matter, written as one word: the news, report or matter that something is so; {cihthu kiza hi} is it is reported that) (j:cih/thu) (r:zd:22394/zd:17275/zd:21908) (q:draft)
cihthu kiza = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:media) (w:it is reported that/word has come that) (d:<cihthu>, the news that, and <kiza>, be heard: a news formula placed after a full statement and before <hi>, marking it as a report the writer has heard and not seen) (r:zd:22394/zd:19717) (q:draft)
cihvai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/media) (w:the matter of/question of) (d:<cih> and <vai> written as one word after a statement: the matter that, the question whether; usually followed by {tawh kisai}, concerning) (j:cih/vai) (r:zd:13282/zd:20305) (q:draft)
cihziau = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:simply say/just say) (d:<cih>, saying, with <ziau>: said simply or lightly, just putting it so) (j:cih/ziau) (r:zd:19816/zd:13112) (q:draft, low confidence)
cihzong = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday/media) (w:also that/even that) (d:<cih>, the word that closes what is said or thought, with <zong>, also, written as one word: that too, even the saying of it; {cihzong kiza hi} is it is also reported that) (j:cih/zong) (r:zd:14846/zd:19600/zd:22377) (q:draft)
cihzong kiza = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:media) (w:it is also reported that/it is also said) (d:<cihzong>, also that, and <kiza>, be heard: closes a sentence of a news report, before <hi>, and marks its content as a further thing that is reported or heard, not seen by the writer) (r:zd:14846/zd:22377/zd:12290) (q:draft)
Ciiimnuai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:social) (j:Ciimnuai) (r:zd:20033) (q:draft)
ciilin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (j:cilin) (r:zd:20172/ts:479) (q:draft)
ciilna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time/everyday) (j:cilna) (r:zd:17224/zd:17162) (q:draft)
ciim = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:everyday/education) (w:sensible/prudent/discerning/wise) (d:of a person, having good sense and sound judgement, beyond schooling; mostly paired with <pil>, as {pil leh ciim}, wise and sensible) (r:zd:11697/zd:24313/zd:20716) (q:draft)
Ciimnuai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:social) (w:Ciimnuai) (d:old settlement in the Tedim area that Zomi tradition names as the place from which the clans spread; also used in the names of a magazine and a school) (r:ts:3372/zd:16288) (q:draft)
ciimtak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/health) (w:carefully/prudently/soundly/thoroughly) (d:<ciim> with <tak>, which makes an adverb: with care and good sense, as in {piltak le ciimtak-in}, wisely and prudently; of sleep, {ihmut ciimtak in}, soundly, getting enough) (j:ciim/tak) (r:zd:17021/zd:23972) (q:draft, low confidence)
ciimtak = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (j:cimtak) (r:zd:21869/zd:20525) (q:draft, low confidence)
Ciimtang = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Ciimtang) (d:place on the road to Tedim, eight or nine miles from the town, known for its ridge and its bends in the road) (r:zd:22577/zd:23767) (q:draft)
ciin = (i:3) (t:part) (f:everyday/media) (w:saying/that) (d:{ci-in} written as one word, <ci>, say, with the ending {-in}: stands after quoted or reported words and before a verb of saying, asking or answering; not the verb plant) (r:zd:15332/zd:23897/zd:24310) (q:draft)
ciindan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/nature) (w:way of planting/method of growing) (d:<ciin>, plant, with <dan>, way, written as one word: how a crop or a flower is planted and grown) (j:ciin/dan) (r:zd:21092) (q:draft)
ciindan = (i:2) (t:n) (f:social) (w:custom/manners/etiquette) (d:the accepted way of behaving among a people, named beside <pau>, language, and <ngeina>, tradition) (r:zd:22686/zd:9435) (q:draft, low confidence)
ciing = (i:2) (t:v) (f:nature/work) (w:plant/grow/cultivate) (d:plant and grow a crop in a field or garden, with the crop named before it, as in {buh ciing}, grow rice; another spelling of <ciin>, not the adjective barren) (s:ciin) (r:ts:479/zd:15767/zd:19875) (q:draft)
ciinhuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:nature/everyday) (w:worth planting/worth keeping) (d:<ciin>, plant, with <huai>, worthy of: worth planting or growing; also said of a person, an example or a saying that is worth taking up and keeping) (b:ciin) (r:zd:20831/zd:25318) (q:draft, low confidence)
ciinna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:nature/work) (w:planting/growing/cultivation) (d:<ciin>, plant, with the noun ending <na>: the planting or growing of a crop, or the place where it is grown, after the name of the crop as in {beng ciinna}, opium growing; not the barrenness of a woman) (r:zd:26708/zd:21099/ts:1202) (q:draft)
ciintheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/nature) (w:can be planted/be able to grow) (d:<ciin>, plant, with <theih>, be able, written as one word: that can be planted or grown) (j:ciin/theih) (r:zd:21006/zd:11675) (q:draft, low confidence)
ciip = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (j:cip) (r:zd:8667) (q:draft, low confidence)
ciitciat = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (j:citciat) (r:zd:9217/zd:9233) (q:draft, low confidence)
cik = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:when) (d:Question word of time, used in {cik ciangin}, when, at what time) (s:cikciangin/cikciang/cikin) (r:19.42.2) (q:draft)
cik = (i:4) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:tiny/very little/very) (d:placed after a word of smallness or nearness such as <neu>, <tawm> or <nai>, it makes the word stronger: {neu cik khat} is a tiny one, {tawm cik cik} a very little and {nai cik} quite near) (r:zd:21159/ts:3506) (q:draft)
cikcik = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:very/tiny/mere) (d:placed after <neu>, small, <naupang>, child, and similar words to stress how small or young: {neu cikcik} is very small, {naupang cikcik} is a mere child) (r:zd:18183/zd:19831/zd:19826) (q:draft)
cikei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not say/say nothing) (d:<ci>, say, and the negative <kei>, written as one word: not say; {bangmah cikei ning} is I will say nothing) (j:ci/kei) (r:zd:17501/zd:16788) (q:draft)
cikhum = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:sugar) (d:<ci>, salt, with <khum>, sweet: sugar) (r:zd:14586/zd:22019) (q:draft)
cikmah = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:never) (d:With <hun> or <ciangin> and a negative verb: at no time, never.) (s:cikmahin/cik)
cikmah hun = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:never/at no time) (d:<cikmah>, never, and <hun>, time: used as {cikmah hun in} before a negative verb, often with <ngei>, for never, at no time) (s:cikmahin) (r:zd:21659/zd:19915/zd:20805) (q:draft)
cikmahhun = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:never/at no time) (d:<cikmah> and <hun> written as one word, followed by <in> or <ciangin> and a negative verb: at no time, never) (j:cikmah/hun) (r:zd:23487/zd:11133) (q:draft)
cikzia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:shudder/shrink from/be horrified) (d:feel horror or disgust at something and shrink from it; {cikzia hetlo in} is without the least qualm, ruthlessly; before <huai> the form is <cikziat>) (r:zd:16323/ts:9677) (q:draft, low confidence)
cikziak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/body) (w:shudder/be horrified/feel one's flesh creep) (d:feel a shiver of horror at a dreadful sight; mostly as {cikziak huai}, horrifying, gruesome) (r:zd:12304/zd:15562) (q:draft)
cikziat = (i:2) (t:v) (f:media/everyday) (w:be horrified/shudder) (d:shudder with horror at a sight of injury or danger rather than feel disgust at a deed; in news {cikziat huai mahmah} is horrifying, dreadful to see, said of accidents, fires and wounds, often beside <mulkimhuai>) (r:zd:17713/zd:15123/zd:17701) (q:draft)
cikziat huai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/media) (w:horrifying/dreadful/shocking) (d:<cikziat>, be disgusted or shudder, and <huai>, worthy of: said of a sight or a deed that makes one shudder; usually the predicate, often followed by {mahmah hi}) (r:zd:16093/zd:17713) (q:draft)
cile = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:if one says/if we say) (d:<ci>, say, with <le>, if, written as one word and followed by {'ng} or <hang>, we: {a taktak in cile'ng} is to tell the truth) (j:ci/le) (r:zd:15926/zd:24313) (q:draft)
cileeng = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:if we say/so to speak) (d:<ci> with <leng>, if, written as one word with a long vowel: if we say, if one puts it so; introduces or closes a way of putting something) (j:ci/leng) (r:zd:22569/zd:25188) (q:draft)
cileh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:if one says/that is to say) (d:<ci>, say, and <leh>, if, written as one word: if one says so; after a question word it introduces the answer, as {banghanghiam cileh}, because) (j:ci/leh) (r:zd:21027/zd:21876) (q:draft)
cilehsa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (j:cilesa) (r:zd:24089/zd:23670) (q:draft)
cilel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:just say/simply say) (d:<ci> and <lel> written as one word, placed after the words quoted: merely says, just says) (j:ci/lel) (r:zd:21908/zd:25322) (q:draft)
cileng = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:if we say/so to speak) (d:<ci>, say, and <leng>, if we, written as one word: if we say, if one says; {a taktak in cileng} is to tell the truth) (j:ci/leng) (r:zd:21547/zd:24432/zd:21376) (q:draft)
cileuleu = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/everyday) (w:say again/also say/say in turn) (d:<ci>, say, and <leuleu>, again or in turn, written as one word: say once more, or add a further statement; in news reports it closes a further thing that is reported) (j:ci/leuleu) (r:zd:11560/zd:12636/zd:14756) (q:draft)
cilgil = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:meticulous/particular/exacting) (d:careful about small details, strict and exacting; {cilgil takin} is carefully, in detail) (r:zd:16385/zd:25928) (q:draft, low confidence)
ciliang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:even say/go so far as to say) (d:<ci>, say, and <liang>, even, written as one word: it is even said, someone goes so far as to say or to call it so; closes a report of something striking) (j:ci/liang) (r:zd:22272/zd:19727) (q:draft)
cillum = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:saliva/spittle) (d:the saliva in the mouth, compare <cil>; {cillum tawh valh}, swallow with the saliva, is to swallow down anger or hardship and bear it in silence) (r:zd:18142/zd:23902) (q:draft)
cilo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not say/say nothing) (d:<ci> and <lo> written as one word: does not say, or without saying; {bangmah cilo}, says nothing, is also said of someone who is unhurt or does not mind) (j:ci/lo) (r:zd:24214/zd:11319/zd:18071) (q:draft)
ciltui = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body/health) (w:saliva/spittle) (d:the liquid of the mouth; {ciltui kai} is drool, and {ciltui siat} is spit) (r:zd:22002/zd:23848) (q:draft)
cimai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:just say/simply say) (d:<ci>, say, with <mai> written as one word; the second part is here a particle placed after a verb, just or simply, not the noun for face: just say, say without more ado) (j:ci/mai) (r:zd:19239/zd:14581) (q:draft, low confidence)
cimawh dongtuak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/media) (w:victims/people in distress/disaster victims) (d:<cimawh>, helpless, and <dongtuak>, one who has met misfortune: the people struck by a flood, fire, war or other disaster and left in need; a number with <mi> follows it) (r:zd:18872/zd:17411) (q:draft)
cimawh dongtuakte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:victims/the needy/people in distress) (d:<cimawh>, helpless, and <dongtuakte>, those who suffer: a pair that names the people struck by a disaster or in need, usually as the object of a verb of helping) (r:zd:26660/zd:20401) (q:draft)
cimawk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media) (w:be said/reportedly say) (d:<ci> and <mawk> written as one word, mostly as {cimawk hi} at the end of a news sentence: it is said, so it is reported, apparently with a note of surprise at what is told) (j:ci/mawk) (r:zd:14535/zd:15095/zd:20466) (q:draft, low confidence)
cimek = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/work) (w:massage) (d:rubbing and pressing the body with the hands; {cimek nasep} is work as a masseur or masseuse) (r:zd:17372/zd:16838) (q:draft)
cimlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:not have enough/be unsated) (d:<cim>, have enough, and <lo>, not, written as one word: not having had enough of something; {ihmut cimlo} is not getting enough sleep) (j:cim/lo) (r:zd:22856/zd:25914) (q:draft, low confidence)
cimloh = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/health) (w:not enough/insufficient/insatiable) (d:<cim>, have enough, with <loh>, not, written as one word: not having had enough of something; {ihmut cimloh} is lack of sleep and {gen cimloh} is beyond telling) (j:cim/loh) (r:zd:21168/zd:22856/zd:24542) (q:draft)
cimna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/everyday) (j:ciimna) (r:zd:24748/zd:21285) (q:draft)
cimna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:health/everyday) (w:sufficiency/having enough/fill) (d:<cim>, have enough, with the noun ending {-na}: having had one's fill of something; {ihmut cimna} is enough sleep, and with nothing to do it is boredom) (b:cim) (r:zd:25914) (q:draft, low confidence)
cimphawng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:pastime/amusement/recreation/diversion) (d:something done or kept to drive away boredom, <cim>, be weary of: a pastime or a companion for one's leisure; also as a verb, pass the time, amuse oneself) (r:zd:23676/zd:21617/zd:24022) (q:draft)
cimul = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:body hair/gooseflesh) (d:the fine hair of the skin; {cimul tho} is the hair stands on end, to have goose bumps from awe, fear or joy) (r:zd:10674/zd:17271) (q:draft)
cina = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:health/everyday) (w:sick/ill) (d:Sick, ill; also used as a verb, be ill or fall sick, often as {cina-in om}) (a:cidam) (r:25.5.17) (q:draft)
cina gim = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:health) (w:seriously ill/gravely ill) (d:<cina>, sick, and <gim>, here heavy, severe: seriously ill, and as a noun a person who is seriously ill or a serious illness; {cina gim mahmah} is very gravely ill) (r:zd:24117/zd:25240) (q:draft)
cinapi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:although it says/though said) (d:<ci>, say, and <napi>, although, written as one word: although he, she or it says so) (j:ci/napi) (r:zd:21461/zd:24492) (q:draft)
cinapuakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/travel) (w:ambulance/carrying of the sick) (d:<cina> and <puakna> written as one word: the carrying of sick people; {cinapuakna mawtaw} is an ambulance) (j:cina/puakna) (r:zd:16586/zd:15575) (q:draft)
cinatlawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health) (w:fall ill/get sick) (d:<cinat>, being sick, with <lawh>, here suffer as a result: fall ill because of something, such as food or a disease, named before it with <hangin>) (j:cinat/lawh) (r:zd:19499/zd:20547/zd:11508) (q:draft)
cinciang = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:time) (w:when it is completed/when it is full) (d:<cin>, be completed, and <ciang>, when, written as one word, said of a period of time: when the time is up, when a year is full) (j:cin/ciang) (r:zd:25917) (q:draft)
cinciangin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:time) (w:when the time comes/when completed) (d:<cin> and <ciangin> written as one word: when a time or an age is reached or completed; {a hun a cinciangin} is when its time has come) (j:cin/ciangin) (r:zd:20568/zd:21837) (q:draft)
Cincinnati = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Cincinnati) (d:a city in the state of Ohio in the United States) (r:zd:11934/zd:9263) (q:draft)
Cinema = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media) (w:cinema/movie theatre/film) (d:a place where films are shown, or the films themselves) (o:English) (r:zd:25589/zd:16340) (q:draft)
cing = (i:3) (t:v) (f:time/everyday) (w:be full/be complete/reach) (d:reach the full number or amount, mostly after <kum>, year: {kum cing} is to be a full number of years old or to be of age; it has nothing to do with guarding) (s:kicing) (r:zd:23512/ts:3562) (q:draft)
cingam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:dare to say/say boldly) (d:<ci> and <ngam> written as one word after the words quoted: dare to say, say with confidence; with <nawnlo>, no longer dare to call someone so) (j:ci/ngam) (r:zd:19166/zd:12044) (q:draft)
cingding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:time) (w:will be complete/will reach) (d:<cing>, here be full or complete, and <ding>, the marker of what is to come, written as one word: after a number of years, will have reached that many years) (j:cing/ding) (r:zd:15905/zd:21551) (q:draft)
cingding = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:will guard/to watch over) (d:<cing>, guard or watch over, and <ding>, the marker of what is to come, written as one word: will guard, the one who is to watch over) (j:cing/ding) (r:zd:20520/zd:19850) (q:draft)
cingei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have said/ever say) (d:<ci>, say, and <ngei>, ever, written as one word: have said at some time; with <lo>, never say) (j:ci/ngei) (r:zd:16897) (q:draft, low confidence)
cingeu = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:say plainly) (d:<ci>, say, with the emphatic <ngeu>, written as one word after the words quoted: said just so, said outright) (j:ci/ngeu) (r:zd:24230) (q:draft, low confidence)
Cinghpi = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (f:nature) (w:rhinoceros/rhino) (r:zd:21102) (q:draft)
cingiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:say expressly/say indeed) (d:<ci> and <ngiat> written as one word: say expressly, really say so, call it just that) (j:ci/ngiat) (r:zd:10874/zd:25318) (q:draft)
cingkhin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:time) (w:have already reached/be already complete) (d:<cing>, here reach the full number, and <khin>, already, written as one word after a length of time: that time has already fully passed) (j:cing/khin) (r:zd:12341/zd:11598/zd:12567) (q:draft)
cinglo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:insufficient/incomplete/lacking) (d:not enough or not complete, with <lo> not; {ki cinglo} is it is not enough and {lungsim cinglo} is not of sound mind) (a:kicing) (r:zd:23388/ts:3508/zd:22923) (q:draft)
cingnailo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:time) (w:not yet complete/not yet a full) (d:<cing>, reach the full amount, and <nailo>, not yet, written as one word: a time is not yet complete; {khakhatzong cingnailo in} is in not even a full month) (j:cing/nailo) (r:zd:12589/zd:16767) (q:draft)
Cingpikot = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel) (w:Cingpikot) (d:a village of the Tedim area in Chin State, named together with Keizang) (r:zd:15947/zd:17208) (q:draft)
cingto = (i:1) (t:v) (f:time/everyday) (w:reach/come up to/amount to) (d:of a number or a length of time, come up to the full figure named; of a set term, be completed) (r:zd:16245/zd:24489) (q:draft, low confidence)
cingzaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:more complete/fuller/more adequate) (d:complete or sufficient, as in <kicing>, with the comparative <zaw>: more complete, better supplied) (r:zd:17776) (q:draft, low confidence)
cinh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:time) (j:cin) (r:zd:15268) (q:draft, low confidence)
cini = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:let us say) (d:<ci> with the first person plural ending <ni>, let us, written as one word: let us say, closing a statement or a supposition) (j:ci/ni) (r:zd:23742/zd:24457) (q:draft)
cinloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be incomplete/fall short/be imperfect) (d:<cin> with the negative <loh>: not be complete or whole; {ka cinloh hang} is because of my falling short) (j:cin/loh) (r:zd:21383) (q:draft, low confidence)
cinlohna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:shortcoming/inadequacy/deficiency) (d:<cin>, be complete, with <lohna>: the state of not being complete or sufficient, a shortcoming; with <ki> before it, of a thing that does not work or flow as fully as it should) (b:cin) (r:zd:19150/zd:9436/zd:12009) (q:draft)
cinna = (i:3) (t:n) (f:time/social) (w:anniversary/completion) (d:the completing of a number of years, from <cin>, be completed: after <kum> and a number it names an anniversary and works as an ordinal, as in {kum 50 cinna pawi}, the celebration of the fiftieth year) (r:zd:16253/zd:17075/zd:11209) (q:draft)
cinni = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:anniversary/day of completion) (d:<cin>, be completed, with <ni>, day: the day on which a number of years, months or days becomes full; {kum 30 cinni} is the thirtieth anniversary) (j:cin/ni) (r:zd:24310/zd:25557) (q:draft)
cinpawi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/time) (w:anniversary/anniversary celebration) (d:<cin>, of a time be completed, with <pawi>, feast, written as one word after a number of years: the feast for the completing of so many years) (j:cin/pawi) (r:zd:18079/zd:12923) (q:draft)
cipah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:say at once/say straight away) (d:<ci> and <pah> written as one word: say something at once, without thinking further or without more ado) (j:ci/pah) (r:zd:12386/zd:26620) (q:draft, low confidence)
cipak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:just say/say briefly) (d:<ci>, say, and <pak>, for a short while, written as one word: say in passing; {cipak ni} and {cipak nihang}, let us just say so, close a remark) (j:ci/pak) (r:zd:16832/zd:22577) (q:draft, low confidence)
cipcipna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:turmoil/unrest) (d:in {buai cipcipna}, from <buai>, be troubled, and the noun ending <na>: a time of great trouble or disturbance) (r:zd:22138) (q:draft, low confidence)
cipeuh = (i:1) (t:det) (f:everyday) (w:every/each/all) (d:<ci> and <peuh> written as one word, placed after a noun: each and every one; {mun cipeuh} is everywhere and {mi cipeuh} is everybody) (j:ci/peuh) (r:zd:16940/zd:17081) (q:draft)
ciphial = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:even say/go so far as to say) (d:<ci>, say, and <phial>, even, written as one word: one could even say, or even if one says) (j:ci/phial) (r:zd:23113/zd:13074) (q:draft)
ciphot = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:say for now/stop here for now) (d:<ci>, say, with <phot>, for the time being; a writer closes an article with {tuazah ciphot ni}, let us say this much for now) (j:ci/phot) (r:zd:24570/zd:17760) (q:draft)
ciphual = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/body) (w:wheal/rash/skin inflammation) (d:a red, raised or inflamed patch on the skin) (r:zd:15984) (q:draft, low confidence)
cipongmawk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:just say/say offhand/claim) (d:<ci>, say, and <pongmawk>, just like that, written as one word: say something just like that, without ground or without thinking) (j:ci/pongmawk) (r:zd:18077/zd:12138) (q:draft)
cipsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:block completely/jam/shut off) (d:<cip>, tightly or completely, with the causative <sak>: make something completely closed or stuck; {Traffic Jam cipsak} is cause a complete traffic jam) (j:cip/sak) (r:zd:17632/zd:11752) (q:draft, low confidence)
cisa = (i:2) (t:v) (f:health) (w:have a fever/be feverish) (d:be hot with fever, said of a person: the noun used as a verb, after <a> and before <ding>, <nuam> or <gawp>) (r:zd:21370/zd:23873) (q:draft)
cisam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:said/it is said) (d:<ci>, say, written as one word with the softening particle <sam>: said, or it is said, closing a reported statement; {bangmah cisam lo} is said nothing at all) (j:ci/sam) (r:zd:16389/zd:12066/zd:17694) (q:draft, low confidence)
cisawnsawn = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media) (w:it is further said/reportedly) (d:<ci>, say, and <sawnsawn>, on and on, written as one word at the end of a statement in a news report: it is said further, the report goes on to say) (j:ci/sawnsawn) (r:zd:15608/zd:17474) (q:draft, low confidence)
cise = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:say/call) (d:<ci>, say, and the emphatic <se> written as one word, after quoted words or a name: {cise uh hi} is they say or they call it so, {cise lo} is do not say so) (j:ci/se) (r:zd:17784/zd:10687) (q:draft, low confidence)
cita = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:say/said) (d:<ci> and <ta> written as one word, after quoted words: said, has now said; with <lawmlawm> or <leuleu>, is even said, said in turn) (j:ci/ta) (r:zd:12337/zd:11581/zd:14903) (q:draft)
citaklo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:social) (w:unfaithful/dishonest/disloyal) (d:<citak> and <lo> written as one word: not faithful, not to be trusted) (j:citak/lo) (r:zd:22228/zd:24275) (q:draft)
citakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:honesty/faithfulness/integrity) (d:<citak>, faithful and honest, with the noun suffix <na>: being honest and reliable in what one does) (s:thumanna) (b:citak) (r:zd:21706/zd:10726) (q:draft)
citaktak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:faithfully/earnestly/diligently) (d:<citak>, faithful, and <tak> written as one word, mostly followed by <in>: in a faithful and earnest way) (s:citakin) (j:citak/tak) (r:zd:14791) (q:draft)
citamawk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/everyday) (w:said/has now said) (d:<ci>, say, with <tamawk> written as one word before <hi>: someone has now said or declared it, with a note of surprise or regret) (j:ci/tamawk) (r:zd:21409/zd:11598) (q:draft)
citawm = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:social) (w:few in number/small in population) (d:of a people, a church or a group: having few members, being a minority) (r:zd:19052/zd:24696/zd:25105) (q:draft)
citciat = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:as it happens/in fact/actually) (d:placed after a verb, often after <kha>, to say that something happens to be so, usually unexpected or not planned; {kizaihkha citciat} is it happened to be recorded) (r:zd:12089/zd:20224/zd:22116) (q:draft)
