donghu = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/politics) (w:temporary/provisional/interim) (d:for the time being only, not lasting or permanent; {donghu nasem} is a temporary worker) (r:zd:26565/ts:1498/zd:21099) (q:draft)
dongkholh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:be a nuisance/be a hindrance/be in the way) (d:be a burden or an annoyance to others, get in the way; {dongkholh sa} is find something a nuisance, and {mit dongkholh} is an eyesore) (r:zd:21874/zd:23767/zd:15674) (q:draft)
donglo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not ask) (d:<dong>, ask, and <lo>, not, written as one word: not ask, not seek advice; in some articles the form seems to stand for another expression, as in {mit donglo}) (j:dong/lo) (r:zd:26531) (q:draft, low confidence)
dongmah = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:everyday/time) (w:right until/all the way to/up to) (d:<dong>, until, and the emphatic <mah> written as one word: right up to a time, a point or an amount; {tu dongmah} is up to this very day) (j:dong/mah) (r:zd:19245/zd:20997/zd:17666) (q:draft)
dongpen = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:time/everyday) (w:until/up to) (d:<dong>, until, with the topic marker <pen>, written as one word: the stretch up to that point, as what the sentence is about) (j:dong/pen) (r:zd:20588/zd:21974) (q:draft)
dongtang = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/social) (w:hindered/obstructed/bothered) (d:finding something in the way or a nuisance; {dongtang sak} is get in the way of someone, and {dongtang sa} is feel something to be a hindrance) (r:zd:15818/zd:17784) (q:draft, low confidence)
dongtuah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:be in distress/meet with hardship/be in trouble) (d:be in the middle of trouble, need or disaster; compare <tuah.2>, meet with; {cimawh dongtuah} is be in distress) (r:zd:12917/zd:25172/zd:22085) (q:draft, low confidence)
dongtuahna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:crisis/calamity/hardship/affliction) (d:a hard time or disaster that comes upon a person or a people, such as famine, war or an epidemic) (r:zd:25293/zd:16254/zd:25287) (q:draft)
dongtuak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:victim/person in distress/sufferer) (d:one who has met with misfortune such as flood, fire, war or sickness and needs help, mostly as <cimawh dongtuak>; also a verb, meet with misfortune) (r:zd:20155/zd:15679/zd:19968) (q:draft)
dongtuakte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:victims/those in distress/the afflicted) (d:plural of <dongtuak>, one who has met with hardship or misfortune: people struck by need, disaster or illness; often <cimawh dongtuakte>) (b:dongtuak) (r:zd:26660/zd:22779) (q:draft)
donlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:ignore/disregard/neglect) (d:<don>, pay attention, and <lo>, not, written as one word: pay no attention to, not care about) (j:don/lo) (r:zd:12904/zd:21701) (q:draft)
donna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/social) (w:contribution/payment/collection) (d:the paying in or collecting of money for a common purpose, as in {sum donna}, a collection, and of a premium or a tax) (r:zd:21282/zd:23304) (q:draft)
