duh = (i:3) (t:v) (f:food/everyday) (w:crave/like/want) (d:be fond of or have a wish for something, above all a food or a drink, without <tui> or <an> before it and so not thirsty or hungry; {zu duh} is like liquor and {a duh bangbang} is whatever one wants) (r:zd:19654/zd:23191/zd:21822) (q:draft)
duhdan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/food) (w:taste/liking/preference) (d:<duh> and <dan> written as one word: the way or the thing one likes, one's taste) (j:duh/dan) (r:zd:17315/zd:13144) (q:draft)
duhhop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:covet/be greedy/crave) (d:want more and more for oneself; mostly said together with <huaiham>, greedy) (s:huaiham) (r:zd:24072/zd:26645) (q:draft)
duhlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food/everyday) (w:not want/not like/have no appetite for) (d:<duh>, want to eat or drink, and <lo>, not, written as one word: not want or not like a food, have no appetite) (j:duh/lo) (r:zd:21557/zd:20896/zd:19859) (q:draft)
dum = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:blue) (d:the colour blue, said of cloth and cord; the same word is used of green plants) (q:draft)
dung = (i:2) (t:prep) (f:nature/travel) (w:along/the length of) (d:after the name of a river, road, ridge or border: along its whole course, as in {gun dung}, along the river, and {lampi dung ah}, along the road; with <zui>, follow, it is following along) (r:zd:23896/zd:25109/zd:23077) (q:draft)
Dungun = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Dungun) (d:district and town in the state of Terengganu, Malaysia) (r:zd:11354/zd:12583) (q:draft)
dungzui = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:everyday) (w:according to/in accordance with/in line with) (d:<dung>, length, with <zui>, follow: placed after a noun, mostly as {dungzui in}, following along that thing, in keeping with it; {tua dungzui in} is accordingly) (r:zd:13070/zd:25569/zd:16415) (q:draft)
dupgawp = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:body/health) (w:badly bruised/livid/blackened) (d:<dup>, dark or livid, with <gawp>, severely: of skin or flesh, turned dark all over from blows or lack of blood) (j:dup/gawp) (r:zd:16101/zd:11744) (q:draft)
Durian = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (f:food/nature) (w:durian) (d:a large tropical fruit with a very strong smell, often said {Durian singgah}) (o:Malay) (r:zd:19447/zd:21961) (q:draft)
Dutch = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:politics/travel) (w:Dutch) (d:of the Netherlands, its people or its language, used as in English before a noun) (o:English) (r:zd:12955) (q:draft, low confidence)
duty = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:duty/shift/turn of duty) (d:a turn of work at a post, said of police, soldiers, guards and nurses; {duty sem} and {duty kuan} are be on duty, and the word is also used alone as a verb) (o:English) (r:zd:15608/zd:19223/zd:14824) (q:draft)
DVB = (i:1) (t:name) (f:media) (w:DVB/Democratic Voice of Burma) (d:Democratic Voice of Burma, a Burmese news broadcaster often named as a source) (o:English) (r:zd:26163/zd:15174) (q:draft)
DVD = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/it) (w:DVD) (d:a disc that holds video or music, often named together with CD) (o:English) (r:zd:19968/zd:21255) (q:draft)
e = (i:2) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:indeed) (d:closes a statement or exclamation, after the verb or after an ending such as <ing> or <hi>, as in {hi hang e}, we are indeed, and gives it a warm or emphatic tone; it is left untranslated, and it does not follow a word of address) (r:zd:25562/zd:24963) (q:draft)
e maw = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<e> and <maw>, two sentence-final words together: closes a sentence in place of <hi>, after an appeal with let us or after a statement, as a gentle appeal or exclamation to the reader, like shall we or you see) (r:zd:15572/zd:25433) (q:draft, low confidence)
Easter = (i:1) (t:name) (f:religion) (w:Easter) (d:the Christian feast of the resurrection of Jesus, in Zolai also {Thawhkik Nipi} or {Thawhkikpawi}) (o:English) (r:zd:9232/zd:21739) (q:draft)
Ebola = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:Ebola) (d:the Ebola virus and the deadly disease it causes, also {Ebola natna} and {Ebola pulna}) (o:English) (r:ts:12490/zd:21974) (q:draft)
economics = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/work) (w:economics/economy) (d:the study of the economy; also used for the economy of a country) (o:English) (r:zd:25584) (q:draft, low confidence)
economist = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/politics) (w:economist) (d:a person who studies or is expert in economics) (o:English) (r:zd:21288/zd:21235) (q:draft)
economy = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/politics) (w:economy) (d:the wealth, trade and work of a country taken as a whole) (o:English) (r:zd:17725/zd:11707) (q:draft)
Edgewood = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Edgewood) (d:place in the state of Maryland in the United States, site of an army chemical and biological centre) (r:zd:15833) (q:draft, low confidence)
Edinburg = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:religion) (w:Edinburgh/Edinburg) (d:the city of Edinburgh in Scotland; also the town of Edinburg in Pennsylvania in America) (r:zd:9219/zd:9231) (q:draft, low confidence)
Edinburgh = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Edinburgh) (d:the capital city of <Scotland>) (r:zd:17992/zd:12512) (q:draft)
edit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/it) (w:edit) (d:edit a text, a recording or a film; also as {edit bawl} and {edit sak}) (o:English) (r:zd:22711/zd:22085) (q:draft)
editor = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/work) (w:editor) (d:the person who prepares and is responsible for the text of a newspaper, magazine or book) (o:English) (r:zd:25268/zd:15474) (q:draft)
Edmonton = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Edmonton) (d:city in the province of Alberta in Canada) (r:zd:22203) (q:draft)
ee = (i:2) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:indeed) (d:sentence-final word of everyday speech and writing, a drawn-out <e>, that gives a statement warmth or emphasis; it follows <hi>, <veh>, <hang> or <ding> and has none of the scorn of the Bible sense) (r:ts:2669/zd:22586/zd:24163) (q:draft)
eeng = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (j:eng) (r:zd:22496/zd:16412) (q:draft)
Egyptian = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:politics) (w:Egyptian) (d:of <Egypt> or its people; the English word, placed before a noun) (o:English) (r:zd:21400) (q:draft)
eh = (i:2) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:and) (d:in informal writing, joins two words or two dates in the way <leh> does, as {pil eh ciim}, wise and prudent; not the exclamation) (s:leh) (r:zd:11697/zd:25569) (q:draft, low confidence)
ei = (i:2) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:indeed) (d:sentence-final word of exclamation in lively speech, giving force to what was just said; not the pronoun we, which stands at the start of its phrase) (r:ts:3446/zd:19630/zd:23436) (q:draft)
ei guai = (i:1) (t:intj) (f:everyday/social) (w:friends/folks) (d:<ei>, we, and <guai>, here a word of address to several people: said at the end of a sentence to draw the hearers or readers in as one's own people, about as my friends or folks) (r:zd:24742/zd:18200) (q:draft, low confidence)
eibek = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:only we/we alone/just ourselves) (d:<ei> and <bek> written as one word: we and no others, ourselves only) (j:ei/bek) (r:zd:22171/zd:19676) (q:draft)
eidan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:our way/our own way) (d:<ei>, we, and <dan>, way, written as one word: the way we do things, our own manner; {eizia eidan} is our own ways and customs) (j:ei/dan) (r:zd:23667) (q:draft)
Eiffel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:tower) (f:travel) (w:Eiffel) (d:only in Eiffel Tower, the iron tower in Paris, France) (r:zd:26566) (q:draft)
eigam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:our country/our land) (d:<ei>, we, and <gam>, country, written as one word: our own country) (j:ei/gam) (r:zd:19676/zd:17651) (q:draft)
eiguak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/social) (w:by ourselves/on our own/alone) (d:<ei>, we, and <guak>, only, written as one word: we alone, only ourselves without others) (j:ei/guak) (r:zd:23488/zd:16788) (q:draft)
eikiang = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:to us/with us/our place) (d:<ei>, we, and <kiang>, side, written as one word: where we are, to us or from us) (j:ei/kiang) (r:zd:16336/zd:22557) (q:draft)
eilam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:our side/our part) (d:<ei> and <lam> written as one word: our side, we on our part, set against {amau lam}, their side) (j:ei/lam) (r:zd:19340/zd:25275/zd:23761) (q:draft)
eile = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:ourselves/we and) (d:<ei>, we, and <le>, and, written as one word; mostly in {eile-ei} or {eile ei}, ourselves, one another among us) (j:ei/le) (r:zd:23758/zd:14927) (q:draft)
eileh = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:ourselves/we ourselves) (d:<ei>, we, and <leh> written as one word, always followed by a second <ei>: {eileh ei} is we ourselves, by ourselves, one another among us) (j:ei/leh) (r:zd:11162/zd:15274/zd:19427) (q:draft)
eilehei = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday/social) (w:we ourselves/among ourselves/one another) (d:<ei>, <leh> and <ei> written as one word, literally we and we: we among ourselves, we to one another) (r:zd:22709/zd:17383) (q:draft)
eima = (i:3) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:ourselves/we ourselves/oneself) (d:<ei>, we, with <ma>, standing alone as the one who acts or is spoken of, we ourselves and not others; it is followed by a verb or by words such as <tung> and <sangin>, not by a noun that it owns) (r:zd:23204/zd:21268) (q:draft)
eimi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:our people/our own people) (d:<ei>, we, and <mi>, people, written as one word: people of our own kind, used by Zomi writers for the Zomi themselves) (j:ei/mi) (r:zd:16337/ts:3125/zd:24043) (q:draft)
eimite = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:our people/our own people) (d:<ei>, we, with <mite>, people, written as one word: our own people, said by Zomi writers of the Zomi) (j:ei/mite) (r:zd:9266/zd:25186) (q:draft)
eipau = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/education) (w:our language/our own language) (d:<ei> and <pau> written as one word: our own language, by which Zomi writers mean Zolai) (j:ei/pau) (r:zd:19676/zd:19371/zd:25573) (q:draft)
eisang = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:than us/than we) (d:<ei>, we, and a short form of <sangin>, than, written as one word: more than us, before us) (r:zd:26444/zd:25927) (q:draft)
eisung = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:social) (w:among ourselves/within us) (d:<ei> and <sung> written as one word: inside us, among our own people) (j:ei/sung) (r:zd:23488/zd:25152) (q:draft)
eitawh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:with us/to us) (d:<ei> and <tawh> written as one word: with us, and before <kituak> or <kilawm> suited to us) (j:ei/tawh) (r:zd:20905/zd:23011/zd:16844) (q:draft)
eite = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:we/us/our) (d:first person plural including the hearer; whether English has we, us or our depends on its place in the sentence) (s:eimau) (b:ei) (r:58.10.15)
eiteng = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday/social) (w:all of us/we ourselves/we) (d:<ei>, we, with <teng>, here all: all of us, we among ourselves, including the hearer) (b:ei) (r:zd:25399/zd:22369/zd:24156) (q:draft)
eizong = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:we also/we too/us too) (d:<ei>, we, and <zong>, also, written as one word) (j:ei/zong) (r:zd:19676/zd:14686) (q:draft)
