hanthawtna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:encouragement/exhortation/motivational talk) (d:noun from <hanthawn>, encourage: words that stir someone to act; {hanthawtna pia} is give encouragement and {hanthawtna nei} is give a talk of exhortation) (b:hanthawn) (r:zd:10743/zd:21037) (q:draft)
hanthohna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/religion) (w:encouragement/exhortation/urging) (d:{hanthoh}, another spelling of <hanthot>, urge, with the noun suffix <na>: words that urge or encourage someone to act) (b:hanthot) (r:zd:12044/zd:21552/zd:20168) (q:draft)
hanthotna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:social/religion) (w:encouragement/exhortation/urging) (d:<hanthot>, urge on, with the noun suffix <na>: words that urge or hearten people, also a short sermon; with <nei> or <pia>, give encouragement or urge) (r:zd:9262/ts:12490/zd:23172) (q:draft)
hap = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/social) (w:snap at/scold/shout at) (d:speak to someone sharply and angrily; paired with <tawng>, threaten, and followed by words such as <pahpah> and <lala> for doing it readily or repeatedly) (r:zd:11653/zd:24131) (q:draft, low confidence)
