ihpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/social) (w:our father/our fathers) (d:<ih>, our, with <pa>, father, written as one word; mostly in {ihpu ihpa te}, our forefathers) (j:ih/pa) (r:zd:8668/zd:18258) (q:draft)
ihpaam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/home) (w:our surroundings/our neighbourhood) (d:<ih>, our, and <paam> written as one word, the second half of the pairs {ihkiim ihpaam} and {ihveng ihpaam}: the area and neighbourhood around us) (j:ih/paam) (r:zd:22584/zd:13297) (q:draft)
ihpai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:we go) (d:<ih>, another spelling of <i>, we, written as one word with <pai>, go: we go, when we go) (j:i/pai) (r:zd:23784/zd:14709/zd:19421) (q:draft)
ihpiak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:we give/that we give) (d:<ih>, we, and <piak>, give, written as one word: we give, or what we give) (j:ih/piak) (r:zd:22171/zd:25275) (q:draft)
ihpilna = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:education/social) (w:our knowledge/our wisdom) (d:<ih>, we or our, and <pilna>, knowledge, written as one word) (j:i/pilna) (r:zd:22652) (q:draft)
ihpu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/social) (w:our forefathers/our ancestors) (d:<ih>, our, written as one word with <pu>, grandfather; found in the pair <ihpu ihpa>, our forefathers) (j:ih/pu) (r:zd:8668/zd:21590) (q:draft)
ihpu ihpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/social) (w:our forefathers/our ancestors) (d:<ihpu>, our grandfathers, paired with <ihpa>, our fathers: our forefathers, the generations before us, mostly followed by <te>) (r:zd:8668/zd:20170) (q:draft)
ihsa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:we consider/we think/we regard) (d:<ih>, we, and <sa>, consider or feel, written as one word: we regard as, we think it to be) (j:ih/sa) (r:zd:25053/zd:23635) (q:draft)
ihsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:we consider/we think/we find) (d:<ih>, we, and <sak>, here feel or consider, written as one word: what we feel or take to be so, as in {nuam ihsak}, what we find pleasant) (j:ih/sak) (r:zd:25932/zd:25926/zd:25919) (q:draft)
ihsep = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:we do/we work) (d:<ih>, a spelling of <i>, we, and <sep> written as one word: that we do, our doing; {ihsep ding} is what we must do) (j:i/sep) (r:zd:25924/zd:15407/zd:25932) (q:draft)
ihsiam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/education) (w:we are skilled/we know how) (d:<ih>, we, and <siam>, be skilled, written as one word: we are good at it, we know how to) (j:ih/siam) (r:zd:21056/zd:19676) (q:draft)
