ihta = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:family) (w:our children/our child) (d:<ih>, our, and <ta>, child, written as one word; often paired as {ihtu ihta}, our grandchildren and children, and {ihta ihnau}, our children and younger ones) (j:ih/ta) (r:zd:11748/zd:12395) (q:draft)
ihtate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:our children) (d:<ih> and <tate> written as one word: our children) (j:ih/tate) (r:zd:16949/zd:14879) (q:draft)
