ihtun = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:we arrive/we reach) (d:<ih>, we, and <tun>, arrive, written as one word before <ciang>, <na> and similar words: when we arrive, where we arrive) (j:ih/tun) (r:zd:16249/zd:10682) (q:draft)
ihzakzak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:that we keep hearing/well-known) (d:<ih> and <zakzak> written as one word: that we hear again and again, said of a person or thing everyone has heard of) (j:ih/zakzak) (r:zd:15816/zd:13236) (q:draft)
ihzat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:we use) (d:<ih>, we, and <zat>, use, written as one word: that we use, our using) (j:ih/zat) (r:zd:25924/zd:22584) (q:draft)
