kanau = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:family) (w:my younger sibling/my younger brother/my younger sister) (d:<ka>, my, and <nau>, here a younger brother or sister, written as one word) (j:ka/nau) (r:zd:16442/zd:25768) (q:draft)
Kanbalu = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:politics/travel) (w:Kanbalu) (d:town and district in Sagaing Region, Myanmar, on the road from Shwebo to Myitkyina) (r:ts:12366) (q:draft)
Kanbawza = (i:1) (t:name) (f:work) (w:Kanbawza) (d:name of a private bank of Myanmar, Kanbawza Bank) (r:zd:15913/zd:17385) (q:draft)
kanbeh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/everyday) (w:research further/inquire further/look into more) (d:<kan>, search or look into, with <beh>, here more, in addition: look further into a matter, find out more about it) (j:kan/beh) (r:zd:20169/zd:24022) (q:draft)
kancian = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/work) (w:investigate/look into/examine closely) (d:<kan>, search, with <cian>, carefully: look into a matter thoroughly to find out what happened) (r:zd:15019/zd:19307) (q:draft)
kancianding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:will investigate thoroughly) (d:<kan>, look into, <cian>, thoroughly, and <ding>, will, written as one word: will investigate fully) (j:kan/cian/ding) (r:zd:21618/zd:19480) (q:draft)
kancianlai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/work) (w:be still investigating/be looking into) (d:<kancian>, investigate, and <lai>, still, written as one word: the inquiry is still going on) (j:kancian/lai) (r:zd:12619/zd:15370) (q:draft)
kancianna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:investigation/inquiry/examination) (d:<kan>, search, with <cian>, thoroughly, and the noun ending {-na}: a thorough looking into a matter, as by the police; {kancianna nei} is carry out an investigation) (r:zd:11389/zd:16131/zd:11229) (q:draft)
kanciansan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:investigate thoroughly/look into) (d:<kan>, look into, with <cian>, clearly, and <san>: examine a matter closely to find out what happened; said of police and authorities, often as {aki kanciansan laitak}, it is being investigated) (r:zd:19054/zd:13135) (q:draft)
Kandawgyi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Kandawgyi) (d:a lake with a park in Yangon; a hotel beside it bears the same name) (r:zd:23729/zd:15842) (q:draft)
kanding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/everyday) (w:to investigate/to look into/to seek) (d:<kan>, search or inquire, and <ding>, will or in order to, written as one word: to look into a matter; {thuthang kanding in} is in order to get the news) (j:kan/ding) (r:zd:13084/zd:20050/zd:13046) (q:draft)
kanei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I have/we hold) (d:<ka>, I, and <nei>, have, written as one word; with a noun of action, I or we held it, as a service or a meeting) (j:ka/nei) (r:zd:20016/zd:12487/zd:20587) (q:draft)
kaneih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I have/that I have) (d:<ka> and <neih> written as one word: that I have or take; {zi kaneih} is my taking a wife) (j:ka/neih) (r:zd:20503/zd:12630/zd:24411) (q:draft)
kaneikei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I do not have/I have no) (d:<ka>, I, and <neikei>, not have, written as one word) (j:ka/neikei) (r:zd:15385/zd:15598) (q:draft)
kanek = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food/everyday) (w:I eat/I take) (d:<ka>, I, and <nek>, eat, written as one word: I eat or we eat, said also of taking medicine; the form used before words such as <ciangin> and <leh>) (j:ka/nek) (r:zd:11508/zd:25616) (q:draft)
kaneu = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:family/time) (w:when I was small) (d:<ka> and <neu> written as one word: I being small; mostly in {kaneu lai}, when I was a child, and {kaneu a kipan}, since I was small) (j:ka/neu) (r:zd:23661/zd:10660) (q:draft)
kang = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:white) (d:white in colour, said of a horse, of hair or of a patch of skin; also written <kaang>) (s:kaang) (a:vom) (q:draft)
kang = (i:4) (t:v) (f:food) (w:fry) (d:cook food in hot oil, said with <sathau>, oil, as in {sathau tawh kikang}, fried in oil; not the burning of a house or the drying up of water) (r:zd:21557) (q:draft, low confidence)
kangah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I get/I receive/I got) (d:<ka>, the first person singular, and <ngah>, get, written as one word: I get or received it) (j:ka/ngah) (r:zd:13148/zd:17971/zd:19779) (q:draft)
kangaihsun = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I think/I consider) (d:<ka> and <ngaihsun> written as one word: I think, I consider) (j:ka/ngaihsun) (r:zd:19676/zd:19302) (q:draft)
