kangdeugawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/body) (w:be badly scalded/be badly burned) (d:of the skin, the mouth or another part of the body, be burned or scalded all over by hot water, acid or the like; <kang>, burn, with {deu} and <gawp>, severely) (r:zd:15521/zd:17986) (q:draft)
kangen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:I ask for/I pray) (d:<ka>, I, and <ngen>, ask, written as one word: I ask for something; {thu kangen} is I pray or I prayed) (j:ka/ngen) (r:zd:12487/zd:20341/zd:15107) (q:draft)
kanget = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:I ask for/I request) (d:<ka>, I, and <nget>, ask for, written as one word: I asked, with <uh> we asked, or what I asked for; {thu kanget} is I prayed) (j:ka/nget) (r:zd:24411/zd:12487/zd:21461) (q:draft)
kangmei = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/nature) (w:fire/blaze) (d:a fire that burns houses or land, from <kang>, burn, and <mei>, fire; {kangmei patau} or {patau kangmei} is a fire emergency) (r:zd:22584/zd:22658) (q:draft)
