kapia = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I give/I gave) (d:the first person marker <ka> written together with <pia>, give: I give or we give, with the giver as the speaker; usually written as two words, {ka pia}) (r:zd:23037/zd:25165/zd:15323) (q:draft)
kapiak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I give/I gave) (d:<ka> and <piak> written as one word: I give or I gave, and with <uh> we gave) (j:ka/piak) (r:zd:16442/zd:23071/zd:25046) (q:draft)
kapian = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/family) (w:I was born/my birth) (d:<ka>, I or my, and <pian>, be born, written as one word; {kapian'na} is my birthplace) (j:ka/pian) (r:zd:17448/zd:17325) (q:draft)
kapiang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/everyday) (w:I was born) (d:<ka> and <piang>, be born, written as one word: I was born) (j:ka/piang) (r:zd:21090) (q:draft)
kapianna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/everyday) (w:my birth/my origin/my birthplace) (d:<ka>, my, and <pianna>, birth or origin, written as one word: my birth, where or from whom I was born) (j:ka/pianna) (r:zd:21090/zd:12370) (q:draft)
kapin = (i:2) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:shooting/firing at) (d:<kap.2>, shoot, with the linking suffix <in>: shooting at someone or something and then doing something else, often after <thautawh>, with a gun, where sense 1 is weeping) (b:kap) (r:zd:17439/zd:11799/ts:9743) (q:draft)
kapkap = (i:2) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:keep shooting/keep firing) (d:<kap.2>, shoot, said twice: fire guns or shells again and again; neighbouring words such as {thaupi tang}, shells, show that it is not weeping) (r:zd:25109) (q:draft, low confidence)
kapkawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:while weeping/in tears) (d:<kap>, weep, and <kawm>, while, written as one word: weeping while doing something else) (j:kap/kawm) (r:zd:17478/zd:19943) (q:draft)
kapkawm = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:while shooting/firing as one goes) (d:<kap>, shoot, and <kawm>, while, written as one word: shooting while doing something else, as while running away) (j:kap/kawm) (r:zd:12845) (q:draft)
kapkawmkawm = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:while weeping/in tears) (d:<kap> and <kawmkawm> written as one word: weeping all the while) (j:kap/kawmkawm) (r:zd:15255/zd:20446) (q:draft)
kapkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:hit/shoot/wound by shooting) (d:<kap>, shoot, with <kha>, happen to reach: hit a person or a part of the body with a shot; also said of the sun striking someone) (b:kap) (r:zd:17439/zd:13131/zd:19478) (q:draft)
kapkhia = (i:2) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:shoot down/fire/shoot) (d:<kap> in its sense of shoot, with <khia>, out: fire a shot, or bring down an aircraft or a bird by shooting; {vanleng kapkhia} is shoot down a plane) (r:ts:6447/zd:14742/zd:24490) (q:draft)
kapkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:shoot down) (d:<kap>, shoot, and <khiat>, out or down, written as one word: bring down an aircraft by shooting, in the form used before words such as <sak> and <khit>) (j:kap/khiat) (r:ts:8273) (q:draft, low confidence)
kapkhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:launcher/firing system) (d:<kap>, shoot, with <khiat>, out, and the noun ending {-na}: a weapon or device from which missiles or rockets are fired) (r:zd:10886/zd:17591) (q:draft)
kapkhiatsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:shoot down) (d:<kap>, shoot, with <khiatsak>, written as one word: shoot an aircraft or missile down) (j:kap/khiatsak) (r:ts:5564/ts:10868) (q:draft)
kapkhuan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:permission to shoot/licence to shoot) (d:<kap>, shoot, and <khuan>, permission, written as one word; {thautawh kapkhuan pia} is give leave to shoot with guns) (j:kap/khuan) (r:zd:14783) (q:draft, low confidence)
kapkik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:shoot back/return fire) (d:<kap>, shoot, and <kik>, back, written as one word: fire back at those who shot) (j:kap/kik) (r:zd:12437/ts:3254) (q:draft)
kapkik = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:cry again/weep again) (d:<kap>, weep, and <kik>, again, written as one word) (j:kap/kik) (r:zd:12319) (q:draft, low confidence)
kapliam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/politics) (w:shoot and wound/wound by shooting) (d:<kap>, shoot, and <liam>, be wounded, written as one word: wound someone with a shot; {kapliam athuak} is one who was shot and wounded) (j:kap/liam) (r:zd:19868/zd:17556) (q:draft)
kapliamkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media) (w:be shot and wounded/shoot and wound) (d:<kapliam>, wound by shooting, with <kha>, happen to: hit and wound someone with a shot) (j:kapliam/kha) (r:zd:19991) (q:draft)
kaplo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:not shoot) (d:<kap>, shoot, and <lo>, not, written as one word: not shoot at, not attack with guns; the same spelling can be <kap>, weep, with <lo>, not weep) (j:kap/lo) (r:zd:17709/zd:12803) (q:draft)
kaploh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:not shoot/not fire) (d:<kap>, shoot, and the negative <loh> written as one word: not shooting; {kaploh phamawh} is cannot but shoot, have to shoot) (j:kap/loh) (r:ts:11979/zd:14859) (q:draft)
kaplumkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:shoot dead) (d:<kaplum>, shoot dead, with <kha>, happen to, written as one word: shoot someone dead, also by accident) (j:kaplum/kha) (r:zd:17032) (q:draft)
kaplumpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media) (w:man who shot dead/gunman) (d:<kaplum> and <pa> written as one word: the man who shot someone dead; after <aki>, {aki kaplumpa}, the man who was shot dead) (j:kaplum/pa) (r:zd:10813/zd:17766) (q:draft)
kaplumpah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:shoot dead at once/shoot dead on the spot) (d:<kaplum>, shoot dead, with <pah>, at once, written as one word) (j:kaplum/pah) (r:zd:13082/zd:15537) (q:draft)
kaplumthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:manage to shoot dead/be able to shoot dead) (d:<kaplum>, shoot dead, and <thei>, able, written as one word: succeed in shooting someone or something dead) (j:kaplum/thei) (r:zd:15537/zd:20310) (q:draft)
kaplup = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:shoot dead/shoot down) (d:form of <kaplum>, shoot dead, used before words such as <thuak> and <khit>; {kaplup thuak} is be shot) (b:kaplum) (r:zd:16313/zd:19973) (q:draft)
kaplupna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:fatal shooting/shooting dead) (d:<kaplup>, form of <kaplum>, shoot dead, with the noun suffix <na>: the act, the time or the place of shooting someone dead; {a ki kaplupna} is where or when someone was shot dead) (r:zd:17614/zd:19324) (q:draft)
kaplupsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:be shot dead/shoot dead) (d:<kaplup>, shoot dead, and <sak>, here marking that the act is done to someone belonging to the speaker, written as one word: with <hongki> before it, one of ours was shot dead) (j:kaplup/sak) (r:zd:15214) (q:draft, low confidence)
kapmasa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:shoot first/fire first) (d:<kap>, shoot, and <masa>, first, written as one word: shoot at someone before being shot at) (j:kap/masa) (r:zd:17030/zd:13082) (q:draft)
kappah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:shoot at once/open fire) (d:<kap>, shoot, and <pah> written as one word: shoot immediately) (j:kap/pah) (r:ts:1610/zd:16926) (q:draft)
kapsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/politics) (w:try to shoot/plan to shoot/fire at) (d:<kap>, shoot, and <sawm>, intend or attempt, written as one word: attempt or plan to shoot at someone or something with a gun or missile) (j:kap/sawm) (r:zd:20087/zd:14933) (q:draft)
Kapteel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel/social) (w:Kapteel) (d:a Zomi village and its land in the Tedim area of Chin State, Myanmar; written in brackets after a personal name it shows the home village) (r:zd:20513/zd:20406) (q:draft)
kapu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:my grandfather/my forefather) (d:<ka> and <pu> written as one word: my grandfather; {kapu kapa te} is my forefathers, and before a name it is said with respect of an older man of the family) (j:ka/pu) (r:zd:16651/zd:15344) (q:draft)
kapua = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:I carry/I am carrying) (d:<ka>, the first person marker, and <pua>, carry, written as one word: I carry, I have with me) (j:ka/pua) (r:zd:10973/zd:17120) (q:draft)
kapumpi = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:body) (w:my body) (d:<ka> and <pumpi> written as one word: my body) (j:ka/pumpi) (r:zd:19021/zd:13314) (q:draft)
kapzan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:blast/shell/shoot to pieces) (d:<kap>, shoot, with <zan>, of uncertain sense here: hit with gunfire, shells or mines so that the target is shattered; only seen in war reports) (r:ts:3110) (q:draft, low confidence)
kapziahziah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/family) (w:weep bitterly/cry and cry) (d:<kap>, weep, and <ziahziah> written as one word: weep freely and without stopping) (j:kap/ziahziah) (r:zd:15385/zd:15368) (q:draft)
kapziahziah = (i:2) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:shoot repeatedly) (d:<kap>, shoot, and <ziahziah> written as one word: fire shot after shot at someone) (j:kap/ziahziah) (r:zd:17969) (q:draft, low confidence)
Karak = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Karak) (d:town in Pahang, Malaysia, named in the articles for the highway between it and Kuala Lumpur) (r:zd:19120/zd:12701) (q:draft, low confidence)
Karaoke = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media) (w:karaoke) (d:singing to recorded music, and the place where this is done) (o:English) (r:zd:12673/zd:12048) (q:draft)
Karen = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people/land) (f:politics/social) (w:Karen) (d:a people of eastern and southern Myanmar and of Thailand, and their land, Karen State) (r:zd:25203/zd:18081/zd:23317) (q:draft)
Karenni = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people/land) (f:politics) (w:Karenni/Kayah) (d:the Karenni or Kayah people of eastern Myanmar and their state, Kayah State; in the news mostly of the Karenni armed groups) (r:zd:22818/ts:6447) (q:draft)
Karnataka = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel) (w:Karnataka) (d:state in the south-west of India; its capital is Bangalore) (r:zd:11382) (q:draft)
kasa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I think/I feel/I find) (d:<ka>, I, and <sa>, feel or consider, written as one word, placed after a describing word: {thupi kasa hi} is I consider it important) (j:ka/sa) (r:zd:17291/zd:24347/zd:23037) (q:draft)
kasak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I find/I consider) (d:<ka>, I, written as one word with <sak>, here the form of <sa> in its sense feel or find to be, that stands before a noun: {lamdang kasak} is what I find strange) (j:ka/sak) (r:zd:19242/zd:23022) (q:draft)
kasakei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I do not think/I do not feel/I do not find) (d:<kasa>, I think or feel, with the negative <kei>, written as one word after a describing word: {dik kasakei hi} is I do not think it right) (j:kasa/kei) (r:zd:15366/zd:24420) (q:draft)
kasakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:what I consider/what I find) (d:<ka>, I, and <sakna>, here the noun form of <sa>, feel or regard as, written as one word after a describing word: what I find to be so, as {kisam kasakna}, what I consider necessary) (j:ka/sakna) (r:zd:22577/zd:22774) (q:draft)
kasakna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:media) (w:my singing) (d:<ka>, I, and <sakna>, singing, written as one word: my singing, in {la kasakna}, my singing of songs) (j:ka/sakna) (r:zd:23666) (q:draft, low confidence)
kasam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:I call/I summon) (d:<ka>, I, and <sam>, call, written as one word: I called, we called someone or called him by a name) (j:ka/sam) (r:zd:16241/zd:15366) (q:draft)
kasang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I accept/I receive) (d:<ka>, I, with <saang>, accept, written as one word: I accept or take what is said or offered) (j:ka/saang) (r:zd:19676) (q:draft, low confidence)
kasang = (i:2) (t:n) (f:education) (w:my school) (d:<ka>, my, with <sang>, school, written as one word: my school; {kasang kah} is I attend school) (j:ka/sang) (r:zd:23797/zd:23014) (q:draft, low confidence)
kasap = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:I call/we call/invite) (d:<ka> and <sap> written as one word: I called or invited, and with <uh>, we called) (j:ka/sap) (r:zd:16442/zd:16511) (q:draft)
kasem = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:work/do) (d:<ka>, I, and <sem> written as one word: I work, I do, I serve as) (j:ka/sem) (r:zd:20892/zd:25192/zd:16245) (q:draft)
