luanziate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/nature) (w:trends/courses/currents) (d:<luanzia>, course or trend, with the plural <te>: the ways things are going; often {khuahun luanziate}, the trends of the times) (b:luanzia) (r:zd:21252/zd:23084) (q:draft)
luatding = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:to be too much/overly) (d:<luat>, too much, and <ding> written as one word after a verb or describing word: to do or be so too much; mostly denied, as {lungmuan luatding hilo}, one should not be too sure) (j:luat/ding) (r:zd:14709/zd:16164) (q:draft)
