mah bangun = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday/religion) (w:just as/in the same way as) (d:the emphatic <mah> with <bangun>, as, the form used when several people are addressed or act: closes a clause, just as that is done, and the main clause follows; the plural counterpart of <mahbangin>) (s:mahbangin) (r:zd:26953/zd:15572/zd:23297) (q:draft)
mah taleh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:even though/although/even if) (d:<mah>, the stressing marker, and <taleh>, even if: placed after the verb of a clause, often after <phial>, even though that is so; the main clause follows) (s:phial) (r:zd:22040/zd:25322) (q:draft)
mah tase = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:even though/although indeed) (d:<mah>, indeed, and <tase>, although: placed after a verb and followed by <leh> or {le uh}, even though that is truly so; the main clause that follows says what holds all the same; compare <taseleh>) (r:zd:21166/zd:22565/zd:21340) (q:draft)
maha = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:work/politics) (w:great/main) (d:Burmese word for great, used in {maha dat line}, the main power line of the national electricity grid) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:24544/zd:10860) (q:draft, low confidence)
maha = (i:2) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (d:<mah>, the emphatic marker, and <a> written as one word after a noun or {tua bang}: just so, at that very place) (j:mah/a) (r:zd:25668) (q:draft, low confidence)
Maharajalela = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel/education) (w:Maharajalela) (d:area and street, Jalan Maharajalela, in Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia; in the articles mostly the name of the Zomi Education Center school there) (r:zd:21906) (q:draft, low confidence)
mahbang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:just as/just like/in the same way) (d:<mah> and <bang> written as one word, followed by <in>: exactly as; {tua mahbang in} is in that same way, likewise) (j:mah/bang) (r:zd:16114/zd:12765/zd:25414) (q:draft)
mahbangin = (i:1) (t:ppm) (f:everyday) (w:just as/just like/in the same way as) (d:<mah> and <bangin> written as one word, placed after a noun or clause: exactly as, in the very same way as; {tua mahbangin} is in that same way, likewise) (j:mah/bangin) (r:zd:20670/zd:19875/zd:21869) (q:draft)
mahbangun = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:just as/just like/in the same way as) (d:<mahbang> and <un> written as one word: exactly as, in the same way as, used where the people spoken of are more than one) (j:mahbang/un) (r:zd:15305/zd:19586) (q:draft)
mahbek = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:only/alone) (d:<mah> and <bek> written as one word after a pronoun or noun: that one alone, no other; {a mahbek} is he alone, usually written {amah bek}) (j:mah/bek) (r:zd:23984/zd:22983) (q:draft)
mahding = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:surely will/really will) (d:the emphatic <mah> and <ding> written as one word after a verb: it will certainly be so; in a question, will it really) (j:mah/ding) (r:zd:23485/zd:16844/zd:21989) (q:draft)
mahhi = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:indeed/truly) (d:emphatic <mah> and sentence-final <hi> written as one word at the end of a statement: it is indeed so) (j:mah/hi) (r:zd:24464/zd:21340) (q:draft)
mahhiam = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:the emphatic <mah> with the question particle <hiam>, written as one word at the end of a question: is it really so, is it indeed) (j:mah/hiam) (r:zd:21392/zd:15116) (q:draft)
mahinzong = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:also just/even on that very) (d:<mahin> and <zong>, also, written as one word after a word of time or place: on that very day too, in that very place too) (j:mahin/zong) (r:zd:14535/zd:17622) (q:draft)
Mahkahmah = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:court/law court) (d:a court of law in Malaysia, where an arrested person is brought before a judge) (s:thukhenzum) (o:Malay, mahkamah) (r:zd:12112/zd:15379) (q:draft)
mahleh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:although/though/even though) (d:<mah> and <leh> written as one word after a verb: although it is so, even though) (s:napi) (j:mah/leh) (r:zd:24375/zd:22584) (q:draft)
mahlo = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:not at all/by no means) (d:<mah> and <lo> written as one word, a strong negative after the verb, mostly as {peuh mahlo}: not at all, certainly not) (j:mah/lo) (r:ts:1202/zd:25186/zd:25515) (q:draft)
mahmah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:the very thing/very/indeed) (d:emphasises the word before it: after a describing word or verb it means very or indeed, after a noun the very one) (s:nakpi/nakpitakin)
mahmahden = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:always very/very much all the time) (d:<mahmah>, very, and <den>, always, written as one word, after a verb or describing word: very much so and constantly) (j:mahmah/den) (r:zd:20153/zd:12053) (q:draft)
mahmahding = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:will be very/will very much) (d:<mahmah> and <ding> written as one word after a verb or describing word: it will be so to a high degree, or is expected to be) (j:mahmah/ding) (r:zd:15099/zd:17955/zd:16934) (q:draft)
mahmahhi = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:very/indeed) (d:<mahmah>, very, and the sentence-final <hi>, written as one word at the end of a statement: it is very much so) (j:mahmah/hi) (r:zd:17933/zd:21003) (q:draft)
mahmahkhat = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/media) (w:a very) (d:<mahmah> and <khat> written as one word, after a describing word: one that is very so, as {minthang mahmahkhat}, a very famous one) (j:mahmah/khat) (r:zd:17547/zd:12244/zd:15245) (q:draft)
mahmahkhin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:already very/very much already) (d:<mahmah>, very, and <khin>, already, written as one word after a describing word or verb: the state is already fully reached) (j:mahmah/khin) (r:zd:17301/zd:11587) (q:draft)
mahmahlai = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:still very) (d:<mahmah> with <lai>, here still, written as one word, after a describing word: still very much so) (b:mahmah) (r:zd:19355/zd:17735) (q:draft)
mahmahleh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:if very/very much as if) (d:<mahmah>, very, and <leh> written as one word: if really so; before <kilawm> it says that something seems very much so) (j:mahmah/leh) (r:zd:21937/zd:15385) (q:draft)
mahmahlel = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:quite/really just/simply very) (d:<mahmah>, very, and <lel>, just, written as one word after a describing word or verb, often before the closing <hi> or <uhhi>: simply very, quite so) (j:mahmah/lel) (r:zd:17899/zd:19215) (q:draft, low confidence)
mahmahliang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:very much indeed/exceedingly) (d:<mahmah>, very, and <liang>, even, written as one word after a verb or describing word: very much indeed, to a striking degree) (j:mahmah/liang) (r:zd:21618/zd:14587) (q:draft)
mahmahlo = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:not at all/not really/hardly) (d:<mahmah> and <lo> written as one word, placed after a verb: not really, not at all; {muzo mahmahlo} is not able to find at all) (j:mahmah/lo) (r:zd:26495/zd:12042) (q:draft)
mahmahmawk = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:very indeed/truly very) (d:<mahmah> and <mawk> written as one word after a describing word: very much so, said with surprise or dismay) (j:mahmah/mawk) (r:zd:14731/zd:15781/zd:12752) (q:draft)
mahmahna = (i:2) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:where there is very much/where very many) (d:before a noun of place such as <gam> or <mun>, the ending <na> means the place where: {atam mahmahna gamkhat} is a country where there are very many of something) (r:zd:12161/zd:17575/zd:15801) (q:draft)
mahmahpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (d:<mahmah>, very, and the topic marker <pen> written as one word after a describing word: the one that is very so, what is very much so) (j:mahmah/pen) (r:zd:19367/zd:17428) (q:draft, low confidence)
mahmahta = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:very much now/indeed now) (d:<mahmah> and <ta> written as one word: very, with the sense that the state has now been reached, as in {haksa mahmahta}, it has become very hard) (j:mahmah/ta) (r:zd:24276/zd:19599) (q:draft)
mahmahtawh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (d:<mahmah>, very, and <tawh>, with, written as one word, before {akibat hangin}: although it is like something that is very so, although it seems very so) (j:mahmah/tawh) (r:zd:19932/zd:15116) (q:draft)
mahmahtek = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:very much, each one/all very) (d:<mahmah> and <tek> written as one word, after a verb or describing word: very much so, said of everyone concerned) (j:mahmah/tek) (r:zd:21279/zd:19807/zd:15507) (q:draft)
mahmahthei = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:can be very) (d:<mahmah>, very, and <thei>, can, written as one word after a describing word or verb: can be very much so) (j:mahmah/thei) (r:zd:16152/zd:19932) (q:draft)
mahmahzong = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:even) (d:<mahmah> and <zong> written as one word after a noun or phrase: even that very one, even itself) (j:mahmah/zong) (r:zd:15609/zd:15056) (q:draft)
mahpan = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:everyday) (w:from that very/right from) (d:<mah>, the very one, and <pan>, from, written as one word: from that same place, source or thing and no other) (j:mah/pan) (r:zd:24234/zd:14654/zd:23906) (q:draft)
mahpeuh = (i:1) (t:det) (f:everyday) (w:whoever/anyone at all/every) (d:<mah> and <peuh> written as one word, placed after a question word: <akua mahpeuh> is whoever it may be, everyone) (j:mah/peuh) (r:zd:17335/zd:12289/zd:25318) (q:draft)
Mahsahlah = (i:1) (t:name) (f:politics) (w:Burma Socialist Programme Party/BSPP) (d:Burmese short name of the Burma Socialist Programme Party, the single ruling party of Burma from 1962 to 1988, and of its government and time) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:21117) (q:draft)
mahta = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:even if/even though) (d:<mah> and <ta> written as one word after a verb and followed by <leh> or <le>: even if it is indeed so, granted that) (j:mah/ta) (r:zd:16897/zd:20358/zd:24244) (q:draft)
mahtaleh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:even though/although/even if) (d:<mah> and <taleh> written as one word after a verb or describing word: even though it is so) (j:mah/taleh) (r:zd:20271/zd:8668) (q:draft)
mahtawh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:with that very/just like) (d:<mah> and <tawh> written as one word, placed after a noun or pronoun: with that very thing, by that itself; with <kibang>, just the same as) (j:mah/tawh) (r:zd:15572/zd:20932/zd:22282) (q:draft)
mahteh = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<mah> with <teh>, placed after a verb or describing word to stress it: indeed, surely) (j:mah/teh) (r:zd:25628/zd:17313) (q:draft, low confidence)
mahuh = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:indeed/the very ones) (d:the emphatic <mah> and the plural <uh> written as one word: they indeed, the very ones, they themselves) (j:mah/uh) (r:zd:20263/zd:21862) (q:draft)
mahzong = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:also/too/even) (d:the emphatic <mah> and <zong>, also, written as one word, placed after the word they add: that very one as well; {a mahzong} is he himself too) (j:mah/zong) (r:zd:16916/zd:23782) (q:draft)
mai = (i:4) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:just/simply) (d:placed after the verb, most often as {hi mai hi}: simply, just, nothing else than; it is not the noun face or front, which stands before <ah> and <lam>) (r:zd:22686/zd:25067) (q:draft)
Maid = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/home) (w:maid/housemaid/domestic worker) (d:a woman who is employed to do the work of a household and lives in it) (o:English) (r:zd:15103/zd:11285) (q:draft)
maiding = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:the particle <mai>, here just or simply, with <ding>, will, written as one word after a verb: will just, may well, should simply; in a question, whether one should just do it) (r:zd:11166/zd:15000) (q:draft, low confidence)
maiet = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:curry favour with/seek to please/win over) (d:<mai>, face, with <et>, look at: seek the favour of someone, try to please or placate, also with gifts or money) (r:zd:16331/zd:21138) (q:draft)
maikah = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:striker/forward) (d:in football, a player of the front line who attacks the goal, named beside <kungpang>, the goalkeeper, and {nungthup}, the defender) (r:zd:15622) (q:draft, low confidence)
