maita = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:just/simply/in the end) (d:placed after a verb at the end of a sentence, before <hi> or <uh>: the thing simply or finally came about, often because nothing else could be done; a word meaning just or simply, not <mai> the face, with <ta>) (r:zd:19295/zd:17187/zd:12167) (q:draft)
maitang kituah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:meet face to face/meet in person) (d:<maitang>, face, and <kituah>, meet: meet face to face, in person; the other person stands before it with <tawh>, and with <in> after it the pair says how people talk or see each other) (r:zd:16961/zd:15584) (q:draft)
maiteng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/travel) (w:front area/area in front) (d:<mai>, front, with <teng>, here in the sense all: the whole space in front of a building or place; {maiteng ah} is all along the front of) (r:zd:11535/zd:13149) (q:draft)
