maituah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:face/confront/meet face to face/deal with) (d:<mai>, face, and <tuah>, bring together, written as one word: turn the face towards someone or something and meet it, face a matter or a person; with <ki> before it, meet each other face to face) (j:mai/tuah) (r:zd:10963/zd:24206/zd:13354) (q:draft)
maituahna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:confrontation/facing/encounter) (d:meeting something or someone face to face: confronting a danger or an enemy, or a personal encounter) (r:zd:10984) (q:draft, low confidence)
maituam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/everyday) (w:face mask/mask/veil) (d:a covering for the face, <mai> with <tuam>, cover: a mask worn against disease or dust, also a veil; <maituam thuah> is wear a mask) (r:zd:24299/zd:23925/zd:24333) (q:draft)
maituam thuah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/everyday) (w:wear a mask/put on a face mask) (d:<maituam>, face mask, and <thuah>, here put on over: wear a face mask; common in health rules, often followed by <hamtang> <ding>, must without fail) (r:zd:24299/zd:24489) (q:draft)
Major = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:major) (d:an army or police officer's rank, above captain) (o:English) (r:zd:25097/zd:17745) (q:draft)
Major = (i:2) (t:n) (f:education) (w:major/main subject) (d:the main subject that a student chooses at a university) (o:English) (r:zd:20979/zd:20137) (q:draft)
majority = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:majority) (d:the greater number, as of seats or votes won in an election, or the larger group of a people) (o:English) (r:zd:20795/zd:16556) (q:draft)
mak = (i:2) (t:num) (f:work) (w:ten million/crore) (d:a number word for large sums of money, ten million, the Indian crore, as in {mak nih}, twenty million; it stands before or after the figure, and some writers use it for a million) (r:zd:23198/zd:16911) (q:draft, low confidence)
makaai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (j:makai) (r:zd:25569/zd:25687) (q:draft)
makaaite = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (j:makaite) (r:zd:25414/zd:25678) (q:draft)
makai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:leader/chief) (d:one who goes in front and is at the head of a tribe, a clan or a group of people) (s:makaipa/ukpi/ulian) (r:13.23.2) (q:draft)
makaiding = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:social/politics) (w:to be leader/future leader/will lead) (d:<makai>, leader or lead, and <ding>, will, written as one word: the one who is to be leader, or will lead) (j:makai/ding) (r:zd:19324/zd:16833) (q:draft)
makaihding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:will lead/to lead) (d:<makaih>, lead, and <ding> written as one word: will lead, is to lead) (j:makaih/ding) (r:zd:24313/zd:19579) (q:draft)
makaihsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/education) (w:lead for/guide for) (d:<makaih>, lead, and <sak> written as one word: lead or guide on behalf of someone; {hong makaihsak} is lead for us) (j:makaih/sak) (r:zd:9448) (q:draft)
makaihzia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:leadership/way of leading/leadership style) (d:<makaih>, lead, with <zia>, manner: the way a person leads) (b:makaih) (r:zd:16897/zd:17958) (q:draft)
makaikhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:a leader/one of the leaders) (d:<makai> and <khat> written as one word: a leader, one leader of a group) (j:makai/khat) (r:zd:16608/zd:10767) (q:draft)
makaipinu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:woman leader/female head/chairwoman) (d:<makaipi>, chief leader, with <nu>, woman: a woman who is at the head of a body, a company or a country) (b:makaipi) (r:zd:12420/zd:20263) (q:draft)
makaipite = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:top leaders/chief leaders/leaders) (d:<makaipi> with the plural <te>: the chief leaders of an organisation, a people or a government) (b:makaipi) (r:zd:23090/zd:24468/zd:24029) (q:draft)
makaiten = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:the leaders) (d:<makaite>, leaders, with the marker <in> shortened to {-n}: the leaders as the ones who act or speak) (j:makaite/in) (r:zd:17958/zd:22925) (q:draft)
makaiteng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:all the leaders/the leaders) (d:<makai>, leader, and <teng>, here in its sense of all of, written as one word: all the leaders, the leaders as a body) (j:makai/teng) (r:zd:23075/zd:23022) (q:draft)
makaithak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:new leader/new leaders) (d:<makai>, leader, and <thak>, new, written as one word: a newly chosen leader or leadership of a group, body or country) (j:makai/thak) (r:zd:12460/zd:20014/zd:12414) (q:draft)
makeup = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body/everyday) (w:make-up/cosmetics) (d:cosmetics put on the face, and the putting on of them) (o:English) (r:zd:15622/zd:15505) (q:draft)
Maku = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (f:religion) (w:Mark) (d:Mark the evangelist, and the Gospel that bears his name, in the spelling of Catholic writers; the Bible text writes <Marka>) (r:zd:23138) (q:draft)
mal = (i:2) (t:n) (f:nature/travel) (w:north) (d:the north, named as the opposite of the south in {sim leh mal}, south and north; not a counted item) (r:zd:19203/zd:21066) (q:draft)
Malacca = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land/city) (f:travel/politics) (w:Malacca/Melaka) (d:state on the west coast of Peninsular Malaysia, and its capital city) (r:zd:11078/zd:15481) (q:draft)
malak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:advance/go forward/proceed) (d:move forward, take a step ahead, used before <ding> and <sawm>; {kalsuan a malak ding} is to advance) (r:zd:15874/ts:3784) (q:draft, low confidence)
malakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:initiative/leadership/taking the lead) (d:{ma la}, take the lead, with the noun suffix {-na}: the act of going first or leading in a matter) (r:zd:25040/zd:21072) (q:draft, low confidence)
malam = (i:2) (t:n) (f:time) (w:the time before/earlier side) (d:<ma>, before, with <lam>, side: after a year, the time before or leading up to it, as {kum 1980 malam}, and beside {nung lam} the front as against the back; the other sense follows a verb, mostly as {pah malam}) (r:zd:9447/ts:3375) (q:draft, low confidence)
Malay = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:social/education) (w:Malay) (d:the Malay people of Malaysia and their language) (r:zd:20909/zd:20033) (q:draft)
Malaysia = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel/politics) (w:Malaysia) (d:country in Southeast Asia where many Zomi live as refugees and workers) (r:zd:20256/zd:13190) (q:draft)
Malaysian = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:politics/media) (w:Malaysian) (d:of Malaysia, the English word placed before a noun; {Malaysian gammi} is a citizen of Malaysia) (o:English) (r:zd:19552/zd:17115/zd:15301) (q:draft)
Malaysiate = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:politics/travel) (w:Malaysians) (d:<Malaysia> with the plural <te>: the people of Malaysia, or Malaysia as a nation) (b:Malaysia) (j:Malaysia/te) (r:zd:25399/zd:11798) (q:draft)
malep = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion/everyday) (w:foretaste/anticipation) (d:the experiencing of a thing before it comes; {vangam malep} is a foretaste of heaven, said of a happy home or of good company; also as a verb, have or live something beforehand) (r:zd:16606/zd:16254/zd:8667) (q:draft, low confidence)
malgawm = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:spelling/spell) (d:<mal>, single item or letter, with <gawm>, join: the putting together of letters to write a word, spelling; {malgawm zia} is the way of spelling) (r:zd:21152/zd:23069) (q:draft)
Malindo = (i:1) (t:name) (f:travel) (w:Malindo) (d:Malindo Air, an airline of Malaysia) (r:zd:18007) (q:draft)
Malkual = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Malkual) (d:name of an area of the Zomi homeland, named together with Cikha and Tonzang; apparently the northern part) (r:zd:25233) (q:draft, low confidence)
Mall = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/travel) (w:mall/shopping mall) (d:a large building with many shops; nearly always in {Shopping Mall} or in the name of one) (o:English) (r:zd:19788/zd:16952/zd:11683) (q:draft)
Maluri = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Maluri) (d:Taman Maluri, a part of Cheras in Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia, with a train station) (r:zd:18147/zd:21057) (q:draft)
mama = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (j:mahmah) (r:zd:16291) (q:draft, low confidence)
man = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:finish/complete) (d:placed after another verb to say that the action is finished; {a man khit ciangin} means after finishing) (s:mankhit/zawhkhit) (a:kipan) (q:draft)
man = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:true/right/correct) (d:true or right, in agreement with the facts or with what ought to be; {a man lo} is false or wrong) (s:maan/mantak) (a:manlo) (q:draft)
man = (i:3) (t:n) (f:work) (w:price/value/cost/payment) (d:what is paid or owed for something: its price, its value or the payment for it; {man pia} is to pay) (s:manzah) (q:draft)
man = (i:5) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:because/since) (d:after a verb and followed by <in>, gives the reason, the same as <manin> written as two words; {ahih man in} is because it is so, therefore) (s:manin) (r:ts:3366/zd:25016/zd:25928) (q:draft)
man ngenloin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:work/everyday) (w:free of charge/without charge/for free) (d:<man>, here the price or fee, and <ngenloin>, without asking: without asking payment, free of charge; stands before the verb that names the service given) (r:zd:23388) (q:draft)
manage = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:manage/handle) (d:English verb used in Zolai sentences for running or handling something) (o:English) (r:zd:19166) (q:draft, low confidence)
Management = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:management) (d:the running of an organisation, and the people who run it; mostly inside English titles such as Board of Management) (o:English) (r:zd:16018/zd:24156) (q:draft, low confidence)
manager = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:manager) (o:English) (r:zd:21876/zd:17295) (q:draft)
manawt = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:advance/go forward/press on/carry forward) (d:<ma>, front, with <nawt>, push: move ahead, make progress, or carry a task forward) (s:mainawt) (r:zd:10730/zd:20043/ts:7228) (q:draft)
manawtna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/work) (w:progress/advance/advancement) (d:<manawt>, advance, with the noun suffix {-na}: a going forward, progress) (s:khantohna) (b:manawt) (r:zd:24059/ts:4831) (q:draft)
manbek = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:only because) (d:<man>, because, and <bek>, only, written as one word, used as {manbek in}: only because, merely for the reason that) (j:man/bek) (r:zd:22451) (q:draft, low confidence)
manbek = (i:2) (t:phrase) (f:work) (d:<man>, price, and <bek>, only, written as one word after a sum: costing only that much) (j:man/bek) (r:zd:19727) (q:draft, low confidence)
Manchester = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Manchester) (d:city in England; also in the name of the football club Manchester United) (r:zd:13072/zd:12632) (q:draft)
manciang = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:time/everyday) (w:when finished/after) (d:<man>, finish, and <ciang>, when, written as one word after a verb or the name of an event: when it is over, after finishing) (j:man/ciang) (r:zd:12044/zd:25319) (q:draft)
mancip = (i:2) (t:v) (f:social) (w:arrest/capture/catch/hold) (d:catch a person and hold him fast, said of police, guards or an attacker and not of a feeling: {Hostage in mancip} is take as a hostage) (r:zd:13061/zd:20444/zd:19536) (q:draft)
Mandalay = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Mandalay) (d:the second largest city of Myanmar) (r:zd:25138/zd:10743/zd:22802) (q:draft)
Mandarin = (i:1) (t:name) (f:education/social) (w:Mandarin) (d:the standard spoken Chinese language; {Mandarin kampau} is the Mandarin language) (r:zd:11630/zd:15315) (q:draft)
mandat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:pandal/pavilion/festival stage) (d:a temporary stage or shelter put up for a festival or meeting, as at the Water Festival) (o:Burmese, mandat) (r:zd:15636/zd:12164) (q:draft)
manding = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:worth/cost/money for) (d:<man>, price, and <ding>, for, written as one word: after an amount, goods worth that much; after a thing, the money needed to pay for it, as {laibu manding}, money for books) (j:man/ding) (r:zd:15084/zd:15681/zd:14692) (q:draft)
manding = (i:2) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:to arrest/to catch/will arrest) (d:<man>, arrest or catch, and <ding>, will, written as one word: in order to arrest, will arrest) (j:man/ding) (r:zd:24948) (q:draft, low confidence)
mang = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday/body) (w:dream) (d:a dream seen in sleep; with <man>, catch, {mang man} is have a dream) (s:mumang) (r:zd:24119/ts:3372) (q:draft)
mang = (i:3) (t:adv) (f:everyday/media) (w:away/gone/lost) (d:placed after a verb of going or fleeing: away for good, so as to be gone or lost, as {taikhia mang}, flee away; {a si a mang} is the dead and the missing) (r:ts:5962/ts:693) (q:draft)
mangbang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:despair/be at a loss/be distressed) (d:be in distress of mind, not knowing what to do and without hope) (r:zd:12688/zd:24024) (q:draft, low confidence)
mangbatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/health) (w:distress/trouble/anxiety) (d:deep trouble of mind; often paired as {lungkham mangbatna}, worry and distress) (r:zd:15942/zd:15709) (q:draft)
mangcip = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/everyday) (w:go missing/disappear/vanish) (d:<mang>, here be lost from sight, with <cip>, completely: disappear without a trace, said of a person, a ship or an aircraft that cannot be found) (r:zd:15820/zd:17141/zd:11904) (q:draft)
mangciplai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media) (w:be still missing) (d:<mangcip>, go missing, and <lai>, still, written as one word: not yet found, still missing) (j:mangcip/lai) (r:zd:17632/zd:15886) (q:draft)
mangenlo = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:work) (w:free of charge/without charge) (d:<man>, price, <ngen>, ask for, and <lo>, not, written as one word: without asking payment, usually followed by <in>) (j:man/ngen/lo) (r:zd:22685/zd:21664) (q:draft, low confidence)
mangg = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:disappear/vanish/pass away) (d:spelling of <mang> in the sense be lost: disappear, vanish; of a person, pass away) (r:zd:23383/zd:21843) (q:draft, low confidence)
mangg = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (j:mang) (r:zd:20176) (q:draft, low confidence)
manggilh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (j:mangngilh) (r:zd:24060/zd:20697) (q:draft)
manghilh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (j:mangngilh) (r:zd:24244/zd:23223) (q:draft)
mangin = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:in a dream) (d:<mang>, a dream, with the marker <in>: in a dream, after <a> or <ka> and before what was dreamed; the obeying sense follows <thu> or the thing obeyed) (r:zd:19108/zd:23680/zd:19709) (q:draft)
Mangkaang = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:politics/social) (w:British/English) (d:the British, the white rulers of Burma before independence; also the English and their language) (r:zd:25569/ts:617) (q:draft)
Mangkam = (i:1) (t:name) (f:education/social) (w:English/English language) (d:the English language, {Mang}, the English or British, with <kam>, speech) (r:zd:9216/zd:23111/ts:9862) (q:draft)
Mangkama = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:education/religion) (w:in English/into English) (d:<Mangkam>, the English language, and <a>, in, written as one word: in English, into English) (j:Mangkam/a) (r:zd:9240/zd:9227) (q:draft)
Mangkamin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:education) (w:in English/into English) (d:<Mangkam>, the English language, and <in> written as one word: in English, into English, as with <teikhia>, translate) (j:Mangkam/in) (r:zd:9211/zd:9234) (q:draft)
Mangkang = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:politics/social) (w:British/English/Englishman) (d:the British, the English, and a person of that people; {Mangkang kumpi} is the British government of colonial times) (r:ts:617/zd:25097/ts:4831) (q:draft)
mangkang kumpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:British government/the British/British rule) (d:<Mangkang>, British, and <kumpi>, king, government: the British government, above all the colonial government that ruled Burma and the Chin Hills; used as subject with <in>) (r:ts:617/zd:18086) (q:draft)
Mangkangte = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:politics/social) (w:the British/the English) (d:the British, <Mangkang> with the plural <te>, spoken of above all as the former colonial rulers of Burma and India) (b:Mangkang) (r:zd:24310/zd:22329) (q:draft)
mangkong = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:office/court) (d:second part of the pair {zumkong mangkong}, also written {zum kong mangkong}: the doors of the offices and of the officials, that is government offices and law courts, the authorities) (r:zd:16442/zd:24060/ts:6443) (q:draft)
mangla = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media) (w:English song/western song) (d:a song in English, as against <Zola>, a Zomi song, and <Kawlla>, a Burmese song; {Mang} is short for <Mangkang>, English, with <la>, song) (r:zd:25170) (q:draft)
Manglai = (i:1) (t:name) (f:education) (w:English) (d:the English language as it is written and read; {Manglai in} is in English) (r:zd:9245/zd:16678/zd:23207) (q:draft)
manglang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (j:manlang) (r:zd:14706/zd:23140) (q:draft)
manglo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:disobey/not heed/not listen) (d:<mang> and <lo> written as one word: not obey, not heed what is said; {thu manglo} is disobedient) (j:mang/lo) (r:zd:19523/zd:19749/zd:24932) (q:draft)
manglo = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not be lost/not vanish) (d:<mang>, be lost or disappear, with <lo>: not be lost, said of a name that is to be kept alive) (j:mang/lo) (r:zd:23651) (q:draft, low confidence)
mangmawh = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:unforgettable/hard to forget) (d:not fading from memory: said of a thing, often from childhood, that stays in the mind) (r:zd:24672/zd:10721) (q:draft, low confidence)
mangmuhna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:Revelation/book of Revelation) (d:written with a capital, {Mangmuhna}, the last book of the New Testament; followed by chapter and verse numbers or by <laibu>, book) (r:ts:3992/zd:24064) (q:draft)
mangngilh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:forget) (d:no longer remember, or fail to keep in mind; {mangngilh kei} is not forget) (a:phawk) (r:1.40.23) (q:draft)
mangngilhloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not forget) (d:<mangngilh> and the negative <loh> written as one word: not forget, used before <ding> and <nading>) (j:mangngilh/loh) (r:zd:14615/zd:20172) (q:draft)
mangnu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:queen/female ruler) (d:apparently a word for lord or ruler with <nu>, which marks a woman: {Dawi mangnu} is the queen of the spirits in a legend; elsewhere a woman's personal name) (r:zd:20513) (q:draft, low confidence)
mangnuamlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:refuse to obey/be unwilling to obey) (d:<mang>, obey, and <nuamlo>, not want, written as one word: not be willing to obey an order) (j:mang/nuamlo) (r:zd:16450/zd:12345) (q:draft)
mangpau = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/social) (w:English/English language) (d:the English language as it is spoken, from {Mang}, the English or British, and <pau>, language; the written language is <Manglai>) (r:zd:22070/zd:12867/zd:17208) (q:draft)
mangpha = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:goodbye/farewell) (d:the parting greeting; {mangpha khak} is to say goodbye, and {mangpha kikhak} to say goodbye to each other) (q:draft)
mangpha khakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:farewell/leave-taking/last respects) (d:<mangpha>, goodbye, and <khakna>, sending: the bidding of goodbye to someone who leaves, and in death notices the last respects paid to the dead, often with a wreath; the object of <nei>, hold, or with <in> as the purpose of a visit) (r:zd:9262/zd:25908) (q:draft)
mangpi = (i:2) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:chief/senior officer/dignitary) (d:in present-day use a person of high rank, of the kind named by the word before it: {galkap mangpi} is an army general, {thukhen mangpi} a judge, {zin mangpi} the guest of honour) (r:zd:11447/zd:9125/zd:24068) (q:draft)
mangsia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/health) (w:nightmare/bad dream) (d:a bad or frightening dream, <mang>, dream, with <sia>, bad; the opposite of {manghoih}, a good dream) (r:zd:25914/zd:22305) (q:draft)
mangta = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:away/completely/for good) (d:<mang>, here in its sense of lost, gone, with <ta>, here already, written as one word after a verb: the action has gone through so that the thing is gone or lost for good) (j:mang/ta) (r:zd:17990/zd:22849/zd:25650) (q:draft)
