Maryland = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel) (w:Maryland) (d:state in the east of the United States, where a Zomi community lives) (r:zd:24287/zd:15833) (q:draft)
masa = (i:3) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:first/before others/foremost) (d:placed after a verb or adjective: do or be so before anything or anyone else, as {khangto masa pen}, the first to develop; after <thupi> or <kisam> it marks what matters most) (r:ts:3164/zd:20979/ts:10085) (q:draft)
masa phot = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:first of all/first/before anything else) (d:<masa>, first, and <phot>, for the time being: placed after a verb, to do that before anything else, often before the ending <ni>, let us, or <in>, do) (r:zd:11395/zd:21219/zd:10746) (q:draft)
masading = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:will first/first of all) (d:<masa>, first, with the future <ding>, written as one word and placed after a verb: will do first, is to be done before anything else) (j:masa/ding) (r:zd:13348/zd:15303) (q:draft)
masak = (i:3) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:put first/give priority) (d:used as a verb of its own, with a person marker as in {i masak}: put a person or a thing first, before the rest; the opposite is <nunun>, put last) (r:zd:25467/zd:23453) (q:draft)
masakding = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:first) (d:<masak>, first, with <ding>, the marker of what is to be done, written as one word after a verb: to do that first, should be done first) (j:masak/ding) (r:zd:21495/zd:15433/zd:19307) (q:draft)
masaknapen = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time/everyday) (w:the very first time/first time) (d:<masakna>, the first time, with <pen>: the very first time that something was done; {a kisak masaknapen} is the first time it was sung) (j:masakna/pen) (r:zd:9220/zd:9253) (q:draft)
masalo = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:not necessarily/not primarily/not really) (d:<masa>, first, and <lo>, not, written as one word and placed after a verb or describing word: not in the first place, not necessarily so) (j:masa/lo) (r:zd:24381/zd:24320) (q:draft, low confidence)
masapenpen = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/time) (w:the very first/first of all) (d:<masa>, first, with the doubled superlative <penpen>, written as one word and placed after a verb: the very first to do it or to be so) (j:masa/penpen) (r:zd:16851/zd:17097) (q:draft)
masaphot = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:first of all/first) (d:<masa>, first, with <phot>, for now, written as one word after a verb: do this first, before anything else) (j:masa/phot) (r:zd:19990/zd:14869) (q:draft)
masasa = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:whoever is first/earliest) (d:<masa>, first, with its last syllable repeated, placed after a verb: each one who does it first, whoever does it before the others) (b:masa) (r:zd:20945/ts:3164/zd:23653) (q:draft)
mask = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:mask/face mask) (d:a covering worn over the mouth and nose against disease, or over the face to hide it; {mask thuah} is wear a mask) (s:maituam/muktuam) (o:English) (r:zd:23812/zd:25119/zd:24049) (q:draft)
Massachusetts = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel) (w:Massachusetts) (d:a state in the northeast of the United States of America, where the city of Boston lies) (r:zd:9253/zd:9221) (q:draft)
Master = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:master's degree/master) (d:the university degree above the first degree; otherwise found in English phrases such as {Master Plan}) (o:English) (r:zd:17812/zd:11452) (q:draft, low confidence)
masuan = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:goal/aim/direction/future) (d:as a noun, what a person or a people is heading for, the aim ahead; {masuan kician} is a clear goal) (r:zd:23343/zd:21037/zd:21003) (q:draft)
masuan = (i:3) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:head for/aim at/pursue) (d:with the goal named before it, set one's course toward that goal, as in {khantohna masuan}, head for progress; not go ahead of another person) (r:zd:21661/zd:23394) (q:draft, low confidence)
mat = (i:2) (t:n) (f:education) (w:mark/score) (d:a mark given in an examination, a loan from Burmese and not the verb catch; {tan sawm on na mat} is the marks with which one passes the tenth standard) (r:zd:24296) (q:draft, low confidence)
mat athuak = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:politics) (w:arrested/detained/captured) (d:<mat>, arrest, and <athuak>, who undergoes: who has been arrested or is held; stands before the noun for the person, or alone as the arrested one) (r:zd:12427/zd:12678) (q:draft)
mataw = (i:1) (t:intj) (f:everyday) (d:exclamation of feeling or emphasis, placed at the end of a sentence, often after <e> or <ei>, or at its beginning: indeed, really, oh) (r:zd:20218/zd:25562) (q:draft, low confidence)
matbeh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:arrest in addition/arrest further) (d:<mat>, arrest, with <beh>, in addition: arrest one more person or more people after earlier arrests; passive {ki matbeh}) (b:mat) (r:zd:16998/zd:22818) (q:draft)
match = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media) (w:match/game) (d:a sports match, mostly of football) (s:kimawlna) (o:English) (r:zd:20145/zd:12829) (q:draft)
matcip = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:hold captive/detain/capture) (d:<mat> and <cip> written as one word: seize and hold fast, keep as a captive) (j:mat/cip) (r:zd:11812/zd:17357) (q:draft)
matding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:to arrest/to catch/to be arrested) (d:<mat>, arrest, and <ding>, will, written as one word: in order to arrest, or that someone is to be arrested; {matding in zong} is search for someone to arrest him) (j:mat/ding) (r:zd:15531/zd:19348) (q:draft)
matdingin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:in order to arrest/to catch) (d:<mat>, arrest, and <dingin>, in order to, written as one word: in order to arrest, said of a person the police are looking for) (j:mat/dingin) (r:zd:20468/zd:12678) (q:draft)
mate = (i:3) (t:part) (f:everyday/social) (w:you know/indeed) (d:colloquial particle at the end of a sentence, often after <ei>, <aw> or <hiven>, that stresses what was said and invites the listeners to agree; not the plural of <ma>) (r:zd:23651/zd:11314/zd:24305) (q:draft, low confidence)
mateh = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:sentence-final expression of colloquial speech that adds force or feeling to a statement, roughly indeed; probably <mah> with <teh>) (r:zd:25624) (q:draft, low confidence)
Mathematics = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:mathematics) (d:the school and university subject mathematics) (o:English) (r:zd:22803/zd:23140) (q:draft)
Maths = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:mathematics/maths) (d:the school subject; also called {ganaan}) (o:English) (r:zd:22803/zd:18244) (q:draft)
matkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:arrest/catch/apprehend) (d:<mat>, seize, with <khiat>, out: catch and take away, arrest; the form of {matkhia} used before words such as <ding> and <pah>, and as a noun in {matkhiat kinei}, an arrest is made) (j:mat/khiat) (r:zd:12496/zd:15385) (q:draft)
matkhiatding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:to arrest/to be arrested) (d:<matkhiat>, arrest, and <ding> written as one word: to arrest, in order to catch, or who is to be arrested) (j:matkhiat/ding) (r:zd:14740/zd:14997) (q:draft)
matkhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:arrest/seizure/capture) (d:<matkhiat>, arrest, with the noun suffix {-na}: the catching of a person or the seizing of goods; {aki matkhiatna mun} is the place where they were caught) (b:matkhiat) (r:zd:15232/zd:21291) (q:draft)
matkhiatsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:seize from/confiscate) (d:<matkhiat> with <sak>, written as one word: take things away from someone by authority; with <ki>, be seized) (j:matkhiat/sak) (r:zd:11310) (q:draft, low confidence)
matkhiattheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:be able to arrest/be able to catch) (d:<mat>, <khiat> and <theih> written as one word, before <nadingin>: so that someone can be caught and taken in) (j:mat/khiat/theih) (r:zd:13131/zd:19365) (q:draft)
matpongten = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:identity card/national registration card/citizenship card) (d:the national registration card of Myanmar, and so the identity or citizenship paper of any country) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:23430/zd:17860) (q:draft)
matpongtin = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:registration card/identity card/registration) (d:the national registration card of Myanmar; also the official registration of a political party) (o:Burmese, hmatpontin) (r:zd:18076/zd:26620/zd:26252) (q:draft)
matsiam = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:work/nature) (w:skilled at catching) (d:<mat> and <siam> written as one word: good at catching animals; {gul matsiam te} are expert snake catchers and {nga matsiam} is a skilled fisherman) (j:mat/siam) (r:zd:18154/zd:20973) (q:draft)
matthuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:be arrested/be caught) (d:<mat>, arrest, with <thuak>, undergo: be arrested, mostly in headlines) (s:kimat) (j:mat/thuak) (r:zd:12394/zd:13205/zd:25016) (q:draft)
Matu = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:social) (w:Matu) (d:a Chin people of the <Matupi> area in the south of Chin State in Myanmar, and their language) (r:zd:11325/zd:26700) (q:draft)
matun = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/social) (w:get ahead/succeed/keep up) (d:reach the front, come out ahead of others or on top of the work; often paired with <gualzo>) (r:zd:23554/zd:21230) (q:draft, low confidence)
Matupi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua/land) (f:travel/politics) (w:Matupi) (d:town in the south of Chin State in Myanmar and the township and district around it) (r:ts:11032/zd:17864) (q:draft)
matut = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:achieve/attain/reach/accomplish) (d:used by itself as a verb, reach an aim or carry a task through to its end, often paired with <gualzawh>, win, and said of <ngimna>, <tupna> and <masuan>, aims and goals) (r:zd:21327/zd:21340/zd:21037) (q:draft)
matutna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/social) (w:success/achievement) (d:success, what one manages to achieve, often paired with <gualzawhna>, victory; the Bible text has {matut zawhna}) (b:matut) (r:zd:21343/zd:25300/zd:24481) (q:draft)
matzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:capture/manage to catch/arrest) (d:<mat>, catch, and <zawh>, be able or succeed, written as one word: succeed in catching or arresting; also win over, as in {lungsim matzawh}, capture the mind) (j:mat/zawh) (r:zd:11934/zd:23207) (q:draft)
mau = (i:4) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:ourselves/our own) (d:after <ei> or <ko>, we, written as a separate word: we ourselves, our own, in the same way as {a mau} for they) (r:zd:22751/zd:22553) (q:draft)
Mauvom = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel) (w:Mauvom) (d:a Zomi village; added in brackets after the name of a person to show the home village) (r:zd:22136) (q:draft, low confidence)
mawh = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:wrongly/amiss) (d:after a verb, shows that the act is done amiss or without good ground: {um mawh} or {up mawh} is suppose or suspect, as <upmawh>, and {sim mawh} is look down on, as <simmawh>; not the verb sin) (r:zd:18134/zd:10725/zd:24231) (q:draft, low confidence)
mawhhi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:be guilty) (d:<mawh> and the sentence-final <hi> written as one word: is guilty, as a court finds; it also occurs as the end of {phamawh hi}, it is necessary) (j:mawh/hi) (r:zd:11555/zd:11850) (q:draft, low confidence)
mawhlo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:politics/religion) (w:not guilty/innocent/without fault) (d:<mawh> and <lo> written as one word: not guilty, without fault) (j:mawh/lo) (r:zd:17398/zd:23513) (q:draft)
mawhlo = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:quite/fairly/rather) (d:placed after a describing word: to no small degree, quite; {minthang mawhlo} is quite famous) (r:ts:10463/zd:11182) (q:draft)
mawhmah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:be guilty indeed/be truly at fault) (d:<mawh>, be guilty, and <mah>, which stresses it, written as one word: is indeed guilty, said in a finding or a verdict) (j:mawh/mah) (r:zd:19548) (q:draft)
mawhnadaan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:punishment/penalty/sentence) (d:the punishment given for an offence, from <mawhna>, wrongdoing, and <daan>, punishment; {mawhnadaan pia} is punish) (s:gawtna) (r:zd:14904/zd:15896) (q:draft)
mawhnadan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/religion) (w:punishment/penalty/sentence) (d:<mawhna>, wrongdoing, with the Burmese loan word for penalty: the punishment given for an offence, such as a fine or prison; {mawhnadan pia} is to punish) (s:gawtna) (r:zd:12708/zd:23670) (q:draft)
mawhneilo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:social/politics) (w:innocent/guiltless/blameless) (d:<mawhnei> and <lo> written as one word: having no guilt, innocent) (j:mawhnei/lo) (r:zd:11639/zd:19025) (q:draft)
mawhpaih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:blame/condemn/find guilty) (d:put the guilt on someone: blame or condemn a person, a plan or a government; of a court, find guilty; from <mawh> and <paih>) (s:mawhsak) (r:zd:11001/zd:10990) (q:draft)
mawhpaihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:condemnation/blame/censure) (d:<mawh> guilt with <paih> throw and the noun suffix {-na}: the laying of blame on someone, a formal condemnation; also used for impeachment) (s:mawhsakna) (r:zd:12279/zd:25687) (q:draft)
mawhpuak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/work) (w:responsibility/duty/burden) (d:what a person has to answer for and carry; {mawhpuak pua} is bear a responsibility, and to say something is the {mawhpuak} of a person is also to hold that person to blame) (s:tavuan) (r:zd:14947/zd:19521) (q:draft)
mawhpuakla = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/social) (w:take responsibility/be in charge) (d:<mawhpuak>, responsibility, with <la>, take, written as one word: take on a duty or the responsibility for something) (b:mawhpuak) (r:zd:11535) (q:draft, low confidence)
mawhpuakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/work) (w:responsibility/duty/obligation) (d:what a person or group is answerable for; {mawhpuakna la} is take responsibility) (s:tavuan) (r:zd:9453/zd:9124/zd:9435) (q:draft)
mawhsutna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:confession of sin/confession) (d:the confessing and clearing of sin, <mawh>; one writer glosses it with English confession, and of priests {mawhsutna neih sak} is have someone make it) (b:mawh) (r:ts:1180/zd:15274) (q:draft, low confidence)
mawhsuutna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:confession/confession of sins) (d:<mawh>, sin, with <suut>, recount, and the noun suffix <na>: telling one's sins, confession) (r:zd:21027/zd:24392) (q:draft)
mawka = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (d:<mawk>, merely, as it happens, with the linking <a> written on to it: after a verb, it is merely so, it just turned out so, and the sentence goes on) (j:mawk/a) (r:zd:22450/zd:9219) (q:draft, low confidence)
mawkbei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:be wasted/go to waste) (d:<mawk>, for nothing, with <bei>, be used up, written as one word: be spent to no purpose, said of time, money or life; {mawkbei sak} is to waste) (j:mawk/bei) (r:zd:19586/zd:22571/zd:14554) (q:draft)
mawkbeisak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:time/work) (w:waste/squander) (d:<mawk>, for nothing, with <beisak>, bring to an end: use up time or money to no purpose) (j:mawk/beisak) (r:zd:12336/zd:21456/zd:25924) (q:draft)
mawkding = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<mawk> and the future marker <ding> written as one word at the end of a question: would, could ever; {bangcih mawkding} is what on earth would one do) (j:mawk/ding) (r:zd:24955/zd:15732) (q:draft)
mawkkoih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:leave alone/let off/overlook/neglect) (d:<mawk>, for nothing, with <koih>, put: leave a person or a matter as it is, without action or punishment; mostly with <lo>, not) (j:mawk/koih) (r:zd:19562/zd:12913/zd:16805) (q:draft)
mawkleh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:if by chance/if ever/supposing) (d:<mawk> and <leh> written as one word, after a verb: if it should happen that, if one just does so) (j:mawk/leh) (r:zd:12945/zd:12708/zd:25924) (q:draft)
mawkmawkbek = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:merely/just/simply) (d:<mawkmawk> and <bek> written as one word: only that and nothing more; mostly with <hilo>, not merely) (j:mawkmawk/bek) (r:zd:15272/zd:12746) (q:draft)
mawkna = (i:3) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:free/free of charge/for nothing) (d:{a mawkna in} with a verb of giving, getting or feeding: without payment, at no cost, not in vain) (r:zd:23212/zd:20572/zd:24130) (q:draft)
mawkngah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:get for nothing/get without effort) (d:<mawk> and <ngah> written as one word: receive something free, without working for it) (j:mawk/ngah) (r:zd:19676/zd:19900) (q:draft)
mawkpiak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:give away/give for nothing/give freely) (d:<mawk>, for nothing, and <piak>, give, written as one word: give without anything in return or without good reason) (j:mawk/piak) (r:zd:19774/zd:24088) (q:draft)
mawksak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:blame/find fault with) (d:put the blame on a person, hold that he is in the wrong; compare <mawhsak>) (r:zd:23043/zd:21803) (q:draft, low confidence)
mawkzat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:waste/squander/use carelessly) (d:<mawk>, carelessly, and <zat>, use, written as one word: use time, money or words without purpose or care) (j:mawk/zat) (r:zd:22474/zd:16379/zd:23156) (q:draft)
mawl = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:play) (d:written apart from the prefix <ki>, as {ki mawl}, it is the verb <kimawl>: play a game or a sport, not the adjective dull) (r:zd:23487/zd:23388/zd:17327) (q:draft)
Mawlaih = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel) (w:Mawlaik) (d:Zolai spelling of Mawlaik, a town on the Chindwin river in Sagaing Region of Myanmar; the articles name it as a place people go to from the Tedim area) (r:zd:13302) (q:draft, low confidence)
Mawlamyine = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel/politics) (w:Mawlamyine/Moulmein) (d:city in the south-east of Myanmar, the capital of Mon State) (r:zd:15188/zd:20155) (q:draft)
mawlmawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:play/be playing) (d:doubled form used after <ki> as {ki mawlmawl}, the same as <kimawl>: play, be busy playing) (r:zd:24682/zd:17661) (q:draft)
mawlna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday/media) (w:play/game/sport) (d:after <ki>, written apart: {ki mawlna} is a spaced spelling of <kimawlna>, play or a game, and has nothing to do with dullness) (r:zd:22282/zd:22260/zd:25200) (q:draft)
mawng = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (f:nature) (w:banyan/banyan tree) (d:the banyan, a large fig tree, often planted in a village; {mawng kung} is a banyan tree) (r:zd:23767/zd:17053) (q:draft)
Mawngken = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel) (w:Mawngken) (d:a Zomi village; written after a personal name to show the home village) (r:zd:23740) (q:draft)
mawngkung = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (f:nature) (w:banyan tree) (d:the banyan, a large fig tree, often standing in the open space of a village; <mawng> with <kung>, tree) (r:zd:15996/zd:15493) (q:draft, low confidence)
Mawsi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (f:religion) (j:Moses) (r:zd:23113) (q:draft)
mawtaw = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:car/motor vehicle/automobile) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:24610/zd:21015/zd:16087) (q:draft)
mawtaw awkcip = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:traffic jam/traffic congestion) (d:<mawtaw>, motor vehicle, and <awkcip>, be caught fast: a traffic jam, or as a statement, the traffic is jammed; common at the end of news headlines) (r:zd:11308/zd:15487/zd:15194) (q:draft)
mawtaw lampi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:motor road/road for vehicles) (d:<mawtaw>, car, and <lampi>, road: a road that cars and trucks can use, as against a footpath or mule track; said of the roads that link the hill towns and villages) (r:zd:12337/zd:20297) (q:draft)
mawtaw tuahsia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/media) (w:car accident/road accident) (d:<mawtaw>, car, and <tuahsia>, meet with misfortune: a car or bus meets with an accident, a road accident; in headlines after the place with <ah>, and {mawtaw tuahsia in} is in or by a road accident) (r:zd:25479/zd:16346) (q:draft)
mawtaw tuahsiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/media) (w:car accident/road accident/traffic accident/crash) (d:<mawtaw>, motor vehicle, and <tuahsiatna>, misfortune: an accident on the road with a car, bus or lorry; {mawtaw tuahsiatna hangin} is because of or in a road accident) (r:zd:14810/zd:20589/zd:17844) (q:draft)
mawtawhawl = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/work) (w:driver/motorist) (d:<mawtaw>, car, with <hawl>, drive: a person who drives a car or other motor vehicle) (r:zd:16143/zd:19902) (q:draft)
mawtawhawlpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/work) (w:driver/motorist) (d:<mawtaw>, car, with <hawlpa>, the man who drives: the driver of a car or bus) (s:mawtawhawl) (j:mawtaw/hawlpa) (r:zd:17200/zd:19925) (q:draft)
mawtawkhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:a car/one car/a vehicle) (d:<mawtaw>, car, and <khat>, one, written as one word: a car, one vehicle; after the kind of vehicle, as {Taxi mawtawkhat}, a taxi) (j:mawtaw/khat) (r:zd:20668/zd:18005) (q:draft)
mawtawneu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:car/small car) (d:<mawtaw>, motor vehicle, with <neu>, small: a car, as against a lorry or bus, <mawtawpi>) (j:mawtaw/neu) (r:zd:13332/zd:12982) (q:draft)
mawtawpei = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:tyre/car wheel) (d:<mawtaw>, car, and <pei>, wheel, written as one word: the wheel or tyre of a motor vehicle) (j:mawtaw/pei) (r:zd:14521/zd:15008/zd:19394) (q:draft)
mawtawpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/work) (w:truck/lorry/heavy vehicle) (d:a large motor vehicle such as a truck or tanker; <mawtaw> with <pi>, big) (b:mawtaw) (r:zd:22858/zd:15410/zd:12837) (q:draft)
mawtawsung = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:travel) (w:in the car/inside the car) (d:<mawtaw>, car, and <sung>, in, written as one word: the inside of a car; {mawtawsung panin} is out of the car) (j:mawtaw/sung) (r:zd:20522/zd:14687/zd:21030) (q:draft)
mawtawte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:cars/vehicles) (d:<mawtaw>, car, with the plural <te>) (b:mawtaw) (r:zd:11409/zd:22686/zd:20781) (q:draft)
mawtawzat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:car in use/vehicle used) (d:<mawtaw> and <zat> written as one word: the car or vehicle that someone uses or drives; {a mawtawzat} is the car he was using) (j:mawtaw/zat) (r:zd:16934/zd:17705/zd:21030) (q:draft)
mawza = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:sock/stocking) (d:a sock, worn on the foot inside the shoe; {mawza kop khat} is a pair of socks) (o:Hindi, moza) (r:zd:21667/zd:24786) (q:draft)
Maxico = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel/politics) (j:Mexico) (r:zd:11548) (q:draft)
Maymyo = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Maymyo/Pyin Oo Lwin) (d:a town near Mandalay in Myanmar, now officially Pyin Oo Lwin, known for its military schools) (r:zd:25097/zd:22802) (q:draft)
Mayor = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:mayor) (d:head of the government of a city or town) (o:English) (r:zd:24453) (q:draft)
mazan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/work) (w:progress/advancement) (d:going forward and getting ahead, named together with victory and success; also used as a verb, {mazan zawk}, get further ahead) (r:zd:18011/zd:22590) (q:draft, low confidence)
mazang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/social) (w:make progress/get ahead/be effective) (d:go forward well in work or in life, be active and get results; often paired with <lawhcing>, succeed) (r:zd:16844/zd:21567/zd:25046) (q:draft, low confidence)
mazanna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/work) (w:progress/success/advancement) (d:going forward and doing well in work or life, often paired with <daupaina> or <lawhcinna>) (r:zd:9435/zd:21228) (q:draft)
