mihing ngeina = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:human nature/the way of man) (d:<mihing>, human being, and <ngeina>, custom: what is natural and usual for people, human nature; {mihing ngeina hi} at the end of a statement says that a thing is only human) (r:zd:16366/zd:25169) (q:draft)
mihinga = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:religion/everyday) (w:as a human/in human form) (d:<mihing> and <a> written as one word: as a human being; {mihinga hong piang} is be born as a human) (j:mihing/a) (r:zd:25475/zd:21780) (q:draft)
mihingkhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:a human being/a person/one person) (d:<mihing> and <khat> written as one word: one human being, a person) (j:mihing/khat) (r:zd:25414/zd:24089) (q:draft)
mihingpen = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/religion) (w:human being/mankind) (d:<mihing>, human being, and the topic marker <pen> written as one word: as for man, as for human beings) (j:mihing/pen) (r:zd:20568/zd:25275) (q:draft)
mihingten = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/religion) (w:humans/human beings/people) (d:<mihingte>, humans, and the marker <in> written as one word, marking human beings as the ones who act) (j:mihingte/in) (r:zd:23975/zd:23792) (q:draft)
mihinna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/religion) (w:human nature/personhood/character) (d:what a person is as a human being, the nature or character of a person) (r:zd:21436) (q:draft, low confidence)
mihoih = (i:3) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:good person/good man) (d:<mi>, person, with <hoih>, good, as a noun in everyday speech: a good, decent person, without the religious weight of righteous; often {mihoih khat}, a good person, and set against <misia>, a bad person) (s:mipha) (a:misia) (r:zd:11872/zd:16433/zd:24253) (q:draft)
mihoihlo = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:bad person/wicked person) (d:<mi> and <hoihlo> written as one word: a person who is not good, the opposite of <mihoih>) (j:mi/hoihlo) (r:zd:21991/zd:15514) (q:draft)
mihon = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:community/congregation/assembly/crowd) (d:<mi>, person, with <hon>, flock or group: a gathered body of people, a community, congregation or crowd) (s:mipi/honpi) (q:draft)
mihuh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:help people/aid others/rescue) (d:<mi>, people, and <huh>, help, written as one word: helping others; before a noun it describes it, as in {mihuh kipawlna}, an aid organisation, and {mihuh te}, the rescuers) (j:mi/huh) (r:zd:13341/zd:14942) (q:draft)
miikmeek = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (j:mikmek) (r:zd:23591) (q:draft)
miim = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food/nature) (j:mim) (r:ts:479/zd:15996) (q:draft)
mikaang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:white person/Westerner/English/British) (d:<mi>, person, with <kaang>, white: a white person, above all the British; {mikaang lai} and {mikaang pau} are the English language, {Mikaang kumpi} the British government) (r:zd:11891/zd:16779/zd:23590) (q:draft)
Mikaangpau = (i:1) (t:name) (f:education) (w:English/English language) (d:the English language, literally the speech of the white people: <mikaang>, white person, with <pau>, language) (r:zd:23590) (q:draft)
mikaangte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:white people/Westerners) (d:plural of <mikaang>: white people, Westerners, above all the British and Americans) (b:mikaang) (r:zd:20956/zd:11891) (q:draft)
mikang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:white person/Westerner/European) (d:<mi>, person, with <kang>, white: a white person, also said of the British who ruled Burma; {mikang pau} is the English language and {mikang gam} the West) (r:zd:25097/zd:17495/zd:16245) (q:draft)
mikang kumpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:British government/British rule/the British crown) (d:<mikang>, white person, and <kumpi>, king or government: the British colonial government that ruled Burma and the Zo hills, in accounts of history; with <te> for its officials and <khutnuai> for being under its rule) (r:ts:301/zd:11244) (q:draft)
mikangpau = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/social) (w:English/English language) (d:the English language, the speech, <pau>, of white people, <mikang>; often written with a capital) (r:zd:26643/zd:16337) (q:draft)
mikangte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:white people/Westerners/Europeans) (d:<mikang>, white person, with the plural <te>: white people, Westerners) (b:mikang) (r:zd:25115/zd:10966/zd:24227) (q:draft)
mikangten = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:social) (w:the white people/the Westerners) (d:<mikangte>, white people, and the subject marker <in> written as one word: the white people, as the ones who act) (b:mikangte) (j:mikangte/in) (r:ts:296/zd:12867) (q:draft)
mikhatbek = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:only one person/one person alone/a single person) (d:<mikhat>, one person, and <bek>, only, written as one word: one person and no more, or one person acting alone) (j:mikhat/bek) (r:zd:15851/zd:22217/zd:19569) (q:draft)
mikhatin = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday/media) (w:someone/a person/one person) (d:<mikhat>, someone, with the subject marker <in>, written as one word: someone as the doer of the action; also by one person, per person) (b:mikhat) (j:mikhat/in) (r:zd:20287/zd:11768) (q:draft)
mikhatpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:one person/one of them) (d:<mikhat>, one person, with the topic marker <pen>, written as one word: one person, as the one spoken about; also each person) (j:mikhat/pen) (r:zd:15641/zd:14564) (q:draft)
mikhatpeuh = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:anyone/someone/any person) (d:<mikhat>, someone, and <peuh>, any, written as one word: anyone at all, any one person) (j:mikhat/peuh) (r:zd:19468/zd:13046) (q:draft)
mikhatzong = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/media) (w:one person also/another person too) (d:<mikhat>, one person, with <zong>, also, written as one word: one person as well, most often {adang mikhatzong}, one other person too) (j:mikhat/zong) (r:zd:17917/zd:15188) (q:draft)
mikhempa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:deceiver/cheat/swindler) (d:<mi>, person, with <khempa>, deceiver, written as one word: a man who deceives people) (s:khempa) (j:mi/khempa) (r:zd:24064/zd:24007) (q:draft)
mikhut = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:other people's hands/the hands of others) (d:<mi>, other people, and <khut>, hand, written as one word: the power or control of others; {mikhut sung} is in the hands of others and {mikhut nuai} under someone else, as an employee) (j:mi/khut) (r:zd:25584/zd:22736) (q:draft)
mikiang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:other people's presence/with others) (d:<mi>, other people, and <kiang>, presence, written as one word, used as {mikiang ah}: at other people's side, with or before others, also at another person's place for work or food) (j:mi/kiang) (r:zd:22983/zd:25923) (q:draft)
mikimin = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:everyone/each person) (d:<mikim> and the marker <in> written as one word: everyone, each person, as the one who acts) (j:mikim/in) (r:zd:20550/zd:24396) (q:draft)
mikmek = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:just/simply/needlessly) (d:placed after a verb: the thing simply happens or is done, mostly something unwelcome or undeserved, as in {thuak mikmek}, just have to suffer it; exact shade not determined) (r:zd:21720/zd:22275) (q:draft, low confidence)
miksi = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (f:nature) (w:ant) (d:an ant; {miksi hon khat} is a swarm of ants) (r:zd:21246/zd:21243) (q:draft)
milak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:public/company/crowd) (d:<mi>, people, with <lak>, midst, written as one word: the company of other people; {milak ah} is in public, among people) (j:mi/lak) (r:zd:17152/zd:21598/zd:22802) (q:draft)
milamdang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:strange person/remarkable person) (d:<mi>, person, and <lamdang>, astonishing, written as one word: a person who is strange or out of the ordinary) (j:mi/lamdang) (r:zd:11945/zd:21003) (q:draft, low confidence)
