milom = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:group of people/body of people) (d:<mi>, person, with <lom>, batch: a number of people taken together, as against one alone) (r:zd:20349/zd:22754) (q:draft, low confidence)
milui = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/religion) (w:old person/old self/old member) (d:<mi>, person, and <lui>, old, written as one word: someone of the old kind, as the old self before faith, or those who have long been in a group or in office, set against <mithak>, the new) (a:mithak) (j:mi/lui) (r:zd:23394/zd:15880/zd:23356) (q:draft)
milungsim = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:people's hearts/a person's mind) (d:<mi>, person, and <lungsim>, heart or mind, written as one word: the mind or heart of people; {milungsim zo} is win people over) (j:mi/lungsim) (r:zd:19654/zd:21309) (q:draft)
