mimawkmawk = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:ordinary person/commoner/nobody in particular) (d:<mi>, person, with <mawkmawk>, ordinary, written as one word: a person of no special rank or standing) (j:mi/mawkmawk) (r:zd:15315/zd:12512) (q:draft)
mimuan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:trusted person/confidant/trusted aide) (d:<mi>, person, with <muan>, trust: a person someone relies on, a trusted helper or adviser of a leader) (r:zd:19934/zd:21657) (q:draft)
min = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:name)
min kitaih = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:name clash case/fraud case) (d:<min>, name, and <kitaih>, collide: a clash of names, said of refugee resettlement files held back because the name or identity of the applicant conflicts with another record, a fraud case; {min kitaih te} are the persons whose files are so held) (r:zd:22608) (q:draft, low confidence)
mina = (i:2) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/religion) (w:in the name of) (d:<min>, name, written together with <a>, a short form of <ah>, in: in the name of, as in {Topa' mina}, in the name of the Lord; not the unit of weight) (r:zd:25668/zd:24338) (q:draft, low confidence)
minam = (i:3) (t:n) (f:social) (w:tribe/people/nation) (d:a people of one descent and language) (r:zai:tribe) (q:draft)
minam hihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:national identity/ethnic identity/nationhood) (d:<minam>, a people, and <hihna>, the fact of being: the fact of being a people or of belonging to one, its identity; a possessive such as <i> or <a> stands before it) (r:zd:25461/zd:21309) (q:draft)
minam it = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:love one's people/be patriotic) (d:<minam>, people or nation, and <it>, love: love one's own people, be devoted to the nation; the object stands before the verb without a marker, and the pair also stands before a noun, as in {minam it zia}, the way of loving one's people) (r:zd:24699/zd:21090/zd:25461) (q:draft)
minam itna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:love of one's people/patriotism/national feeling) (d:<minam>, a people or nation, and <itna>, love: love of one's own people, the feeling that moves a person to work for the nation) (r:zd:24033/zd:12306) (q:draft)
minam khangto = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:developed nation/advanced people) (d:<minam>, a people, and <khangto>, grow: a people that has advanced in learning and prosperity, a developed nation, said beside {gam khangto}, a developed country; the same two words also form a clause, a people advances) (r:zd:22713/zd:24028/ts:4564) (q:draft)
minam kician = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:established nation/recognised people/people in its own right) (d:<minam>, a people or nation, and <kician>, firm, well-founded: a people that stands as a full nation in its own right, with its own name, language and recognition; often with <khat> after it and a people's name before it, {Zomi minam kician khat}) (r:zd:21815/zd:23762) (q:draft)
minam party = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:ethnic party/ethnic political party) (d:<minam>, a people or ethnic group, and <party>, political party: a political party that stands for one ethnic group, as against a party of the whole country; a term of the politics of Myanmar) (r:zd:22989/zd:23011/zd:22365) (q:draft)
minam puan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/social) (w:national dress/traditional cloth/ethnic costume) (d:<minam>, people or nation, and <puan>, cloth: the woven cloth or dress that marks a people, worn at festivals; {Zo minam puan} is the Zo national dress, set against {fashion puan}) (r:zd:22303/zd:11076) (q:draft)
minamdang = (i:3) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:other ethnic group/another people/other nationality) (d:a people or ethnic group other than one’s own, also one living in the same country, as the non-Zomi peoples of Myanmar; not only a foreigner from abroad) (r:zd:12336/zd:14992/zd:9425) (q:draft)
minamke = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:sub-tribe/ethnic subgroup/branch of a people) (d:one of the branches into which a people, <minam>, divides; paired with {pauke}, a branch of a language) (b:minam) (r:zd:16342/zd:24009) (q:draft, low confidence)
minamkee = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:sub-tribe/ethnic subgroup/branch of a people) (d:<minam> people with {kee}, branch: one of the smaller groups into which a people is divided, each often with its own speech) (r:zd:22802/zd:16509) (q:draft, low confidence)
minamkhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:one people/a nation/a people) (d:<minam>, people, and <khat>, one, written as one word: a people or nation, one people) (j:minam/khat) (r:zd:25866) (q:draft)
