na = (i:3) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:already/beforehand) (d:placed before a verb whose subject is not you, it shows that the action took place earlier or away from the speaker, as in {na om hi}, was there; often left untranslated, while the pronoun {na} means you or your) (r:ts:3271/ts:301/ts:3508) (q:draft, low confidence)
