nileh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:time) (w:day and) (d:<ni>, day, and <leh>, and, written as one word; other uses in the articles, such as {ki nileh}, are not clear) (j:ni/leh) (r:zd:21547/zd:17521) (q:draft, low confidence)
nilohte = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<niloh>, continually, with the plural <te>, after a verb: those who keep on doing it, the ones who are always doing so) (j:niloh/te) (r:zd:21279) (q:draft, low confidence)
nima = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:before the day) (d:<ni>, day, and <ma>, before, written as one word after a date or an event and often followed by <in>: before that day; {Sihvui nima nitak} is the evening before the day of the funeral) (j:ni/ma) (r:zd:10745/zd:13069) (q:draft, low confidence)
nimit = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:date) (d:the day, month and year of an event or of a letter; written as a label before the date in notices and announcements) (r:zd:23246/zd:25311) (q:draft)
nin = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/home) (w:dirty/unclean) (d:dirty, not clean; the opposite of <siang>, clean) (s:nit/kihhuai) (a:siang/siangtho) (r:41.7.2) (q:draft)
nin = (i:3) (t:n) (f:home/everyday) (w:rubbish/garbage/waste/litter) (d:things thrown away, household waste, rather than dirt on a surface; brought out by <paih>, throw away, and by {nindum}, a rubbish bin) (r:zd:16862/zd:20131/zd:22444) (q:draft)
ninbung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:rubbish bin/trash can/dustbin) (d:a container into which rubbish is thrown) (r:zd:12373/zd:23727/zd:21239) (q:draft)
ning ei = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<ning>, the ending of the first person singular for what the speaker will do, and the sentence-final <ei>, which here is not the pronoun we: closes a sentence in which the speaker announces or affirms warmly what he will do or feels, I will indeed, let me; often after <mah>) (r:zd:10725/zd:21305) (q:draft, low confidence)
ning maw = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:shall I/let me) (d:<ning>, I will, and <maw>, the question word: closes a sentence in which the speaker says what he means to do and asks the hearer to agree, shall I, let me, all right; stands after the verb) (r:zd:23957/zd:17663/zd:20280) (q:draft, low confidence)
