ningin = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<ning>, I will, with the linking <in>, written as one word: I will do this, and then; joins a first-person statement of intent to the next clause) (j:ning/in) (r:zd:20513/zd:23037) (q:draft)
ningniang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/body) (w:limply/droopingly/listlessly) (d:placed after a verb, describes something that droops, hangs or lies limp, or is done without spirit; {vul ningniang} is to be downcast and worn out) (r:zd:20646/zd:22683) (q:draft, low confidence)
