nuamlai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:still want to) (d:<nuam> and <lai> written as one word, placed after a verb: still want to do it) (j:nuam/lai) (r:zd:17804/zd:24955) (q:draft)
nuamlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not want/be unwilling) (d:<nuam> and <lo> written as one word: after a verb, not want to do it; after <lung>, heart, not happy, as in {a lung nuamlo}, he is unhappy) (j:nuam/lo) (r:zd:19662/zd:22586/zd:12928) (q:draft)
nuamlote = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:those who do not want to/the unwilling) (d:<nuam> and <lote> written as one word, after a verb: those who do not want to do it) (j:nuam/lote) (r:zd:11571/zd:25206/zd:16424) (q:draft)
nuamlua = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:want very much/be eager/long to) (d:placed after a verb, <nuam.1> want with <lua>, too much: want very much to do what the verb says, as in {sem nuamlua}, be eager to work; not the being happy of the other sense) (b:nuam) (r:ts:3125/zd:22827/zd:23773) (q:draft)
nuammahmah = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:very pleasant/want very much) (d:<nuam> and <mahmah>, very, written as one word: very pleasant or comfortable, and after a verb want very much to do it) (j:nuam/mahmah) (r:zd:19166/zd:23745) (q:draft)
nuampah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:want at once/be glad at once) (d:<nuam> and <pah> written as one word: after a verb, want to do it right away; of a state, become pleasant or happy at once) (j:nuam/pah) (r:zd:12504/zd:21115) (q:draft, low confidence)
nuampeuh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:whoever wants to/anyone wishing to) (d:<nuam>, want, and <peuh>, any, written as one word after a verb: anyone at all who wants to do it) (j:nuam/peuh) (r:zd:25212/zd:14826) (q:draft)
