pawlin = (i:4) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:group/side/forces) (d:<pawl>, group, with the subject marker <in>, after the name of an army, an armed group or <ko>, we: that group as the doer of the act, as {SAC pawlin}, the SAC side) (r:ts:4734/ts:8784/ts:6741) (q:draft)
pawlkhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:a group/some) (d:<pawl>, group, with <khat>, one: one group; after a noun it means some of them) (s:honkhat)
pawlkhat leuleu = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:some others/others again/others in turn) (d:<pawlkhat>, some, and <leuleu>, again, in turn: opens a sentence that sets a second group against one just mentioned, others for their part; followed by <in> as subject, or after a noun, {khua pawlkhat leuleu}, some other villages) (r:ts:479/zd:17685) (q:draft)
