phadeuh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:mostly/for the most part/usually) (d:placed after a verb or describing word: for the most part, more often than not, to a rather great degree; {a phadeuh in} at the head of a sentence is mostly, above all) (r:zd:20787/zd:16695/zd:21340) (q:draft)
phadiakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (d:<phadiak>, especially, with the noun suffix {-na}, written as one word after a verb or describing word: the place or thing where this is most so, as in {atam phadiakna}, where there are the most) (j:phadiak/na) (r:zd:12634/zd:13350/zd:17355) (q:draft)
phadiakte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:those who especially/the most) (d:<phadiak>, especially, with the plural <te>, after a verb or describing word: those who are so most of all; {a ki-it phadiakte} is those who love one another most) (b:phadiak) (j:phadiak/te) (r:zd:20769/zd:11594) (q:draft)
phading = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:amount to/reach/number) (d:<pha>, reach a number or an amount, and <ding> written as one word: will come to, is thought to come to; used when a number is estimated, as {mi 3 bang phading}, about three people) (j:pha/ding) (r:zd:16442/zd:20582/zd:12519) (q:draft)
phahi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:amount to/come to/reach) (d:<pha>, reach a number or amount, with the sentence-final <hi> written as one word: after a count or measure, it comes to that many) (j:pha/hi) (r:zd:19164/zd:17790) (q:draft)
Phaileeng = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:social/travel) (w:Phaileng) (d:a Zomi village; its people and their speech are called by its name, {Phaileeng mi} and {Phaileeng pau}) (r:zd:21182/ts:261) (q:draft)
phaitam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:yard/back yard/courtyard) (d:the open ground belonging to a house; dictionaries give courtyard and back yard, and {phaitam lam} is the yard side of the house) (r:zd:14804/zd:24240) (q:draft, low confidence)
Phaiza = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:social) (w:Phaiza) (d:a Zomi village, {Phaiza khua}, also given after a personal name to show where the person is from) (r:zd:24806) (q:draft)
phaka = (i:1) (t:v) (f:time) (w:on reaching/at the age of) (d:<phak>, reach, with the ending {-a}, written as one word: on reaching a number of years; {kum 9 a phaka} is when he was nine years old) (j:phak/a) (r:zd:24320/zd:9214) (q:draft)
phakhinding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:will have reached/probably amount to) (d:<phakhin>, have reached a number, and <ding>, will, written as one word: the number is thought to have reached so many already; mostly after a number with <bang>, about) (j:phakhin/ding) (r:zd:12553/zd:14859) (q:draft)
phakhinta = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:have reached/have already reached) (d:<phakhin>, have already reached, with <ta>, written as one word after a number: an age or a count has now reached that number) (j:phakhin/ta) (r:zd:17049/zd:12618/zd:14770) (q:draft)
phakin = (i:2) (t:v) (f:time) (w:reach/attain) (d:<phak>, reach an age, with the linking ending <in>: on reaching, after <kum> and a number, as in {kum 43 a phakin}, at the age of 43; not the word for leprosy) (r:zd:9222/zd:23138/zd:11279) (q:draft)
phakloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not reach/be beyond) (d:<phak>, reach, and the negative <loh>, written as one word: not reaching, out of reach; {theih phakloh} is beyond what one can know) (j:phak/loh) (r:zd:22713/zd:24963) (q:draft, low confidence)
phakma = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:before reaching) (d:<phak>, reach, and <ma>, before, written as one word and followed by <in>: before reaching an age or a place; {kum 40 a phakma in} is before he reached the age of 40) (j:phak/ma) (r:zd:20736/zd:22159) (q:draft)
Phalaam = (i:1) (t:name) (f:travel/politics) (j:Falam) (r:zd:20176/zd:19166) (q:draft)
phalai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:still number/amount to) (d:<pha>, here reach a number, and <lai>, still, written as one word after a count: still amount to, number as many as) (j:pha/lai) (r:zd:20401/zd:14740) (q:draft, low confidence)
phalbi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time/nature) (w:winter/cold season) (d:the cold season of the year, winter, set against <khuakhal>, summer; {phalbi lai} is in winter) (s:phabi/phaibi) (a:khuakhal/khualkhal) (r:22.2.11) (q:draft)
phallo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:not allow/forbid/refuse permission) (d:<phal>, permit, and <lo>, not, written as one word: not allow; {ki phallo} is it is not allowed) (s:khaam) (j:phal/lo) (r:zd:12487/zd:19455/zd:14767) (q:draft)
phalloh = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:social/politics) (w:not permitted/unauthorised/forbidden) (d:<phal> and <loh> written as one word: not permitting, without the permission of; {kumpi phalloh} is not permitted by the government, illegal) (j:phal/loh) (r:zd:20930/zd:23784/zd:19427) (q:draft)
phalna kician = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/work) (w:valid permit/legal documents/proper authorisation) (d:<phalna>, permission, and <kician>, firm or sound: an official permit that is valid, above all the papers that allow a foreigner to stay or work in a country; {phalna kician neilo} is without valid documents, undocumented) (r:zd:13255/zd:20912/zd:24297) (q:draft)
phalna omlo = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:politics/work) (w:without permission/without a licence/illegally) (d:<phalna>, permission, and <omlo>, there not being: followed by <in>, without permission or licence, said of what is done unlawfully; the one whose permission is lacking stands before it in the possessive, {kumpi' phalna omlo in}) (r:zd:20909/zd:18952) (q:draft)
phalna omlopi = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:politics/social) (w:without permission/without a permit/illegally) (d:<phalna>, permission, with <omlopi>, there being none: without permission or a licence, followed by <in> and a verb for what is done unlawfully) (r:zd:11649/zd:11594) (q:draft)
phalnawnlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:no longer allow/no longer permit) (d:<phal>, allow, and <nawnlo>, no longer, written as one word; with <ki> before it, be no longer allowed) (j:phal/nawnlo) (r:zd:11833/zd:11854) (q:draft)
phalo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not reach/not amount to) (d:<pha>, here reach or amount to, and <lo>, not, written as one word: not reaching a number or level, not much, not quite) (j:pha/lo) (r:zd:22278/zd:17634) (q:draft, low confidence)
phaltakin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:social/religion) (w:generously/willingly/freely) (d:<phal>, willing, with <takin>, written as one word: giving or allowing gladly, without holding back) (j:phal/takin) (r:zd:17685/zd:22938) (q:draft)
Phaltang = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel) (w:Phaltang) (d:a village near the border of India and Myanmar; {Phaltang khuathak} is New Phaltang, also called Bulphek) (r:zd:20315) (q:draft, low confidence)
phalvetlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:not allow at all/forbid/refuse to let) (d:<phal>, allow, and <vetlo>, not at all, written as one word: not allow in any way) (j:phal/vetlo) (r:zd:13151/zd:12676) (q:draft)
pham = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/family) (w:pass away/die) (d:die, a gentle and poetic word used with respect of people; {pham sate} are those who have passed away) (s:si) (r:zd:24086/zd:9421/zd:15809) (q:draft)
phamahmah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:very much/greatly/indeed) (d:<pha> and <mahmah> written as one word and placed after a verb or describing word: very much, to a great degree; the first part strengthens the second and does not mean good) (j:pha/mahmah) (r:zd:25866/zd:15274/zd:12688) (q:draft)
phamawhlo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:all right/not a problem/not matter) (d:<phamawh> and <lo> written as one word: it does not matter, there is no harm in it) (j:phamawh/lo) (r:zd:11487/zd:17841) (q:draft)
phamawhta = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have to/must) (d:<phamawh>, necessary, and <ta>, the marker of a change, written as one word: after a verb with <loh>, not doing it was no longer possible, had to) (j:phamawh/ta) (r:zd:12998/zd:15280) (q:draft)
phamawk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:amount to/reach/number) (d:<pha>, here reach, with <mawk>, written as one word after a number or a measure: come to that much, be as many or as high as that) (j:pha/mawk) (r:zd:12567/zd:12854) (q:draft)
phamna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/family) (w:death/passing) (d:<pham>, pass away, with the noun suffix <na>: death, a gentle and poetic word) (s:sihna) (b:pham) (r:zd:25277/ts:301) (q:draft)
phamsa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:the deceased/the departed/the dead) (d:poetic and respectful word for those who have died; {phamsa te phawkna} is a remembrance of the departed) (s:misi) (r:zd:12024/zd:23388) (q:draft)
phan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:home/work) (w:weave/plait/knit) (d:make a thing by interlacing strips or threads by hand, such as a basket, a mat or knitted clothing) (r:ts:3375) (q:draft, low confidence)
phangphang = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:one after another/in a rush) (d:after a verb, of many people or things doing the same thing suddenly and in quick succession, as leaving, arriving or going astray; it carries no blame of rashness) (r:zd:15941/zd:21908/zd:25181) (q:draft, low confidence)
phapan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:time/everyday) (w:have just reached/be only just) (d:<pha>, here reach an amount, with <pan>, here only just, written as one word: have only now reached an age or a length of time, as in {kum 15 bek phapan}, only just 15 years old) (j:pha/pan) (r:zd:16713/zd:12087/zd:11484) (q:draft)
phapha = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:social/media) (w:earnestly/sincerely/kindly) (d:after a verb of inviting, informing or thanking in a notice or letter, as {kong zawn phapha uh hi}, we earnestly invite you, and {kizasak phapha}, it is hereby made known: a polite strengthening of the request, not care in doing something) (r:zd:22539/zd:22590/zd:21510) (q:draft)
Pharaoh = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (f:religion) (w:Pharaoh) (d:title of the king of ancient Egypt, in its English spelling; the Bible text writes <Faro>) (s:Faro) (o:English) (r:zd:16897/zd:22275) (q:draft)
Pharisee = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:religion) (w:Pharisee) (d:member of the Pharisees, a Jewish religious party strict in keeping the law, in the English spelling; the Bible text writes <Farisai>) (s:Farisai) (o:English) (r:zd:17883/zd:11256) (q:draft)
Pharoah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (f:religion) (j:Faro) (r:zd:21137) (q:draft)
phasak = (i:3) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:amount to/total/make up) (d:after a number or quantity, bring the count to that number, or reckon it at that number, <pha>, reach, with the causative <sak>; {nam 8 bang phasak} is make eight kinds in all) (r:zd:11769/zd:16302/ts:3375) (q:draft)
phasan = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:greatly/considerably) (d:placed after a verb: to a marked degree) (r:zd:25176/zd:9220) (q:draft, low confidence)
phat = (i:3) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:carefully/thoroughly/well) (d:after a verb of thinking or examining, such as <ngaihsut>, <kikup>, <kisit> and <et>: do it with care, go over it well; not {phat}, praise, and often followed by <huai> or <ding>) (r:zd:25136/zd:21049) (q:draft)
phata = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:reach/amount to/number) (d:<pha>, here reach or amount to, and <ta>, now, written as one word after a number: has now reached that number, amount or age) (j:pha/ta) (r:zd:21690/zd:11619/zd:19080) (q:draft)
phatak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:well/properly/thoroughly) (d:<pha>, good, with <tak>, written as one word: well, properly, with care; mostly as the second half of a pair, {hoihtak phatak in}, well and properly) (j:pha/tak) (r:zd:19371/zd:22334/zd:11670) (q:draft)
phatdiak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:especially/particularly/most of all) (d:form of <phadiak> used before a noun or before words such as <uh> and <ding>: {atam phatdiak hun} is the time when there are most) (b:phadiak) (r:zd:15822/zd:11253/zd:20877) (q:draft)
phatota = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:have reached/have risen to) (d:<phato>, reach up to, with <ta>, now: a growing number has now reached this figure, common in headlines that count the dead) (j:phato/ta) (r:zd:12194/zd:14858/zd:20023) (q:draft)
phatphat = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:carefully/closely/thoroughly) (d:placed after a verb such as <et>, <sim> or <ngaih>: doing it with care and attention, as in {et phatphat}, look closely; not the doubled <phat>, praise) (r:zd:10672/zd:13302/zd:20176) (q:draft)
phatsakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:self-praise/pride/conceit) (d:found after <ki> as {ki phatsakna}, the same as <kiphatsakna> written in two words: a high opinion of oneself, pride) (b:phatsak) (r:zd:19124) (q:draft)
phattuam nading = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:social) (w:for the benefit of/for the good of/benefit) (d:<phattuam>, benefit, and <nading.2>, for: placed after the one who gains, for the benefit or good of that person or group; {mipi phattuam nading} is the public good, and with <in> after it the phrase gives a purpose) (r:zd:21876/zd:21224) (q:draft)
phatuam = (i:2) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:be saved/be spared/be eased) (d:said of a cost or a burden, as <sumbei>, expense, <hunbei>, time spent, <sing>, firewood, or a fire: become less, be saved or eased, where sense 1 is said of the thing that does good) (r:zd:21259/zd:11658) (q:draft, low confidence)
phatuamding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:will save/will benefit/will help) (d:<phatuam>, be of use, and <ding>, will, written as one word: will be of benefit; of cost or time, will be saved or reduced) (j:phatuam/ding) (r:zd:11308/zd:15067/zd:20104) (q:draft)
phatuamna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:benefit/advantage/profit/use) (d:<phatuam>, be of use, with the noun ending <na>: the good or gain that comes from something; {aituam phatuamna} is personal gain) (s:hamphatna) (b:phatuam) (r:zd:23332/zd:16588) (q:draft)
phawk = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:remember) (d:keep or bring back in mind, the opposite of <mangngilh>, forget) (s:phawkkik/phawkkha) (a:mangngilh)
phawkciat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:each remember/all keep in mind) (d:<phawk> and <ciat> written as one word: remember, every one of us or of you, as in a request for prayer) (j:phawk/ciat) (r:zd:15565/zd:14967) (q:draft)
phawkciatni = (i:1) (t:v) (f:religion/social) (w:let us each remember) (d:<phawk>, remember, and <ciatni>, let us each, written as one word; {thungetna ah phawkciatni} is let us each remember them in prayer) (j:phawk/ciatni) (r:zd:11259/zd:12290) (q:draft)
phawkden = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:always remember/keep in mind) (d:<phawk>, remember, and <den>, always, written as one word: never forget, keep in mind at all times) (j:phawk/den) (r:zd:10687/zd:23602) (q:draft)
phawkding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:to remember/to bear in mind/to note) (d:<phawk> and <ding> written as one word: to be remembered, something one should keep in mind; {phawkding thu} is a point to note) (j:phawk/ding) (r:zd:17355/zd:22019/zd:19092) (q:draft)
phawkhuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:worth remembering/notable/to be kept in mind) (d:<phawk>, remember, with <huai>, worthy of: that ought to be remembered or noticed; at the end of a sentence, it should be remembered that) (j:phawk/huai) (r:zd:23394/zd:24375/zd:22754) (q:draft)
phawkkhalo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not notice/be unaware) (d:<phawkkha> and <lo> written as one word: not notice, not realise that something is happening) (j:phawkkha/lo) (r:zd:12304/zd:11780/zd:19871) (q:draft)
phawkkik = (i:2) (t:v) (f:health/body) (w:regain consciousness/come to/come round) (d:after <khua>, or alone of someone who had fainted: become conscious again, where the other sense is recalling a thing to mind) (r:zd:14824/zd:12304/zd:17547) (q:draft)
phawklo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:not notice/be unaware) (d:<phawk> and <lo> written as one word: not notice, not be aware of; {khua phawklo} is to be unconscious) (j:phawk/lo) (r:zd:12290/zd:16302) (q:draft)
phawkloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not remember/be unaware/not notice) (d:<phawk> and <loh> written as one word: not remember, not be aware of; {i phawkloh kal in} is while we are not aware, without our noticing) (j:phawk/loh) (r:zd:12784/zd:20568/zd:24370) (q:draft)
phawknawnlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/everyday) (w:lose consciousness/be unconscious) (d:<phawk> and <nawnlo> written as one word; with <khua>, {khua phawknawnlo}, no longer aware of anything, unconscious) (j:phawk/nawnlo) (r:zd:12733/zd:14635/zd:12304) (q:draft)
phawkni = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:let us remember/let us keep in mind) (d:<phawk>, remember, and the ending <ni>, here let us, written as one word; {thungetna ah phawkni} is let us remember it in prayer) (j:phawk/ni) (r:zd:19080/zd:11827) (q:draft)
phawkpan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:only then notice/realize only then) (d:<phawk>, be aware, with <pan>, begin: notice or realize something only at that moment, not before) (j:phawk/pan) (r:zd:12669/zd:18128) (q:draft)
phawkthak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be reminded/remember afresh) (d:<phawk>, remember or be aware, and <thak>, new, written as one word: call to mind again, be reminded; with <huai>, worth being reminded of) (j:phawk/thak) (r:zd:14709/zd:12596) (q:draft)
phawng = (i:2) (t:v) (f:social) (w:stir/move/prompt/awaken) (d:with <lungsim> or <ngaihsutna>, mostly after <hong>: stir the heart or the thoughts, of words, a question or a memory that will not leave someone at rest) (r:zd:16315/zd:25265/zd:15767) (q:draft)
phazo = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:enough/sufficient) (d:said of what is sufficient; {phazo hi} means that is enough, often said to stop someone)
pheek = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:mat) (d:mat for lying on, in {lupna pheek}, sleeping mat) (q:draft)
phei = (i:3) (t:adv) (f:everyday/travel) (w:across/over) (d:placed after a verb of going, coming or giving, as in {pai phei}, {hawh phei} and {pia phei}: the action goes across to a person or place on the same level, not up or down; not the noun {phei}, thigh) (r:zd:16243/zd:22040/zd:9228) (q:draft)
pheiphei = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:on and on/one after another/continually) (d:placed after a verb: the action goes on and on or passes from one to the next, as in {en pheiphei}, keep looking on, and {ci pheiphei}, keep on saying) (r:zd:21218/zd:19826) (q:draft, low confidence)
phek = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (j:pheek) (r:zd:15286) (q:draft, low confidence)
phek = (i:2) (t:v) (f:body/home) (w:plait/braid) (d:weave strands together, as hair into plaits; the word also counts the plaits, as {phek thum}, three plaits) (r:ts:3375) (q:draft, low confidence)
phekap = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:card playing/gambling at cards) (d:playing cards, especially for money; named with drink and drugs as a harmful habit) (r:zd:15329) (q:draft, low confidence)
phelhhuan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:fight a fire/work to put out) (d:<phelh>, put out a fire, with a second part that is not explained: work at putting out a fire, said in the articles of firefighters and others who do so in numbers; {phelhhuan ngeingai} is fight the fire hard) (b:phelh) (r:zd:13092/zd:12736) (q:draft, low confidence, the part huan is not explained)
phelhkik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:put out again/extinguish) (d:<phelh>, put out a fire, and <kik>, back or again, written as one word: bring a fire that has broken out back under control; mostly passive, {ki phelhkik}) (j:phelh/kik) (r:zd:12750/zd:15669) (q:draft)
phelhsiang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:extinguish completely/put out) (d:<phelh>, put out a fire, with <siang>, clean: put a fire out completely) (b:phelh) (r:zd:17289/zd:16239/zd:15686) (q:draft)
phelhsiangthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:be able to put out/manage to extinguish) (d:<phelhsiang> and <thei> written as one word: be able to put a fire out completely) (j:phelhsiang/thei) (r:zd:14865/zd:14575) (q:draft)
phelhsiangzo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:put out completely/manage to extinguish) (d:<phelh>, put out a fire, <siang>, clean, and <zo>, be able, written as one word: succeed in putting a fire out completely; {ki phelhsiangzo} is the fire was fully put out) (j:phelh/siang/zo) (r:zd:17729/zd:17917/zd:20335) (q:draft)
phelhsiangzopan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:finally put out/manage to extinguish) (d:<phelhsiang> and <zopan> written as one word: only then manage to put a fire out completely) (j:phelhsiang/zopan) (r:zd:14545/zd:21164) (q:draft)
phenghawlgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:drive recklessly/drive wildly) (d:<pheng>, rashly, and <hawlgawp>, drive wildly, written as one word: drive a vehicle fast and without any care) (j:pheng/hawlgawp) (r:zd:15953/zd:15201) (q:draft)
pheta = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:time) (w:as soon as/the moment) (d:<phet> with the linking <a> written as one word, placed after a verb: as soon as, the moment that) (j:phet/a) (r:zd:23989) (q:draft, low confidence)
phi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/work) (w:sit/take/answer) (d:take an interview or a test and answer its questions; {interview phi} is to go through an interview) (r:zd:21664/zd:22074) (q:draft, low confidence)
phial = (i:4) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:almost/nearly/practically) (d:after a word of totality or frequency such as <khempeuh>, <gambup> or <nisim>, shows that the statement holds for nearly the whole: {mi khempeuh phial}, almost everyone, <nisim phial>, almost every day) (r:zd:20919/zd:17162/ts:6697) (q:draft)
phialbang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:about/as many as/nearly) (d:<phial> and <bang> written as one word after a number: about that many, as many as) (j:phial/bang) (r:zd:20850/zd:20369/zd:13188) (q:draft)
phialding = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:would even/might almost) (d:<phial> and <ding> written as one word after a verb, mostly followed by <in>: it would even go as far as that, said of what is feared, thought or supposed) (j:phial/ding) (r:zd:12105/zd:25188) (q:draft, low confidence)
phialkapgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/politics) (w:shoot at random/fire wildly at) (d:<phial> and <kapgawp>, shoot severely, written as one word: open fire on people without choosing a target; the sense of <phial> here is taken from the sentences) (j:phial/kapgawp) (r:zd:12803/zd:17461) (q:draft)
phialleh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:even if/as if) (d:<phial> and <leh>, if, written as one word after a verb: even if it should be so; before <kilawm> it means it almost seems that, it is as though) (j:phial/leh) (r:zd:21796/zd:12693) (q:draft)
phialmah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:practically/almost/even) (d:<phial> and <mah> written as one word: stresses that something is as good as so, practically, all but; with <leh> <zong>, even if) (j:phial/mah) (r:zd:9231/zd:21458) (q:draft, low confidence)
phialmawk = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:practically/almost/one might even say) (d:<phial> and <mawk> written as one word after a verb or describing word: stresses that the statement goes that far, it is practically so) (j:phial/mawk) (r:zd:17208/zd:11130) (q:draft, low confidence)
phialphial = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:almost/nearly/just about) (d:placed after a describing word: so close to it that one could almost say so; {kikim phialphial} is just about equal) (s:dektak) (r:zd:25165/zd:14804) (q:draft, low confidence)
phialta = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:almost/nearly/even if) (d:<phial> and <ta> written as one word, placed after a verb: almost or nearly so, and before <zongin> even if it really were so) (j:phial/ta) (r:zd:22272/zd:23653) (q:draft)
phialzong = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:even if/even though) (d:<phial> and <zong> written as one word, placed after the verb and often followed by <in>: even if it should be so) (j:phial/zong) (r:zd:14709/zd:24641/zd:25790) (q:draft)
phialzongin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:even if/even though) (d:<phial> and <zongin> written as one word after a verb: even if that is so) (j:phial/zongin) (r:zd:20725/zd:20162) (q:draft)
phiat = (i:4) (t:v) (f:body/home) (w:wash/wipe clean) (d:after <mai>, face: {mai phiat} is wash the face, as on getting up in the morning) (r:zd:24276/zd:21918/zd:23036) (q:draft)
phiat = (i:5) (t:v) (f:health) (w:abort) (d:after <nau>, child: {nau phiat} is end a pregnancy, and also the noun abortion) (r:zd:25323) (q:draft, low confidence)
phiatding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:will erase/to be removed/to be struck out) (d:<phiat>, erase, and <ding> written as one word: to be erased or removed, as a name from a list or a tattoo from the skin) (j:phiat/ding) (r:zd:21309/zd:21876) (q:draft)
phiatkik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/it) (w:delete/remove/erase) (d:<phiat>, erase, and <kik>, back, written as one word: take away again something that was written, posted or made) (j:phiat/kik) (r:zd:20287/zd:23008/zd:20697) (q:draft)
phiatmaiding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:will abolish/will cancel/will remove) (d:<phiatmai>, wipe out, and <ding>, will, written as one word: will do away with it altogether, said of a tax or a rule) (j:phiatmai/ding) (r:zd:19674/zd:19685) (q:draft)
phih = (i:2) (t:v) (f:work) (w:fill in/fill out/complete) (d:write what is asked into a form, after the English word <form>: {form phih} is fill in a form; a present-day use apart from the meaning spit) (r:zd:25248/zd:23973/zd:24006) (q:draft)
Philadelphia = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Philadelphia) (d:city in the state of Pennsylvania in the United States) (r:zd:22040/zd:23776/zd:11901) (q:draft)
Philipi = (i:1) (t:name) (f:religion) (j:Filippi) (r:zd:15422/zd:16929) (q:draft)
Philippine = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:politics/travel) (w:Philippines/Philippine) (d:the Philippines, an island country of Southeast Asia, as in {Philippine gam}; also what belongs to it) (o:English) (r:zd:16906/zd:16944) (q:draft)
Philippines = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel/politics) (w:Philippines) (d:country of many islands in Southeast Asia) (r:zd:11219/zd:13104/zd:10785) (q:draft)
Philistine = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:religion) (w:Philistine) (d:English spelling of the name of the Philistines, a people of the Bible; the Bible text writes <Filistia>) (s:Filistia) (r:zd:25281/zd:25142) (q:draft)
philosopher = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:philosopher) (d:a thinker who studies the nature of knowledge, truth and life; used in Zolai sentences after the name of a people or place) (o:English) (r:zd:8668/zd:23893) (q:draft)
philosophy = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:philosophy) (d:philosophy as a subject of study) (o:English) (r:zd:9216/zd:21288) (q:draft)
phin = (i:2) (t:v) (f:nature) (w:drizzle/rain lightly) (d:of rain, fall lightly in fine drops, after <guah> and often followed by <seuhseuh> or {nelhnelh}; not the sense provoke) (r:zd:14824/zd:25630) (q:draft)
phisian = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:clear away/get rid of/wipe out) (d:remove a trouble or a wrong completely, said of problems and hardships) (r:zd:21869/zd:17976) (q:draft, low confidence)
phitkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:nature/everyday) (w:spurt out/spout/shoot out/burst out) (d:<phit> with <khia>, out: be forced out under pressure, as lava and ash from a volcano or air that has built up; also of anger held in for long that bursts out) (r:zd:23113/zd:17411) (q:draft)
phitphet = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:to the brim/chock-full/tightly) (d:after <dim>, full, and verbs of loading such as <pua> and <tuang>, not of time: filled or packed completely, with no room left) (r:zd:11375/zd:12790/zd:17375) (q:draft)
Phoenix = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Phoenix) (d:city in the state of Arizona in the United States, home of a Zomi community; the name also occurs in the names of other places and organisations) (r:zd:15805) (q:draft)
phok = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:nature/travel) (w:bumpy/rough/uneven) (d:of a surface or a road, uneven, full of bumps and holes) (r:zd:21421) (q:draft, low confidence)
pholaak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (j:pholak) (r:zd:11415/zd:23670) (q:draft)
pholhkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:bring out/reveal/disclose/dig out) (d:take out what is hidden or buried; of a matter, lay it open and make it known) (r:ts:11162/zd:23670) (q:draft, low confidence)
phone = (i:1) (t:n) (f:it) (w:phone/telephone) (o:English) (r:zd:20822/zd:12441) (q:draft)
phong = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:wake/awaken/rouse) (d:wake someone from sleep) (s:khanglosak/phawng) (q:draft)
phonggyi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:Buddhist monk/monk) (d:a Buddhist monk of Myanmar; {phonggyi sang} is a monastery school) (o:Burmese, hpongyi) (r:zd:23869/zd:20834) (q:draft)
phonglo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:rouse/revive/stir up) (d:wake something up again: stir the heart of people, bring back strength or a custom, or bring up again what is past; often followed by <kik>, again) (r:zd:17877/zd:22116) (q:draft)
photding = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:will first/for the time being) (d:<phot>, first or for now, and <ding>, will, written as one word after a verb: will do it first, will do it for the time being) (j:phot/ding) (r:zd:16786/zd:20295) (q:draft)
photni = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:let us first) (d:<phot>, first or for now, written as one word with the ending <ni>, let us, placed after a verb: let us do this first, let us do it for the time being) (j:phot/ni) (r:zd:19108/zd:20845) (q:draft)
Photo = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/it) (w:photo/photograph/picture) (d:a picture taken with a camera; {photo zaih} is to take a photo) (o:English) (r:zd:21365/zd:17983/zd:26163) (q:draft)
Photographer = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/work) (w:photographer) (d:a person who takes photographs; the Zolai word beside it in the articles is <manzaih>) (o:English) (r:zd:11780/zd:13293) (q:draft)
photphot = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:just/first/for now) (d:<phot> said twice, after a verb and mostly in a request: just do it, go ahead and do it for now) (b:phot) (r:zd:22474/zd:21598/zd:22473) (q:draft)
phuahna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/everyday) (w:composing/composition/making up) (d:<phuah>, compose or make up, with the noun ending <na>: the composing of a song or poem; {zuau phuahna} is the making up of lies, fabrication) (b:phuah) (r:zd:9254/zd:12269) (q:draft)
phuahsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/social) (w:compose for/name/give a name to) (d:<phuah> with <sak>, do for another: compose a tune or words for someone or for a song, or give a name to someone or something) (j:phuah/sak) (r:zd:9220/zd:17446/zd:9261) (q:draft)
phuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:name/call/give a name) (d:give a name to a child, a place or a thing, with <min>, name) (s:phuah)
phuaka = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/religion) (w:compose) (d:<phuak>, compose a song, and the linking <a> written as one word: composed, and then) (j:phuak/a) (r:zd:9224/zd:9255/zd:9257) (q:draft)
phuaknu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/religion) (w:composer/author/writer) (d:<phuak>, compose, with <nu>, woman: the woman who composed a song or its words; {la phuaknu} is the woman who wrote a song) (b:phuak) (r:zd:9260/zd:9220) (q:draft)
phuakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/religion) (w:composer/author/writer) (d:<phuak>, compose, with <pa>, man: the man who composed a song, its words or its tune; {la phuakpa} is the writer of a song) (b:phuak) (r:zd:9245/zd:9244) (q:draft)
phuaksiam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/religion) (w:skilled composer/gifted writer) (d:<phuak>, compose, and <siam>, skilled, written as one word: a person good at composing songs or tunes, as in {la phuaksiam}) (j:phuak/siam) (r:zd:9223/zd:9241) (q:draft)
phuakte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/social) (w:composers/authors/makers) (d:<phuak>, compose or make up, and the plural <te> written as one word: those who compose a song or coin a word, or who make up a story; {la phuakte} is the writer or writers of a song) (j:phuak/te) (r:zd:25475/zd:25580) (q:draft)
phual = (i:3) (t:n) (f:health/body) (w:lump/bump/pimple) (d:a small raised spot or lump that comes out on the skin or in the flesh, said with <po>, come out, as in {a phual hong po}) (r:zd:20926) (q:draft, low confidence)
phualsatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:camp/encampment/military camp/base) (d:<phualsat>, set up camp, with the noun suffix <na>: the place where troops are stationed, a military camp or post) (b:phualsat) (r:ts:3446/ts:4653/ts:9033) (q:draft)
Phualva = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (f:nature) (w:hornbill) (d:the hornbill, a large forest bird taken as an emblem of the Zomi; in most articles part of the name Phualva Lungtuak Media) (r:zd:20800) (q:draft)
Phualva Lungtuak = (i:1) (t:name) (f:media) (w:Phualva Lungtuak) (d:<Phualva>, hornbill, and <lungtuak>, be of one mind: name of a Zomi news group, mostly as {Phualva Lungtuak Media}, given as the source or the translator at the head or foot of an article) (r:zd:20078/zd:20464) (q:draft)
phuangkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/work) (w:initiate/set up/launch/bring forth) (d:<phuang>, start, with <khia>, out: set something new going, such as a committee, a plan or a teaching) (s:phuankhia) (b:phuang) (r:zd:21040/zd:17060) (q:draft)
phuanin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/work) (w:found/set up/establish) (d:<phuan>, set up, and <in> written as one word: setting up a committee, school or organisation, and then doing what follows) (j:phuan/in) (r:zd:24595/ts:6945) (q:draft)
phuankhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/work) (w:found/establish/set up) (d:<phuan>, set up, with <khia>, out: start an organisation, a company or a church; {a phuankhia pa} is the founder) (r:zd:21720/zd:14531/zd:25447) (q:draft)
phuankhiapa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/work) (w:founder) (d:<phuankhia>, found or set up, with <pa> for a male person: the man who founded an organisation, a company or a movement) (r:zd:9257/zd:24957/zd:17577) (q:draft)
phuat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:found/establish/set up) (d:found an organisation such as a church, a party or an armed group) (b:phuan) (r:zd:12337/zd:25562) (q:draft)
phuba = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:revenge/vengeance) (d:a wrong that is to be paid back; {phuba la} is take revenge) (s:phu) (r:zd:20116/zd:9124) (q:draft)
phuhkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:establish/found/set up) (d:<phuh>, found, with <khiat>, out: bring an organisation, a committee or a state into being; the form used before <ding> and <uh>) (r:ts:4823/ts:7820/zd:25020) (q:draft)
phuitong = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (f:nature) (w:cherry/cherry tree) (d:a tree of the Chin hills that blossoms in December, and its fruit; {phuitong pak} is cherry blossom and {phuitong gah} is the cherry fruit; Phuitong is also the name of a village) (r:zd:11400/zd:24276) (q:draft)
Phuket = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Phuket) (d:island and province in the south of Thailand, visited by many tourists) (r:zd:17239/zd:14869) (q:draft)
phukhagawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:crash badly/smash into/pile up) (d:<phukha> and <gawp> written as one word: strike against with great damage; {ki phukhagawp}, of vehicles, is crash into one another) (j:phukha/gawp) (r:zd:15613/zd:12967/zd:20353) (q:draft)
phul = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:brave/face/push through) (d:go straight at a hardship or an obstacle and force a way through it, as in {haksatna phul}; {phul khak} is run into, come up against) (r:zd:22736/zd:23835) (q:draft, low confidence)
phulgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/politics) (w:ram into/plough into) (d:drive a vehicle with force into a crowd of people; the second part is <gawp>, violently) (r:zd:11470/zd:13061) (q:draft, low confidence)
phulna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature/health) (w:outbreak/springing up) (d:<phul>, gush out or spring up, with the noun suffix <na>: the springing up or breaking out of something; {phulna mun} is the place where a disease breaks out) (b:phul) (r:zd:24609/zd:24453) (q:draft, low confidence)
phulphei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:plough through/ram through) (d:of a vehicle, drive into and across a crowd or a place; from one headline that is repeated) (r:zd:11691) (q:draft, low confidence)
phulpheigawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:plough into/ram into/run down) (d:of a vehicle or its driver, drive straight into and through people who are in the way; the ending <gawp> shows that the act is violent and does great harm) (r:zd:12955/zd:12559) (q:draft)
phulum = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (f:nature) (w:winged termite/flying termite) (d:an insect that swarms up out of the ground and flies high; the proverb {phulum phulna dingin leikha in petlet} says that it bursts out only because the <leikha> under the ground bites it; which insect is meant is not certain) (r:zd:11024/zd:24688) (q:draft, low confidence)
phulum = (i:2) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:ram to death/run down and kill) (d:<phu>, drive straight into, with <lum>, lie down, here to death, written as one word: kill by driving into) (r:zd:10855) (q:draft, low confidence)
phumna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/religion) (w:burial/burying/immersion) (d:<phum>, bury or immerse, with the noun suffix <na>: the putting of a body or a thing into the ground, {suang phumna} the setting of a stone, or immersion in water) (b:phum) (r:zd:25908/ts:3179) (q:draft)
phung = (i:2) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:clan/family/lineage) (d:the family line a person belongs to) (s:beh) (q:draft)
phung = (i:3) (t:n) (f:everyday/religion) (w:foot/base) (d:the lower end on which an upright thing stands, as in {singlamteh phung}, the foot of the cross; not the clan and not a wall) (s:bul) (r:zd:23936) (q:draft, low confidence)
phungcing = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:social/family) (w:well established/flourishing/thriving) (d:of a family line, a church or an organisation: strong, firmly rooted and with many members) (r:zd:26310/zd:19676) (q:draft, low confidence)
phungpha = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:nature/social) (w:flourishing/thriving/prolific) (d:of a plant, growing in a full clump with many shoots; of a family, a people or an organisation, growing in number and doing well) (r:zd:24176/zd:12166/zd:23343) (q:draft)
phungpi = (i:2) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:centre/root/main body/heart) (d:the main stem from which the rest grows: the home or centre of a people or an empire, the parent body of several organizations, the root of a trouble; paired with <bulpi> in {a phungpi leh a bulpi}) (r:zd:25573/zd:25094/zd:20125) (q:draft)
phungvuh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/work) (w:nurture/foster/support/build up) (d:care for a person, a group or a gift so that it grows and stands firm; said of a church, a party, a people or a talent. The literal sense, heaping earth around the foot of a plant, is not attested in the articles) (r:zd:25172/zd:24003/zd:24381) (q:draft, literal sense to be confirmed)
phungzi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:Buddhist monk/monk) (d:a Buddhist monk; {phungzi sang} is a monastery, and the word is also used for a Christian monk) (o:Burmese, hpongyi) (r:zd:23113/ts:2189/ts:1657) (q:draft)
phunlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:not grumble/not complain/without complaining) (d:<phun>, grumble, and <lo>, not, written as one word; {phunlo in} is without grumbling, and {phunlo paulo in} is without complaint or a word) (j:phun/lo) (r:zd:24673/zd:20941/zd:15384) (q:draft)
phuphei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/media) (w:crash into/ram/run into) (d:of a vehicle or a person: drive or rush straight into something or someone and hit it, as a car hits a tree or a road divider) (r:zd:11472/zd:12974) (q:draft)
phut = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:encounter/meet with/run into) (d:come upon a person or a difficulty without planning it, not set something up; in this meaning {phut} stands before <khak>, as in {phut khak}, happen to meet) (r:zd:21462/zd:23791) (q:draft, low confidence)
phutding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:to establish/will found/to set up) (d:<phut> and <ding> written as one word: will set up or found, in order to establish a state, a province or an organisation) (j:phut/ding) (r:zd:22293/zd:15824) (q:draft)
phutkhak = (i:2) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:collide/crash/run into) (d:of vehicles, after <ki> or <aki> and often with <tawh>, strike against each other in a road accident, not merely meet on the way) (r:zd:20589/zd:16731) (q:draft)
phutkhakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:collision/crash/encounter) (d:<phutkhak>, come up against, with the noun suffix <na>: a running into something, mostly of vehicles; also a meeting with hardship) (b:phutkhak) (r:zd:12569/zd:11666) (q:draft)
phutkhakpih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:collide with/run into) (d:<phutkhak> and <pih> written as one word: meet or strike together with something; {aki phutkhakpih mawtaw} is the car that it collided with) (j:phutkhak/pih) (r:zd:15429/zd:12105) (q:draft)
phutkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:establish/found/set up) (d:<phut>, set up, with <khia>, out, written as one word: found an organisation, a government or a country) (j:phut/khia) (r:zd:20673/ts:3289) (q:draft)
phutkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:establish/found/set up) (d:form of <phutkhia>, found or set up, used when a word such as <ding> follows; {gam phutkhiat} is to found a country) (b:phutkhia) (j:phut/khiat) (r:zd:23994/zd:25105) (q:draft)
phuut = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:encounter/run into/face) (d:meet with something hard, come up against it; {i phuut khop} is what we face together, said beside {i thuak khop}, what we bear together) (r:zd:21517/zd:22334) (q:draft, low confidence)
Physics = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:physics) (d:the science of matter and energy, as a subject of study) (o:English) (r:zd:15845/zd:22556) (q:draft)
Phyu = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel) (w:Phyu) (d:town in Bago Region of Myanmar; the same word, Burmese for white, is also part of Burmese personal and place names) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:17202) (q:draft, low confidence)
pi = (i:2) (t:n) (f:family) (w:grandmother) (d:grandmother, the mother of one's father or mother) (q:draft)
pi = (i:4) (t:n) (f:social) (w:Mrs/Madam) (d:title of respect written before the name of a married or older woman, the same word as grandmother used as a title) (r:ts:3168/zd:24806) (q:draft)
pi = (i:5) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:while/although/without) (d:after <lo>, not, and followed by <in>: while or although something is not so, without it; the same {pi} as in <napi>, although) (r:zd:22019/zd:22495) (q:draft)
pia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:give/grant) (d:hand something over to someone or grant it; {thu pia} is give an order and <thupha pia> is bless) (a:ngah/lak)
piaciat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:each give/all give) (d:<pia> and <ciat> written as one word: every one gives, each for his part; {tha piaciat ni} is let us each give support) (j:pia/ciat) (r:zd:11064/zd:20007/zd:20446) (q:draft)
piading = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:will give/to give) (d:<pia>, give, and <ding>, will, written as one word: will give, in order to give, to be given) (j:pia/ding) (r:zd:19249/zd:22704/zd:24331) (q:draft)
piahi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:give/grant) (d:<pia> and the sentence ending <hi> written as one word: gives, gave) (j:pia/hi) (r:zd:23602/zd:21409) (q:draft)
piakbeh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:give more/give in addition/pay extra) (d:<piak>, give, with the ending {-beh}, in addition: give or pay something more on top of what was given) (b:piak) (r:zd:12327/zd:22448/zd:20670) (q:draft)
piakdan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:way of giving/manner of giving) (d:<piak> and <dan> written as one word: the way something is given; {min piakdan} is the way of naming) (j:piak/dan) (r:zd:15637/zd:20576) (q:draft)
piakding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:to give/to be given) (d:<piak> and <ding> written as one word: will give, to be given, or what is to be given; {sum piakding} is money to be paid) (j:piak/ding) (r:zd:15571/zd:24370) (q:draft)
piakei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not give/do not give) (d:<pia>, give, and the negative <kei>, written as one word: {piakei in} and {piakei un} are do not give, {piakei ning} is I would not give) (j:pia/kei) (r:zd:20263/zd:23733) (q:draft)
piakhiate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:those who give/things given) (d:<piakhia>, give out, with plural <te>: the people who give something away, or the things that are given) (b:piakhia) (j:piakhia/te) (r:zd:25572/zd:22408) (q:draft)
piakhinta = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have given/have already given) (d:<pia> and <khinta> written as one word: has already given; with <thu>, has given an order or instruction) (j:pia/khinta) (r:zd:19018/zd:21330) (q:draft)
piakkhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion/social) (w:giving/generosity/donation/dedication) (d:<piakkhiat>, give out, with the noun suffix <na>: the giving away of money, goods or oneself for others or for God) (b:piakkhiat) (r:zd:24119/zd:21561/zd:18107) (q:draft)
piakkholh = (i:2) (t:v) (f:work/social) (w:pay in advance/prepay) (d:of money, with <sum>: give it ahead of time, before the need comes, as a contribution paid beforehand to a funeral fund; not a word or command given beforehand) (r:zd:21843) (q:draft, low confidence)
piakkul = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:must give/have to pay) (d:<piak> and <kul> written as one word: it is necessary to give or to pay; with <lo>, need not pay) (j:piak/kul) (r:zd:23863/zd:25824/zd:22581) (q:draft)
piakkulding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:will have to pay/will have to give) (d:<piakkul> and <ding> written as one word: it will be necessary to pay or give) (j:piakkul/ding) (r:zd:11308/zd:19373) (q:draft)
piakkullo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:need not pay/need not give) (d:<piakkul> and <lo> written as one word: there is no need to give or to pay) (a:piakkul) (j:piakkul/lo) (r:zd:19563/zd:20197) (q:draft)
piakleh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:if one gives/when one gives) (d:<piak>, give, with <leh>, if or when, written as one word: if or when someone gives; {thupha na piakleh} is if you bless) (j:piak/leh) (r:zd:21044/zd:17481) (q:draft)
piakloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not give) (d:<piak> and <loh> written as one word: not giving, not given; {piakloh phamawh} is must be given, and {piakloh omlo} is there is none who is not given) (j:piak/loh) (r:zd:23437/zd:21370) (q:draft)
piakna = (i:3) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:giving/presentation) (d:the act of giving, after the word for what is given: {letsong piakna} is the giving of gifts, {sisan piakna} giving blood, <thupha piakna> the giving of a blessing; not the thing that is given) (r:zd:17634/zd:24361/zd:19249) (q:draft)
piakpiak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:keep giving/give again and again) (d:doubled form of <piak>, give: go on giving, give repeatedly) (b:piak) (r:zd:23676/zd:11674) (q:draft)
piaksak = (i:3) (t:v) (f:religion/social) (w:grant/bestow/give) (d:give something to a person as a favour, where <sak> marks that the giving is for the good of the receiver and no third person is involved; mostly after <hong> in the wish {Topa'n thupha hong piaksak tahen}, may the Lord grant you blessing) (r:zd:17409/zd:15379/zd:10892) (q:draft)
piaksawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:try to give/offer/intend to give) (d:<piak>, give, with <sawm>, intend, written as one word: be about to give, offer or attempt to give) (j:piak/sawm) (r:zd:14701/zd:19814) (q:draft)
pial = (i:2) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:go out/step outside/go beyond) (d:after <pua>, outside, as in {kong pua pial}, go out of the door, and {gam pua pial}, go out of the country: go out past a boundary, with no thought of going wrong) (r:zd:21117/ts:7876) (q:draft, low confidence)
pialai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:give more/give in addition/also give) (d:<pia>, give, with the ending {-lai}, still or further: give something more, give as well) (b:pia) (r:zd:23136/zd:21590/zd:20587) (q:draft)
pialo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:not give/not provide/withhold) (d:<pia> and <lo> written as one word: does not give; in job notices {an pialo} means that food is not provided) (j:pia/lo) (r:zd:20577/zd:12336) (q:draft)
pian = (i:3) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:somewhat/rather/a little/seemingly) (d:after a verb or adjective, softens the statement: it is so to some degree or seems to be so, as in {hi zaw pian hi}, it is rather so; not birth and not a likeness of a thing) (r:zd:18927/zd:15474/zd:25222) (q:draft)
pianawnlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:no longer give/not give any more) (d:<pia>, give, and <nawnlo>, no longer, written as one word: stop giving or issuing something; after <ki> be no longer given) (j:pia/nawnlo) (r:zd:11587/zd:17097) (q:draft)
piancil = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:first come into being/originate/begin) (d:used as a verb, mostly after <hong>: come into being for the first time, said of a country, a group or an event; sense 1 is the noun for that time) (r:zd:25020/zd:23057) (q:draft, low confidence)
Piancit = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel/politics) (w:France) (d:France, in a name taken from Burmese; {Piancit pai} is the going of Zomi men to France in 1917, remembered at its hundredth year in 2017) (o:Burmese, pyinthit) (r:zd:11549/zd:18086) (q:draft)
piandang = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:unusual/strange/peculiar/different) (d:<pian>, form or appearance, with <dang>, other: of another kind than the usual, out of the ordinary) (r:zd:23298/zd:25094) (q:draft)
pianga = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:arise and/come about and/be born and) (d:<piang> and the linking <a> written as one word: something comes about or is born, and the sentence goes on) (j:piang/a) (r:zd:19193/zd:21605/zd:11135) (q:draft)
piangding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:will happen/will come about) (d:<piang>, happen or come into being, and <ding>, will, written as one word) (j:piang/ding) (r:zd:20355/zd:23832) (q:draft)
pianggawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/social) (w:break out/erupt/happen violently) (d:<piang> happen with <gawp>, which shows that the action is severe, written as one word: of trouble, a fight or an accident, break out) (j:piang/gawp) (r:zd:15937/zd:16225/zd:13330) (q:draft)
pianghi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:happen/occur/arise) (d:<piang> and the sentence ending <hi> written as one word: it happens or happened, it comes about) (j:piang/hi) (r:zd:17848/zd:19562/zd:21323) (q:draft)
pianghiam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:happen) (d:<piang> and the question particle <hiam> written as one word, at the end of a question: did it happen; {banghang in pianghiam} is why it happened) (j:piang/hiam) (r:zd:14738/zd:15535) (q:draft)
piangkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/everyday) (w:be born together/arise together/coincide) (d:<piang>, be born or come about, and <khawm>, together, written as one word: be born of the same parents or at the same time, come into being together) (j:piang/khawm) (r:zd:21096/zd:21458) (q:draft)
piangkhin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:have happened/have already occurred) (d:<piang>, happen, and <khin>, already, written as one word: have already happened or come about, often after a count of cases) (j:piang/khin) (r:zd:19662/zd:11715/zd:20682) (q:draft)
piangleuleu = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/everyday) (w:happen again/occur again) (d:<piang>, happen, and <leuleu>, again, written as one word) (j:piang/leuleu) (r:zd:15292/zd:20023) (q:draft)
pianglo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not happen/not come about/not arise) (d:<piang>, come into being or happen, with <lo>, not, written as one word) (j:piang/lo) (r:zd:12337/zd:22140/zd:21050) (q:draft)
piangna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/everyday) (j:pianna) (r:zd:19571/zd:21426) (q:draft, low confidence)
piangngei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:have happened before/once happened) (d:<piang> and <ngei> written as one word: have happened or taken place at an earlier time) (j:piang/ngei) (r:zd:20892/zd:15431/zd:19981) (q:draft)
piangpah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:happen at once/arise immediately) (d:<piang>, happen, and <pah>, at once, written as one word: come about straight away) (j:piang/pah) (r:zd:21110/zd:12136/zd:15201) (q:draft)
piangpiang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:keep happening/happen again and again/come about) (d:<piang>, happen, said twice: happen repeatedly or one after another; {piangpiang lel} is it simply comes about) (b:piang) (r:zd:22046/zd:23810/zd:20999) (q:draft)
piangsakgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/social) (w:cause havoc/stir up badly) (d:<piangsak>, bring about, with <gawp>, severely: cause something in a violent or ruinous way, mostly {buaina piangsakgawp}, cause a serious disturbance) (j:piangsak/gawp) (r:zd:14589/zd:12172) (q:draft)
piangsaklo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:not cause/not bring about) (d:<piangsak>, cause, and <lo>, not, written as one word: does not cause or produce it) (j:piangsak/lo) (r:zd:14826/zd:13230) (q:draft)
piangte = (i:2) (t:n) (f:media/everyday) (w:events/happenings/occurrences) (d:after <thu> or a word such as <lamdang>, the things that have happened: {thu piangte} are events and {na lamdang piangte} are wonders that took place, not the produce of field or sea) (r:zd:9139/zd:24119/zd:20454) (q:draft)
piangthak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:religion) (w:be born again/born again) (d:<piang>, be born, with <thak>, new: be born again in the Christian sense, come to new faith; {mi piangthak} is a born-again person) (r:zd:20218/zd:8667/zd:23676) (q:draft)
piangthakte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:the born again/born-again believers) (d:<piangthak>, born again, with the plural {-te}: those who are born again, born-again Christians) (b:piangthak) (r:zd:23394/zd:23740/zd:22784) (q:draft)
piangtheihiam = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/media) (w:how it could happen) (d:<piang>, happen, and <theihiam> written as one word: could it happen; closes an indirect question after <bangci bangin>, how, or <banghang>, why) (j:piang/theihiam) (r:zd:15403/zd:17727) (q:draft)
piangtheilo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:impossible/cannot happen) (d:<piang>, happen, and <theilo>, unable, written as one word: cannot come about, not possible) (j:piang/theilo) (r:zd:17297/zd:19816) (q:draft)
piangthu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:event/happening/occurrence) (d:<piang>, happen, with <thu>, matter, written as one word: a thing that happens, usually as {a piangthu}) (j:piang/thu) (r:zd:24276/zd:20682) (q:draft)
pianist = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media) (w:pianist/piano player) (o:English) (r:zd:17634) (q:draft)
pianken = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/religion) (w:nature/inborn nature) (d:what a person or thing has from birth; also glossed as nature in speaking of the two natures of Christ) (r:zd:24381) (q:draft, low confidence)
pianleh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:if it happens/if it arises/when it comes about) (d:<pian>, come about, and <leh>, if, written as one word: if or when the thing named happens or appears) (j:pian/leh) (r:zd:21092/zd:23443) (q:draft)
pianloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:not happen/not arise/not come about) (d:<pian> and <loh> written as one word, before words such as <nading> and <hangin>: not come into being, not happen) (j:pian/loh) (r:zd:20004/zd:23487/zd:19875) (q:draft)
pianna nu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:birth mother/own mother/natural mother) (d:<pianna>, birth, and <nu>, mother: the mother who gave birth to someone, as against a stepmother or a woman addressed as mother; a possessive stands before it; {pianna nu leh pa} is one's own parents) (r:zd:19571/zd:24117/zd:26953) (q:draft)
Pianni = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time/social) (w:birthday/founding day/anniversary) (d:<pian> and <ni> written as one word: the day on which a person was born or an organisation was founded) (j:pian/ni) (r:zd:17011) (q:draft, low confidence)
piannop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:want to become/wish to be) (d:<pian>, come to be, with <nop>, want: wish to be or to turn out a certain way; {na piannop dan} is what you want to become) (j:pian/nop) (r:zd:20917/zd:20725/zd:19731) (q:draft)
piano = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/religion) (w:piano) (d:the musical instrument; {piano tum} is play the piano) (o:English) (r:zd:23653/zd:9248/zd:9214) (q:draft)
pianpah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:happen at once/come about immediately) (d:<pian> and <pah> written as one word: come about right away; in other sentences <pian> after a verb seems to mean somewhat, rather) (j:pian/pah) (r:zd:21989) (q:draft, low confidence)
pianpian = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:gradually/somewhat/more and more) (d:placed after a verb or describing word: the state is beginning to be so or is slowly becoming so, often followed by <ta>) (r:zd:22928/zd:15234/zd:19154) (q:draft)
pianpih = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:nature/inborn character) (d:used alone as a noun, after a possessor such as {kei'} or <ama>: the nature a person or thing has from birth; {kei' pianpih in} is by my nature) (r:zd:9231) (q:draft, low confidence)
piansaknate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature/religion) (w:creation/created things/creatures/nature) (d:<piansakna> with the plural ending <te>: the things that were created, the created world) (b:piansakna) (r:zd:23975/zd:15035) (q:draft)
pianta = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:rather/somewhat) (d:placed after a verb or describing word: it has by now become rather so, it seems to have come to that, as in {sawt pianta}, it has been rather long) (j:pian/ta) (r:zd:23890/zd:23014/zd:23603) (q:draft, low confidence)
piante = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (d:<pian>, likeness, and plural <te>, written as one word after a describing phrase: those that seem to be so, the ones of that sort) (j:pian/te) (r:zd:21978/zd:11177) (q:draft, low confidence)
pianthak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:religion) (w:be born again/be regenerated) (d:<pian>, be born, with <thak>, new: be born again in the Christian sense; also as a noun, the new birth) (r:zd:23394/zd:20281/zd:26664) (q:draft)
pianthakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:new birth/regeneration/conversion) (d:<pian>, be born, with <thak>, new, and the noun suffix <na>: being born again, the conversion of a person to faith) (r:zd:25288/zd:21052) (q:draft)
piantheihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:possibility/coming about) (d:<piantheih>, can come about, with the noun ending {-na}: the coming about of something, and what makes it possible; {a piantheihna dingin} is so that it can come about) (b:piantheih) (r:zd:25712/zd:21279) (q:draft)
Piantit = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:politics/travel) (w:France/French) (d:France, often as {Piantit gam}; {Piantit pau} and {Piantit lai} are the French language) (o:Burmese, pyinthit) (r:zd:17437/zd:21978/zd:19571) (q:draft)
pianuamlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:be unwilling to give/refuse to give) (d:<pianuam>, want to give, with the negative <lo>, written as one word) (j:pianuam/lo) (r:zd:11454/zd:11182) (q:draft)
piapah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:give at once/give right away) (d:<pia>, give, and <pah>, at once, written as one word: give or grant without delay) (j:pia/pah) (r:zd:24069/zd:12304/zd:20176) (q:draft)
piapia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:keep giving/give repeatedly) (d:<pia>, give, said twice: give again and again or go on giving; with <ki>, be given one after another) (b:pia) (r:zd:14992/zd:24231/zd:21168) (q:draft)
piasa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:have given/already given) (d:<pia>, give, with the ending {-sa}, already done: given; {hong piasa teng} are those who have given, in lists of donors) (b:pia) (r:zd:11011) (q:draft)
piaudung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature/travel) (w:beach/shore/coast) (d:<piau>, bank, and <dung>, length, written as one word: the land along the edge of the sea, a beach; {tuipinawl piaudung} is a sea beach) (s:tuipinawl) (j:piau/dung) (r:zd:17649/zd:12066) (q:draft)
piaunel = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature) (w:sand) (d:the sand of a riverbank or a shore) (s:sehnel) (r:ts:4831/zd:25115) (q:draft)
piazel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:keep giving/give again and again) (d:<pia> and <zel> written as one word: give time after time) (j:pia/zel) (r:zd:21826/zd:17478) (q:draft)
pibawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:honour/esteem/treat as important) (d:treat a person or an event as great and show it honour and attention) (r:zd:23466/zd:20264/ts:301) (q:draft)
