sepleh = (i:2) (t:v) (f:work) (w:if one does) (d:<sep> and <leh.3> written as one word: if one works or does) (j:sep/leh) (r:zd:22282) (q:draft, low confidence)
seplehbawl = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/everyday) (w:work/activity/undertaking) (d:<sep>, work, <leh>, and, and <bawl>, make, written as one word: what one does and makes, work and activity of every kind) (j:sep/leh/bawl) (r:zd:16844/zd:20477/zd:21037) (q:draft)
seploh = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:not do/leave undone) (d:the form of {sem lo} used before another word: not doing a task; {seploh phamawh} is what cannot be left undone, a thing that must be done) (r:zd:20892/zd:20823/zd:21817) (q:draft)
sepman = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:wages/pay) (d:<sep>, work, with <man>, price: what is paid for work done) (s:thaman) (j:sep/man) (r:zd:22451) (q:draft, low confidence)
