suuk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:get worse/worsen/decline) (d:go down, become worse or lower; {suuk zaw} is worse than and {suuk semsem} is worse and worse; a long-vowel form related to <suk>, down) (r:zd:20550/zd:20908) (q:draft)
suuksia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:get worse/deteriorate/be worse) (d:go down and become bad, of a situation or of the condition of a sick person; with <zaw>, worse than) (r:zd:20823/zd:23846) (q:draft)
suut = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/education) (w:recount/relate/trace/go through) (d:tell or go through a matter point by point, as a history, a story or the meaning of something; the same word as <sut.3>, written with a long vowel; also found in personal names) (r:zd:24594/zd:24682/ts:3372) (q:draft)
suutna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/media) (w:study/tracing/examination/exposition) (d:<suut>, go through point by point, with the noun suffix <na>: the tracing or careful examining of a matter; {khanggui suutna} is genealogy, the tracing of descent) (b:suut) (r:zd:24071/zd:23086) (q:draft)
