tading = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday/time) (w:will now/be about to) (d:<ta> and <ding> written as one word after a verb: the thing will happen from now on, is now going to happen; frequent at the end of headlines) (j:ta/ding) (r:zd:11109/zd:24354/zd:11527) (q:draft)
tading = (i:2) (t:prep) (f:everyday) (w:for) (d:after a noun, with <in>: for, as far as that one is concerned; seems to be the same as <ading>) (r:zd:25601) (q:draft, low confidence)
tadinghi = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday/time) (w:will now/is about to) (d:<ta>, <ding> and the sentence-final <hi> written as one word after a verb: closes a statement that the thing will now happen) (j:ta/ding/hi) (r:zd:19727/zd:20104) (q:draft)
