tah = (i:2) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:now/then) (d:placed after a verb at the end of a clause, with the sense now, then; before {ci-in}, saying or thinking, it closes a thought that takes the thing as now settled; not the verb of sense 1) (r:zd:12541/zd:11206/zd:20862) (q:draft, low confidence)
tahi = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<ta> and <hi> written as one word at the end of a sentence: <ta> shows that a state has now come about or changed, now, already, and <hi> ends the statement) (j:ta/hi) (r:zd:19676/zd:18011/zd:12093) (q:draft)
