Tanahmerah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel/politics) (w:Tanah Merah) (d:Tanah Merah in Malaysia written as one word; in the articles the immigration detention camp there, from which detained people are sent home) (r:zd:21550/zd:21156) (q:draft, low confidence)
Tanai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel/politics) (w:Tanai) (d:a town and township in Kachin State, Myanmar) (r:zd:15417/zd:17616) (q:draft)
Tanakha = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body/home) (w:thanaka) (d:the yellowish paste of ground bark that people in Myanmar rub on the face as a cosmetic; {tanakha kinuh} is to put it on) (o:Burmese, thanakha) (r:zd:19812/zd:11337) (q:draft)
tanau = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/social) (w:relative/kin/kinsman) (d:a member of one's own family or clan) (s:behpa/sanggam) (q:draft)
tanau meltheih = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/social) (w:relatives and friends/kith and kin) (d:<tanau>, relative, and <meltheih>, acquaintance, set side by side without <leh>: relatives and acquaintances, all the people one is close to; common in messages of condolence with <khempeuh>, all) (r:zd:21365/zd:24150) (q:draft)
tanbang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:equal level/standing) (d:the level or standing of a person beside others; seen with <kim>, as {gual tawh tanbang kim}, be on a level with one's peers, and {tanbang kim sak}, make equal) (r:zd:22203/zd:24682) (q:draft, low confidence)
tanei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family) (w:have a child/bear a child/have young) (d:<ta> and <nei> written as one word: have a child or children; of an animal, have young) (j:ta/nei) (r:zd:21945/zd:24951) (q:draft)
tang = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:piece/unit/round) (d:counting word placed between a thing and its number for single small or round things such as bricks, bullets, bombs and votes, as in {leisek tang khat}, one brick; it is not the seed of a plant) (r:zd:24696/ts:10538) (q:draft)
tangdin = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:politics) (w:independent/standing alone) (d:standing by oneself; {mimal tangdin} is an independent candidate or member of parliament, one who belongs to no party) (r:zd:24646/zd:24697) (q:draft)
tangek = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:baby/infant/little child) (d:<ta>, child, and <ngek>, tender, written as one word: one's own baby or very young child) (j:ta/ngek) (r:zd:24276/zd:19871) (q:draft)
tangh = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:measles) (d:measles, also {tangh natna}; used for rubella as well) (r:zd:12336) (q:draft, low confidence)
tangh = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:lump/piece/chunk) (d:a solid piece or lump of something; {tangh khat} is one chunk, and {dangka tangh} seems to be pieces of money, coins) (r:zd:20627) (q:draft, low confidence)
tanghtangh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:persistently/always/steadily) (d:placed after a verb: keep on doing it, every time or without giving up) (r:zd:25625/zd:23731/zd:24421) (q:draft, low confidence)
tangial = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (d:emphatic word placed after a verb, before <hi> or <leh>: really, indeed, in fact; {nong sap tangial leh} is if you really call me) (r:zd:21908/ts:301) (q:draft, low confidence)
Tangkak = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Tangkak) (d:town and district in the state of Johor, Malaysia, next to Muar) (r:zd:20508) (q:draft)
tangkhat = (i:1) (t:num) (f:everyday) (w:one/a single one) (d:<tang>, here the counter for small round things such as grains, pills, bullets, eyes and votes, and <khat> written as one word: one of them) (j:tang/khat) (r:zd:14826/zd:25534/zd:20087) (q:draft)
tangkokhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/social) (w:announce/proclaim/make public) (d:<tangko>, announce, with <khia>, out: make something known to the public, as a government or the police do) (s:genkhia/pulak) (b:tangko) (r:zd:20254/zd:25094) (q:draft)
tangkona nei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/politics) (w:announce/make an announcement/proclaim) (d:<tangkona>, announcement, and <nei>, have: to make a public announcement or proclamation; what is announced stands before it, often a statement ending in <cih> or {ci'n}) (r:zd:12494/zd:18200) (q:draft)
tangkosa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/politics) (w:already announced/as announced) (d:<tangko>, announce, and <sa>, already done, written as one word; {a tangkosa mahbangin} is just as was announced) (j:tangko/sa) (r:zd:17097/zd:19964) (q:draft)
tangkosak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/politics) (w:announce/have proclaimed/issue) (d:<tangko>, proclaim, with the causative <sak>: have something announced or made known to the public, as a warning or alert) (j:tangko/sak) (r:zd:20023/zd:24029) (q:draft)
tanglo = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/body) (w:motionless/still/without moving) (d:not moving at all; mostly {tanglo in}, without stirring, standing or lying still) (r:zd:12904/zd:25908) (q:draft)
tangmi = (i:2) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:representative/delegate/member of parliament) (d:a person chosen to speak and vote for a group, such as the delegate of a church or village or an elected member of a parliament; {mipi tangmi} is a representative of the people) (r:zd:12341/zd:21221) (q:draft)
tangmite = (i:2) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:representatives/delegates/members of parliament) (d:people chosen by vote to speak for the public in a parliament or council, after <teel>, elect, or {mipi'}, of the people; they are elected, not sent by a ruler as an envoy is) (r:zd:12984/zd:22758/zd:25461) (q:draft)
tangnawnlo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:body/health) (w:motionless/no longer moving/lifeless) (d:<tang>, here in the sense stir or move, with <nawnlo>, no longer: not moving any more, said of one who lies unconscious or dead) (r:zd:12304/zd:14935/zd:11560) (q:draft)
tangnih = (i:1) (t:num) (f:everyday) (w:two) (d:<tang>, here the counting word for small round things such as eggs, teeth and bullets and for verses, and <nih>, two, written as one word: two of them) (j:tang/nih) (r:zd:12192/ts:296) (q:draft)
Tangnuam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel) (w:Tangnuam) (d:a Zomi village near Lamka in Manipur, India) (r:ts:4569/zd:23022) (q:draft, low confidence)
tangpi = (i:2) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:the public/community/common people) (d:the people as a whole and what concerns or belongs to all of them, as against one person, <mimal>: {tangpi ading} is for the public and {tangpi vai} is public affairs; it also pairs with <tangta>; not the adverb that strengthens a word of seeing) (s:mipi) (r:zd:22910/zd:20905/zd:16604) (q:draft)
tangpi tangta = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:the general public/common people/ordinary citizens) (d:the pair of <tangpi> and <tangta>: the people at large, ordinary people as against rulers and officials; often after <mipi> or the name of a country) (s:mipi) (r:zd:21908/zd:9124) (q:draft)
tangsak = (i:3) (t:v) (f:social/religion) (w:count as/regard as/make into) (d:after a word for a standing such as <midik>, <mihai> or <innteek>, cause someone to rank as that; {midik tangsak} is count as righteous, written joined in <diktangsak>) (r:zd:14791/zd:21063/zd:25573) (q:draft)
tangsam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:lack/be short of/be in need) (d:be without what is needed; written after a separate <ki> as {ki tangsam}, the same as <kitangsam>) (s:tasam) (r:zd:24673/zd:23167) (q:draft)
tangta = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:common people/the public/civilians) (d:the people at large, ordinary citizens; mostly in the pair <tangpi tangta>, the general public, and in texts on war, civilians) (r:zd:10743/zd:16588/zd:9124) (q:draft)
tangtak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/travel) (w:straight/directly/straightforwardly) (d:in a straight line, without turning aside, and of speech plainly and directly; mostly as {tangtak in}) (r:zd:21837/zd:21063/zd:24276) (q:draft)
tangtangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:making a point of/taking care to) (d:<tangtang> and <in> written as one word after a verb: doing it on purpose and steadily, making a point of it) (j:tangtang/in) (r:zd:21332/zd:25711) (q:draft, low confidence)
tangtat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:go one's own way/act alone/break away) (d:act on one's own apart from the group, without consulting or working with others; named as a fault together with <phengphi> and self-interest) (r:zd:16640/zd:23902/zd:21720) (q:draft)
tangtawn = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:ancient times/long ago/of old) (d:the far past; {tangtawn pan} is from of old, since long ago, and before a noun it is ancient; probably the same word as <tangtawng>) (s:tangtawng/tanglai) (r:zd:23476/zd:16101/zd:19612) (q:draft)
tangte = (i:3) (t:n) (f:everyday/politics) (w:rounds/shells/balls/grains) (d:<tang>, a grain or single round piece, with the plural <te>: single round things such as bullets, bomb and rocket shells, golf balls or stars, after the name of the thing as in {thaupi tangte}, {bomb tangte}, {aksi tangte}) (r:zd:23367/ts:301/zd:16500) (q:draft)
tangtel = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (f:nature) (w:earthworm/worm) (r:zd:24079/zd:23022) (q:draft)
tangtha = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/social) (w:unpaid labour/volunteer work) (d:work done without pay, given freely or demanded by an authority; {tangtha kuan} is go and do such work) (r:zd:10935/zd:22755) (q:draft)
tangthu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/education) (w:story/account) (d:an account of what happened, as in {vantung leh leitung tangthu}, the story of the heavens and the earth)
tangval = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:boy/youth/young man) (d:a young unmarried man; {tangval lai} is still young) (a:nungak) of unmarried adult man
tangvalno = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:young man/youth/lad) (d:<tangval>, young man, with <no>, young: a youth or young lad; {a tangvalno tungin} is in his early youth) (b:tangval) (r:zd:21608/zd:20145/zd:22040) (q:draft)
tangzai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:wide/broad/extensive) (d:wide in extent or scope, said of land, work, vision and thinking; {tangzai zaw} is wider and {a tangzai takin} is widely; built on <zai>, wide) (r:zd:23554/zd:14791/zd:21911) (q:draft)
tangzaisak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/education) (w:broaden/widen/extend) (d:<tangzai>, wide, with the causative <sak>, written as one word: make wider, broaden a view or an aim) (b:tangzai) (j:tangzai/sak) (r:zd:18958/zd:14791) (q:draft)
tani = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:let us now) (d:<ta>, now or already, and <ni>, let us, written as one word at the end of a sentence: let us do so now) (r:zd:20899) (q:draft, low confidence)
Tanintharyi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel/politics) (w:Tanintharyi/Tenasserim) (d:the southernmost region of Myanmar, with the towns Myeik, Dawei and Kawthaung) (r:zd:17941/zd:15913) (q:draft)
Tank = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/home) (w:tank) (d:a large container for water, oil or gas) (o:English) (r:zd:17450/zd:20335/zd:15928) (q:draft)
Tank = (i:2) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:tank) (d:an armoured fighting vehicle with a gun) (o:English) (r:ts:889/zd:11003) (q:draft)
Tanker = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/work) (w:tanker) (d:a lorry or ship built to carry oil, gas or another liquid; mostly as {Oil Tanker} and {Gas Tanker}) (o:English) (r:zd:17455/zd:12398) (q:draft)
tankhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:first grade/standard one) (d:<tan>, school class, with <khat>, one, written as one word: the first class of primary school, above <tanlang> and far below <tansawm>) (r:zd:24502) (q:draft)
tankhia = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:cut off/cut away/sever) (d:<tan>, cut, with <khia>, out: cut a part off or cut through a thing to take it away, said of locks, bars, plants and parts of the body; not the setting free of a person) (r:zd:20595/zd:12788) (q:draft)
tankhiatsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/body) (w:cut off/sever) (d:<tankhiat>, cut off, with <sak>: cut off a part of another person's body, or with <ki> have it cut off) (j:tankhiat/sak) (r:zd:20732/zd:12331) (q:draft)
tanlang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:kindergarten/preparatory class) (d:the class below the first grade, {tan khat}, at school) (r:zd:25288/zd:24502) (q:draft, low confidence)
tanlawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (j:taanlawh) (r:zd:24227/zd:11707) (q:draft)
tann = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:grade/class/standard) (d:a school grade, followed by its number: {tann 10} is the tenth grade) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:19232) (q:draft, low confidence)
tano = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:child/little child/young child) (d:<ta> child with the ending {-no}, young or small: the child of someone, said with affection or of a young child; {tano te} is the children) (b:ta) (r:zd:21389/zd:11581/zd:10929) (q:draft)
tansak = (i:2) (t:v) (f:work/politics) (w:ransom/have redeemed) (d:<tan>, redeem, with the causative <sak>: let a captive be bought free; {sum tawh tansak} is release someone for a ransom) (r:zd:11600) (q:draft, low confidence)
tansang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:higher education/higher grade/advanced level) (d:<tan>, here grade or class, with <sang>, high: the upper level of schooling, study beyond school; {lai tansang} is a person of higher learning and {tansang pilsinna} is higher education) (r:zd:22341/zd:22736) (q:draft)
tansawm = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:tenth grade/tenth standard/matriculation) (d:<tan>, school class, with <sawm>, ten: the tenth and last class of high school in Myanmar and the examination that ends it; {tansawm ong} is pass it) (r:zd:19676/zd:19952/zd:23276) (q:draft)
tanu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:daughter) (d:a female child of her parents) (a:tapa)
tanu tapa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:children/sons and daughters/offspring) (d:<tanu>, daughter, and <tapa>, son, set side by side without a joining word: the children of a couple, daughters and sons together; a number or the plural <te> follows) (s:tate) (r:zd:20281/zd:11831/zd:21511) (q:draft)
tanumei = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:daughter/female child) (d:<ta>, child, with <numei>, female: a daughter, set against <tapasal>, a son) (s:tanu) (r:zd:21853/zd:16294/zd:14597) (q:draft)
tanuno = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:little daughter/young daughter) (d:{tanu no} written as one word, <tanu>, daughter, followed by a word for young or little) (b:tanu) (r:zd:20083) (q:draft)
tanupi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/work) (w:secretary/general secretary) (d:the secretary of an organisation, placed after the name of the body or of its section, as in {Genvai tanupi}, the secretary for funeral affairs) (r:zd:16813/zd:22489) (q:draft, low confidence)
tanute = (i:2) (t:n) (f:media/social) (w:staff/team/workers/correspondents) (d:the people who carry out the work of an organisation, written after its name, as in {Tongsan Media tanute}, the staff of a news site who sign a report; not daughters) (r:ts:3179/zd:11375/zd:24073) (q:draft)
tap = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:hearth/fireplace) (d:the fireplace of a house; {tap tungah} is on the hearth, and <tapkual> is the hearth and the space around it) (r:zd:9223) (q:draft)
tap = (i:2) (t:v) (f:social/family) (w:name after/take the name of) (d:take a name from a person or a place; <mintap> is a name taken over in this way, and {a tap sak} is name something after someone) (r:zd:23990/zd:17879) (q:draft, low confidence)
tapa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:son) (d:a male child of his parents; after a name, son of that person) (a:tanu)
tapasal = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:son/male child) (d:<ta>, child, with <pasal>, male: a son) (s:tapa) (r:zd:18927/zd:12271) (q:draft)
Tape = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/everyday) (w:tape/adhesive tape) (d:sticky tape for binding or sealing, and the tape that police stretch round a place; {Tape Record} is a tape recorder) (o:English) (r:zd:14543/zd:15686) (q:draft)
tapeuh = (i:2) (t:part) (f:everyday/social) (w:please/do) (d:after a verb and before the command endings <un>, <in> or <ni>, makes an earnest plea, do so or with <kei> do not; not the wish with <hen>) (r:zd:19943/zd:12487/zd:12177) (q:draft)
Tapidaw = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:Christian) (d:a Christian, a follower of Jesus Christ; also describes a thing as Christian, as in {Tapidaw pawlpi}, a Christian church) (s:Christian/Khristian) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:24064/zd:13354) (q:draft)
tapidaw upna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:Christianity/Christian faith) (d:{tapidaw}, Christian, and <upna>, faith: the Christian faith, Christianity as a belief, set against <biakna>, religion, and the old <lawki> customs) (r:zd:21175/zd:23394) (q:draft)
tapidawte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:Christians/believers) (d:plural of {tapidaw}, a Christian, literally a disciple) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:23394/zd:24064) (q:draft)
tapong = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:rebel/insurgent) (d:an armed rebel against the government) (o:Burmese, thabon) (r:zd:14821/zd:15412) (q:draft, low confidence)
tapongte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:rebels/insurgents) (d:<tapong> with the plural <te>: armed rebels) (b:tapong) (j:tapong/te) (r:zd:14821/zd:19239) (q:draft)
taptung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:hearth/fireplace) (d:the place in the house where the cooking fire is kept) (r:zai:hearth) (q:draft)
target = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/everyday) (w:target) (d:someone or something aimed at or attacked; {Target in nei} is have as a target; the Zolai verb is <ngim>) (o:English) (r:zd:12130/zd:11805) (q:draft, low confidence)
Tarmac = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:tarmac/apron/runway surface) (d:the paved ground of an airport where planes stand and move) (o:English) (r:zd:12693/zd:19912) (q:draft)
tat = (i:4) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:act/behave/conduct oneself) (d:do things or behave in a certain way, mostly as {gam tat}, the two parts of <gamtat> written apart, and before <zia> or <dan>, manner; not the breaking of a cord or the redeeming of the other senses) (s:gamtat) (r:zd:11176/zd:19859/zd:23538) (q:draft)
tatak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (j:taktak) (r:zd:20728/zd:20719/zd:20328) (q:draft)
tatawh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/work) (w:at each/apiece at) (d:the distributive <ta>, each, with <tawh>, with, written as one word after an amount: at that much each, at that rate) (j:ta/tawh) (r:zd:15994/zd:13020) (q:draft, low confidence)
tatdan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:custom/practice/conduct/tradition) (d:the established way in which a people or a person acts, often named together with <ngeina>, culture, and <omdan>, way of life) (r:zd:15794/zd:15652/zd:11714) (q:draft)
taten = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:children) (d:<tate>, children, with the marker <in> shortened to {-n} and written as one word: the children as the ones who do the action) (j:tate/in) (r:zd:21886/zd:24168) (q:draft)
tateu = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:placed after a verb and before <zongin>: even though it really is so, however much; {ahi tateu zongin} is even though it is indeed so) (r:zd:22487/zd:21974) (q:draft, low confidence)
Tatmadaw = (i:1) (t:name) (f:politics) (w:Tatmadaw/Myanmar armed forces) (d:the armed forces of Myanmar, under their Burmese name; with <te> also the soldiers of that army) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:12888/zd:16455) (q:draft)
tatsat loin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:without ceasing/continuously/without a break/incessantly) (d:<tatsat>, break off, and <loin>, without: placed before a verb, the action goes on without stopping; in war news said of shooting and bombing) (r:ts:5635/ts:911/ts:1277) (q:draft)
tatsatlo = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time/everyday) (w:without a break/continuously/nonstop) (d:<tatsat> and <lo> written as one word: without stopping, round the clock) (j:tatsat/lo) (r:zd:18200/zd:20365) (q:draft)
tattoo = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:tattoo) (d:a mark or picture made in the skin with ink) (o:English) (r:zd:12364/zd:22983) (q:draft)
tattung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:pagoda/stupa) (d:a Buddhist pagoda, as the Shwedagon in Yangon; with <milim>, an idol or shrine that is worshipped) (r:zd:22849/zd:17745) (q:draft)
tatzia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:conduct/behaviour/way of acting/practice) (d:the way a person or a people act and behave; often paired as {omzia tatzia}) (r:zd:23394/zd:23008/zd:24304) (q:draft)
tau = (i:2) (t:v) (f:body/health) (w:groan/moan) (d:make low sounds of pain or grief, often after {thum in} and beside <kap>, weep; a verb, not the noun {tau}, altar) (s:atau) (r:zd:23539/zd:22779/zd:24119) (q:draft)
tau = (i:3) (t:n) (f:home/work) (w:platform/stand/booth) (d:a raised structure of any kind, of which the altar is one: a stand on which goods are laid out for sale, a shelter built to rest in, and in {nai tau} a clock tower) (r:zd:22002/zd:17883) (q:draft, low confidence)
Tauleng = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:social) (w:Tauleng) (d:a Zomi village in Chin State, Myanmar; written after the name of a person it says which village the person is from, and {Tauleng Khua Kipawlna} is the association of its people) (r:zd:19273/zd:25562/zd:22138) (q:draft)
Taunggyi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Taunggyi) (d:the capital city of Shan State in Myanmar) (r:zd:15978/zd:10907) (q:draft)
Taungoo = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Taungoo/Toungoo) (d:a city of Bago Region in Myanmar, on the road from Yangon to Nay Pyi Taw) (r:zd:17822/zd:17252) (q:draft)
Taungphila = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Taungphila) (d:a ward of the town of <Kalaymyo>) (o:Burmese) (r:ts:1610/zd:18187) (q:draft)
Taungzalat = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Taungzalat) (d:a quarter of the town of <Kalaymyo>; also in the names of a hotel and a newspaper there) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:21904) (q:draft, low confidence)
tautau = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:on and on/steadily/continually) (d:after a verb of doing, as <leng>, <tai>, <pai>, <hanciam> or <za>: the action keeps going without a break; not the groaning of the other sense) (r:ts:3125/zd:15861/zd:21358) (q:draft)
tavuan la = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/social) (w:take responsibility/take charge) (d:<tavuan>, responsibility, and <la>, take: take on the responsibility or the charge of something; the one who takes it stands before with <in>, and a thing or place taken charge of stands directly before the pair) (r:zd:21876/zd:20486/zd:9266) (q:draft)
Tawau = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Tawau) (d:town and district on the south-east coast of Sabah, Malaysia) (r:zd:17959) (q:draft)
tawdap = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/family) (w:nappy/diaper) (d:the cloth put under the bottom of a baby, from <taw.2>, bottom, and <dap.1>, pad; {nau tawdap} is a baby's nappy) (r:zd:19593/zd:22701) (q:draft)
tawdap = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:underlying basis/underlay) (d:what lies beneath something as its base, said of the heart or mind: {lungsim tawdap} is the underlying state of mind) (r:zd:24977) (q:draft, low confidence)
tawh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:and) (s:leh)
tawh akibang = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:similar to/like/resembling/the same as) (d:<tawh>, with, and <akibang>, that is alike: placed after a noun and before another noun, which is like or resembles the first; before <ahi> <hi>, is the same as) (r:zd:19327/ts:3508) (q:draft)
tawh kibang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be like/be the same as/resemble) (d:<tawh>, with, and <kibang>, alike: placed after a noun, be like it or the same as it; with <lo> it is be unlike) (r:ts:301/zd:23729/zd:23896) (q:draft)
tawh kibangin = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:everyday/social) (w:like/in the same way as/together with) (d:<tawh>, with, and <kibangin>, alike: placed after a noun or pronoun, like it or in the same way as it; in messages of condolence, sharing the grief of the people named before it) (r:zd:22644/zd:25624) (q:draft)
tawh kigamla = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be far from/be distant from/keep away from) (d:<tawh>, with, and <kigamla>, be far apart: the place or person from which there is distance stands before <tawh>, where English says from; with <lo> it means not far from, near) (r:zd:21013/zd:24067/zd:25668) (q:draft)
tawh kimuhna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/media) (w:meeting with/interview with) (d:<tawh>, with, and <kimuhna>, here the noun of <kimu>, meet one another: placed after the name of a person or group, a meeting or interview with them; common as the heading of a report) (r:zd:22595/zd:21372) (q:draft)
tawh kinai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:be near to/be close to) (d:<tawh>, with, and <kinai>, be near: placed after a noun, be near that place or close to that person; where English says near to, Zolai says near with) (r:zd:12487/zd:23935/zd:24119) (q:draft)
tawh kipawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:join with/ally with/side with/associate with) (d:<tawh>, with, and <kipawl>, form one group: placed after the name of a person, group or body, join forces with it, be its ally or partner) (r:zd:22046/zd:15188) (q:draft)
tawh kipelh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be free from/escape from/keep away from/be apart from) (d:<tawh>, with, and <kipelh>, escape or keep away: the thing that is avoided or escaped stands before <tawh>, where English says from and not with) (r:zd:23057/zd:13242/zd:23792) (q:draft)
tawh kisaiin = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:everyday) (w:concerning/regarding/in connection with) (d:<tawh>, with, and <kisaiin>, being related: placed after a noun or noun phrase, about or concerning it; the form with <in> joins the phrase to the verb that follows, while {tawh kisai} stands before a noun or as a heading) (s:tawhkisai) (r:zd:23083/zd:9424) (q:draft)
tawh kiteh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be measured by/be compared with/be judged by) (d:<tawh>, with, and <kiteh>, be measured: placed after a noun that names the standard, be measured, valued or judged by it) (r:zd:26026/zd:22019/zd:21288) (q:draft)
tawh kithuah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:keep company with/associate with/work together with) (d:<tawh>, with, and <kithuah>, be joined: placed after the name of a person or group, be together with them, as a companion or a partner in work; of things, be fitted with) (s:kipawl) (r:zd:12487/zd:9245/ts:3261) (q:draft)
tawh kituak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be in accordance with/suit/fit) (d:<tawh>, with, and <kituak>, agree: placed after a noun, agree with it, fit it or be in keeping with it) (r:zd:24217/zd:21461/zd:23113) (q:draft)
tawh kituakin = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:everyday/social) (w:in accordance with/according to/in keeping with/in proportion to) (d:<tawh>, with, and <kituakin>, fitting: placed after a noun, in a way that fits or matches it, as a law, a custom, a position or an amount) (r:zd:11147/zd:21013/zd:24217) (q:draft)
tawh kizom = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:be connected with/be linked to/contact/keep in touch with) (d:<tawh>, with, and <kizom>, be joined: placed after a noun, be linked to or bound up with it; of persons, be in touch with someone, and as a command, {tawh kizom in}, get in touch with, in notices that give a name or a telephone number; {tawh kizom in} after a matter also means in connection with it) (r:zd:21991/zd:16655/zd:12544) (q:draft)
tawh kizop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:be in contact with/connect with/be linked to) (d:<tawh>, with, and <kizop>, be joined: placed after a noun for a person or body, keep in touch or have dealings with it; {tawh kizop ding} is to get in contact with) (r:zd:19139/zd:15071) (q:draft)
tawh tehna = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:everyday) (w:compared with/in comparison with) (d:<tawh>, with, and <tehna>, measuring: placed after a noun or a number and usually followed by <in>, {tawh tehna in}, compared with that thing; what follows says how the subject differs, often with <zaw>, more) (r:zd:23830/zd:22329/zd:23529) (q:draft)
tawhaa = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:everyday) (w:with/by means of) (d:<tawh>, with, and the linking ending <a> written long and joined to it: with or by something, and so) (j:tawh/aa) (r:zd:19239) (q:draft, low confidence)
tawhding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/travel) (w:to be dug/to dig) (d:the form of <to>, dig, that is used before endings, with <ding> written as one word: that is still to be dug, said of a pit or of a new road) (b:to) (r:zd:16035) (q:draft, low confidence)
tawhin = (i:2) (t:prep) (f:everyday) (w:with/by) (d:<tawh.2>, with, and the ending {-in}, after a noun or after <dan> and <hang>: with, by means of or through; not the kindling of a fire) (s:tawh) (r:zd:20627/zd:25390/zd:19210) (q:draft)
tawhkisai = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:everyday) (w:concerning/about/regarding/related to) (d:<tawh> and <kisai> written as one word, placed after a noun: concerning it, to do with it) (j:tawh/kisai) (r:zd:25928/zd:25917/zd:25916) (q:draft)
tawhkizui = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:in accordance with/according to) (d:<tawh> and <kizui> written as one word after a noun: in keeping with it, according to it) (j:tawh/kizui) (r:zd:25919/zd:15941) (q:draft)
tawhzong = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:everyday) (w:also with/even with/with as well) (d:<tawh>, with, and <zong>, also, written as one word after a noun: with that too, or even with that) (j:tawh/zong) (r:zd:11058/zd:17152/zd:16360) (q:draft)
tawi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:hold/carry/bear) (d:hold or carry in the hand or arms) (s:len) (r:41.9.36) (q:draft)
tawikawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:while holding/while carrying) (d:<tawi>, hold, and <kawm>, while, written as one word: holding or carrying something in the hand or arms while doing something else) (j:tawi/kawm) (r:zd:19583/zd:14917/zd:10929) (q:draft)
tawilo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not hold/not carry/be without) (d:<tawi>, hold or carry, and <lo>, not, written as one word: not carrying something, without it in hand, as {permit tawilo}, holding no permit) (j:tawi/lo) (r:zd:19966/zd:21843/zd:22683) (q:draft)
tawina = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:carrying/bearing/holding) (d:<tawi>, hold or carry, with the noun suffix <na>: the carrying or bearing of something, as in {thau tawina}, the bearing of arms; in {pah tawina} it is the second half of <pahtawina>, honor, written apart) (b:tawi) (r:ts:1485/zd:24165/zd:21302) (q:draft)
tawisang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:lift up/exalt/raise/uphold) (d:<tawi>, hold, with <sang>, high: hold high, raise the standing of a people, a faith or a way of life) (r:zd:17655/zd:21099/zd:8668) (q:draft)
tawitawi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:carry around/keep holding) (d:<tawi>, hold or carry, said twice and written as one word: keep carrying, carry about with one) (b:tawi) (r:zd:11457/zd:11527) (q:draft)
tawldamtak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/health) (w:restfully/at ease/comfortably) (d:<tawldam> and <tak> written as one word, followed by <in>: in a rested and relaxed way) (j:tawldam/tak) (r:zd:21869/zd:15425) (q:draft)
tawlet = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:window) (d:an opening in the wall of a house or ship for light and air; {tawlet panin} is from or through the window) (q:draft)
tawlkhatsung = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:for a while/for some time) (d:<tawlkhat> and <sung> written as one word: for a short time, during a while) (j:tawlkhat/sung) (r:zd:23037/zd:17304/zd:14922) (q:draft)
tawlmahmah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:body/everyday) (w:be very tired/be exhausted) (d:<tawl> and <mahmah> written as one word, the first word here in the meaning be tired: be very tired) (j:tawl/mahmah) (r:zd:15577/zd:20195) (q:draft)
tawlnga = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/body) (w:rest) (d:stop working or moving in order to recover strength) (s:tawldam)
tawlngak hun = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time/work) (w:rest time/break/time off/holiday) (d:<tawlngak>, rest, and <hun>, time: a time of rest, a break in work or school, a holiday; said with verbs such as <la>, <zang> and <pia>) (r:zd:16799/zd:20902) (q:draft)
tawlpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:a good while/quite a while/some time) (d:<tawl>, a while, with <pi>, great: a fairly long stretch of time, in {tawlpi khat}, quite a while, and {tawlpi khat sung}, for quite a while) (r:zd:14824/zd:14780/zd:9235) (q:draft)
tawlpi = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:work/body) (w:wearily/laboriously) (d:<tawl>, be weary, with <pi>: paired with <gimpi> as {gimpi tawlpi-in}, with toil and weariness, wearing oneself out) (r:zd:23590/zd:19816) (q:draft)
tawlpih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:tire oneself for/take trouble over/labour for) (d:<tawl>, be weary, with <pih>: grow tired for someone or over a task, mostly paired with <gimpih> in words of thanks) (s:gimpih) (b:tawl) (r:zd:21421/zd:15527) (q:draft)
tawlpikhat = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:for quite a while/for some time) (d:<tawl>, a while, with the ending for great and <khat>, one: a fairly long while, longer than <tawlkhat>; {tawlpikhat sung} is for quite some time) (r:zd:12904/zd:17117/zd:16247) (q:draft)
tawlpikhatsung = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:for quite a while/for some time) (d:<tawlpikhat>, quite a while, and <sung>, during, written as one word) (j:tawlpikhat/sung) (r:zd:16373/zd:15577/zd:12376) (q:draft)
tawm = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:few/little/small) (d:small in number or amount; {tawm khat} is a little, a few, and {tawm mahmah} very few) (s:tawmno) (a:tam) (q:draft)
tawmbang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:somewhat/a little/roughly) (d:<tawm>, little, and <bang>, like, written as one word: a small amount, to some degree, or about so much) (j:tawm/bang) (r:zd:22065/zd:25915) (q:draft, low confidence)
Tawmging = (i:1) (t:name) (c:beh) (f:family/social) (w:Tawmging) (d:a Zomi clan name; one writer adds <Tawmbing> in brackets beside it) (r:zd:20414) (q:draft, low confidence)
tawmlai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:still few/still little/still young) (d:<tawm>, few, with <lai>, still, written as one word: still small in number or amount; {kum tawmlai} is still young in years) (j:tawm/lai) (r:zd:20889/zd:20167) (q:draft)
tawmlo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:not few/not little/quite a lot) (d:<tawm>, few, and <lo>, not, written as one word: not a small number or amount, considerable) (j:tawm/lo) (r:zd:24043/ts:10463) (q:draft)
tawmmahmah = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:very few/very little) (d:<tawm> and <mahmah> written as one word: very few, very little) (j:tawm/mahmah) (r:zd:14507/zd:20769) (q:draft)
tawmna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:fewness/smallness/scarcity) (d:<tawm>, few, with the noun ending <na>: the being few or small of something, or the place where it is few, the opposite of <tamna>; here <tawm> is not the word for oneself that follows a verb) (a:tamna) (r:zd:24736/zd:20145/zd:23932) (q:draft)
tawmno khat = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:a little/a few/a small amount) (d:<tawmno>, very few, and <khat>, one: a small number or amount of the thing named before it, as {sum tawmno khat}, a little money; also alone, a little) (s:tawmkhat) (r:zd:24007/zd:25919) (q:draft)
tawmpen = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:at least/at the minimum) (d:{a tawmpen} before a number or an amount: not less than that, at least; the adjective sense compares things, this one sets a lower limit) (r:zd:21168/zd:20588/zd:16150) (q:draft)
tawmsemsem = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:become fewer/decrease/grow less) (d:<tawm>, few, with <semsem>, more and more, written as one word: fewer and fewer, less and less) (j:tawm/semsem) (r:zd:13295/zd:20076) (q:draft)
tawmta = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/food) (w:a little each/a little at a time) (d:<tawm>, little, with <ta> in the sense of each: a small amount each time or for each one) (r:zd:21826/zd:24060) (q:draft)
tawmta = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:become few/run low) (d:<tawm>, few or little, with <ta> as the marker of a change that has come about: has become little) (r:zd:17806) (q:draft, low confidence)
tawmtuam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:decrease/become fewer/lessen) (d:become smaller in number or amount than before) (r:zd:11707/zd:25165/zd:17192) (q:draft)
tawmveisung = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:for a short while/within a short time/briefly) (d:<tawmvei>, a short while, with <sung>, within, written as one word: for a short time; {tawmveisung in} is in a short time, quickly) (j:tawmvei/sung) (r:zd:15307/zd:16239) (q:draft)
tawmzaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:less/fewer/smaller/scarcer) (d:<tawm>, few, with <zaw>, more: fewer, less; <sangin> marks what it is compared with) (a:tamzaw) (b:tawm) (q:draft)
tawmzawk = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/health) (w:less/fewer/lower) (d:<tawm>, little, and <zawk>, more, written as one word; the form of <tawmzaw> used before <nadingin> and <leh>: be less, become lower) (j:tawm/zawk) (r:zd:22019/zd:25414) (q:draft)
tawmzawte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:minority/the fewer) (d:<tawmzaw>, fewer, with the plural <te>: those who are fewer, the minority, set against {a tamzaw}, the majority) (b:tawmzaw) (r:zd:22758/zd:10732) (q:draft)
tawndan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:custom/practice/tradition/way of life) (d:the way a people or a body does things by habit, named together with <ngeina>, custom; from <tawn>, follow a way, and <dan>, manner) (r:zd:23893/zd:17213) (q:draft)
tawng = (i:3) (t:v) (f:family/social) (w:scold/rebuke/tell off) (d:speak angry words to someone for a fault, as a parent to a child, without the threat of harm of the other verb sense; often paired with <tai> as {hong tawng hong tai}) (r:zd:20818/zd:12386) (q:draft)
tawngtawng = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:keep threatening/keep quarrelling) (d:<tawng>, threaten, said twice for something that goes on and on; after <ki> it is threaten or quarrel with one another again and again) (b:tawng) (r:zd:25357/zd:23594) (q:draft, low confidence)
tawnlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:not go by way of/not follow) (d:<tawn>, go along a way, and <lo>, not, written as one word: not take that road, bridge or course) (j:tawn/lo) (r:zd:17760/zd:11590) (q:draft)
tawnte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (d:<tawn>, walk along, with the plural <te>: those who walk along a way, those who follow it) (b:tawn) (j:tawn/te) (r:zd:16625/zd:26645) (q:draft)
tawntung = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/time) (w:continuously/nonstop/always/forever) (d:placed after a verb: going on without stopping or without end; {uk tawntung} is reign for ever) (s:paisuak)
tawntung = (i:3) (t:adj) (f:religion/time) (w:eternal/everlasting) (d:placed before a noun, not after a verb: lasting for ever, as in <tawntung nuntakna>, eternal life, and {tawntung sihna}, eternal death; {tawntung ading} is for ever) (r:zd:25620/zd:11022) (q:draft)
tawntung nuntakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:eternal life/everlasting life) (d:<tawntung>, forever, and <nuntakna>, life: eternal life, the Christian term; the object of <ngah>, <nei> and <pia>, receive, have and give) (r:zd:21121/zd:25484) (q:draft)
tawp = (i:4) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:utmost/best/limit) (d:the furthest point of what can be done, after <theih> or <hihtheih>; {a hihtheih tawp} is the best one can do and {a hoih theih tawp in} is as well as it can) (r:zd:16797/zd:16312) (q:draft)
tawp = (i:5) (t:n) (f:time) (w:end) (d:the point where something ends, as a noun after <a> and before <dong>, until; {a pat pan a tawp dong} is from the beginning to the end) (r:zd:15637) (q:draft, low confidence)
tawp dong = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:to the end/until the end/to the last) (d:<tawp>, end, and <dong>, until: mostly as {a tawp dong} or {a tawp dong in}, right to the end, said of work, effort or endurance that does not stop before the finish; <dong> here is not ask) (r:zd:17488/zd:17055/zd:17955) (q:draft)
tawpdong = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:to the end/until the end) (d:<tawp>, end, and <dong>, until, written as one word, mostly as {a tawpdong}: right to the end) (j:tawp/dong) (r:zd:23590/zd:16340) (q:draft)
tawpna ah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:finally/in the end/at last) (d:<tawpna>, end, and <ah>, at: with <a> before it, {a tawpna ah}, at its end, begins a sentence and means in the end, finally) (r:zd:23616/zd:16951/zd:20818) (q:draft)
tawpni = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:last day/closing date/deadline) (d:<tawp> with <ni>: the last day of something, also the closing date for a list or registration; {ni tawpni} is the last of days) (r:zd:25937/zd:12336) (q:draft)
tawpsan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:give up/quit/abandon/stop) (d:<tawp>, stop, with the ending {-san}, leaving behind: stop doing something and leave it, give up a work, a habit or an effort) (r:zd:22807/zd:22711/zd:12023) (q:draft)
tawsat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:caning/stroke of the cane) (d:<taw>, bottom, with <sat>, beat: a beating on the buttocks with a cane, given as a punishment by a court; as a verb, punish by beating, also said of God) (r:zd:14505/zd:15484) (q:draft)
tawsawn = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:urge/encourage/spur on/exhort) (d:push a person on to act, by words or by example; {hong tawsawn} is it urges us) (r:zd:15324/zd:23822/zd:13076) (q:draft)
tawsawnna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:urging/prompting/instigation/impetus) (d:<tawsawn>, push on or urge, with the noun suffix <na>: the pushing of a person to do something, for good or for bad) (b:tawsawn) (r:zd:24418/zd:10730/zd:11024) (q:draft)
tawt = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:health/body) (w:blind/go blind) (d:form of <taw>, blind, said of the eyes and used before a following word, as in {mit a tawt hangin}, although his eyes were blind) (b:taw) (r:zd:9231) (q:draft, low confidence)
tax = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/politics) (w:tax) (d:money that people and businesses must pay to the government; {tax pia} is pay tax) (s:siah) (o:English) (r:zd:24742/zd:15586) (q:draft)
taxes = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/politics) (w:taxes/tax) (d:the English plural of <tax>, used in Zolai sentences for tax in general; {taxes pia} is pay tax and {taxes khangsak} is raise taxes) (s:siah) (b:tax) (o:English) (r:zd:23982/zd:24006) (q:draft)
Taxi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:taxi/cab) (o:English) (r:zd:15636/zd:16148/zd:11308) (q:draft)
tazong = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:family) (w:children also/and children) (d:<ta> child and <zong> also written as one word, mostly before a number: and also has so many children) (j:ta/zong) (r:zd:12470/zd:11540) (q:draft)
TB = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:tuberculosis/TB) (d:the lung disease tuberculosis, mostly as {TB natna}) (o:English) (r:zd:12752/zd:14740) (q:draft)
TBA = (i:1) (t:name) (f:religion) (w:Tedim Baptist Association/TBA) (d:abbreviation used as the name of the Tedim Baptist Association, an association of Baptist churches in the Tedim area formed in 1948) (r:zd:24595/zd:24068) (q:draft)
TCF = (i:1) (t:name) (f:religion) (w:TCF) (d:abbreviation used for more than one church fellowship, among them Tedim Christian Fellowship, Tonzang Christian Fellowship and Tauleng Christian Fellowship) (r:zd:25240/zd:12039) (q:draft, low confidence)
Teachers = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:teachers) (d:English plural used in news writing for the teachers of a school, usually followed by the plural <te>) (o:English) (r:zd:20572/zd:13343) (q:draft, low confidence)
team = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/work) (w:team) (d:a group of people who play or work together, as a sports side, a rescue team or a gospel team) (o:English) (r:zd:17674/zd:16556/zd:19080) (q:draft)
teamte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/social) (w:teams/team/team members) (d:the English word team with the plural <te>, written as one word: the teams, or the people of one team) (o:English, team) (r:zd:20730/zd:22888) (q:draft)
teamwork = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/social) (w:teamwork) (d:working together as a team, in sport and in any shared work) (o:English) (r:zd:21761/zd:22171) (q:draft)
tebang = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:such as/for instance) (d:the plural <te> and <bang> like written as one word after a noun: the likes of these, these for instance; it picks out one group as an example or for emphasis) (j:te/bang) (r:zd:19644/zd:23784) (q:draft)
tebek = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:only those/only) (d:the plural <te> and <bek> written as one word, placed after a noun or clause: only those, they alone) (j:te/bek) (r:zd:15274/zd:23479/zd:22856) (q:draft)
tebel = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:the plural <te> and <bel> written as one word after a noun: as for those, marking a group as the topic, often in contrast with others; <bel> here means as for, not most) (j:te/bel) (r:zd:15606/zd:15187/zd:16720) (q:draft)
Tebrau = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Tebrau) (d:an area of Johor Bahru in Malaysia, also the name of a main road there) (r:zd:21341/zd:19197) (q:draft)
technical = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:work/education) (w:technical) (d:English word placed before a Zolai noun, as in {technical pilna}, technical knowledge; most often it stands inside English names and terms) (o:English) (r:zd:20007/zd:20041) (q:draft, low confidence)
Technician = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:technician) (d:a person trained to work with machines or laboratory equipment; mostly written with a capital) (o:English) (r:zd:15103/zd:21554) (q:draft)
