teek = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/family) (w:old/aged) (d:advanced in years, said of people; also as a verb, grow old) (s:ham/khangham) (a:khangno) (r:1.18.11) (q:draft)
Teeklui = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel) (w:Teeklui) (d:a village near Tedim in Chin State, Myanmar) (r:zd:14992/zd:22444) (q:draft)
teekte = (i:2) (t:n) (f:family) (w:parents-in-law/in-laws) (d:the father and mother of the spouse, chiefly what a wife calls the parents of her husband, with a possessive as in {na teekte}; named beside the own <nu leh pa>, mother and father) (r:zd:26953/zd:19593/zd:24176) (q:draft)
teekte = (i:3) (t:n) (f:home) (w:owners/householders/hosts) (d:after <inn>, house: {inn teekte}, the owners of a house or the hosts with whom one stays, the plural of <innteek> written as two words) (r:zd:22827/zd:14946) (q:draft, low confidence)
