zadah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:dislike/resent/detest/take offence at) (d:<za>, hear, with <dah>: be displeased at what one hears or meets with, dislike it strongly) (s:mudah) (r:zd:23361/zd:23428/zd:19898) (q:draft)
zaha = (i:2) (t:n) (f:health) (w:medicine/medical supplies) (d:echo word that stands only after <zatui>, medicine: <zatui zaha> is medicines and medical supplies of every kind; not the adverb of amount) (r:zd:25189/zd:12541/zd:23848) (q:draft)
zahaa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:medicine/remedy) (d:said after <zatui> in the pair {zatui zahaa}, medicines and remedies of every kind) (r:zd:16038/zd:22584) (q:draft, low confidence)
Zahau = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:social/politics) (w:Zahau) (d:a Chin people and their former chiefdom in the Falam area of the Chin Hills; also used as a family name) (r:ts:3168/zd:18081) (q:draft, low confidence)
zahding = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/work) (w:amount to be/extent to be) (d:<zah>, amount, and <ding>, will, written as one word, after a verb or noun: the amount or extent that will be or ought to be, as how much something will cost, how long a prison term will be, or as much as the body needs) (j:zah/ding) (r:zd:19906/zd:12140/zd:25914) (q:draft)
zahdong = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:to the extent that/so much that/to such a degree) (d:<zah>, amount, and <dong>, until, written as one word after a clause: to the point that, so much that what is named happens) (j:zah/dong) (r:zd:21690/zd:26097) (q:draft)
zahdongin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:to the point that/so much that/to the extent of) (d:<zah>, amount, and <dongin>, up to, written as one word after a clause: so much that, to the degree that what the clause says comes about) (j:zah/dongin) (r:zd:20545/zd:19427) (q:draft)
zahkhat = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:equally/likewise/at the same time) (d:<zah>, amount, and <khat>, one, written as one word: to the same degree; {tua zahkhat in} is just as much, likewise, at the same time) (j:zah/khat) (r:zd:17060/zd:14696) (q:draft, low confidence)
zahkhatin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:inasmuch as/just as/likewise) (d:<zahkhat> and <in> written as one word: after a clause, to the same degree as, since; {tua zahkhatin} is likewise) (j:zahkhat/in) (r:zd:22709/zd:21279) (q:draft)
zahkhop = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:to the point of/enough to/so much that) (d:<zah>, amount, with <khop>, enough, written as one word after a verb or clause: to such a degree that, enough for it; often followed by <ding> or <dingin>) (j:zah/khop) (r:ts:1796/zd:20125) (q:draft)
zahlak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:be put to shame/be embarrassed/be disgraced) (d:be shamed before others, lose face; {zahlak takin} is shamefully) (r:zd:20032/zd:19139/zd:23907) (q:draft)
zahmawh = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body/social) (w:private parts/genitals/sex organ) (d:the private parts of the body; before another noun, to do with sex: {zahmawh video} is a pornographic video and {zahmawh natna} a venereal disease) (r:zd:24202/zd:22808) (q:draft)
zahmawhvai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:sexual matter/indecency/sexual abuse) (d:<zahmawh> with <vai>, matter, written as one word: sexual matters, in news mostly of sexual offences; {zahmawhvai tawh bawlsia} is abuse sexually) (j:zahmawh/vai) (r:zd:20416/zd:20482) (q:draft)
zahsang = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:more than/than the amount) (d:<zah>, amount, with <sang> in the sense than, written as one word: than the amount that is needed, hoped for or owned; compare <sangin>) (j:zah/sang) (r:zd:20071/zd:21219) (q:draft)
zahtaak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (j:zahtak) (r:zd:25923/zd:24123/ts:11679) (q:draft)
zahtaakhuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:social) (j:zahtakhuai) (r:zd:11400/zd:20862) (q:draft)
zahtaakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (j:zahtakna) (r:zd:26565/zd:23148/zd:25165) (q:draft)
zahtak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:respect/honor) (d:show respect or honor to a person, such as parents, elders or rulers) (s:zaktak/pahtawi/zahtakbawl) (a:simmawh/zahko) (q:draft)
zahtakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:respect/honour/reverence) (d:the respect or honor shown to a person) (s:kihtakna/pahtawina) (a:simmawhna/zahkona) (b:zahtak) (q:draft)
zahtakna lianpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:great respect/deep respect) (d:<zahtakna>, respect, and <lianpi>, great: mostly in the formula {zahtakna lianpi tawh}, with great respect, respectfully, by which an invitation, announcement or word of thanks is made) (r:zd:15379/zd:11340) (q:draft)
zahtaksak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:respect/honor/treat with respect) (d:<zahtak>, respect, with the ending <sak>: hold a person, a custom or a thing in respect) (b:zahtak) (r:zd:25824/zd:24963) (q:draft)
zahtaksiam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/family) (w:know how to respect/be respectful) (d:<zahtak>, respect, and <siam>, skilled, written as one word: be good at showing respect) (j:zahtak/siam) (r:zd:9448) (q:draft)
zahtampi = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/religion) (w:many times as much/manifold) (d:<zah> and <tampi> written as one word; {a zahtampi in} is many times over, said in the blessing that God may repay a giver many times what was given) (j:zah/tampi) (r:zd:21664) (q:draft)
zaih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/everyday) (w:photograph/film/shoot/record) (d:take a picture or record a film with a camera; {man zaih} is take a photograph and {Video zaih} is record a video) (r:zd:20859/zd:15125/zd:16101) (q:draft)
zaihin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/it) (w:record/film/photograph) (d:<zaih> and <in> written as one word: having filmed, photographed or recorded something, said before what is then done with it) (j:zaih/in) (r:zd:15019/zd:20008/zd:21627) (q:draft)
zaihkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/it) (w:record/film/capture on camera) (d:<zaih>, record or film, with <kha>: happen to record on video or get on camera; {Video ki zaihkha} is was caught on video) (j:zaih/kha) (r:zd:18083/zd:20738) (q:draft)
zaihkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/social) (w:photograph together/record together) (d:<zaih>, take a picture, and <khawm>, together, written as one word; {ki zaihkhawm} is have a photo taken together, or be recorded at the same time) (j:zaih/khawm) (r:zd:21837/zd:19536) (q:draft)
zaihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/it/health) (w:filming/photographing/recording/imaging) (d:<zaih>, photograph or film, with the noun suffix <na>: the taking of a picture, video or scan, and also the device that takes it) (b:zaih) (r:zd:17115/zd:14795/zd:20408) (q:draft)
zaihpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media) (w:cameraman/person filming) (d:<zaih> and <pa> written as one word: the man who films or photographs something) (j:zaih/pa) (r:zd:20767) (q:draft)
zaihpah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media) (w:film at once/photograph at once/record immediately) (d:<zaih> and <pah> written as one word: take a photograph or record a video at once) (j:zaih/pah) (r:zd:14694/zd:13041) (q:draft)
zaihpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:media) (w:the one who filmed/the taking of a photo) (d:<zaih>, photograph or film, and <pen> written as one word: the taking of a photo or video as the topic of the sentence, or the person who took it; {Video zaihpen in genkhia hi} is the one who filmed the video said) (j:zaih/pen) (r:zd:12267/zd:16365) (q:draft, low confidence)
zaihsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/health) (w:photograph/film/scan) (d:take a photo, a video or a medical scan of someone or something: <zaih>, record an image, with <sak>) (r:zd:17694/zd:16133/zd:14597) (q:draft)
zaihsim = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/it) (w:film secretly/photograph secretly) (d:<zaih>, take a picture or record a film, done in secret and without the knowledge or permission of the person filmed) (b:zaih) (r:zd:12444) (q:draft)
zaihsimsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/social) (w:film secretly/record without consent) (d:<zaihsim>, film in secret, with a further ending: take a photograph or video of someone without that person knowing) (b:zaih) (r:zd:16696) (q:draft)
zaila = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/religion) (w:song/hymn) (d:word of songs and festive writing for a song; {zaila awi} is sing songs) (s:la) (r:zd:21170/zd:17215) (q:draft)
zaitak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/social) (w:broadly/widely/broad-mindedly) (d:<zai>, wide, with <tak>, which makes an adverb: in a broad way, with a broad mind) (j:zai/tak) (r:zd:19316/zd:24275) (q:draft)
zakang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/politics) (w:heroin/white narcotic) (d:<za>, drug, with <kang>, white: heroin, named beside <zavom>, black drug, opium; also said of other white narcotic powders) (r:zd:10797/zd:25532) (q:draft)
zakbeh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/everyday) (w:hear further/learn in addition) (d:<zak>, hear, and <beh>, in addition, written as one word: hear more about a matter; in news, {ki zakbeh} is it is further reported, usually after the name of the source) (j:zak/beh) (r:zd:15447/zd:17538/zd:16885) (q:draft)
zakbehna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media) (w:further news/further report/update) (d:<zak>, hear, <beh>, here in addition, and the noun suffix <na>: what is heard further about a matter; {zakbehna aomleh} is if more is heard, the usual close of a news report) (r:zd:11625/zd:11532/zd:13326) (q:draft)
zakciangin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:when one hears/on hearing) (d:<zak>, hear, and <ciangin>, when, written as one word: when someone hears or heard something) (j:zak/ciangin) (r:zd:21869/zd:16983) (q:draft)
zakdah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:dislike/resent/take offence at) (d:form of <zadah>, dislike what one hears, used before endings and other words such as <leh>, <huai> and <uh>) (b:zadah) (r:zd:25063/zd:23090) (q:draft)
Zakhai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people/land) (f:politics/social) (w:Rakhine/Arakan) (d:the Rakhine people and their land on the west coast of Myanmar; {Zakhai gam} is Rakhine State) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:22641/zd:16336/zd:22072) (q:draft)
Zakhaite = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:politics/social) (w:Rakhine people/the Rakhine) (d:<Zakhai> with the plural ending <te>: the Rakhine people of Myanmar) (b:Zakhai) (r:zd:24120) (q:draft)
zakhang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/social) (w:be promoted/rise in rank) (d:<za>, rank, with <khang>, rise: be raised to a higher rank or office, also the promotion itself; {zakhang sak} is promote someone) (r:zd:22312/zd:19969) (q:draft)
zakhu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:tobacco smoke/cigarette smoke) (d:the smoke of tobacco, from <za>, tobacco, and <khu>, smoke) (r:zd:21006/zd:15286) (q:draft)
zakngei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have heard before/have ever heard) (d:<zak>, hear, and <ngei>, ever, written as one word) (j:zak/ngei) (r:zd:15528/zd:15861) (q:draft)
zaknop = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:everyday/media) (w:pleasant to hear/enjoyable to listen to) (d:said of speech, a story or music itself, not of the hearer's wish: pleasant to listen to; {zaknop sa} and {zaknop kisa} are find it pleasant to hear) (r:zd:20673/zd:20587/zd:21925) (q:draft)
Zakoh = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (f:religion) (w:Jacob/James) (d:a spelling of the Bible name <Jakob> used by some writers, for the patriarch Jacob and for the letter of James; also a personal name) (r:zd:22827/zd:16833) (q:draft, low confidence)
zaksakding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:to inform/will inform/to make known) (d:<zaksak>, cause to hear or tell, and <ding>, will or to, written as one word) (j:zaksak/ding) (r:zd:11445/zd:19059) (q:draft)
zaksakna nei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/politics) (w:issue a notice/make an announcement/give a warning) (d:<zaksakna>, announcement, and <nei>, have: make an announcement, issue a notice or warning, said of an authority; what is announced stands before it, often as words ending in {ci'n}, saying, and the people addressed stand before that) (r:ts:9579/zd:17439) (q:draft)
zakzak = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:to and fro/about/back and forth) (d:after a verb of movement, not from <zak>, hear: with quick movement that goes on to and fro, as in {phiasak zakzak}, keep waving, and {vak zakzak}, scurry about) (r:zd:13009/zd:20490) (q:draft, low confidence)
zalaih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/work) (w:succeed/take over the office of/replace) (d:take the place of another in a rank or office, from <za.2>, office, and <laih>, replace; {a zalaih} is his successor) (j:za/laih) (r:zd:25203/zd:11053) (q:draft)
Zalen = (i:1) (t:name) (f:media) (w:Zalen) (d:a Chin news outlet of Myanmar, named as the source of reports) (r:zd:19213/zd:19624) (q:draft)
zalian = (i:2) (t:n) (f:work/politics) (w:senior officer/high official/officer) (d:a person who holds high rank, not the rank itself; often after <galkap> or before <khat>, as in {galkap zalian khat}, a senior army officer) (s:ulian) (r:zd:25314/zd:23198) (q:draft)
zalo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/body) (w:not hear/unheard) (d:<za>, hear, with the negative <lo>, written as one word: not hear, not have heard of; {khua zalo} is deaf) (j:za/lo) (r:zd:16892/zd:13328) (q:draft)
zalom = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:century) (d:a hundred together; {kum zalom} is a century, and a number after it counts the centuries: {kum zalom 21} is the 21st century) (r:zd:25099/zd:22371/zd:16254) (q:draft)
Zalui = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel/nature) (w:Zalui) (d:a place and stream in the Tedim area, named as a source of water and of hydroelectric power for the town) (r:zd:21259/zd:22584) (q:draft, low confidence)
zam card = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:ZAM card/ZAM membership card) (d:the initials {ZAM} of the Zomi Association of Malaysia and <card>: the membership card of that association, written {ZAM Card}, asked for beside the UN card in notices to Zomi refugees in Malaysia) (r:zd:19320/zd:12695) (q:draft)
ZAM Thupuak = (i:1) (t:name) (f:media) (w:ZAM News/ZAM bulletin) (d:ZAM, an association of Zomi in Malaysia, and <thupuak>, news: title of the news bulletin of that association, offered as a PDF file) (r:zd:19320) (q:draft, low confidence)
zam zum = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:ZAM office) (d:ZAM, the Zomi Association of Malaysia, and <zum>, office: the office of that association, where members come for help, forms and cards; written {ZAM zum}) (r:zd:22652/zd:23400) (q:draft)
zan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:night) (d:the dark part of the day, the opposite of <sun>, day; {sun leh zan} is day and night and {zan khat} is one night) (a:sun)
zanah = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/everyday) (w:tobacco) (d:tobacco, the leaf that is smoked or chewed) (r:zd:15237) (q:draft)
zanciang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:at night/by night) (d:<zan>, night, and <ciang>, when, written as one word: at night, when night comes; set against {sun ciang}, by day) (j:zan/ciang) (r:zd:12510/zd:16038/zd:14985) (q:draft)
zandiak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time/media) (w:recently/the other day/just lately) (d:a short time ago, in the last few days; often {zandiak in} or {zandiak mahmah in}, only very recently) (r:zd:23361/zd:25824) (q:draft)
zanga = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:using/by using/with) (d:<zang>, use, written together with the linking <a>: using a thing or a power to do what follows, as in {thuneihna zanga}, using authority; not the number five hundred) (r:zd:14552/zd:21044/zd:9254) (q:draft)
zangden = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:use regularly/keep using/always use) (d:<zang>, use, and <den>, always, written as one word: use something all the time or on a regular basis) (j:zang/den) (r:zd:14555/zd:15445) (q:draft)
zangding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:will use/to use/to spend) (d:<zang>, use, and <ding> for what is to come, written as one word: will use or spend, in order to use; {hunnuam zangding} is to spend a pleasant time) (j:zang/ding) (r:zd:12364/zd:20481/zd:22553) (q:draft)
zangdingin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:in order to use/in order to spend) (d:<zang> and <dingin> written as one word: in order to use something or to spend time; {hunnuam zangdingin} is to spend a holiday) (j:zang/dingin) (r:zd:17100/zd:12444) (q:draft)
zangei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have heard/have ever heard) (d:<za>, hear, with <ngei>, ever, written as one word: have heard before; with <keng> or <lo>, have never heard) (j:za/ngei) (r:zd:17162/zd:16291/zd:24496) (q:draft)
zanggam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature/travel) (w:plain/plains/lowland) (d:level land as a <gam>, country: the plains, set against {mualtung gam}, the hill country; in news the lowland of Myanmar or the valley of Manipur) (r:ts:1428/ts:3375/zd:26708) (q:draft)
zangh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (j:zang) (r:zd:19159/zd:24068/zd:10761) (q:draft)
zanghlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not use) (d:<zangh> and <lo> written as one word: does not use, without using) (j:zangh/lo) (r:zd:23441/zd:23476) (q:draft)
zanghthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (j:zangthei) (r:zd:21279/zd:19816) (q:draft)
zangiak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:spend the night/stay overnight) (d:<zan>, night, and <giak>, lodge, written as one word: stay somewhere for the night) (j:zan/giak) (r:zd:17632/ts:2942) (q:draft)
zangkei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not use/do not use) (d:<zang> and the negative <kei> written as one word: do not use, not using) (j:zang/kei) (r:zd:24276/zd:20917) (q:draft)
zangkhia = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/education) (w:put to use/apply/practise) (d:bring out and make use of what one has or has learned, such as a skill, a custom or knowledge, with no thought of it running out; often after {sin in}, having learned) (r:zd:24060/zd:15853) (q:draft)
zangkhial = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:misuse/use wrongly/abuse) (d:<zang>, use, with <khial>, wrong: use something in a wrong way or for a wrong purpose) (j:zang/khial) (r:zd:13305/zd:9434/zd:20875) (q:draft)
Zangkong = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Yangon/Rangoon) (d:the Zolai name of Yangon, the largest city of Myanmar) (s:Yangon) (r:zd:22941/zd:16288) (q:draft)
Zangkung = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Yangon/Rangoon) (d:Zolai name of Yangon, the largest city and former capital of Myanmar) (r:zd:20176/zd:19239) (q:draft)
zangleng = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:if one uses) (d:<zang>, use, and the conditional <leng> written as one word: if I or we use, when one uses) (j:zang/leng) (r:zd:23049/zd:25824) (q:draft)
zangnawnlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:no longer use/not use any more) (d:<zang> and <nawnlo> written as one word: no longer use) (j:zang/nawnlo) (r:zd:11587/zd:16408) (q:draft)
zangsaklo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not let use/not allow to use) (d:<zangsak>, let use, and <lo>, not, written as one word: not allow someone to use a thing) (j:zangsak/lo) (r:zd:15260/zd:11941) (q:draft)
zangsiam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:use well/make good use of/use skilfully) (d:<zang> and <siam> written as one word: use a thing, a time or a skill well) (j:zang/siam) (r:zd:19455/zd:20125) (q:draft)
zangta = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:now use/have come to use) (d:<zang>, use, with <ta>, which marks what has now come about; as a word of songs and of a dance, {zangta lam}, its meaning is not determined) (b:zang) (r:zd:22446/zd:15324) (q:draft)
zangtam = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:nature) (w:flat/level) (d:of land, flat and even; {zangtam sak} is make level) (r:zd:23198) (q:draft, low confidence)
zangtheiding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/it) (w:will be able to use/can be used) (d:<zangthei> and <ding> written as one word: will be able to use; after <ki> it is passive, can be used) (j:zangthei/ding) (r:zd:16302/zd:11768/zd:20095) (q:draft)
zangtheilo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:cannot use/be unable to use) (d:<zang>, use, and <theilo>, unable, written as one word: cannot use; after <ki> cannot be used, be out of use) (j:zang/theilo) (r:zd:12357/zd:11725) (q:draft)
zangtuam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:be lighter/be relieved/feel lighter) (d:become lighter, less heavy; of the mind, feel relieved, as in {lungsim zangtuam}) (r:zd:22779/zd:21142) (q:draft, low confidence)
Zangtui = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel/social) (w:Zangtui) (d:apparently a village of the Zomi area: written after personal names as the home village and named in a traditional song) (r:ts:301) (q:draft, low confidence)
zanguh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:use/employ) (d:<zang>, use, and the plural marker <uh> written as one word: they use) (j:zang/uh) (r:zd:19390/zd:11135) (q:draft)
zangvetlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not use at all/never use) (d:<zang> and <vetlo> written as one word: not use a thing at all) (j:zang/vetlo) (r:zd:22983/zd:20000) (q:draft)
zangzang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:keep using/use all along) (d:<zang>, use, said twice: go on using, have been using all along) (r:zd:21925/zd:24068) (q:draft, low confidence)
zangzang = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:continually/on and on) (d:placed after a verb: the action goes on without stopping, as singing or the flowing of tears) (r:zd:11135/zd:16121) (q:draft, low confidence)
zanhun = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:night time/night) (d:<zan>, night, and <hun>, time, written as one word: the time of night, which follows {nitakhun}, the evening) (j:zan/hun) (r:zd:24231/zd:19381) (q:draft)
zanitak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:last night/yesterday evening) (d:the evening of <zani>, yesterday; {a zanitak in} is on the evening before) (r:zd:23249/zd:17583) (q:draft)
zankhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:one night/a night) (d:<zan>, night, and <khat>, one, written as one word: a single night; {zankhat thu in} is overnight, in one night) (j:zan/khat) (r:zd:17426/zd:18046) (q:draft)
zankhatthu = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:overnight/in one night) (d:<zankhat> and <thu> written as one word, followed by <in>: in a single night, overnight) (j:zankhat/thu) (r:zd:20276/zd:19176) (q:draft)
zankhuamial = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time/nature) (w:dark of night/night darkness) (d:<zan> and <khuamial> written as one word: the darkness of night, the time when night has fallen dark) (j:zan/khuamial) (r:zd:17187/zd:19826) (q:draft)
zankim = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:midnight) (d:<zan>, night, with <kim>, half: the middle of the night; {zankim lai takin} is right at midnight) (a:sunkim)
zankimlam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:around midnight/late at night) (d:<zankim>, midnight, and <lam>, toward, written as one word: the time around midnight, the late night hours; {zankimlam in} is around midnight) (j:zankim/lam) (r:zd:11081/zd:15896/zd:19164) (q:draft)
zanlam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:night/night-time/at night) (d:<zan>, night, with <lam>, side: the night part of the day; after the name of a day, on the night of that day, and before a clock time, at night) (r:zd:11899/zd:12464/zd:17551) (q:draft)
zanmah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:that very night/the same night) (d:<zan>, night, and <mah>, the very, written as one word: on that very night) (j:zan/mah) (r:zd:20131/zd:11717) (q:draft)
zanni = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time/everyday) (w:yesterday) (d:the day before today; with <in>, {zanni-in}, it tells when something happened) (q:draft)
zannitak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:last night/yesterday evening) (d:<zan> and <nitak> written as one word: in the evening or night of yesterday) (j:zan/nitak) (r:ts:7320/zd:19176) (q:draft)
zanpuan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:blanket/bedcover) (d:a cloth to cover oneself with when sleeping, <zan>, night, with <puan>, cloth) (r:zd:21826/zd:26411/zd:19826) (q:draft)
zansim = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:every night/nightly/night after night) (d:<zan>, night, with <sim>, each, built like <nisim>, every day: every night, often followed by <in>) (r:zd:12510/zd:18241) (q:draft)
zantawh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:by night/at night) (d:<zan>, night, and <tawh>, with, written as one word; found in the pair {suntawh zantawh}, day and night, without a break) (j:zan/tawh) (r:zd:20997/zd:21869/zd:14652) (q:draft)
zantha = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:all night/through the night) (d:found only in {zantha pai}, also divided {zan thapai}: right through the night, late into the night without sleep) (r:zd:20945/zd:24231) (q:draft, low confidence)
zanvak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:carolling/Christmas carol singing) (d:going round at night at Christmas to sing and bring greetings; {zanvak la} is a Christmas carol) (r:zd:26097/zd:16506) (q:draft, low confidence)
zanzan = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (d:placed after a verb, often with <peuh> before it: just, readily, without much thought, as people are apt to do or say) (r:zd:25749/zd:20594) (q:draft, low confidence)
zasakkhin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/everyday) (w:have informed/have notified) (d:<zasak>, inform, and <khin>, already, written as one word; after <ki> it is passive, {ki zasakkhin}, has been informed) (j:zasak/khin) (r:zd:20263/zd:14738) (q:draft)
zasakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/social) (w:announcement/notice/notification) (d:<zasak>, make known, with the noun ending {-na}: an announcement; {zasakna nei} is make an announcement) (b:zasak) (r:ts:5635/zd:15629/zd:17344) (q:draft)
zasakpah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:inform at once/notify immediately/report at once) (d:<zasak>, inform, and <pah>, at once, written as one word: let someone know straight away, said mostly of calling the police or an ambulance) (j:zasak/pah) (r:zd:12490/zd:12488/zd:12040) (q:draft)
zasaksawn = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/social) (w:pass on/inform/let others know) (d:<zasak>, inform, and <sawn>, on, written as one word: pass news on to others, let someone know) (j:zasak/sawn) (r:zd:14694/zd:17872/zd:15180) (q:draft)
zasan = (i:2) (t:n) (f:food) (w:chilli/chili pepper/hot pepper) (d:the hot red fruit eaten as a vegetable and spice, named with dishes and other vegetables and with <meh>, <thak> and <khum>; not the red paint of a house) (r:zd:21048/zd:20851) (q:draft)
zatam = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:many/countless/multitude of) (d:<za> hundred with <tam> many, placed after a noun: very many, in their hundreds; a word of songs and elevated style, as in {mi zatam}, the multitude of people) (r:zd:9429/zd:22962) (q:draft, low confidence)
zatampi = (i:1) (t:num) (f:everyday) (w:hundreds/many hundreds) (d:<za>, hundred, and <tampi> written as one word: several hundred, hundreds of) (j:za/tampi) (r:zd:16367/zd:16840) (q:draft)
zatamte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:the many/multitudes) (d:<zatam>, very many, with the plural <te>: the many, as in {mi zatamte}, the many people; a word of songs and elevated style) (b:zatam) (r:zd:24253/zd:16038) (q:draft)
zatang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:pill/tablet) (d:medicine in the form of a small solid grain that is swallowed, set against <zatui>, liquid medicine) (r:zd:21664/zd:22151/zd:20908) (q:draft)
zatangte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:pills/tablets) (d:plural of <zatang>: medicine in the form of pills or tablets) (b:zatang) (r:zd:24276/zd:21239) (q:draft)
zatcing = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/work) (w:efficient/economical) (d:of money or resources, used well so that they go a long way and suffice) (r:zd:15972/zd:17409) (q:draft, low confidence)
zatdan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:way of using/use/usage) (d:<zat>, use, with <dan>, way: how something is used or is to be used; {sum zatdan} is how to use money) (s:zatzia/zatna) (r:zd:21991/zd:17344/zd:15857) (q:draft)
zatding = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/work) (w:to use/for use/to be used) (d:<zat>, use, and <ding>, the marker of what is to come, written as one word: that is to be used, for use; {zatding sum} is money to spend) (j:zat/ding) (r:zd:20917/zd:12420) (q:draft)
zatdingin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:to use/for use/in order to use) (d:<zat>, use, and <dingin>, in order to, written as one word: for use, to be used, to be observed) (j:zat/dingin) (r:zd:17822/zd:20254/zd:22707) (q:draft)
zateep = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/everyday) (w:cigarette/cigar/tobacco) (d:tobacco rolled for smoking, a cigarette or cigar; {zateep teep} is smoke a cigarette) (r:zd:10929/zd:20764) (q:draft)
zatep = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/everyday) (w:tobacco/cigarette/smoking) (d:tobacco that is smoked, a cigarette; {zatep tep} is to smoke) (r:zd:12774/zd:22734/zd:13112) (q:draft)
zatepding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/everyday) (w:smoke/smoking) (d:<zatep>, tobacco or smoking, with <ding>, written as one word: to smoke, the act of smoking that is to happen) (j:zatep/ding) (r:zd:15822/zd:17301) (q:draft)
zatepna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:smoking/tobacco smoking) (d:the act or habit of smoking tobacco; <zatep>, smoke tobacco, with the noun ending {-na}) (r:zd:24276/zd:16259/zd:12746) (q:draft)
zathuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:worth using/fit to use/useful) (d:<zat>, use, with <huai>, worthy of: good or proper to use; {zathuai lo} is not fit to be used) (b:zat) (r:zd:23780/zd:21032/zd:22136) (q:draft)
zatkhialhna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:misuse/abuse/wrong use) (d:<zat>, use, with <khialhna>, wrong: using something wrongly, misuse) (r:zd:22543/zd:24217) (q:draft)
zatkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:spend/use up/put to use) (d:<zat>, use, with <khiat>, out: spend money or put something to use; {sum zatkhiat na} is spending, expenditure) (j:zat/khiat) (r:zd:25928/zd:25916) (q:draft)
zatkhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/everyday) (w:spending/expenditure/use/consumption) (d:<zatkhiat>, spend or put to use, with the noun suffix {-na}: the spending of money or the using of strength and other things) (b:zatkhiat) (r:zd:25916/zd:23198) (q:draft)
zatkhop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:use together/share) (d:<zat>, use, and <khop>, together, written as one word: use or have in common, share with others) (j:zat/khop) (r:zd:9449/zd:24217/zd:18164) (q:draft)
zatkhopna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:joint use/sharing/using together) (d:<zatkhop>, use together, with the noun ending <na>: the using of one thing by two or more together) (b:zatkhop) (r:zd:23929/zd:24303) (q:draft)
zatkhuan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:permission to use/right to use) (d:<zat>, use, with <khuan>, permission: leave or right to use something; {zatkhuan pia} is allow its use) (r:zd:12016/zd:11710) (q:draft)
zatkullo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:need not use) (d:<zat>, use, and <kullo>, need not, written as one word: there is no need to use, not needing to be used) (j:zat/kullo) (r:zd:16133/zd:13355) (q:draft)
zatloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not use/avoid using) (d:<zat> and <loh> written as one word: not using something; {zatloh ding} is should not be used) (j:zat/loh) (r:zd:24252/zd:14650/zd:24395) (q:draft)
zatlohding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:not to be used/must not use) (d:<zat>, use, and <lohding>, not to, written as one word: that a thing is not to be used, often in a warning or a ban) (j:zat/lohding) (r:zd:11854/zd:15237) (q:draft)
zatluat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:use too much/use a lot/overuse) (d:<zat> and <luat> written as one word: use very much or too much) (j:zat/luat) (r:zd:22650/zd:22553) (q:draft)
zato = (i:2) (t:n) (f:health) (w:hospital/clinic) (d:the place where the sick and wounded are treated, in present-day writing far more frequent than the doctor; {zato ah} is at the hospital and <zato kipuak> is be taken to hospital) (s:zatopi) (r:zd:21850/ts:6573/zd:24234) (q:draft)
zato kipuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health) (w:be taken to hospital/be hospitalized) (d:<zato>, doctor or hospital, and <kipuak>, be carried or sent: be taken to hospital, said of an injured or sick person; <zato> stands without a place marker and the person taken stands before the pair) (r:zd:20966/ts:6573/zd:15157) (q:draft)
zato lupna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:hospital bed/hospital) (d:<zato>, here hospital, and <lupna>, bed: a hospital bed; a number after it gives the size of a hospital, {zato lupna 100} is a hospital of 100 beds, and with a place name before it the pair names that hospital) (r:zd:17168/zd:24016) (q:draft)
zatolum = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health) (w:be in hospital/be hospitalised/be an in-patient) (d:<zato>, here the hospital, and <lum>, lie down, written as one word: lie in hospital as a patient; also the patient who is admitted, as in {cina zatolum}) (j:zato/lum) (r:zd:17474/zd:14640/zd:17641) (q:draft)
zatopi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:hospital/general hospital) (d:<zato> with the augmentative {-pi}: a hospital, especially the main hospital of a town) (b:zato) (r:zd:24158/zd:24572/zd:23533) (q:draft)
zatpak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:use for the time being/use right away) (d:<zat>, use, and <pak>, at once or for a short while, written as one word: use something at once or as a stopgap; {zatpak theih} is ready to be used) (j:zat/pak) (r:zd:22543/zd:17426) (q:draft, low confidence)
zatpen = (i:2) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:the one used/using) (d:<zat>, use, with the topic marker <pen> written on to it, after the name of a thing: the thing that someone uses, or the using of it, as what the sentence is about; not the superlative of {zatpen} the one most used) (r:zd:17318/zd:17143/zd:20056) (q:draft)
zatpih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:use with/spend with/share the use of) (d:<zat>, use, with <pih>, together with: use something with or for someone; {hun zatpih} is spend time with someone) (b:zat) (r:zd:25512/zd:23554/zd:25221) (q:draft)
zatsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:used/already used/customary) (d:<zat>, use, with the ending {-sa}, already: that has been used, as used things to be thrown away or recycled; also what someone has always used or practised) (r:zd:23935/zd:21815/zd:21075) (q:draft)
zatsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:intend to use/try to use/plan to use) (d:<zat>, use, and <sawm>, intend, written as one word) (j:zat/sawm) (r:zd:18086/zd:15414) (q:draft)
zatsiam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:use well/use skilfully/make good use of) (d:<zat> and <siam> written as one word: know how to use something and use it well, as time, money or technology) (j:zat/siam) (r:zd:22023/zd:23367/zd:24862) (q:draft)
zatsiamna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/education) (w:skilful use/good use/skill in using) (d:<zatsiam>, use well, with the noun suffix {-na}: the ability to use something well, as time, knowledge or words) (b:zatsiam) (r:zd:9425/zd:25687) (q:draft)
zatsuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:keep using/go on using) (d:<zat>, use, and <suak>, on without stopping, written as one word: continue to use) (j:zat/suak) (r:zd:23075/zd:22778) (q:draft)
zattak = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/work) (w:useful/usable/fit for use) (d:<zat>, use, with <tak>, worthy of: worth using, of use to someone; {zattak het lo} is of no use at all) (r:zd:24673/zd:11452) (q:draft)
zattang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:substitute/common use) (d:a thing used in the place of another, or what is in ordinary use; {zattang in} is in place of, serving as) (r:zd:17607/zd:24303) (q:draft, low confidence)
zattheihding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/it) (w:be able to use/can be used) (d:<zattheih>, can be used, and <ding> written as one word: so that it can be used, or that it will be usable) (j:zattheih/ding) (r:zd:11827/zd:15505/zd:11506) (q:draft)
zattheihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:ability to use/usability/use) (d:<zattheih>, can be used, with the noun ending {-na}: the ability or right to use something, or the place or way in which it can be used; {a ki zattheihna mun} is a place where it can be used) (b:zattheih) (r:zd:21239/zd:24089/zd:23022) (q:draft)
zatui kibawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health) (w:be treated/receive treatment) (d:<zatui>, medicine, and <kibawl>, be done: be given medical treatment; the hospital or clinic stands before it with <ah>, and the active form is {zatui bawl}, treat a patient) (r:zd:13131/zd:17794) (q:draft)
zatui kibawlding = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:health) (w:for medical treatment/to be treated) (d:<zatui>, medicine, and <kibawlding>, will be done: to be given medical treatment; followed by <in>, in order to be treated, before a verb of taking to hospital such as <kipuak>) (r:zd:15577/zd:14523) (q:draft)
zatui zaha = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:medicines/medical supplies/medication) (d:<zatui>, medicine, with <zaha>, here an echo word that only pairs with it: medicines of every kind, medicine and medical supplies as a whole) (r:zd:25189/zd:23729/ts:2690) (q:draft)
zatuilamsang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/education) (w:medical field/medicine/pharmacy) (d:<zatui> and <lamsang> written as one word: the field of medicine, medical matters) (j:zatui/lamsang) (r:zd:20236/zd:16767) (q:draft)
zatuisai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/work) (w:pharmacy/drugstore/chemist) (d:<zatui>, medicine, with <sai>, shop: a shop where medicine is sold) (b:zatui) (j:zatui/sai) (r:zd:12575/zd:12364) (q:draft)
zatuite = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:medicines/drugs) (d:plural of <zatui>: medicines, also drugs) (b:zatui) (r:zd:23729/zd:24276) (q:draft)
zatzat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:keep using/use regularly) (d:<zat> said twice: use again and again, or what one habitually uses) (b:zat) (r:zd:23910/zd:20135/zd:22650) (q:draft)
zatzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:have used/have been in use) (d:<zat>, use, and <zawh>, here after or finish, written as one word: since it was put to use, as in {aki zatzawh kum 2}, two years in use; also use up an amount) (j:zat/zawh) (r:zd:21366/zd:24607) (q:draft, low confidence)
zavat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:epidemic/plague/pestilence) (d:a deadly disease that spreads quickly among many people, used with <pul>, <pulpi> and <natna>; {sungpai zavat} is cholera) (r:zd:24250/zd:23889) (q:draft)
zavom = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/politics) (w:opium) (d:<za>, drug, with <vom>, black: opium, the black drug, often named together with <zakang>, the white drug, heroin; {zavom ciing} is grow opium) (r:zd:10797/zd:25488) (q:draft, low confidence)
zaw = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:everyday) (w:than/more) (d:marks the comparative, more or rather; it follows the describing word, and the thing compared stands before it with <sangin>)
zaw hamtang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:rather/all the more/in fact) (d:<zaw>, more or rather, and <hamtang>, insistently: placed after a verb or describing word and before <hi>, states firmly that the thing is rather so, or so all the more, against what might be expected) (r:zd:21085/zd:12167/zd:16312) (q:draft, low confidence)
zawdeuhta = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:somewhat more now/rather better now) (d:<zawdeuh>, somewhat more, with <ta>, here the marker of a change that has now come about, written as one word after a describing word: has now become rather more so) (j:zawdeuh/ta) (r:zd:14850/zd:11927/zd:15795) (q:draft)
zawdiak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:especially/more particularly/all the more) (d:<zaw>, more, and <diak>, especially, written as one word after a verb or describing word: more so than the rest) (j:zaw/diak) (r:zd:17919/zd:22569) (q:draft)
zawding = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:more/rather) (d:<zaw> and <ding> written as one word after a verb or describing word: will be more so, would rather) (j:zaw/ding) (r:zd:15949/zd:22989/zd:14947) (q:draft)
Zawgyi = (i:1) (t:name) (f:it) (w:Zawgyi) (d:a font and way of encoding Burmese script on phones and computers, widely used in Myanmar before the change to Unicode) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:20095/zd:23049) (q:draft)
zawh = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be able/can/manage) (d:form of <zo> placed after another verb: be able to do it, manage it; with <loh> or <kei>, not be able) (r:zd:23896/zd:25109) (q:draft)
zawh = (i:3) (t:prep) (f:time) (w:after/since) (d:after a verb or <tua>, that: after it is finished, since it was done; {tua zawh ciangin} is after that, and a number of years may follow) (r:ts:11162/zd:17049/ts:301) (q:draft)
zawh ciang = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:time) (w:after/once finished) (d:<zawh>, finish, and <ciang>, when: placed after a verb, a noun of time or <tua>, after it is done or after that time; {tua zawh ciang} is after that) (r:zd:23037/zd:24144/ts:11162) (q:draft)
zawh kum = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:time) (w:years since/years after) (d:<zawh>, here having finished, and <kum>, year: placed after a verb and before a number, that many years since or after the action; {a tun zawh kum 5} is five years since he arrived) (r:zd:22802/zd:9220/ts:3284) (q:draft)
zawh nading = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:in order to be able to/so that one can) (d:<zawh>, here the form of <zo>, be able, manage, and <nading>, for the purpose of: placed after a verb, in order to be able to do it, so that it can be done; often followed by <in> and a main clause that names what is needed or done) (r:zd:22556/zd:19408) (q:draft)
zawh nadingin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:so that one can/in order to be able to/in order to manage) (d:<zawh>, form of the verb win that after another verb means be able or manage to, and <nadingin>, in order to: placed after a verb and closing the clause of purpose, so that the action can be achieved; without a verb before it, in order to defeat or to finish something) (r:zd:20778/zd:14791) (q:draft)
zawh nang = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:in order to be able to/so as to manage/so that one can) (d:<zawh>, form of the verb win that after another verb means be able or manage to, and <nang>, here not the pronoun you but the short form of <nading>, for the purpose of: placed after a verb, in order to be able to do it; a noun or a verb of striving or preparing follows) (s:zawh nadingin) (r:zd:21271/zd:22157) (q:draft)
Zawhang = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (f:religion) (w:John) (d:the name John in an older spelling, of John the Baptist and of the Gospel of John printed in 1923; the Bible text writes <Johan>) (r:zd:22544/zd:17168/zd:20324) (q:draft)
zawhciang = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:time/everyday) (w:after/when finished) (d:<zawh>, finish, and <ciang>, when, written as one word after a verb: after doing, once it is done; a short form of <zawhciangin>) (j:zawh/ciang) (r:zd:19166/zd:22922) (q:draft)
zawhciangin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:time) (w:after/when finished) (d:<zawh>, finish, and <ciangin>, when, written as one word after a verb or <tua>: after doing so, when it was done; {tua zawhciangin} is after that) (j:zawh/ciangin) (r:zd:24142/zd:24739/zd:23797) (q:draft)
zawhding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be able to/can be done) (d:<zawh> and <ding> written as one word after a verb: that can be done or finished; {gen zawhding hilo} is that cannot be told) (j:zawh/ding) (r:zd:20202/zd:19856/zd:19455) (q:draft)
zawhi = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:more/rather) (d:<zaw>, more or rather, and the sentence ending <hi> written as one word: it is more so, or it is rather so) (j:zaw/hi) (r:zd:23770/zd:10864) (q:draft)
zawhkei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:cannot/be unable/not win) (d:<zawh>, be able or win, and <kei>, not, written as one word: after a verb, not be able to do it; alone, not win) (j:zawh/kei) (r:zd:20950/zd:19174/zd:24495) (q:draft)
zawhlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:cannot/be unable to) (d:<zawh>, be able or overcome, and <lo>, not, written as one word; after a verb: not manage to do it) (j:zawh/lo) (r:zd:20091/zd:26049) (q:draft)
zawhloh lungdamna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:inexpressible gratitude/thanks beyond words) (d:<zawhloh>, that cannot be done, and <lungdamna>, joy or thanks: used after <gen>, say, as {gen zawhloh lungdamna}, thanks that cannot be told; a formula of public acknowledgement to donors and helpers, who stand before it with <tungah>) (r:zd:14887/zd:15275) (q:draft)
zawhlohna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:inability/failure) (d:the fact of not being able, placed after a verb: {up zawhlohna} is inability to believe and {ngah zawhlohna} is failure to get) (b:zawhloh) (r:zd:21262/zd:24347/zd:23823) (q:draft)
zawhlohte = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:those unable to/those that could not) (d:<zawhloh> and <te> written as one word after a verb: the ones who cannot do it, or the ones for whom it could not be done, as in {a damsak zawhlohte}, those they could not heal) (j:zawhloh/te) (r:zd:15006/zd:12998) (q:draft)
zawhna dingin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:in order to be able to/so as to manage to) (d:<zawhna>, being able or overcoming, and <dingin>, in order to: placed after a verb, so that the action can be accomplished; {neih zawhna dingin} is in order to be able to have) (r:zd:21410/zd:19599) (q:draft)
zawhngeu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature/home) (w:cat) (r:zai:cat) (q:draft)
zawhsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:try to finish/aim to complete) (d:<zawh>, finish or complete, with <sawm>, intend or try: set out to finish a task or reach a goal) (j:zawh/sawm) (r:zd:17152/zd:15720/zd:21083) (q:draft)
zawhthawh thutawh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:social/politics) (w:by force/forcibly/under compulsion) (d:<zawhthawh>, force, and <thutawh>, by way of: placed before a verb, do it to someone by force or against that person's will) (r:zd:19145/zd:19398) (q:draft)
zawhthawhbawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:bully/oppress/mistreat/harass) (d:<zawhthawh>, force, with <bawl>, do, written as one word: treat someone roughly or unfairly by force, often paired with <simmawhbawl>, treat with contempt) (j:zawhthawh/bawl) (r:zd:15366/zd:21601) (q:draft)
zawhthawhthu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:force/compulsion) (d:<zawhthawh> and <thu> written as one word; {zawhthawhthu tawh} is by force) (j:zawhthawh/thu) (r:zd:23670/zd:19990) (q:draft)
zawhuh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:time) (d:<zawh>, here finish, with the plural <uh>, written as one word after a verb and before <ciangin>: after they had done it, when they had finished) (j:zawh/uh) (r:zd:17060/zd:25390) (q:draft, low confidence)
zawi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/nature) (w:path/track/trail) (d:a narrow path or track made by people or animals passing; also a way or channel, as in {thupha zawi}, a path of blessing) (r:zd:18107/zd:24320) (q:draft)
zawitawn = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:follow along/be in line with/be related to) (d:<zawi>, path, with <tawn>, go along: go the same way as something; mostly with the prefix <ki> written apart, {tawh ki zawitawn}, which is <kizawitawn>) (r:zd:22023/zd:21739/zd:15047) (q:draft)
zawkzawk = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (d:<zawk>, more, said twice after a verb of wanting such as <deih> or <ut>: whichever one prefers) (b:zawk) (r:zd:23479/zd:21939) (q:draft)
zawl = (i:3) (t:n) (f:social) (w:friend/close friend/sworn friend) (d:a close friend, and in the old custom the sworn friend that a person or a village keeps; {zawl aw} is the way to address a friend) (s:lawm) (r:zd:19116/zd:23424/zd:23554) (q:draft)
zawl = (i:4) (t:n) (f:social) (w:sweetheart/lover) (d:the person one courts: {zawl lai} is a love letter and {zawl hel} is to court) (r:zd:23006/zd:22683) (q:draft, low confidence)
zawlla = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/social) (w:love song/courting song) (d:a song of love between a young man and a young woman, <la>, song, joined to the word for a sweetheart or lover; set against {Pasian la}, hymns and gospel songs) (r:zd:16216/zd:23130/zd:14804) (q:draft)
zawlo = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:not more/not rather) (d:<zaw> and <lo> written as one word after a verb or describing word: not more so, not rather; {thupi zawlo} is not the more important thing) (j:zaw/lo) (r:zd:15324/zd:11831/zd:20518) (q:draft)
zawlpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:friend/close friend/companion) (d:a close male friend of a man; {maak thakpa' zawlpa} is the friend of the bridegroom) (s:lawmpa) (r:zd:25054/ts:261) (q:draft)
zawlthu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:words of love/courtship/love talk) (d:the talk of a young man and woman who are courting; {zawlthu gen} is speak of love to someone, court) (r:zd:14804/zd:17986) (q:draft)
zawmah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:even more/what is more) (d:<zaw>, more, with the emphatic <mah>, written as one word, mostly in {zawmah lai} at the end of a statement: even more so, and what is more; written with a capital, {Zawmah} is a different word, the name of the Romans in writing about ancient history, as in {Zawmah galkap}, the Roman army) (j:zaw/mah) (r:zd:9433/zd:23086) (q:draft, low confidence)
zawmawk = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:rather/instead/in fact) (d:<zaw>, more or rather, and <mawk>, unexpectedly, written as one word after a verb or describing word: it turns out rather to be so, against what was expected) (j:zaw/mawk) (r:zd:12869/zd:12756/zd:24386) (q:draft)
zawmcip = (i:1) (t:v) (f:body/health) (w:be exhausted/be utterly weak/be weary) (d:<zawm>, weak, with <cip>, completely: be worn out and without strength, from tiredness or hunger) (j:zawm/cip) (r:zd:24030/zd:17605) (q:draft)
zawn = (i:2) (t:v) (f:social) (w:invite/call on/urge) (d:ask someone to come or to take part; after <kong> it is the usual close of a notice, {kong zawn uh hi}, we invite you, and <zawn phapha> is invite warmly; not the form of <zawng>, poor) (r:zd:16506/zd:20968/zd:17674) (q:draft)
zawn phapha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:earnestly invite/urge/appeal to) (d:a verb written like <zawn>, be poor, but here meaning invite or call upon, and <phapha>, well: a closing formula of notices, {kong zawn phapha uh hi}, we earnestly invite or urge you, after a clause that says what the readers are asked to do) (r:zd:13291/zd:21906) (q:draft, low confidence)
zawng = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/work) (w:poor/needy) (d:having little money or property; also used as a verb, be poor or become poor) (s:cimawh/genthei) (a:hau) (q:draft)
zawngkhaal = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:body/health) (j:zawngkhal) (r:zd:21198) (q:draft)
zawngtah = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (f:food/nature) (w:tree bean/stink bean) (d:a tree, Parkia, grown in the Zomi hills for its long edible pods, and the pods themselves) (r:zd:22448/zd:18258) (q:draft)
zawngte = (i:2) (t:n) (f:nature) (w:monkeys) (d:the animal monkey, as in <zawngmaw>, with the plural <te>: monkeys; the sentence speaks of animals of the forest, not of people in need) (r:zd:12117) (q:draft, low confidence)
zawpah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:more right away/more at once) (d:<zaw>, more, and <pah>, at once, written as one word after a describing word or verb: it becomes more so straight away) (j:zaw/pah) (r:zd:23487/zd:20895) (q:draft)
zawpian = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:rather/somewhat more/tend to) (d:<zaw>, more, and <pian>, likeness, written as one word and placed after a verb or describing word before <hi>: it is rather so, it seems or tends to be so) (j:zaw/pian) (r:zd:26566/zd:16844) (q:draft, low confidence)
zawsawp = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (j:zawsop) (r:zd:19425/zd:25926) (q:draft, low confidence)
zawta = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:more now/even more) (d:<zaw>, more, and the particle <ta> written as one word, after a verb or describing word: it has now become more so) (j:zaw/ta) (r:zd:21974/zd:23025/zd:21421) (q:draft)
Zawtah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (f:religion) (w:Joseph) (d:another form of the Bible name Joseph, used for the son of Jacob and for Joseph of Arimathea) (s:Josef) (r:zd:21939/zd:22827) (q:draft)
zawthei = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:can more/be more able to) (d:<zaw>, more, and <thei>, can, written as one word after a verb: can do it more, is more likely to) (j:zaw/thei) (r:zd:22701/zd:24672) (q:draft)
zawzaw = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<zaw>, more, said twice: whichever is the more so; {khat zawzaw} is either one, one or the other) (b:zaw) (r:zd:12695/zd:22780) (q:draft)
zawzek = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:rather/somewhat more/even) (d:<zaw>, more, and <zek>, a little, written as one word after a verb or describing word: rather, somewhat more than expected) (j:zaw/zek) (r:zd:17264/zd:21656) (q:draft, low confidence)
zawzen = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:even/actually/really) (d:placed after a verb in a plain statement or question, often before <hi>, to stress that something really is so or went that far; without <zong> there is no supposition) (s:zen) (r:zd:24699/zd:18026/zd:24457) (q:draft)
ZBCM = (i:1) (t:name) (f:religion) (w:Zomi Baptist Convention of Myanmar/ZBCM) (d:a body of Zomi Baptist churches with its head office in Myanmar, written with its initials; also in the names of its member churches abroad) (r:zd:14579/zd:25268) (q:draft)
ZCA = (i:1) (t:name) (f:religion/social) (w:ZCA) (d:English abbreviation of a Zomi church body; the articles write it out both as Zomi Christian Alliance and as Zomi Christian Assembly) (o:English) (r:zd:15379/zd:15407) (q:draft, low confidence)
ZCD = (i:1) (t:name) (f:politics) (w:ZCD/Zomi Congress for Democracy) (d:abbreviation of Zomi Congress for Democracy, a Zomi political party in Myanmar) (r:zd:23071/zd:24481/zd:12337) (q:draft)
ZCDC = (i:1) (t:name) (f:social) (w:ZCDC/Zomi Community Development Center) (d:abbreviation of Zomi Community Development Center, a building project of the Zomi community) (r:zd:24358/zd:24649) (q:draft, low confidence)
ZCLS = (i:1) (t:name) (f:religion/education) (w:Zomi Christian Literature Society) (d:abbreviated name of the Zomi Christian Literature Society, a publisher and bookshop of Zolai books with its office in Kalaymyo) (r:zd:20142/zd:21502) (q:draft)
Zealand = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel/politics) (w:New Zealand) (d:second word of the name New Zealand, a country in the Pacific; written {New Zealand gam}) (o:English) (r:zd:20484/zd:12630) (q:draft)
Zechariah = (i:1) (t:name) (f:religion) (j:Zekhariah) (r:zd:21845) (q:draft)
zeek = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/home) (w:manage/budget/use carefully) (d:handle money, time or goods with care so that they are well used; {sum zeek} is manage money) (r:zd:25919/zd:24119/zd:24751) (q:draft)
zeelzeel = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (j:zelzel) (r:zd:23077/zd:24733) (q:draft)
zeelzuul = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:all over the place/here and there/in disorder) (d:placed after a verb: the action goes on everywhere and without order, as talk that goes round or people who stay scattered; probably the same word as <zelzul>) (r:zd:16651/zd:18200) (q:draft, low confidence)
zeetna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (j:ze-etna) (r:zd:17488/zd:15662) (q:draft)
Zeisu Khazih = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (f:religion) (w:Jesus Christ) (d:<Zeisu>, Jesus, and <Khazih>, Christ: the name and title together, as used by the churches that write the name in this spelling; often after <Topa>, Lord) (r:zd:23394/zd:24064) (q:draft)
zek = (i:2) (t:v) (f:work/home) (w:spend/use/manage) (d:the verb <zeek> written with a short vowel: spend or use money and goods, often paired with <zat> and with <kep>, keep; {sum zek} is spending money) (s:zeek) (r:zd:25916/zd:25919/zd:17685) (q:draft)
zekai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:be slow/be late/delay) (d:be late or slow in doing something, put it off; mostly with a negative, {zekai lo}, without delay) (a:kinawh) (r:10.20.5) (q:draft)
zeksiam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:spend wisely/manage money well) (d:be skilful, <siam>, in spending or laying out money and goods; paired with <zangsiam>, use skilfully) (r:zd:25928/zd:18086) (q:draft, low confidence)
zelding = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (d:<zel>, repeatedly or in turn, with <ding>, will, written as one word after a verb: will do or be so again and again, or in turn) (j:zel/ding) (r:zd:20814/zd:19676/zd:16463) (q:draft)
zelna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:repeated doing/habit) (d:<zel>, repeatedly, with the noun suffix {-na}, placed after a verb: the doing of it again and again, or the place where it is usually done; {nong phawk zelna uh} is your remembering me time after time) (b:zel) (r:zd:23428/zd:20792) (q:draft)
zelte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:those who often) (d:<zel>, habitually, with the plural <te> written as one word after a verb: those who do it often or regularly) (j:zel/te) (r:ts:1278/zd:24276) (q:draft)
zelzal = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:brightly/sleekly/smoothly) (d:descriptive word placed after a word of colour, quality or motion, giving a picture of something that shines, is smooth or moves swiftly: {kang zelzal} is gleaming white, {hoih zelzal} fine and smart) (r:zd:16130/zd:20516) (q:draft, low confidence)
zelzel = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:repeatedly/again and again/often) (d:placed after a verb to show that the action happens over and over) (s:zel/zeel/kikkik/tamvei) (r:18.33.29) (q:draft)
zelzelding = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:will keep on/again and again/regularly) (d:<zelzel>, repeatedly, and <ding>, will, written as one word after a verb: will or should go on doing it time after time) (j:zelzel/ding) (r:zd:12908/zd:18289/zd:16442) (q:draft)
zelzelkhat = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (d:<zelzel> and <khat> written as one word after a verb: one who does it again and again, a person or thing that habitually does so) (j:zelzel/khat) (r:zd:18154/zd:21332) (q:draft)
zen tam = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:I wonder/how very) (d:the emphatic <zen>, really, with <tam>, here a question word at the end of a sentence and not many: closes a question or exclamation that begins with a word such as <bang> or <bangzah>, I wonder what, how very much) (r:zd:21925/zd:25484) (q:draft, low confidence)
zenin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (d:the emphatic <zen> with <in>, written as one word after a verb: even, going so far as to) (j:zen/in) (r:ts:301) (q:draft, low confidence)
zenzen hangin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:even though/even if/although indeed) (d:<zenzen>, really, at all, and <hangin>, although: placed after a verb or a clause, even though that is really so, even if it comes to that; the main statement follows) (r:zd:25711/zd:21511) (q:draft)
zenzenin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:if by chance/in case/supposing) (d:<zenzen> and <in> written as one word; {a zenzenin} at the start of a sentence introduces a supposed case: if it should happen that) (j:zenzen/in) (r:zd:16340/zd:21257) (q:draft)
zenzenleh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:if by any chance/in case/should it happen) (d:<zenzen> by chance with <leh> if, placed after the verb: if it should happen that; after <kei> if it should not) (j:zenzen/leh) (r:zd:19550/zd:23867) (q:draft)
zenzenlo = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:not at all/by no means/not really) (d:<zenzen> and <lo> written as one word after a verb: not at all; {hi zenzenlo} is it is by no means so) (j:zenzen/lo) (r:zd:24481/zd:24381/zd:25203) (q:draft)
zepgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:whip severely/cane/thrash) (d:<zep> in the sense whip or beat with a cane, belt or rod, not decorate, with <gawp>, severely, written as one word: beat hard and many times) (j:zep/gawp) (r:zd:12255/zd:20461) (q:draft)
Zero = (i:1) (t:num) (f:everyday/education) (w:zero/nought) (d:the number 0, or the point 0 on a scale such as temperature) (o:English) (r:zd:12831) (q:draft)
zeuhzeuh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:now and then/from time to time/occasionally) (d:placed after a verb: the action happens at intervals, again and again but not all the time; often with {khat veivei}, sometimes, or <zel>) (r:zd:24276/zd:11715/zd:13181) (q:draft)
zezen = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:even/really/to that extent) (d:emphatic word placed after a verb or describing word: even, to such a degree; with a negative, not even, not at all; compare <zenzen>) (r:zd:22858/zd:23130) (q:draft, low confidence)
Zhejiang = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel) (w:Zhejiang) (d:province on the east coast of China) (r:zd:11466/zd:14521) (q:draft)
Zhou = (i:1) (t:name) (f:politics/social) (w:Zhou) (d:the Zhou dynasty of ancient China, from which some writers on Zomi history derive the name Zo; also a Chinese family name) (r:zd:8375/zd:19159) (q:draft)
zi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:wife) (d:a married woman in relation to her husband; {zi la} or {zi-in la} is take a wife, marry) (a:pasal)
ziading = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/media) (w:way/manner) (d:<zia>, way, and <ding>, to be, written as one word after a verb: the way something is to be done, how to do it; common in headings) (j:zia/ding) (r:zd:23191/zd:25749/zd:24038) (q:draft)
ziah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (d:used doubled, {ziah ziah}, after a verb: steadily, in a continuous flow, one after another without holding back; the same as <ziahziah> written as two words) (r:zd:23037/zd:11262) (q:draft)
ziahziah = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday/media) (w:in quick succession/one after another/heavily) (d:placed after a verb of action, as <kap ziahziah>, keep firing, and {bomb khiat ziahziah}, drop bomb after bomb: the action goes on in quick succession or in great numbers, with no thought of giving) (r:ts:8304/zd:17776/ts:5448) (q:draft)
ziahziahna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:profusion/bustle) (d:<ziahziah>, freely and in great numbers, with the noun suffix <na>, placed after a verb: the doing of it by many or without stop, and before <mun> or a place word the place where this goes on) (b:ziahziah) (r:zd:18918/zd:16410) (q:draft)
ziahziahta = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/media) (w:already fully/already in full swing) (d:<ziahziah> after a verb with <ta>, already, written as one word: the action is already going on freely and at full strength, as a fire already blazing or a work already well under way) (j:ziahziah/ta) (r:zd:13161/zd:17097) (q:draft, low confidence)
ziahzuah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (d:placed after a verb for things scattered or pouring out all over, as luggage thrown about or sweat running) (r:zd:21020/zd:20545) (q:draft, low confidence)
ziak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:reason/cause/because of) (d:the reason or cause of something; after a noun or clause, usually as {ziak in} or {ziak-a}, because of, and {tua ziak in} is therefore; it stands where the Bible text has <hang>) (s:hang) (r:zd:21340/zd:12074/zd:21079) (q:draft)
ziakaai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (j:zekai) (r:zd:24086/zd:24496) (q:draft)
ziakai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (j:zekai) (r:zd:9212/zd:15067/zd:23974) (q:draft)
ziakaiding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:time/travel) (w:will be delayed/will be late) (d:<ziakai>, be late, and <ding>, will, written as one word: there will be a delay, often after the length of time) (j:ziakai/ding) (r:zd:15167/zd:12494/zd:12581) (q:draft)
ziakailo = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:without delay/in less than/not taking long) (d:<ziakai>, be late or take long, and <lo>, not, written as one word; after a length of time with <zong>: in not even that long) (j:ziakai/lo) (r:zd:11729/zd:17703) (q:draft)
ziakaina = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/time) (w:delay/hindrance/obstacle) (d:<ziakai>, be late, with the noun suffix {-na}: a delay, or something that holds back) (b:ziakai) (r:zd:11482/zd:16511) (q:draft)
ziakaisak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/time) (w:delay/make late/hold up) (d:<ziakai>, be late, with the causative <sak>: cause a flight, a train or a journey to be late; also used for be delayed) (r:zd:17430/zd:17624/zd:12309) (q:draft)
ziakaituam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:time/travel) (w:be delayed/be later than planned) (d:<ziakai>, be late, with a second part meaning all the more: be later than the set time, be delayed by so much) (b:ziakai) (r:zd:17297/zd:14895) (q:draft)
ziakaizaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:time/travel) (w:later/more delayed/slower) (d:<ziakai>, be late, and <zaw>, more, written as one word: later than the time planned or than usual, with the amount of time before it and <sangin>, than) (j:ziakai/zaw) (r:zd:13094/zd:16287) (q:draft)
ziakin = (i:1) (t:ppm) (f:everyday) (w:because of/on account of) (d:placed after a noun or a clause to give the cause; {tua ziakin} is because of that, therefore) (r:zd:16157/zd:16521) (q:draft)
zial = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:roll/scroll/stick) (d:a rolled thing, as a noun and as a counter after the thing named: {lai zial}, a scroll, and {zaa zial khat}, one cigarette, where the verb sense is the act of rolling up) (r:zd:15810/zd:20841/zd:20434) (q:draft)
zialkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:catch and roll in) (d:<zial>, roll, and <kha>, happen to, written as one word: of a wheel or moving stair, catch and roll in a hand or cloth by accident) (j:zial/kha) (r:zd:22864) (q:draft, low confidence)
ziapen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (d:<zia>, way or manner, and the topic marker <pen> written as one word: the way that something is or happened, as for the way) (j:zia/pen) (r:zd:16897/zd:11764) (q:draft)
ziau lel = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:just/simply/without more ado) (d:<ziau>, at once or easily, and <lel>, here the particle merely, not be defeated: placed after a verb, the action is done simply, offhand, with no further thought) (r:zd:25928/zd:21605) (q:draft, low confidence)
ziauding = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (d:<ziau> and <ding> written as one word after a verb: will simply or readily do, is just to be done; {Install ziauding} is one just has to install it) (j:ziau/ding) (r:zd:11457/zd:17901) (q:draft)
ziauhi = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (d:<ziau>, swiftly and lightly, and the sentence ending <hi> written as one word, placed after a verb: it is done at once or simply) (j:ziau/hi) (r:zd:23784/zd:20905) (q:draft)
ziauhziauh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:readily/easily/freely) (d:placed after a verb: the action is done lightly and readily, again and again or wherever wanted, as in {zat ziauhziauh}, use readily, and {hawh ziauhziauh}, visit freely; compare <ziau>) (r:zd:22391/zd:23776) (q:draft, low confidence)
ziauna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (d:<ziau> with the noun suffix <na>, after a verb: the act of simply or readily doing it, as in {up ziauna}, mere believing, and {sim ziauna}, just reading) (j:ziau/na) (r:zd:25571/zd:19816/zd:11697) (q:draft, low confidence)
ziauthei = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:can suddenly/can easily) (d:<ziau>, swiftly and lightly, and <thei>, able, written as one word, placed after a verb: it can happen all at once or with ease) (j:ziau/thei) (r:zd:19614/zd:23784) (q:draft)
ZIDCA = (i:1) (t:name) (f:social) (w:ZIDCA/Zomi Innkuan DC Area) (d:abbreviation of Zomi Innkuan DC Area, the association of the Zomi community in the Washington D.C. area of the United States) (r:zd:24910/zd:25912) (q:draft)
ziding = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:wife-to-be/fiancee/bride) (d:<zi>, wife, and <ding> written as one word: the woman who is to become the wife of someone; {ziding in la} is take as wife) (j:zi/ding) (r:zd:16350/zd:25318) (q:draft)
zihziah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:in great numbers/all over/everywhere) (d:expressive word placed after a verb, showing that many people or things do it together or that it happens all over a place: {dim zihziah} is full everywhere, crowded) (r:zd:18927/ts:10085/zd:20486) (q:draft)
zii = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/everyday) (w:market/bazaar) (d:a market or shop where food and goods are bought; {zii pai} is go to the market, go shopping) (s:sumbuk) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:22203/zd:23756/zd:25918) (q:draft)
zii = (i:2) (t:n) (f:family) (j:zi) (r:zd:21853/zd:21079) (q:draft)
ziingsang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (j:zingsang) (r:zd:21003/zd:21279/zd:17860) (q:draft)
Zika = (i:1) (t:name) (f:health) (w:Zika/Zika virus) (d:a virus spread by mosquitoes and the illness it causes) (r:zd:12941/zd:16177) (q:draft)
zikzek = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:utterly/completely) (d:placed after a verb or describing word to stress it: {dai zikzek} is utterly quiet, {siacip zikzek} is completely destroyed) (r:ts:301/zd:12772) (q:draft, low confidence)
zilzial = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:trailing/drawn out) (d:descriptive adverb placed after a word: long, smooth and trailing, as hair or noodles, or drawn out, as a nasal voice) (r:zd:24086/zd:22658) (q:draft, low confidence)
Zimbabwe = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:politics/travel) (w:Zimbabwe) (d:a country in southern Africa) (r:zd:23488) (q:draft)
zin = (i:2) (t:n) (f:social) (w:guest/stranger/traveller) (d:one who is away from home, a guest in a house or a foreigner in a land; {zin do} is to show hospitality and {zin tunna inn} is a guest room or an inn) (s:khualmi/leengla/mikhual) (r:60.4.9) (q:draft)
zin kawikawi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:travel around/tour/journey about) (d:<zin>, here a verb, to travel or be away from home, and <kawikawi>, about: to travel from place to place, to tour, as a preacher, a trader or a leader does; the places stand before it with <ah> or the purpose with <in>) (r:zd:21978/zd:15681) (q:draft)
zinbuk = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:guest house/inn/hotel/lodge) (d:<zin>, guest or traveller, with <buk>, hut: a house where travellers pay to stay) (r:zd:24188/ts:301/zd:23957) (q:draft)
zinc = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/nature) (w:zinc) (d:a metal and a mineral found in food) (o:English) (r:zd:24276) (q:draft, low confidence)
zinding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/politics) (w:will visit/to travel/to visit) (d:<zin>, travel, and <ding> written as one word: will travel to a place, is to visit it; common in headlines about official visits) (j:zin/ding) (r:zd:15726/zd:16663/zd:17192) (q:draft)
zineiding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family) (w:will marry/about to take a wife) (d:<zinei>, take a wife, and <ding> written as one word: of a man, going to marry, in order to marry) (j:zinei/ding) (r:zd:18129/zd:12504) (q:draft)
zing = (i:3) (t:n) (f:time) (w:morning/tomorrow) (d:the morning, as in <zing an>, breakfast, and {zing sang}, written together <zingsang>; with <ciang> or <ni> after it, the next morning or tomorrow, as <zingciang>) (r:zd:21918/zd:15393/ts:3125) (q:draft)
zing an = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:food/time) (w:breakfast) (d:the morning meal) (r:zai:breakfast) (q:draft)
zingan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food/time) (j:zing an) (r:zd:22868/zd:22019) (q:draft)
zingciang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time/everyday) (w:tomorrow/the next day) (d:also the day after an event: {a zingciang ni}) (a:zani) (q:draft)
zinglam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:morning/in the morning) (d:<zing>, morning, with <lam>, side: the morning part of the day, also used before a clock time) (s:zingsang) (r:zd:16678/zd:12695) (q:draft)
zingling = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature) (j:zinling) (r:zd:19908/zd:12177) (q:draft)
zingni = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:tomorrow) (d:the day that is coming, the day after today; also the time to come, as in {hauhna zingni}, a tomorrow of prosperity) (s:zingciang) (r:zd:25171/zd:22557) (q:draft)
zingsang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:morning) (d:the early part of the day; {a zingsang ciangin} is in the morning or the next morning, and {zingsang tungin} is early in the morning) (a:nitak)
zingsang khuavak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:daybreak/dawn/morning light) (d:<zingsang>, morning, with <khuavak>, daylight: the time when it grows light in the morning; followed by a word of time, as in {zingsang khuavak dong}, until daybreak, and {zingsang khuavak phetin}, as soon as day breaks) (s:phalvak) (r:zd:19826/zd:22779/zd:17060) (q:draft)
zingsanglam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:morning/morning time) (d:<zingsang> and <lam> written as one word: the morning part of the day; with <in>, in the morning) (j:zingsang/lam) (r:zd:16373/zd:17917) (q:draft)
zingsangsim = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:every morning/each morning) (d:<zingsang>, morning, and <sim>, here each or every, written as one word: every morning; often with <in>) (j:zingsang/sim) (r:zd:14763/zd:12674/zd:24276) (q:draft)
zingsangtung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:early morning/dawn) (d:<zingsang>, morning, and <tung> written as one word: the early part of the morning; {zingsangtung in} is early in the morning) (j:zingsang/tung) (r:zd:14826/zd:15292/zd:18125) (q:draft)
zingsangtunglam = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:early in the morning/in the early hours) (d:<zingsang> <tung> <lam> written as one word: around the earliest part of the morning, before or about dawn) (j:zingsang/tung/lam) (r:zd:17058/zd:14969/zd:21466) (q:draft)
zingteh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:tomorrow) (d:tomorrow, when the next morning comes) (s:zingciang) (r:zd:17428/zd:17213) (q:draft)
zingthawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:time/everyday) (w:get up in the morning/rise) (d:form of <zingtho> used before words such as <ciangin> and <phet>: get up in the morning; also the getting up itself) (b:zingtho) (r:zd:25909/zd:21417) (q:draft)
zingtung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:early morning/daybreak) (d:the early part of the morning, about daybreak; {zingtung an} is breakfast) (r:zd:21876/zd:23022) (q:draft)
zingvai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:affairs/plans/future) (d:the affairs and coming days of a household or a people, literally the business of the morning, often paired with {nitak vai}; {zingvai hawm} is to deliberate and plan together) (r:zd:9448/zd:25110) (q:draft, low confidence)
zinkawikawi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:travel around/tour/go from place to place) (d:<zin>, travel, and <kawikawi>, about, written as one word: travel around from place to place) (s:vakkawikawi) (j:zin/kawikawi) (r:zd:12674/zd:19260) (q:draft)
zinkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:travel out/go abroad/set out on a journey) (d:form of <zinkhia>, go away on a journey, used before words such as <ding> and <ni>, and as a noun, a trip away) (b:zinkhia) (r:zd:26495/zd:12581) (q:draft)
zinling = (i:2) (t:v) (f:nature) (w:quake/shake) (d:used as a verb, the earth quakes or an earthquake strikes, as in {zinling hi}; the place is marked by <ah> and the strength by <tawh>) (r:zd:11738/zd:15338/zd:17202) (q:draft)
zinlinggawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:nature/media) (w:be struck by a severe earthquake/quake violently) (d:<zinling> and <gawp> written as one word: the earth quaked severely, a strong earthquake struck) (j:zinling/gawp) (r:zd:14716/zd:17632) (q:draft)
zinlingna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature) (w:earthquake/quake) (d:<zinling>, earthquake, with the noun suffix <na>: the event of an earthquake) (s:zinling) (b:zinling) (r:zd:11219/ts:2753) (q:draft)
zinmang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:chief guest/guest of honour) (d:the honoured guest at a festival or meeting, from <zin>, guest) (r:zd:22357/zd:15865) (q:draft)
zinmangpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:chief guest/guest of honour) (d:<zin>, guest, with <mangpi>, lord: the chief guest of a festival or public gathering) (r:zd:15622/zd:17877/zd:22357) (q:draft)
zinpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/travel) (w:host/host family/lodging) (d:the household with which a guest or a visiting group stays) (r:zd:15637) (q:draft, low confidence)
zinto = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:travel up/go up) (d:<zin> travel, with <to> upward: travel up to a place; {a zinsuk a zinto} are those travelling down and up) (b:zin) (r:zd:11101/zd:22773) (q:draft)
zintunbuk = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:hotel/guest house/inn) (d:<zintun>, lodge as a guest, with <buk>, here a hut or shelter: a house where travellers pay to stay; writers often add the English word Hotel beside it) (s:zintunna) (r:zd:13262/zd:12007) (q:draft)
zintung = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:lodge/stay as a guest/put up) (d:<zin>, guest, with <tung>, arrive: stay somewhere as a traveller or guest, in a hotel or in another person's house; <zintun> is the form used before endings) (s:zintun) (r:ts:4831/zd:15842/zd:23086) (q:draft)
zintung = (i:2) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:guest/lodger) (d:a person who is staying in a hotel or a house as a guest, often {zintung te}) (r:zd:13262/zd:22040) (q:draft)
ZIOK = (i:1) (t:name) (f:social) (w:ZIOK) (d:short name of a Zomi community organisation in the United States, apparently <Zomi Innkuan> of Oklahoma; {ZIOK kipawlna} is the ZIOK organisation) (r:zd:26238/zd:11387) (q:draft, low confidence)
Zip = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:zip/zipper) (d:the zip fastener of trousers or a bag; {zip kai} is pull the zip) (o:English) (r:zd:17930/zd:15387) (q:draft)
ZIS = (i:1) (t:name) (f:social) (w:ZIS) (d:abbreviated name of the Zomi community organisation in Singapore) (r:zd:17120/zd:21241) (q:draft, low confidence)
ZIUSA = (i:1) (t:name) (f:social) (w:Zomi Innkuan USA/ZIUSA) (d:abbreviation of Zomi Innkuan USA, the national association of the Zomi communities in the United States) (r:zd:16813/zd:13207) (q:draft)
zizon = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/social) (w:looking for a wife/wife-seeking) (d:<zi>, wife, and <zon>, seek, written as one word: the seeking of a wife) (j:zi/zon) (r:zd:20316) (q:draft)
ZNC = (i:1) (t:name) (f:politics) (w:Zomi National Congress/ZNC) (d:a Zomi political party in Myanmar, later named Zomi Congress for Democracy, ZCD) (r:zd:26252/zd:24481) (q:draft)
ZNCM = (i:1) (t:name) (f:politics/social) (w:Zomi National Council of Myanmar) (d:abbreviation of Zomi National Council of Myanmar, a Zomi organisation in Myanmar) (r:zd:19378) (q:draft)
ZNTV = (i:1) (t:name) (f:media) (w:ZNTV/Zomi National TV) (d:short for Zomi National TV, a Zomi television and news channel) (r:zd:24024/zd:24594) (q:draft)
zo = (i:4) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be able to/manage to/succeed in) (d:placed after another verb, be able to do it or succeed in doing it, as in {lakhia zo} manage to capture and {mu zo} be able to find; with <lo>, be unable to) (r:ts:3687/ts:3280/zd:25109) (q:draft)
zo nawn = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:no longer able/cannot any more) (d:<zo>, be able, and <nawn>, any longer: placed after a verb and before a negative such as <lo>, <kei> or <keng>, no longer able to do it) (r:zd:20771/zd:22683/ts:6842) (q:draft)
zo tuan = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:still not able/not able even so) (d:<zo>, be able, and <tuan>, even so: placed after a verb and followed by a negative such as <lo> or <kei>, the action still cannot be done, in spite of what was said before) (r:zd:25357/zd:21246) (q:draft)
Zodial = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/home) (w:Zomi scarf/Zomi sash) (d:a band of Zomi traditional cloth, <dial>, worn round the neck or over the shoulders and hung on guests and leaders as a mark of honour) (r:zd:26097/zd:26708/zd:20587) (q:draft)
zoding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:will be able to/can manage) (d:<zo>, in its use after a verb for being able to do it, and <ding> written as one word: will be able to, will manage to) (j:zo/ding) (r:zd:22736/zd:23311/zd:15586) (q:draft)
Zogam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:social/politics) (w:Zogam/Zoland) (d:{Zo} with <gam>, country: the homeland of the <Zomi>) (r:zd:23554/zd:24682/zd:24471) (q:draft)
Zogamah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:travel/social) (w:in Zogam/to Zogam) (d:<Zogam>, the land of the Zomi, and the place marker <ah> written as one word: in or to Zogam) (j:Zogam/ah) (r:zd:15527/zd:17168/zd:22371) (q:draft)
Zogambup = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:social/politics) (w:the whole of Zogam/all Zogam) (d:<Zogam> and <bup>, whole, written as one word: the whole Zo homeland, or all its people) (j:Zogam/bup) (r:zd:23431/zd:22754) (q:draft)
Zoheisa = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (f:nature) (w:Zoheisa flower) (d:a wild flower of the Zo hills, described as bright red and growing on large trees; also the name of a magazine and of groups; the English name of the plant is not known from the articles) (r:zd:17081/zd:21822) (q:draft, low confidence)
zohi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:has been done/has come about) (d:<zo>, finish or manage, with the sentence-final <hi>, written as one word after a verb: the action is done or has come to be so) (j:zo/hi) (r:zd:22695/zd:12867) (q:draft)
Zohun = (i:1) (t:name) (f:media/religion) (w:Zo programme/Zo service) (d:literally Zo time: the name of the Zo language radio programme of the Burmese broadcasting service, and of a Zo language church service) (r:zd:15861/zd:16974) (q:draft, low confidence)
