zolai simbu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:Zolai reader/Zolai primer) (d:Zolai, the Zomi written language, and <simbu>, here a book for reading, from <sim>, read, and <bu>, book, and not the bird: the school reader from which children learn to read Zolai, first made by J. H. Cope and issued by grade, as in {Zolai simbu tan thum}, the reader for grade three) (r:zd:11891/zd:23717/zd:23207) (q:draft)
zolam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/media) (w:Zo dance/Zomi traditional dance) (d:<zo>, Zomi, and <laam>, dance, written as one word: the traditional dance of the Zomi, named together with {zola}, Zo song) (j:zo/laam) (r:zd:14579/zd:15794) (q:draft)
zolam = (i:2) (t:n) (f:nature/travel) (w:north/the highland side) (d:<zo>, here the cold high country, and <lam>, direction: the direction opposite to {simlam}; taken here as north, the reviewer should confirm the compass point) (r:zd:23394) (q:draft, low confidence)
Zoland = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:politics) (w:Zoland) (d:English-style name for the homeland of the Zo people, <Zogam>; in news mostly in the name of the armed group PDF Zoland) (s:Zogam) (r:zd:23436/ts:7016) (q:draft)
zoleh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:if able to/if one manages to) (d:<zo>, be able, manage, and <leh>, if, written as one word after a verb: if it can be done, if one manages to do it) (j:zo/leh) (r:zd:21092/zd:21110) (q:draft)
